  FT["PH-H16644"] = {"id":"PH-H16644","coverage":"full","language":"en","sourceName":"The LawPhil Project — Arellano Law Foundation","sourceUrl":"","fetchedAt":"2026-10-28","articleCount":1,"structureMode":"WHOLE","title":{"zh":null,"en":"MALAGAÑANG RESIDENCE 07 THE PRESIDENT OF THE PHILIPPINES BY THE PRESIDENT OF THE PHILIPPINES CREATING THE PRESIDENTIAL COMPLAINTS AND ACTION COMMITTEE UNDER THE OFFICE OF THE PRESIDENT.","orig":"MALAGAÑANG RESIDENCE 07 THE PRESIDENT OF THE PHILIPPINES BY THE PRESIDENT OF THE PHILIPPINES CREATING THE PRESIDENTIAL COMPLAINTS AND ACTION COMMITTEE UNDER THE OFFICE OF THE PRESIDENT."},"level":"law","status":"active","docNumber":"Executive Order No. 19","issuingBody":"President of the Philippines","completenessNote":"全文，共 1 条；逐字取自 LawPhil PDF 文本化成果（第三方 OCR，非机翻），原始文件 EO_00019_1954.txt","textQuality":"ocr-vendor","sourceFile":"菲律宾/法律原文/07_行政命令_EO/EO_00019_1954.txt","country":"PH","countryName":"菲律宾","layer":"intl","articles":[{"id":"PH-H16644-A1","no":1,"noLabel":{},"text":{"en":"• 2 ..\nlities of the government, including government-owned or con-\ntrolled corporations are performing the duties entrusted to\nTo receive, process and evaluate, and to conduct\nor cause the performance of preliminary fact-finding inves-\ntigations of, sworn complaints against the acts, conduct or\nbehaviour of any official or emplovee of any of the execu-\ntive depariments, bureaus, offices, agencies, or instrumen-\ntalities of the government, including government-owned or\ncontrolled corporations;\nTo refer and/or recommend to the governmental agen-\ncy concerned for appropriate action all such complaints as\nmay be received by the Committee to the end that justice,\neconomy, efficiency and a high standard of morality may be\nobserved and effected in the various branches, departments,\nbureaus, offices, agencies and instrumentalities of the\ngovernment, including government-owned or controlled corr\nTo keep the Fresident of the Philippines informed\non the implementation of government measures designed to\nimprove the public service and the efficiency of government\n0. To make and submit from time to time appropriate\nrecommendations for the improvement of the administration\nof the government and its essential services and operations;\n£.\nTo perform such other duties and related functions\nas the President of the Philippines may from time to time\nassign to it.\n4. The Chairman of the Prosidential Complaints and Action\nCommittee is hereby athorized to utilize and allow the use of\nany form of transportation or means of conveyance in his official\ntravels or those of the Committee personnel.\n5. The Chairman or his representative may summon witnesses\nby subpoena and subpocna daces teum, administer oaths and take\ntestimony relevant to the preliminary fact-finding investigation\nconducted by them.\n..\nAll departments\n- 3 -\n6. All departments, bureaus, offices,\nagencies and instru-\nmentalities of the government, including the government-owned\nand controlled corporations, are enjoined to extend full assist-\nance and cooperation to the Chairman of the Presidential Com-\nplaints and Action Committee or his representative.\nTo facilitate\nthis arrangement, the heads of all executive departments, bureaus,\noffices, agencies and instrumentalities of the government, includ-\ning government-owned and controlled corporations, shall designate\nan official whose services shall be made available to the Presi-\ndential Complaints and Action Committee whenever such services\nare required on matters pertaining to their respective departments,\nbureaus, offices, agencies or entities.\nThis Executive Order supersedes Executive Order No. 1,\ndated December 30, 1953.\nDone in the City of Manila, this 17th day of March, in the\nyear of Our Lord, nineteen hundred and fifty-four, and of the\nIndependence of the Philippines, the eighth.\n(SGD.). RAMON MAGSAYSAY\nPresident of the Philippines\nBy the President:\nFRED RUIZ CASTRO\nExecutive Secretary\n3"}}],"pack":"ph-p157"};
  FT["PH-H16645"] = {"id":"PH-H16645","coverage":"full","language":"en","sourceName":"The LawPhil Project — Arellano Law Foundation","sourceUrl":"","fetchedAt":"2026-10-28","articleCount":1,"structureMode":"WHOLE","title":{"zh":null,"en":"MALACANANG RESIDEUCE OF THD PRESIDENT OF THe PHILIPPINES BY THE PRESIDENT OF THE PHILIPFILES EXCUTIVE ORDER NO. 19 PRESCRIBING RULES AND REGULATIONS FOR APPEALS TO THE OFTICE OP THE PRESIDENT AID FOR FINALITY OF DECISIONS TIEREOF.","orig":"MALACANANG RESIDEUCE OF THD PRESIDENT OF THe PHILIPPINES BY THE PRESIDENT OF THE PHILIPFILES EXCUTIVE ORDER NO. 19 PRESCRIBING RULES AND REGULATIONS FOR APPEALS TO THE OFTICE OP THE PRESIDENT AID FOR FINALITY OF DECISIONS TIEREOF."},"level":"law","status":"active","docNumber":"Executive Order No. 19","issuingBody":"President of the Philippines","completenessNote":"全文，共 1 条；逐字取自 LawPhil PDF 文本化成果（第三方 OCR，非机翻），原始文件 EO_00019_1966.txt","textQuality":"ocr-vendor","sourceFile":"菲律宾/法律原文/07_行政命令_EO/EO_00019_1966.txt","country":"PH","countryName":"菲律宾","layer":"intl","articles":[{"id":"PH-H16645-A1","no":1,"noLabel":{},"text":{"en":"filing of petitions for reconsideration, so that\nthere will be stability and finality of administra-\ntive decisions and frivolous appeals may be dis-\nisidortOg Tho Philippinos, by virtue of the povors\n, TOREFORE, I, FERDIlAID D. MARCOS, Fro-\nvested in me by law, do hereby pronulgate the Pol-\nlowing rules and rogulations for the purpose:\n1. Unless otherwise provided or governed by\nspecial laws or where time io clearly of the ossence,\nan appeal to the Office of the President, which\nis nat a mactor of right in the absence of statu-\ntory provisions to that effect, shall be taken\nwithin thirty (30) days, reckoned fron recoipt of\nthe decision or action appealed froti,\n2. Failure to appeal within the prescribed\nperiod shall rendor the decision or action subject\nthereof final and executory.\n3. The appeal should bo filed diroctly with the\noffico of the President. It shall be in vriting and\nshall specifically sot forth tho particular action\nto which exception is taken, with the reasons, au-\nthorities and precedents relied upon for the re-\nversal of the disputed docision or action, with\nnotice thereof to tho adverse party and the office\nwhich rendered the decisions involvod.\n4. Deciaions of the Office of the Fresident in\nthe cases covered by this Ordor as onuerated in\nClause 7 hereof shall, unless othervise expressly\nprovided in tho decisions on spocial cases of an\nurgent nature, become final after the lapse of fif-\nteen (15) davs fros recoist of a cony thereof by\nthe parties involved, unless a petition or request\nfor reconsideration is reasonably filed by the ag-\ngrieved party to stop the runnine of the\nbased on any of the follovine grounds:\ndecision is not in confority with the applicable\nlaw or ovidenco presented; (b) newly discovered evi-\ndence which could not, with reasonable diligence,\nhave been discovered and be produced whon the\n32\ndecision was still under advisement and which, if\npresented, would probably alter the result thereof;\nor (c) fraud, accident, aistake or excusable neg-\nligence which ordinary prudence could not have\nguarded against and by reason of which the aggrieved\nparty has probably been impaired in his rights.\n5. Petitions for reconsideration filed after\nthe aforesaid period shall not be entertained un-\nless tho Office of the resident, for exceptionally\nmeritorious causes, decides to act thereon, pro-\nvided that only one potition for roconsideration\nby any party shall be allowed.\n6. A fee of twenty pesos (720.00) shall be\ncharged for every appeai or petition for reviow\nfiled with this Office, the foos collocted to\naccrue to and constituto a part of tho general\nfund of the National Governnent.\n7. The Rules of Court shall apply in a sup-\npletory character henever practicable and convo_\n8. The foregoing rules shall apply to and be\nobserved in appeals to chis Office taken by pri-\nvate parties adversely affected by docisions of tho\ndepartments, offices and entities specified below,\nas woll as othor appeals of similar nature not\ngoverned by special laws.\n(1) Department of Agriculture and Natural\n(a) Public land applications\nForestry concassions\nFishpond applications\n(d) Revocation of license of fishing boats\n(2) Department of Finance:\n(a) Anti-dumpine cases\n(6)\nI-I-rprodatin of aport peguita\n(c) Tax exeuptions under the\nCustoms Code\n(d) Sauggling cases\n33\ndecision was still under auvisement and which,\npresented, would probably alter the result thereof;\nor (c) fraud, , accident, mistake or excusable neg-\nligence which ordinary prudence could not have\nguarded against and by reason of which the aggrieved\nparty has probably been impaired in his rights.\n5. Petitions for reconsideration filed after\nthe aforesaid period shall not be entertained un-\nless tho Office of tho Frosident, for exceptionally\nmeritorious causes, decides to act thereon, pro-\nvided that only one petition for reconsideration\nby any party shall be allowed.\n6. A lee of twenty pesos (720.00) shall be\ncharged for every appeal or potition for reviow\nfiled with this Office, the foes collated to\naccrue to and constituto a part of the reneral\nfund of the Mational Governient.\n7. The Rules of Court shall apply in a sup-\npletory character\nWhenever practicablo and convo-\n8. The foregoing rules shall apply to and be\nobserved in appeals to chis Office taken by pri-\nvate parties adversely affectod by docisions of tho\ndepartments, offices and entities specified below,\nas woll as other appeals of siniler nature not\ngoverned by special laws.\n(1) Department of Agriculture and Natural\n(a) Fublic land applications\nForestry concessions\n(c) Fishpond applications\n(a) Revocation of license of fishing boats\n(2) Department of Finance:\n(a) Anti-dumping cases\nIstorproda&l a of acert seruita\n(c) Tax exemptions undor the Tariff and\nCustoms Code\n(d) Smuggling cases\n33\n(3) Department of Public Works and Communi-\n(al Obstruction to navigation and communal\nfishing grounds\n(b) Awards of contracts for public worles\n(4) Department of General Services:\n(a) Sales and/or leases of residential,\ncommercial and industrial government\nlots and buildings\n(6) Avards of contracts for materials,\nsupplies, equipment, services, etc.\n(5) Government-oned or controlled corporations:\n(a) Awards of contracts\n(6) Land Authority (formerly Land Tenure\nAdministration)\n'(7) Gamos and Amusements Board\n(a) Decisions, order or rulings of the\nBoard affecting racing clubs, jai-alai\ncorporation and other persons or enti-\nThis order shall take effect fifteen (15) days\nafter its publication in the Official Gazette,\nDone in the City of Manile, this 2nd day of\nApril, in the year of Our Lord, rineteen hundred\nand sixty-six.\n(SGD.) FERDINANO D.\nPresident of the Fhilippines\nBy the Fresident:\n(SGD.) RAFABL 11. SALAS\nExecutive Secretary"}}],"pack":"ph-p157"};
