  FT["PH-H16705"] = {"id":"PH-H16705","coverage":"full","language":"en","sourceName":"The LawPhil Project — Arellano Law Foundation","sourceUrl":"LawPhil (HTML full text only)  |  https://lawphil.net/executive/execord/eo1945/eo_24_1945.html","fetchedAt":"2026-10-28","articleCount":1,"structureMode":"WHOLE","title":{"zh":null,"en":"Amending Executive Order No. 371 of October 2, 1941, Fixing the Maximum Selling Prices of Certain Articles of Prime Necessity, and Promulgating Rules and Regulations for the Enforcement Thereof.","orig":"Amending Executive Order No. 371 of October 2, 1941, Fixing the Maximum Selling Prices of Certain Articles of Prime Necessity, and Promulgating Rules and Regulations for the Enforcement Thereof."},"level":"law","status":"active","docNumber":"Executive Order No. 24","issuingBody":"President of the Philippines","promulgatedDate":"1945-03-10","completenessNote":"全文，共 1 条；逐字取自 LawPhil PDF 文本化成果（第三方 OCR，非机翻），原始文件 EO_00024_1945_html.txt","textQuality":"ocr-vendor","sourceFile":"菲律宾/法律原文/07_行政命令_EO/EO_00024_1945_html.txt","country":"PH","countryName":"菲律宾","layer":"intl","articles":[{"id":"PH-H16705-A1","no":1,"noLabel":{},"text":{"en":"MALACAÑAN PALACE\nBY THE PRESIDENT OF THE PHILIPPINES\n[ Executive Order No. 24, March 10, 1945 ]\nAMENDING EXECUTIVE ORDER NO. 371 OF OCTOBER 2, 1941, FIXING THE MAXIMUM SELLING\nPRICES OF CERTAIN ARTICLES OF PRIME NECESSITY, AND PROMULGATING RULES AND\nREGULATIONS FOR THE ENFORCEMENT THEREOF.\nWHEREAS, in view of the shortage of food, other articles of prime necessity, and services caused by the war,\nit is essential to the welfare of the people that the fixing of the maximum selling prices of such articles as\npromulgated on October 2, 1941, be continued with such modifications as circumstances may require.\nNOW, THEREFORE, I, SERGIO OSMEÑA, President of the Philippines, by virtue of the authority vested in\nme by the Constitution and the laws of the Philippines, do hereby prescribe and promulgate the following\nschedule of maximum prices in the province of Leyte.\nMAXIMUM SELLING PRICES\nPRODUCTUNITPRICES PAID BY WHOLESALERPRICES PAID BY RETAILERPRICES PAID BY\n1. RICE-ELONGcavan\n0.11\n2. RICE NATIVE UNHUSKED (PALAY)cavan3.00\n3. CORN-MILLEDcavan\n0.07\n4. CORN-GRAINcavan\n5. WHEAT-FLOUR-AMERICAN OR AUSTRALIAN12-lb sack\n6. VEGETABLE LARDkilo0.320.330.35\n7. CORN BEEF, CANNED12 oz tin (case 48)\n8. SARDINES, CANNED15 oz tin (case 48)\n9. SUGAR, BROWN REFINEDpicul (63.25 kilo)\n0.05\n11. MILK-CONDENSEDCase 48 cans (14 oz)\n12. MILK EVAPORATEDCase 48 cans (14 oz)\n13. VIENNA SAUSAGE, CANNEDCase 48 cans (4 oz)\n14. PORK AND BEANS, CANNEDCase 48 cans (16 oz)\n0.40\n0.60\n17. CARABAO MEATKilo\n0.45\nFirst class\nSecond class\nThird class\nFourth classkilo\n\"\n\"\n\"\n0.40\n0.30\n0.20\n0.10\nFirst class\nSecond class\nThird class\nFourth classkilo\n\"\n\"\n\"\n\"\n0.80\n0.60\n0.40\n0.20\n20. FISH (SALTED BUT NOT DRIED):\nFirst class\nSecond class\nThird class\nFourth classkilo\n\"\n\"\n\"\n0.60\n0.45\n0.30\n0.15\n21. FISH; SALTED, SMALL, such as Cinamos, Bolinaw, Bagon etc.Petroleum can (5 gal)\n(See appendiz Page 4)\n5.00\n0.36\n23. VEGETABLES:\nCaguedilla\nGabi1 Petroleum can (5gal)\nSmall bundle\n\"\n0.50\n0.01\n0.10\n0.10\n0.01\n0.01\n0.01\n0.01\n0.05\n24. CHICKENSEach depending on size\n0.25\n1.20\n25. BANANASEach\n0.01\nLarge size bars\n(approx. 1 kilo)\nSmall size bars\n(approx. 1/2 kilo)Each\n0.30\n0.16\nUnder shirt\nHandkerchief\nPillow case\nMattress cover\nDemins per suit\nMinimum chargeEach (pair)\n\"\n\"\n\"\n\"\n\"\n\"\n\"\n\"\n\"\n\"\n\"\n\"\n\"\n0.15\n0.15\n0.15\n0.05\n0.05\n0.05\n0.02\n0.02\n0.02\n0.15\n0.05\n0.20\n0.25\n0.05\n0.50\n0.50\n0.20\nDone at the City of Manila, this 10th day of March, in the year of Our Lord, Nineteen Hundred and Forty-five,\nand of the Commonwealth of the Philippines, the tenth.\n(Sgd.) SERGIO OSMEÑA\nPresident of the Philippines\nBy the President:\n(Sgd.) ARTURO B. ROTOR\nSecretary to the President"}}],"pack":"ph-p157"};
