  FT["PH-H16793"] = {"id":"PH-H16793","coverage":"full","language":"en","sourceName":"The LawPhil Project — Arellano Law Foundation","sourceUrl":"","fetchedAt":"2026-10-28","articleCount":1,"structureMode":"WHOLE","title":{"zh":null,"en":"TO PROVIDE FOR THE~E~;ION OF A CHAIRMAN FROM AMONG THE MEMBERS OF COMMISSION ON POPULATION BOARD","orig":"TO PROVIDE FOR THE~E~;ION OF A CHAIRMAN FROM AMONG THE MEMBERS OF COMMISSION ON POPULATION BOARD"},"level":"law","status":"active","docNumber":"Executive Order No. 32","issuingBody":"President of the Philippines","completenessNote":"全文，共 1 条；逐字取自 LawPhil PDF 文本化成果（第三方 OCR，非机翻），原始文件 EO_00032_1992.txt","textQuality":"ocr-vendor","sourceFile":"菲律宾/法律原文/07_行政命令_EO/EO_00032_1992.txt","country":"PH","countryName":"菲律宾","layer":"intl","articles":[{"id":"PH-H16793-A1","no":1,"noLabel":{},"text":{"en":"leadership\nin the Board.\n.\n~Philippines,\n1.\nPresidential\nDecreemended\nto read as follows:\n79,\n6.\nI.-:ommissioners\nPopulaticbn\nCommission\nof Commissioners,\nhereinafter\n(11)\ngovernment\n(~)\nas representatives\n..\nand Development\nDirector-General\nDevelopment\nThe Secretary\nThe Secretary\nGovernment\nThe Secretary\nand Employment\nThe Secretary\nof Agriculture\n..\nThe Secretary\nof Agrarian\nThe Secretary\nof Trade and Industry\nSECTIONimmediately.\n3.\n~"}}],"pack":"ph-p157"};
  FT["PH-H16794"] = {"id":"PH-H16794","coverage":"full","language":"en","sourceName":"The LawPhil Project — Arellano Law Foundation","sourceUrl":"","fetchedAt":"2026-10-28","articleCount":2,"structureMode":"ARTICLE","title":{"zh":null,"en":"CREATING A TASK FORCE TO INVESTIGATE AND PROSECUTB SUGAR SMUGGLING","orig":"CREATING A TASK FORCE TO INVESTIGATE AND PROSECUTB SUGAR SMUGGLING"},"level":"law","status":"active","docNumber":"Executive Order No. 32","issuingBody":"President of the Philippines","completenessNote":"全文，共 2 条；逐字取自 LawPhil PDF 文本化成果（第三方 OCR，非机翻），原始文件 EO_00032_1998.txt","textQuality":"ocr-vendor","sourceFile":"菲律宾/法律原文/07_行政命令_EO/EO_00032_1998.txt","country":"PH","countryName":"菲律宾","layer":"intl","articles":[{"id":"PH-H16794-A3","no":3,"noLabel":{"en":"SECTION 3"},"text":{"en":"Advisorv Council - There is hereby createcl an Advisory Council on\nSugar Smuggiing to be composed of the following:\nl. Administrator of the Sugar Rtgulatory Aclministration (SRA) - Chairma,\n2. Commissioner, Economic Intelligence and Investigation Bureau (llIIB) - Vice\n3. Four (4) representatives from the Sugar Planters/Federation - Mernber\n4. Two(2) representatives from the PAOCC _ Member\nThe technical anci aciministrative support staff of the Presidential Anti-Organized Crime\nCommission (PAOCC) and the technical and administrative staff of the Sugar ltegulatory\nAdministration (SRA) shall serve as the Secretariat of the Advisory Council."}},{"id":"PH-H16794-A4","no":4,"noLabel":{"en":"SECTION 4"},"text":{"en":"Futtctions of the Advisorv Council - The Advisory Council Bhall\nperform the following functions:\n1. Provide technical information on local a,d frlreign shipme,ts of sugar.;\n2 Recommend policies, programs, activities and compouition of the 1:ask Force;\n3. Provide equipment and logistics of the secretariat and the Task Force;\n4. Recommend to the Chairman of the PAOCC the system of rewards and incentives for\ninformants; and\n5. Perform other functions as may be directed by the chairman of the pAocc.\nSECTIOI{ 5. Powers and Functions\nshall have the following powers and functions:\nThe Task Force on Sugar Smuggling\na. Conduct intelligence and counter-intelligence operations to identify persons or groups\ninvolved in the smuggling of sugar;\nb. Issue warrant and detention orders on\nused in the smuggling of sugar;\nthe smuggled sugar as well as on tlie vessel\nCause or direct the arrest and investigation of persons involvecl in sugar smuggling;\nRefer the case at hand, as the Task Force may rleem proper and necessary to the\nDepartment of Justice and/or other appropriate law enforcement ug\"rr\"i., for\ninvestigation or prosecution;\nFollow-up the progress of cases taken cognizance of by the Task Force on Sugar\nSelect and recruit from the Economic Intelligence and Investigation Bureau (EIIB),\nBureau of customs (Boc), philippine ports Authority gra), prrilippine coast\nGuard' PNP, NBI, AFP and other law enforcement ageircies for detail'to the Task\nForce subject to the confonnity of the agency \"on\"\"*\"d;\n\ng' Enlist the assistanoe of any government agency or office inciuciing government\ncorporation in the drive against sugar smuggling; and\ni1' Grant monetary rewards or inceBtives to informants giving vital information leacling\nto the apprehe,sion of persons invorved in sugar srnuggling-.\nThe provisions of Memorandum order No. 225 with respect to the delineation of\nI'nctions among government agencies shall not apply to the operations of the..Task Force on\nSugar Smuggling.\nSECTION 6' sqoervision aqd control - The Task Force on sugar smuggling shall\nlre under the supervision and control ;ath\" P..rrd*tial Anti-organized crime commission.\nSECTI0N 7' operatins Guidelines - The chairman of presiclential Anti-organizetl\ncrime commission (PAocc) may pto*urgut\" operating guidelines as maybe necessary to\nimplernent this Executive order in corisultation wiuith\" aari.\"ry;;;;.il \"\"'\nSECTION 8' Dkposition o,{- cqnfuc.oted saenr. - The sugar confiscatecl by the\ngoverrunent from sugar smuggling shall be t \"taio t.urt t y tte National iood Authority (NFA)\nto be sold to the public. The proceeds of the sale shall be remitted to the presiclential Anti-\norganized crime commission (PAocc) to be used in the payment of rewards or incentives to\ninformants and operatives and for trre operations of the Task Force.\nSECTION 9' Effectivitv - This Executive order shall take effect immediately.\nDone in the city of Manila tnis l6'9aay of october in the year of our. Lor6. Nineteen\nI-lundred and Ninety-Eight.\n.TOSEPH EJETTCITO ESTRADA\nBy the President:\nIIONALDO B. ZAI\\{ORA\nExecutive Secrelarv"}}],"pack":"ph-p157"};
  FT["PH-H16795"] = {"id":"PH-H16795","coverage":"full","language":"en","sourceName":"The LawPhil Project — Arellano Law Foundation","sourceUrl":"","fetchedAt":"2026-10-28","articleCount":3,"structureMode":"ARTICLE","title":{"zh":null,"en":"MALACAÑANG PMS LIBRARY","orig":"MALACAÑANG PMS LIBRARY"},"level":"law","status":"active","docNumber":"Executive Order No. 32","issuingBody":"President of the Philippines","completenessNote":"全文，共 3 条；逐字取自 LawPhil PDF 文本化成果（第三方 OCR，非机翻），原始文件 EO_00032_2001.txt","textQuality":"ocr-vendor","sourceFile":"菲律宾/法律原文/07_行政命令_EO/EO_00032_2001.txt","country":"PH","countryName":"菲律宾","layer":"intl","articles":[{"id":"PH-H16795-A1","no":1,"noLabel":{"en":"SECTION 1"},"text":{"en":"Paragraphs 1.7 a and b of Executive Order No. 219 dated\nJanuary 3, 1995 are hereby amended to read as follows:\n\"1.7. Constituting a Single Negotiating Panel. To represent\nthe Philippines in all negotiations leading to the conclusion of Air\nServices Agreements or similar arrangements and succeeding\nnegotiations or consultation talks regarding these Air Services\nAgreements or similar arrangements, a single Negotiating Panel is\nhereby constituted composed of representatives of the following\ngovernment agencies:\nDepartment of Transportation and\nCommunications\nDepartment of Foreign. Affairs\nDepartment of Tourism\nDepartment of Trade and Industry\nCivil Aeronautics Board\n- Vice-Chairman\nand such other person/s as may be authorized by the President.\" J\nPOMA Outgoing • 04865"}},{"id":"PH-H16795-A2","no":2,"noLabel":{"en":"SECTION 2"},"text":{"en":"All orders, circulars, memoranda, rules, regulations and\nother issuances or parts thereof inconsistent herewith are hereby superseded or\namended accordingly."}},{"id":"PH-H16795-A3","no":3,"noLabel":{"en":"SECTION 3"},"text":{"en":"This Executive Order shall take effect immediately following\nits publication in a newspaper of general circulation.\nCity of Manila, August 22, 2001.\nBy the President:\n69. 1°.\nALBERTO G. ROMULO\nExecutive Secretary\nPMS LIBRARY\n18110 01110 0111 1081\nPMS LIBRARY ECODE002029"}}],"pack":"ph-p157"};
  FT["PH-H16796"] = {"id":"PH-H16796","coverage":"full","language":"en","sourceName":"The LawPhil Project — Arellano Law Foundation","sourceUrl":"","fetchedAt":"2026-10-28","articleCount":7,"structureMode":"ARTICLE","title":{"zh":null,"en":"MALACAÑAN PALACE BY THE PRESIDENT OF THE PHILIPPINES INSTITUTING THE PUBLIC TRANSPORT ASSISTANCE PROGRAM - PANTAWID PASADA","orig":"MALACAÑAN PALACE BY THE PRESIDENT OF THE PHILIPPINES INSTITUTING THE PUBLIC TRANSPORT ASSISTANCE PROGRAM - PANTAWID PASADA"},"level":"law","status":"active","docNumber":"Executive Order No. 32","issuingBody":"President of the Philippines","completenessNote":"全文，共 7 条；逐字取自 LawPhil PDF 文本化成果（第三方 OCR，非机翻），原始文件 EO_00032_2011.txt","textQuality":"ocr-vendor","sourceFile":"菲律宾/法律原文/07_行政命令_EO/EO_00032_2011.txt","country":"PH","countryName":"菲律宾","layer":"intl","articles":[{"id":"PH-H16796-A1","no":1,"noLabel":{"en":"SECTION 1"},"text":{"en":"The Public Transport Assistance Program - Pantawid\nThe \"Public Transport Assistance Program\" (PTAP) is hereby\nestablished which shall provide targeted relief to the public transport sector to\ncushion the impact of high fuel prices on the riding and consuming public. The\nDepartment of Energy (DOE) is hereby designated as the lead agency to\nimplement the PTAP."}},{"id":"PH-H16796-A2","no":2,"noLabel":{"en":"SECTION 2"},"text":{"en":"Disbursement of the PTAP Funds. The PTAP shall be\nimplemented in coordination with the ICC consistent with the members' specific\nresponsibilities pursuant to Section 3, AO No. 6 (s. 2011). Specifically, the\nDepartment of Transportation and Communications (DOTC), Department of\nFinance (DOF), and the Department of Energy (DOE) are jointly authorized to\ndetermine the monthly funding requirement of the PTAP. The PTAP shall\npartially subsidize the average consumption of the identified public transport\ngroup; Provided, That disbursement shall be made per franchisee and on the\nnumber of franchised units based on information to be provided by the DOTC\nthrough the Land Transportation Franchising and Regulatory Board (LTFRB):\nProvided further, That the DOE shall use smart cards to ensure the integrity of\nthe disbursements.\nUpon the recommendation of the ICC, the DOE may review the list of\nthose entitled to the PTAP to include other sectors whose operations may be\nclassified as sensitive to high oil prices, and it may also suspend the PTAP when\nit determines that the impact of fuel costs on these sectors no longer exists\nIn the case of tricycles, the PTAP shall also subsidize a portion of their\naverage consumption. The Department of the Interior and Local Government\n(DILG) shall coordinate with Local Government Units (LGUs) for the joint\nimplementation of the PTAP; Provided: That funding for PTAP for tricycles shall\nbe subject to availability of counterpart funds of the respective LGUs.\nAfter the first month of implementation, the DOE shall submit to the ICC\na report on the status of the accomplishments of the PTAP. The ICC shall\nsubmit its recommendations to the President regarding the continued\nimplementation of the program and its projected requirements.\nFunding Source of the PTAP. The initial funding\nrequirements of the program shall be FOUR HUNDRED FIFTY MILLION PESOS\n(P450,000,000.00) which shall be sourced from the Special Account in the\nGeneral Fund (SAG) of the DOE under Fund 151, to be released by the\nDepartment of Budget and Management (DBM) subject to the submission of the\nBureau of the Treasury (Br) Certification on the availability of deposited\n2\nOtice of thp Prembert of the \"Ohtloptes\n\ncollections with the SAG of the DOE and to existing laws and the usual\ngovernment budgetary, accounting and auditing rules and regulations."}},{"id":"PH-H16796-A4","no":4,"noLabel":{"en":"SECTION 4"},"text":{"en":"Implementation of the PTAP. In the implementation of the\nPTAP, the DOE shall coordinate with the following departments:\n(a) Department of National Defense (DND);"}},{"id":"PH-H16796-A5","no":5,"noLabel":{"en":"SECTION 5"},"text":{"en":"Duty to Extend Assistance to the PTAP. The\ndepartments, bureaus, offices, agencies or instrumentalities of the Government,\nincluding government-owned and/or controlled corporations and government\nfinancial institutions are hereby directed to extend such assistance and support\nto the PTAP, as may be necessary, for its successful implementation."}},{"id":"PH-H16796-A6","no":6,"noLabel":{"en":"SECTION 6"},"text":{"en":"Implementing Guidelines. The DOE as Lead, DBM, DILG,\nDOF, and DOTC shall promulgate the rules and regulations for the\nimplementation of this Order within fifteen (15) days from effectivity hereof."}},{"id":"PH-H16796-A7","no":7,"noLabel":{"en":"SECTION 7"},"text":{"en":"Separability. If any provision of this Executive Order is\ndeclared invalid or unconstitutional, the other provisions unaffected shall remain\nvalid and subsisting."}},{"id":"PH-H16796-A8","no":8,"noLabel":{"en":"SECTION 8"},"text":{"en":"Effectivity. This Executive Order shall take effect\nimmediately upon publication in a newspaper of general circulation.\nDONE, in the City of Manila, this Ist\nthe Year of our Lord, Two Thousand and Eleven.\nBy the President:\nPAQUITO N. OCHOA, JR.\nExecutive Secretary\n@thre of the President of the Philippines"}}],"pack":"ph-p157"};
  FT["PH-H16797"] = {"id":"PH-H16797","coverage":"full","language":"en","sourceName":"The LawPhil Project — Arellano Law Foundation","sourceUrl":"","fetchedAt":"2026-10-28","articleCount":5,"structureMode":"ARTICLE","title":{"zh":null,"en":"MALACAÑAN PALACE BY THE PRESIDENT OF THE PHILIPPINES INCLUSION OF THE DEPARTMENT OF TRANSPORTATION AND THE DEPARTMENT INFORMATION AND COMMUNICATIONS TECHNOLOGY AS MEMBERS OF THE NATIONAL DISASTER RISK REDUCTION AND MANAGEMENT COUNCIL","orig":"MALACAÑAN PALACE BY THE PRESIDENT OF THE PHILIPPINES INCLUSION OF THE DEPARTMENT OF TRANSPORTATION AND THE DEPARTMENT INFORMATION AND COMMUNICATIONS TECHNOLOGY AS MEMBERS OF THE NATIONAL DISASTER RISK REDUCTION AND MANAGEMENT COUNCIL"},"level":"law","status":"active","docNumber":"Executive Order No. 32","issuingBody":"President of the Philippines","completenessNote":"全文，共 5 条；逐字取自 LawPhil PDF 文本化成果（第三方 OCR，非机翻），原始文件 EO_00032_2017.txt","textQuality":"ocr-vendor","sourceFile":"菲律宾/法律原文/07_行政命令_EO/EO_00032_2017.txt","country":"PH","countryName":"菲律宾","layer":"intl","articles":[{"id":"PH-H16797-A1","no":1,"noLabel":{"en":"SECTION 1"},"text":{"en":"NDRRMC Composition. The DICT and the DOT are hereby\nincluded as members of the NDRRMC.\nTHE PRESIDENT OF THE PHILIPPINES"}},{"id":"PH-H16797-A2","no":2,"noLabel":{"en":"SECTION 2"},"text":{"en":"Funding Requirements. Funding requirements for the\nimplementation of this Order shall be included in the respective budgets of the DICT\nand the DOTr."}},{"id":"PH-H16797-A3","no":3,"noLabel":{"en":"SECTION 3"},"text":{"en":"Repeal. All orders, rules and regulations, issuances or any part\nthereof inconsistent with the provisions of this Executive Order are hereby repealed,\namended or modified accordingly."}},{"id":"PH-H16797-A4","no":4,"noLabel":{"en":"SECTION 4"},"text":{"en":"Separability. If any section or part of this Order is held\nunconstitutional or invalid, the other sections or provisions not otherwise affected\nshall remain in full force and effect."}},{"id":"PH-H16797-A5","no":5,"noLabel":{"en":"SECTION 5"},"text":{"en":"Effectivity. This Executive Order shall take effect immediately.\nDONE, in the City of Manila this 12t lay of\nOur Lord, Two Thousand and Seventeen.\n, in the year of\nBy the President:\nSALVADOR C. MEDIALDEA\nExecutive Secretary 3\nREPUBLIC OF THE PHILIPPNES"}}],"pack":"ph-p157"};
  FT["PH-H16798"] = {"id":"PH-H16798","coverage":"full","language":"en","sourceName":"The LawPhil Project — Arellano Law Foundation","sourceUrl":"","fetchedAt":"2026-10-28","articleCount":10,"structureMode":"ARTICLE","title":{"zh":null,"en":"MALACAÑAN PALACE BY THE PRESIDENT OF THE PHILIPPINES STREAMLINING THE PERMITTING PROCESS FOR THE CONSTRUCTION OF TELECOMMUNICATIONS AND INTERNET INFRASTRUCTURE","orig":"MALACAÑAN PALACE BY THE PRESIDENT OF THE PHILIPPINES STREAMLINING THE PERMITTING PROCESS FOR THE CONSTRUCTION OF TELECOMMUNICATIONS AND INTERNET INFRASTRUCTURE"},"level":"law","status":"active","docNumber":"Executive Order No. 32","issuingBody":"President of the Philippines","completenessNote":"全文，共 10 条；逐字取自 LawPhil PDF 文本化成果（第三方 OCR，非机翻），原始文件 EO_00032_2023.txt","textQuality":"ocr-vendor","sourceFile":"菲律宾/法律原文/07_行政命令_EO/EO_00032_2023.txt","country":"PH","countryName":"菲律宾","layer":"intl","articles":[{"id":"PH-H16798-A1","no":1,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 1"},"text":{"en":"Coverage. This Order shall cover all GAs and instrumentalities, including\ngovernment-owned or -controlled corporations, as well as LGUs, involved in the issuance of\npermits, licenses, clearances, certifications, and authorizations that are required for the\na. Construction, installation, repair, operation, and maintenance of Shared Passive\nTelecommunications Tower Infrastructure; and\nErection of poles, installation of aerial and underground cables and facilities,\nunderground fiber ducts, ground terminals and other transmission or similar\ntelecommunications and internet infrastructure and facilities, and other passive\ninfrastructures.\n2. Streamlined\nRequirements for the Construction of\nTelecommunications and Internet Infrastructure. No other national or local permit or\nclearance shall be required in the construction, installation, repair, operation, and\nmaintenance of telecommunications and internet infrastructure, except for the following\nrequirements:\nBuilding Permit issued by the Office of the Building Official;\nHeight Clearance Permit from the Civil Aviation Authority of the Philippines (CAAP),\nexcept when the proposed structure is outside the CAP Critical Areas and below fifty\n(50) meters in height above the elevation of the ground;\nc. Homeowners and other community clearances;\nClearances from other government agencies, whenever applicable:\nEnvironmental Compliance Certificate (ECC), if the proposed project site is within an\nenvironmentally critical area;\nSpecial Use Agreement in Protected Areas, if the proposed project site is a protected\nill. Free and Prior Informed Consent, if the proposed project site is within an ancestral\niv. Land Use Conversion from the Department of Agrarian Reform (DAR) Central Office,\nif the proposed project site requires the conversion of an agricultural land of more\nthan five (5) hectares, or from the DAR Regional Office, if the said land is five (5)\nhectares and below;\nClearance from Laguna Lake Development Authority, if the proposed project site is\nwithin the Laguna de Bay region;\nClearance from the Philippine Economic Zone Authority (PEZA), if the proposed site\nis within an economic zone or any other area owned, administered or operated by\nStrategic Environment Plan Clearance from the Palawan Council for Sustainable\nDevelopment, if the proposed project site is within the Province of Palawan; and\nOther requirements as mandated by the Constitution and existing laws.\n2\n\nThe following shall not be required from applicants in securing a Building Permit, a\nFire Safety Evaluation Clearance, a Barangay Clearance, or a Locational Clearance:\nSangguniang Panlungsod/Bayan Resolution;\nSangguniang Barangay Resolution;\nC. ECC or Certificate of Non-Coverage, if the proposed site of construction is outside an\nenvironmentally critical area;\nd. Certificate of Safety Evaluation from the Department of Health and the Food and Drug\nAdministration: and\ne. Certified True Copy of National Telecommunications Commission (NTC) Provisional\nAuthority or Certificate of Public Convenience and Necessity or Certificate of\nRegistration to Provide Telecommunication Services."}},{"id":"PH-H16798-A3","no":3,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 3"},"text":{"en":"Applicability. The streamlined requirements under Section 2 hereof shall\napply to all pending and new applications for securing the above permits, licenses,\nclearances, certifications, and authorizations, submitted by the following:\na. Public Telecommunications Entities (PTs), which are holders of Certificates of Public\nConvenience and Necessity or Provisional Authorities granted by the NTC;\nb. Cable TV (CATV) Operators, which are registered as Value-Added Service (VAS)\nProviders and authorized to offer internet access service;\nC. VAS Providers, which are registered with the NTC to offer internet access service and\ncontracted by the DICT under the Free Public Internet Access Program in Public Places;\nd. ICT Technology Providers or Physical Infrastructure Contractors, which are contracted\nby PTEs or CAT Operators to rollout or construct, install, and/or establish their\ninfrastructure;\ne. Independent Tower Companies, which are registered with the DICT;\nDistribution Utility Owners, which are covered by a franchise issued by the Congress of\nthe Philippines; and\ng. All authorized contractors of the foregoing entities."}},{"id":"PH-H16798-A4","no":4,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 4"},"text":{"en":"Action on the Application. All covered applications not acted upon within\nthe prescribed period as provided under existing laws, shall be deemed approved pursuant\nto Section 10 of RA No. 9485, as amended, provided, that all documentary requirements\nand required fees indicated in the Citizen's Charter of the covered agencies and LGUs have\nbeen submitted and paid, respectively."}},{"id":"PH-H16798-A5","no":5,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 5"},"text":{"en":"One-Stop Shop for Construction-Related Applications. All cities and\nmunicipalities shall set up a One-Stop Shop for Construction Permits, preferably at the Office\nof the Building Official, which will provide frontline services to applicants who are securing\nbuilding permits and other related certificates, including permits and certificates for\nconstruction of telecommunications and internet infrastructure."}},{"id":"PH-H16798-A6","no":6,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 6"},"text":{"en":"Zero Backlog Policy. Subject to existing laws, rules and regulations, all\ncovered government agencies and LGUs are enjoined to implement the Zero Backlog Policy\nin all applications for permits and clearances covered by this Order. They shall annually\nsubmit their list of pending applications and compliance reports to the ARTA, copy furnished\nthe Office of the President."}},{"id":"PH-H16798-A7","no":7,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 7"},"text":{"en":"Technical Working Group. A Technical Working Group (TWG) on\nTelecommunications and Internet Infrastructure is hereby created as an oversight body to\n3\n\nensure the effective and efficient implementation of this Order. The TWG shall be chaired by\nthe DICT, with the ARTA, NTC, Department of Public Works and Highways, and Department\nof the Interior and Local Government as members thereof."}},{"id":"PH-H16798-A8","no":8,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 8"},"text":{"en":"Implementing Rules and Regulations. Within sixty (60) working days\nfrom the effectivity of this Order, the TWG shall formulate rules and regulations necessary\nto effectively implement this Order."}},{"id":"PH-H16798-A9","no":9,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 9"},"text":{"en":"Repeal. All orders, rules and regulations, and other issuances or parts\nthereof which are inconsistent with the provisions of this Order are hereby repealed or\nmodified accordingly."}},{"id":"PH-H16798-A10","no":10,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 10"},"text":{"en":"Separability. If any part or provision of this Order shall be held invalid or\nunconstitutional, the provisions not affected thereby shall remain in full force and effect."}},{"id":"PH-H16798-A11","no":11,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 11"},"text":{"en":"Effectivity. This Order shall take effect immediately upon publication in\nthe Official Gazette or in a newspaper of general circulation.\nDONE, in the City of Manila, this 4th day of July\nTwo Thousand and Twenty-Three.\n, in the year of Our Lord,\nBy the President\nLUCAS P. BERSAMIN\nExecutive Sedretary\nOffice of the President\nMALACAÑANG RECORDS OFFICE\nZANY E. FERROLTAO-SMAD\n74-2\n4\nREPUBLIC OF THE PHILIPPINES"}}],"pack":"ph-p157"};
  FT["PH-H16799"] = {"id":"PH-H16799","coverage":"full","language":"en","sourceName":"The LawPhil Project — Arellano Law Foundation","sourceUrl":"LawPhil (HTML full text only)  |  https://lawphil.net/executive/execord/eo1936/eo_33_1936.html","fetchedAt":"2026-10-28","articleCount":1,"structureMode":"WHOLE","title":{"zh":null,"en":"Creating the Deportation Board","orig":"Creating the Deportation Board"},"level":"law","status":"active","docNumber":"Executive Order No. 33","issuingBody":"President of the Philippines","promulgatedDate":"1936-05-29","completenessNote":"全文，共 1 条；逐字取自 LawPhil PDF 文本化成果（第三方 OCR，非机翻），原始文件 EO_00033_1936_html.txt","textQuality":"ocr-vendor","sourceFile":"菲律宾/法律原文/07_行政命令_EO/EO_00033_1936_html.txt","country":"PH","countryName":"菲律宾","layer":"intl","articles":[{"id":"PH-H16799-A1","no":1,"noLabel":{},"text":{"en":"MALACAÑAN PALACE\nBY THE PRESIDENT OF THE PHILIPPINES\n[ EXECUTIVE ORDER NO. 33, May 29, 1936 ]\nCREATING THE DEPORTATION BOARD\nWHEREAS, for the purpose of conducting investigations in the manner specified in section sixty-nine of the\nAdministrative Code and recommending deportation of aliens in such cases as may require it, there has\nheretofore been constituted a board under Executive Order Numbered Four hundred ninety-four, as amended\nby Executive Order Numbered Four hundred ninety-four, as amended by Executive Orders Numbered Six\nhundred fifty-six and Seven hundred ninety-two; and\nWHEREAS, in view of the changes brought about by the establishment of the Commonwealth Government, it\nbecomes necessary and expedient to continue the functions of such board under rules and regulations\nconsistent with the supervision and control of foreign affairs by the United States Government, as set forth in\nthe Act of Congress of March twenty-fourth, nineteen hundred and thirty-four, and as embodied in Ordinance\nNumbered Two of the Constitution; and the President of the United States has delegated to the United States\nHigh Commissioner the duties and functions necessary to the exercise of such supervision and control;\nNOW, THEREFORE, by virtue of the powers conferred upon me by the Constitution and the existing laws, I\nhereby name and appoint the Solicitor-General, the Provost Marshal General, the Insular Collector of Customs\nand the Chief of Police of the City of Manila, the first as chairman and the last three, or their authorized\ndeputies, as members, of a board which is hereby constituted, to be known as the Deportation Board, with\nauthority to take action on all complaints that certain persons in the Philippines are undesirable aliens, and\nconduct investigations thereunder in the manner prescribed in section sixty-nine of the Administrative Code,\nand thereafter to recommend the deportation of aliens in such cases as may require, all in accordance with,\nand in pursuance of, the following rules and regulations:\n1. Every person complained against before the Deportation Board shall be informed of the charge or charges\nagainst him and shall be allowed not less than three days from notice thereof for the preparation of his\ndefense. He shall have the right to be heard by himself or counsel, to produce witnesses in his own behalf and\nto cross-examine the opposing witnesses.\n2. The proceedings before the Board shall be reduced to writing, and a full record of the proceedings shall be\nkept in all cases and shall include a statement of the findings and conclusions of the Board signed by the\nmembers thereof. A majority of the members shall constitute a quorum and a vote of three of them shall be\nnecessary to arrive at a decision. Any dissent from the majority opinion shall also be reduced to writing and\nfiled with the records of the proceedings.\n3. The findings and recommendations of the Deportation Board, with a full record of the proceedings, shall be\ntransmitted to the Office of the President for appropriate action. In the event deportation is recommended, the\nrecord and findings shall be transmitted to the United States High Commissioner to the Philippine Islands for\nsuch further action as may be deemed necessary and proper, including arrangements for actual deportation\nwith the government concerned. Upon completion of such arrangements and proper notice, final order of\ndeportation will be issued by the President of the Philippines."}}],"pack":"ph-p157"};
  FT["PH-H16800"] = {"id":"PH-H16800","coverage":"full","language":"en","sourceName":"The LawPhil Project — Arellano Law Foundation","sourceUrl":"LawPhil (HTML full text only)  |  https://lawphil.net/executive/execord/eo1944/eo_33_1944.html","fetchedAt":"2026-10-28","articleCount":1,"structureMode":"WHOLE","title":{"zh":null,"en":"Reducing By Thirty Per Centum the Tax on All Permanent Plants and Trees for the Year 1944","orig":"Reducing By Thirty Per Centum the Tax on All Permanent Plants and Trees for the Year 1944"},"level":"law","status":"active","docNumber":"Executive Order No. 33","issuingBody":"President of the Philippines","promulgatedDate":"1944-02-03","completenessNote":"全文，共 1 条；逐字取自 LawPhil PDF 文本化成果（第三方 OCR，非机翻），原始文件 EO_00033_1944_html.txt","textQuality":"ocr-vendor","sourceFile":"菲律宾/法律原文/07_行政命令_EO/EO_00033_1944_html.txt","country":"PH","countryName":"菲律宾","layer":"intl","articles":[{"id":"PH-H16800-A1","no":1,"noLabel":{},"text":{"en":"MALACAÑAN PALACE\nBY THE PRESIDENT OF THE PHILIPPINES\n[ Executive Order No. 33, February 3, 1944 ]\nREDUCING BY THIRTY PER CENTUM THE TAX ON ALL PERMANENT PLANTS AND TREES FOR\nBy virtue of the powers vested in me by law, I, JOSE P. LAUREL, President of the Republic of the\nPhilippines, do hereby reduce by thirty per centum the real property tax on all permanent plants and trees on\nany taxable real property for the calendar year 1944: Provided, That this reduction shall not be enforced in any\nmunicipality or city where the general revision of real property assessments undertaken in 1941 and\nsubsequent years have already been made effective\nDone at the City of Manila, this 3rd day of February, in the year of Our Lord, nineteen hundred and forty-four,\nand of the Republic of the Philippines, the first.\nJOSE P. LAUREL\nPresident of the Republic of the Philippines\nBy the President:\nPEDRO SABIDO\nExecutive Secretary"}}],"pack":"ph-p157"};
  FT["PH-H16801"] = {"id":"PH-H16801","coverage":"full","language":"en","sourceName":"The LawPhil Project — Arellano Law Foundation","sourceUrl":"","fetchedAt":"2026-10-28","articleCount":8,"structureMode":"ARTICLE","title":{"zh":null,"en":"MALACANAN PALACE BY 13 PROSIDENTE OF THE PHILIPPINTES DROUTIVE ORDER TO. US CREATIG THE BANKING DIVISION OF THE NAMIORTAT IREASURY, ; 00: MOITUBALIM CF ME PRITIPPI: ES","orig":"MALACANAN PALACE BY 13 PROSIDENTE OF THE PHILIPPINTES DROUTIVE ORDER TO. US CREATIG THE BANKING DIVISION OF THE NAMIORTAT IREASURY, ; 00: MOITUBALIM CF ME PRITIPPI: ES"},"level":"law","status":"active","docNumber":"Executive Order No. 33","issuingBody":"President of the Philippines","completenessNote":"全文，共 8 条；逐字取自 LawPhil PDF 文本化成果（第三方 OCR，非机翻），原始文件 EO_00033_1945.txt","textQuality":"ocr-vendor","sourceFile":"菲律宾/法律原文/07_行政命令_EO/EO_00033_1945.txt","country":"PH","countryName":"菲律宾","layer":"intl","articles":[{"id":"PH-H16801-A1","no":1,"noLabel":{"en":"Sec 1"},"text":{"en":"The General Authority and Regulations contained herein\nshall accompany and be a part of Executive Order No. 3s dated\nMarch 10, 1945, which creates the Banking Division of the National\nTreasury, Commonwealth of the Philippines. Said Division shall be\nreferred to hereinafter as the Bank. Its principal domicile and\nplace of business shall be in the Oity of Manila."}},{"id":"PH-H16801-A2","no":2,"noLabel":{"en":"Sec 2"},"text":{"en":"The said Bank shall have power:\n(a) To ascept deposits;\n(b) To make loans;\n(c) To engage in exchange and other banking operations;\n(a) To adopt and use a seal;\n(e) To make contracts;\n(f) To sue and be sued;\n(a) To exercise the powers sranted herein and such incidental\npowers as may be necessary to transact the business of banking.\nDEPOSITS AND WITHDRAMAIS\nThe Bank is hereby authorized to receive deposits and may\npay interest thereon, from the Commonwealth of the Philippines, the\nprovinces, municipalities, Fostal Savings Bank, firms, companies,\ncorporations, private persons, allied governments, their departments,\nagencies and armed forces, of demand, time and savings funds, subject\n\n- 2 -\nwithdrawal by check or presentation of savings bank book."}},{"id":"PH-H16801-A4","no":4,"noLabel":{"en":"Sec 4"},"text":{"en":"The Bank shell at all times keep on hand in its vaults a\nsum in lamful money either of the Philippines or of the United States\nwhich shall be computed as follows:\nIwenty per cent of the demand deposits outstanding and\ncredited on its books, and of the fized deposits meturing within thirty\ndays: PROVID.D, That if the Bank shall have funds subject to check with\nNational Banks or Federal Reserve Banks in the United States, such funds\nmay be considered as constituting a part of the twenty ver cent specified\nin this section up to a sum to bs fixed from time to time by the secretary\nof Finance, with the approval of the President of the Philippines.\nFive per centum of the total savings deposits.\nWhenever the reserve kept by the Bank in its vaults, as required\nin this section shall be balow the amount herein prescribed, the Bank shall\nnot diminish the amount of such reserve by mains any new loans or discounts\nuntil the required proportion between the aggregate amount of its deposits\nand its reserve has been restored.\nIOANIS ITD DIVESCIENTIS"}},{"id":"PH-H16801-A5","no":5,"noLabel":{"en":"Sec 5"},"text":{"en":"To enable said Bank to be of the greatest possible assistance\nto the economy of the Philippines during the period of emergency, it is\nhereby authorized:\n(a) To make personal and business loans with or without security;\nTo make chattel mortgage loans;\nTo make real estate loans;\nTo make loans against insuranse policies;\nTo engage in installment financing;\nTo engage in foreien trade financing:\n\n- 3\n(b) To purohase or discount promissory notes, drafts and bills\nof exchange issued or drawn for agricultural, industrial or commercial\npurposes, or the proceeds of which have been used or are to be used for\nsuch purposes.\n(c) To make loans on, or to discount notes secured by, harvested\nand stored crops; PROVIDED, That no loan on the security of such harvested\nand stored crops shall exceed seventy per centum of the market value\nthereof on the date of the loan: PROVIDED, FURTHY, that the crops so\nmortgaged shall be insured by the mortgasor for the benefit of the Bank\nfor their entirs merket value; and PROVIDED, finally, That if, owing to\nany cirownstance whatever the value of the crops given as security shall\ndiminish, the mortgagor shall obligate himself to furnish additional\nsecurity or refund such tart of the loan as the Bank may deen necessary.\nSuch loans shall be granted for a period of three months, subject to\nthree months' extension, in the discretion of the Bank.\n(d) To make loans to agriculturists in installments, secured by\ngrowing or standing erops of the natural products of the Philippines such\nas rice, hemp, copra, sugar, tobacco, corn, maguey, etc., not in excess of\nthree-fifths of the estimated value of such crops: FROVIDED, HOWLVER, That\nbefore granting such loans, the Bank may require additional security in\nthe nature of mortgages on real estate or chattel mortgages, including\nthose on live stock, machinery, and agricultural implements, or personal\nbonds with sufficient surety or sureties, satisfactory to the Bank.\n(e) To make loans fo agricultural purposes, secured by first\nmortgages on real estate in the Philippines. Such loons shall not exceed\nsixty per cent of the actual value of said real estate, including the\nvalue of the permenent improvements thereon, such as buildings and\nmachinery if the same form an integral part of the agricultural develop\n\nPROVIDED, HOWVEK, That wherever the bank may deem it advisable,\nmortgages shall contain a clause obliging the mortgagor to insure to\nor Pull value in the name of the Bank, such buildings and improve-\nThe due date of said mortgages shall not be more than five years\non the date thereof. The said mortgages, may by their tarms, be made\nArable at one time, or in installments. Application for such loans\nball be in writing and under oath, and shall contain among other things:\nA detailed description of the real estate;\nAn appraisal thereof at its reasonable market value;\nÀ full statement of the purposes for which the loan\nIt shall be unlawful to use the proceeds of said loan or any part\nthereof for any purpose or purposes, except the purpose or purposes set\nOft in said application.\nAny violation of this clause shall be sufficient\ncause for the rescission of the contract and the foreclosure of the mortgage.\nAny Justice of the Peace, in his capacity as notary public\ner-officio, shall render service free of charge to any person applying\nfor an agricultural or crop loan not exceeding Two Hundred Pesos from\nthe Bank, either in administerins the oath or in the acknowledsment of\nInstruments relative to said loan. Any Resister of Deeds shall make\nproper entry in the books and records of his office, free of charge, of\near instruments relative to agricultural or crop loans not exceeding Iwo\nHundred Pesos made to any borrower by the Bank.\n(f) To make loans to the several provincial and municipal\novernments and to any other branch or subdivision of the Commonwealth\nof the Philippines on promissory notes suaranteed by the National\nlovernment, as shown by the endorsement thereon of the Secretary of\n\n- 5 -\nhence, approved by the President of the Philippines, or to purchase\noas lawfully issued by the Commonwealth of the Philippines, or by\nhuh provincial and municipal governnents and any other branch or\nmdivision of the Commonwealth of the Philippines.\n(g) Generally, to make advances, or discount paper for agri-\nDuatural, manufacturins, industrial, or commercial purposes: PROVIDAD, mai\nLoans, discounts or advances made under this section (excepting loans\nrathorized in preceding sub-section e), shall have maturities not\ncreeeding one year.\nThe total liabilities to the Bank of any person, or of any\ncompany, corporation, or firm, including in the liabilities of the\ncempany or firm, the liabilities of the several members thereof, shall\nat no time exceed fifteen per centum of the designated working fund of\nthe Bank, and in addition to the fifteen per centum of the designated\nworking fund of the Bank, hereinbefore provided for, the total liabilities\nof any borrower may amount to a further fifteen ver centu of said work-\ning fund of the Bank, provided such additional liabilities are secured by\nshipping documents, warenouse receipts or other similar documents\ntransferring or securing title covering readily marketable staples, when\nsuch staples are fully covered by insurance and when such staples have\na market value equal to at least one hundred twenty-five ver centum of\nsuch additional liabilities. The discount of bills of exchance drawn\nin good faith against actually existing values and the discount of\ncommercial or business paper actually owned by the person negotiating\nthe same shall not be computed when determining as money the total\nliabilities permitted under this restriction.\n\n= 6 =\nthe Bank shall not make any loan upon the stock of any\ncorporation as collateral if the aggregate market value of all such\nDock held as collateral exceeds an amount equal to fifteen per centum\nthe designated working fund of the Bank.\nThe term \"loan\" whenever used in this General Authority and\nregulations, includes overdrafts and trust receipt facilities.\nADMINISTRATION\nSec. 6, The affairs, business an administration of the Bank shall\nhe directed and its assets managed and preserved by the Chier of the\nranking Division of the National Ireasury, Commonwealth of the\nmilippines, referred to hereinafter as the Chief. He shall be appoint-\na and may be removed only by the President of the Philippines, and his\nsalary shall be fixed by the Fresident.\nPOWERS OF THE CHIEF OF THE BANKING DIVISION\n'Sec. 7. The Chief, shall among other duties, powers and authority,\no charged with the following:\n(a) Fix the rates of discount, remittance fees or exchange to be\ncharged by said Bank, and to issue regulations governins deposits;\n(b) To fix in agreement with the Loan Committee, the rates of\ninterest that may be paid on deposits and charged on loans;\n(o) Before any loans, discounts or other advances are made in\nsecordance with the authority of the Ion Committee, he shall cause\nthe officer or agent designated for this purpose to obtain in proper\nform and hold safely, the required security, and in case of a mortgage,\norder the recistration of the proper documents in the office of the\nRegister of Deeds of the city or province in which the property is\n\n(a) Establish accounts with such bank or banks outside of the\nilippines as may be designated as depositaries by the President of the\nenflippines.\n(e) With the consent of the President of the Philippines, to\nestablish an agency in New York, N. I., U.s.., and to appoint an agent\nmo shall be authorized to appoint an assistant or assistants and\nengage such employees as he may deem necessary.\nThis agency in New York\nshall be empowered to engage in such transactions as are permitted by\nthe New York State banking laws and regulations governing agencies of\nforeign banks.\n(f) Establish branches or agencies or the bank in provinciai\ncapitals and other municipalities of the Philippines where, in his\nJudgment, the industrial, commercial or agricultural development or\nrehabilitation require it.\nThe agents and other officers and emplovees of said branches\nor agencies shall be appointed and may be removed by the Chief.\n(s) All signature authorizations shall be issued by the Chief,\nprovided that in the case of checks, drafts, or other instruments\ndirecting the payment of money; two authorized signatures shall be\n(h) The Chief may appoint as agents, cashiers or tellers of\nbranches or agencies, the provincial or municipal treasurers, who\nshall in this case furnish bond and receive sun additional compensa-\ntion as the Chief may determine, and shall be removable by the Chief, as\nsuch agents, cashiers, or tellers.\n(a) To make all contracts on behalf of the said Bank and to\nenter into all obligations required in the conduct of the business of\n\n(J) To furnish, upon request of the Secretary of Finance, or the\nresident of the Philippines, any information in his possession regard-\nthe the operations of said Bank.\nLOAN COMMITTEE"}},{"id":"PH-H16801-A8","no":8,"noLabel":{"en":"Sec 8"},"text":{"en":"All loans and other credit facilities extended by the Bank\nchall be authorized by a Ian Committee consisting of a Chairman and\nto additional members.\nThey shall be appointed or removed only by\nthe President of the Philippines who shall fix their compensation.\nThe duties of the Ion Committee shall be:\n(a) To authorize such loans and credit facilities as in their\nJudgment are proper and in accord with the purposes of Executive Order\n53\ndated March 10, 1945, and to specify conditions under which\nofficers or agents of the Bank may extend loans and credit racilities\nauthorized by the Committee.\n(b) To extend authority and prescribe limits as to amounts and\nmaturities under which officers and agents of the Bank may grant loans\nand credit facilities without prior reference to the Committee.\n(c) To study and recommend to the President of the Philippines\na detailed plan for early extension of small relief and rehabilitation\n(d) To cause a permanent record to be kept of the minutes of\nits meetings.\nThe Chief of the Banking Division shall not be a member\nof the loan Committee, but he or the officers or agents designated by\nand responsible to him shall be charged with the handling of all loans\ngranted under authority of the Committee,\nDecisions of the Committee shall be made by majority vote.\n\n7\nLEGAL GOURDEL\nSec. 9, Tue Secretezy of Justios shall be attorney for said Beni\nand may, whenever as way deem it proper, in specific cases dalegate\nhis duties to to Suliciton-Aarevel, tas fiscal of tha City of Manila,\nor any provincil fisoul, as the oase may va: IsoliDed, adasral, moat\nthe Chier of said Bank, with the approval of the Secretery of Justice,\nshall have power to, employ such additional attoreys as may Da nacassany.\nSoc. 10. Tas Aucitor Genoral shall be ar-officio auditor us the\nBank and shell, with the advice and consent of the Fresident of the\nPhilippines, appoint a repraseutstive vno shall be the dier or tho\nAuditing Section of the Bank. All the other emplogeos of the section\nshall be appointed by the Auditor Genoval, wo will the approval of the\nPresident or the Philippines, shell fix the salarias of tho samo, as\nwell as tiet or his reprecentative, una omise of the ceovion. The\nexpenses or uno seation end the salaries end traveling expenses on the\nemplovees Unereor shall be payable by the Bonk. The representative or\nthe Auditor General susll wake a monthly report on the condition of the\nBenk to the Fresident on te Flilipuices, through the Secretary of\nFinance, to the Auciuor General and to the Chief. The roport shall\ncontain emons other tings a statement f the resourcos and liabilisics,\nIncluing earnings und asperses, the working fund of the Bank, and\nundivido profits, as woll as the losses, bad deuts, and overdus accounts\ncarried in the Bank's assets, as of the day in which the stataments ara\n\n~ 10\nSec. 1l. all tie other officers, gents, and employees of the Bank\nshall be appointed anú removed by the Chiat.\nSaid ufficers, agenus,\nand employees shall not us subject to the Civil vervics Law, and tirsir\ndutias and congonsation saeli De fixed y unlo Shiat."}},{"id":"PH-H16801-A12","no":12,"noLabel":{"en":"Sec 12"},"text":{"en":"The Lembers vi the Loan Gormittee, and all officers, agemos\nand employees o the Bank Shall ve vondeú and Unair fidaliuy insured in\naccordano with the grovisions us uno Fublis Borcias Law.\nSeo. 10. The Secretas, 66 Zinedivo, tia sur lion Gonoral, Edo uns\nTatters reprossatativs, use cuisi or the Auditing Section vi tho Bunk\nare hereby prohivated 2ous. Nscoming incooted to said Denk, civestly or\nindirectly.\n•07.35 99 4.\nINGELICO INES.\nSeo. Ic. Tho Dent cic1l Lou, divestly or indirecuis, grant Ivans to\nany of the newders of the Loos. Sommitte, the Chier, owns officers and\nemployees of tho Leak, hor to agenus or enployees of use vancies or\nagencies, and no ioan smell be grented to a corporation, partership or\ncompany wherein any mender uf the Loan Concittee is a shareholder, partner,\nagent or amployee in any mamor, exoopo by the unaninous vote of the members\nof the committee, excluding the nemuer interested,\nAOQUISIRIOL A D. PLOPUSAL OF CAL SLUT\nThe Bank is narcy audiorized to purchase and un or leasa\nsuch real estate as may be necessary for the purpose of carrying on its\n\nbasiness. It is also authorized to hola such real estate as it may\nrind necessary to acquire in una collection of debts qua to the said\nBank or to its branches; but real estate accuired in the collation\nop debts shall be sold by seid Bank within five years after the date\nor its acquisivion.\nVARGAOUSES"}},{"id":"PH-H16801-A16","no":16,"noLabel":{"en":"Sec 16"},"text":{"en":"The Bank is hereby autorized to buy erect, or lease\nwarehouses for depositing therein goods given to it in pledge or oustody,\nin any provincial capital or any municipality where the commercial,\nindustrial, or agricultural development or rehabilitation of the place\nmay require it.\nFROLIBITED RM UNERATIO?\nSeo. 17. No fees or charge of any kind by way of commission shall\nbe exacted, demanded or paid, for obtaining loans, and any vIllcer,\nemployee, or agent of tha Bank exacting, demandins, or receiving any\nfee for service in obtaining a loan or for use of his influence to\nobtain a loan, shall be punished as hereafter provided."}},{"id":"PH-H16801-A18","no":18,"noLabel":{"en":"Sec 18"},"text":{"en":"The Chief of the Banking Division or any member of the\nLoan Committes who knowingly violates or knowingly permits any of the\nofficers, agents, or aployees of the Bank to violate any of the\nprovisions of this Goneral Authority and Regulations, and any officer,\nagent, or employae of the Bank who violates any of the provisions\nthereof, and any person aiding and abetting the violation of any of\nthe provisions thereof, shall be punished y a fine not to exceed\n\n- 12 -\non Thousand Fesos, or by imprisonment not to exceed five years,\nor by both such fine and imprisonment.\nDone in City of Lanila, this 10th day of March, in the year of\nour Lord, nineteen hundred and forty-five, and of the Cormoiwealth\nof the Philippines, the tenth.\nPresident of the Philippines\nBy the Frssident:\nSecretary to the President"}}],"pack":"ph-p157"};
  FT["PH-H16802"] = {"id":"PH-H16802","coverage":"full","language":"en","sourceName":"The LawPhil Project — Arellano Law Foundation","sourceUrl":"","fetchedAt":"2026-10-28","articleCount":1,"structureMode":"WHOLE","title":{"zh":null,"en":"MALACAÑAN PALACE BY THE PRESIDENT OF THE PHILIPPINES PROMULGATING RULES AND REGULATIONS TO CARRY OUT THE PROVISIONS OF REPUBLIC ACT NUMBERED THIRTY ENTITLED \"AN ACT AUTHOR- OTHER HEIRS, OF A DECEASED OFFICER OR MEMBER OF ANY POLICE FORCE OR SIMILAR GOVERNMENTAL ORGANIZATION ENGAGED IN THE MAINTENANCE OF PEACE AND ORDER, APPROPRIATING FUNDS THERE-","orig":"MALACAÑAN PALACE BY THE PRESIDENT OF THE PHILIPPINES PROMULGATING RULES AND REGULATIONS TO CARRY OUT THE PROVISIONS OF REPUBLIC ACT NUMBERED THIRTY ENTITLED \"AN ACT AUTHOR- OTHER HEIRS, OF A DECEASED OFFICER OR MEMBER OF ANY POLICE FORCE OR SIMILAR GOVERNMENTAL ORGANIZATION ENGAGED IN THE MAINTENANCE OF PEACE AND ORDER, APPROPRIATING FUNDS THERE-"},"level":"law","status":"active","docNumber":"Executive Order No. 33","issuingBody":"President of the Philippines","completenessNote":"全文，共 1 条；逐字取自 LawPhil PDF 文本化成果（第三方 OCR，非机翻），原始文件 EO_00033_1946.txt","textQuality":"ocr-vendor","sourceFile":"菲律宾/法律原文/07_行政命令_EO/EO_00033_1946.txt","country":"PH","countryName":"菲律宾","layer":"intl","articles":[{"id":"PH-H16802-A1","no":1,"noLabel":{},"text":{"en":"- 2 -\n3. Until provision is made otherwise, the benefits\nafforded in Republic Act No. 30 shall accrue only in cases\nof death occurring on or after January 1, 1946:\nThat such sums out of the appropriation provided in said\nAct remaining unexpended at the close of the present fis-\ncal year may be paid as benefits to cases of death occur-\nring after June 30, 1947, if the cause thereof be parti-\ncipation in a campaign conducted before July 1, 1947.\n4. The Auditor General, with the concurrence of the\nSecretary of the Interior, shall issue the necessary ins-\ntructions for the proper and expeditious identification\nof the beneficiary or beneficiaries as authorized by\nRepublic Act No. 30.\nSaid instructions should tend to\neliminate unnecessary requirements and delay so that the\nbeneficiary or beneficiaries, once identified, may promptly\nreceive the amount or amounts due to them under said Act.\nWhenever there will be no confusion, actual payment of the\ngratuity should be made to only one of the rightful claim-\nants who may have been duly authorized by the others to\nreceive the amount for all of them.\n5. All officers and employees, be they National or\nof the local governments, who participate in the perfeo-\ntion of the claim or in the preparation of the necessary\nare directed to assist in\never possible way, any applicant for tratuity under Bald\n6. All claims for gratuity shall be given preferen-\ntial attention and to expedite the movement from office\nto office of the claim papers, each of said papers should\nbe prepared originally with sufficient number of copies.\n7. The offices or bureaus concerned shall not deal\nwith intermediaries or persons who represent themselves\nas acting in behalf of claimants.\n8. No warrant covering the payment of gratuities shall\nhe delivered to any person other than the payee.\na payee cannot personally take delivery of such warrant, it\nshould be mailed without delay.\n9. Documents and other papers relating to claims for\ngratuities shall be considered confidential.\n- 3 -\nDone at the City of Manila, this\nday of Decem-\nber, in the year of Our Lord, nineteen hundred and forty-\nsix, and of the Independence of the Philippines, the first.\nBy the President:\nEMILIO ABELLO\nChief of the Executive Office"}}],"pack":"ph-p157"};
  FT["PH-H16803"] = {"id":"PH-H16803","coverage":"full","language":"en","sourceName":"The LawPhil Project — Arellano Law Foundation","sourceUrl":"","fetchedAt":"2026-10-28","articleCount":1,"structureMode":"WHOLE","title":{"zh":null,"en":"MALACAIIAIIG RESIDINICE OF TO PRESIDSITT OF TUS PHILIPPINES BY THE PRESIDDIT OF TID PHILIPPIES BXECUTIVE ORODE 110. 33 CREATING A SPECIAL COMIISTED ON SOVEMENT INVEST- MENTS AND DEFITTING ITS POTBAS AID FULICTIOUS.","orig":"MALACAIIAIIG RESIDINICE OF TO PRESIDSITT OF TUS PHILIPPINES BY THE PRESIDDIT OF TID PHILIPPIES BXECUTIVE ORODE 110. 33 CREATING A SPECIAL COMIISTED ON SOVEMENT INVEST- MENTS AND DEFITTING ITS POTBAS AID FULICTIOUS."},"level":"law","status":"active","docNumber":"Executive Order No. 33","issuingBody":"President of the Philippines","completenessNote":"全文，共 1 条；逐字取自 LawPhil PDF 文本化成果（第三方 OCR，非机翻），原始文件 EO_00033_1966.txt","textQuality":"ocr-vendor","sourceFile":"菲律宾/法律原文/07_行政命令_EO/EO_00033_1966.txt","country":"PH","countryName":"菲律宾","layer":"intl","articles":[{"id":"PH-H16803-A1","no":1,"noLabel":{},"text":{"en":"The Chairman of the National Eco-\nnomic Council or his Representative . Member\nThe Director-General, Presidential\nDeonomic Staff or his Represen-\n...\n• .\nThe Chairman, Development Sank of\nthe Philippines, or his Representative , Member\nThe General Manager, Government\nService: Insurance System, or his\nRepresentative.\n...\n..\nThe Fresident, Philippine National\nBank or his lepresentative .\nThe Special Committee on Government Investments\nshall have the folloving duties and responsibilities:\na, To study, analyse, and determine the actual\nFincncial conditions and capital requirements\nof government corporations end instrumentali-\nties and to recommend remedial measures neces-\nsary therefor\nb, To study and recommend appropriate policies\napplicable uniformly to the different gene-\nral classes of government corporations and\ninstrumentalities;\nc. To determine the propriety of disposing of\nall or any part of the assets or stocks of\nany government corporation or instrumentality,\nand to formulate and recommend policies re-\nlating to such disposition, including such\nguidelines, safeguards and procedures as\nshall be observed in the event of disposi-\ntions, dissolution or liguidation;\nd. Generally, to coordinate the investment po-\nlicies of all government finencial institu-\ntions for the purposo of attaining maximum\nuse of available resources and particulariy,\nto undertako periodic onalysis and review of\nthe investment portfolios of these financial\ninstitutions with a view to sheping them into\nan integrated annual pro ram of capital trans-\n64\ne. To study and recommond reorganization mea-\nsures for government corporations and ins-\ntrumentalities in order to gear their ad-\nministrative machinery to the resuirements\nof economic developaent, and\nf. To recommend measured, both administrative\nand legislative, designed to attain fully\nthe objective herein set forth.\nThe Presidential Iconomic Staff shall act as\nthe Secretariat of the Special Committee and shall\nrender the necessary staff support and technical\nassistance.\nThe Special Comittee ard the Secretariat are\nhereby authorised to secure date and information ad-\nrectly from all government offices, agencies, cor-\nporations, and entities and to consult with offi-\ncials and personnel thereof, on matters roleted to\nthe above functions.\nThe officers and personnol of all goverment\noffices, agencies, corporation and entities are\nhereby enjoined to render full support and coope-\nration to the Speciel Committee and the Secreta-\nrat in the discherge of their functions.\nThis Order shall take effect immedietely.\nDone in the City of ianila, this 21st day of\nJuly, in the year of Our Lord, nineteen hundred and\n(s6o.) PADIAID D. MARCOS\nFresident of the Fhilippines\nBy the Fresident:\n[sca.) RAFABL 1-. SALAS\nExecutive Secretary\n65"}}],"pack":"ph-p157"};
