  FT["PH-H16817"] = {"id":"PH-H16817","coverage":"full","language":"en","sourceName":"The LawPhil Project — Arellano Law Foundation","sourceUrl":"","fetchedAt":"2026-10-28","articleCount":1,"structureMode":"WHOLE","title":{"zh":null,"en":"MALACANANG AMENDIr-K; EX:EX:UTIVE ORDER 00.","orig":"MALACANANG AMENDIr-K; EX:EX:UTIVE ORDER 00."},"level":"law","status":"active","docNumber":"Executive Order No. 34","issuingBody":"President of the Philippines","completenessNote":"全文，共 1 条；逐字取自 LawPhil PDF 文本化成果（第三方 OCR，非机翻），原始文件 EO_00034_1992.txt","textQuality":"ocr-vendor","sourceFile":"菲律宾/法律原文/07_行政命令_EO/EO_00034_1992.txt","country":"PH","countryName":"菲律宾","layer":"intl","articles":[{"id":"PH-H16817-A1","no":1,"noLabel":{},"text":{"en":"ment of the Interior\nand Local Government or\nany government official\nas may be designated Py\nthe President,\nas Cl1airman. x x x\"\n'\nThis Order shall\ntake effect\nimmediately.\nDONE in the City\nyear of Our lord,\n'--- ,---\n\"\n,\nBy the President:\n'\\\n--\nE>tecuti ve secretar~\n~"}}],"pack":"ph-p157"};
  FT["PH-H16818"] = {"id":"PH-H16818","coverage":"full","language":"en","sourceName":"The LawPhil Project — Arellano Law Foundation","sourceUrl":"","fetchedAt":"2026-10-28","articleCount":6,"structureMode":"ARTICLE","title":{"zh":null,"en":"EXECUTIVE ORDER NO. FOR THE RESTRUCTURING COMPUTER CENTER","orig":"EXECUTIVE ORDER NO. FOR THE RESTRUCTURING COMPUTER CENTER"},"level":"law","status":"active","docNumber":"Executive Order No. 34","issuingBody":"President of the Philippines","completenessNote":"全文，共 6 条；逐字取自 LawPhil PDF 文本化成果（第三方 OCR，非机翻），原始文件 EO_00034_1998.txt","textQuality":"ocr-vendor","sourceFile":"菲律宾/法律原文/07_行政命令_EO/EO_00034_1998.txt","country":"PH","countryName":"菲律宾","layer":"intl","articles":[{"id":"PH-H16818-A1","no":1,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 1"},"text":{"en":"Declaration of Policy. It is hereby declared the policy of the Government, in\nfurtherance of national development, to create the appropriate environment for, and\nrationalize the use and application of, information techrlology, tal attain the following\nobjectives:\n(a) To optimize the use of information technology in meeting socio-economic\ndevelopment needs and in addressing national concerns such as poverty, crime,\neducation, health and environment;\n(b) To ensure the protection of mission-critical and highly secure public and private:\nsector data from hostile attacks that could endanger peace arId order, national security\nand the operation of public utilities;\n(c) To ensure the protection of privacy rights in consideration ,Iof the right to information\nand the duty to enforce laws;\n(d) To ensure that the procurement of computer hardware\"and software will safeguard the\npublic interest in terms of optimum serviceability, quality, benefits and economy;\n(e) To ensure compatability of all government hardware and software;\n(f) To provide the mechanisms for the effective evaluation of information technologies\nbefoTe and during their (!,ctual use in government applications; .,\n\n(g) To encourage the development of government-wide information systems and\nnetworks to provide data and information needed for development planning and\ndecision-making;\n(h) To optimize the use of information technology in electronic governance, thus\nachieving greater effectiveness, efficiency, accessibility, and accountability in public\n(i) To ensure that the use of information technology will support and enhance national\ncompetitiveness in the global arena;\n(j) To maximize the potential of information technology in increasing national\nproductivity and creating national wealth;\n(k) To support the formation and sustainability of knowledge-based industries, thus\ncreating new local employment opportunities and reducing overseas employment.\n(1) To promote the development, retention and optimum utilization of qualified\ninformation technology human resources.\""}},{"id":"PH-H16818-A2","no":2,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 2"},"text":{"en":"Functions and Powers of the National ComDuter Center lNCC). The NCC\n(a) It shall be the implementing arm of all government computerization and electronic\nnetworking policies, programs and projects, and all other IT -related activities of\ngovernment;\n(b) It shall devise and implement an integrated government computerization program\ncoordinating all existing government entities, taking into account all their existing\nplans, programs, proposals, software and hardware inventory, installed systems and\n(c) It shall design and build an integrated government informatio~ infrastructure GII);\n(d) It shall review and approve proposed Information Systems Plans (ISPs) of National\nGovernment Agencies (NGAs), State Universities and Colleges (SUCs),Government\nOwned and Controlled\nCorporations (GOCCs), and Government Financial\nInstitutions (GFls), determine their funding requirements and endorse such funding\nrequirements to the Department of Budget Management (DBM) or the BOT Center;\n(e) It shall audit the computer hardware and software inventory of all government entities\nto make sure that computer systems are used to its full potential;\n(t) It shall facilitate the transfer and re-assignment of all computer hardware and\nsoftware that are not being used by government entities;\n(g) It shall function as a backup computing facility in the event that the computer systems\nof other government entities become inoperable;\n(h) It shall conduct periodic monitoring and evaluation of existing ISPs, and determine\nappropriate upgrades and modifications as necessary;\n(i) It shall facilitate the requests and service the needs of local government units (LGUs),\nthe legislative and judicial branches, as well as the constitutiqgal commissions, if and\n~\nShall remaIn as an executive agency under the Office of the President and shall have the\nfollowing functions and powers:\n\nwhen these independent entities decide to\nbecome part of\ngovernment\ncomputerization and electronic networking programs, and projects;\n(j) It shall assist other government information technology installations in the\nsupervision, regulation or rationalization of their services, and for this purpose may\nconduct management audits whenever necessary;\n(k) It shall promote the use of electronic commerce in government-to-government and\ngovernment-to-private transactions;\n(1) It shall promote IT exports and investments, promote public and private sector\ncooperation, implement innovative IT -related activities, and promote public access to\ninformation technologies;\n(m)It shall organize and manage a Strategic Data Center (SDC) that shall service, the\nExecutive Information System (EIS) and the Decision Support System (DSS) needs\nof the Office of the President, and create a national database on IT as part of the\nnational statistical system;\n(n) It shall represent NGAs, SUCs, GOCCs and GFIs in IT -related negotiations and\nprovide them bid management;\n(0) It can enlist the assistance of any Department, Bureau, Office, Agency or\ninstrumentality of government; including GOCCs and GFIs in the furtherance of its\n(p) Perform such other functions as may be necessary to implement the provisions of this\nExecutive Order.\n."}},{"id":"PH-H16818-A3","no":3,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 3"},"text":{"en":"IT Action Agenda. The NCC shall be implementing and coordinating agency\nof the IT Action Agenda for the 21 sl Century (IT21) and its successor plans.\nThe NCC shall recommend changes and/or improvements in IT21, through the National\nInformation Technology Council (NITC).\nNCC shall provide Secretariat services to the NITC."}},{"id":"PH-H16818-A4","no":4,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 4"},"text":{"en":"Director General. The management of the NCC shall be vested in a Director\nGeneral who shall be the chief executive officer thereof and who shall be appointed by\nthe President of the Philippines. The Director General of the NCC shall have the\nequivalent rank of a cabinet Undersecretary, and shall have the following powers,\nfunctions and duties:\n(a) Direct and manage the affairs of the NCC, including the National Computer Institute\n(NCI) and the Philippine Software Development Institute (PSDI);\n(b) Implement policies, programs and projects as may b~ adopted pursuant to the\nprovisions of this Executive Order;\n(c) Undertake periodic review of policies, programs and projects;\n(d) Protect and preserv~ the secrecy and security ofNCC data holqings;\n\n(e) Appoint employees of the NCC in accordance with the approved budget and staffing\npattern thereof and discipline or remove them in accordance with existing laws;\n(t) Disburse, administer and obligate appropriations of the NCC;\n(g) Coordinate with appropriate law enforcement agencies the investigation and\nprosecution of Intellectual Property Rights (IPR) violators and computer-related\ncrime offenders;\n(h) Perform such other functions. as may be necessary to implement the objectives of this\nExecutive Order.\""}},{"id":"PH-H16818-A5","no":5,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 5"},"text":{"en":"All issuances, orders, rules and regulations or parts thereof which are\ninconsistent with any of the provisions of this Executive Order are hereby repealed or\nmodified accordingly."}},{"id":"PH-H16818-A6","no":6,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 6"},"text":{"en":"This Executive Order shall take effect immediately\nin the City of Manila this ~\n1998.\n(~\n.~.\n'\nfoSEPH EJERCiTO\nBy authority of the President:\n--~~\"2...\nRONALDOZAMORA\nExecutive Secretary"}}],"pack":"ph-p157"};
  FT["PH-H16819"] = {"id":"PH-H16819","coverage":"full","language":"en","sourceName":"The LawPhil Project — Arellano Law Foundation","sourceUrl":"","fetchedAt":"2026-10-28","articleCount":5,"structureMode":"ARTICLE","title":{"zh":null,"en":"MALACAÑANG PMS LIRRARV RECONSTITUTING THE NATIONAL SECURITY COUNCIL AND FOR OTHER PURPOSES","orig":"MALACAÑANG PMS LIRRARV RECONSTITUTING THE NATIONAL SECURITY COUNCIL AND FOR OTHER PURPOSES"},"level":"law","status":"active","docNumber":"Executive Order No. 34","issuingBody":"President of the Philippines","completenessNote":"全文，共 5 条；逐字取自 LawPhil PDF 文本化成果（第三方 OCR，非机翻），原始文件 EO_00034_2001.txt","textQuality":"ocr-vendor","sourceFile":"菲律宾/法律原文/07_行政命令_EO/EO_00034_2001.txt","country":"PH","countryName":"菲律宾","layer":"intl","articles":[{"id":"PH-H16819-A1","no":1,"noLabel":{"en":"SECTION 1"},"text":{"en":"The National Security Council (NSC) is hereby\nreconstituted and shall be composed of the following:\nPresident as Chairperson;\nb. Vice-President;\nSenate President;\nSpeaker of the House of Representatives;\nSenate President Pro-Tempore;\nDeputy Speakers for Luzon, Visayas and Mindanao;\ng. Majority Floor Leader of the Senate;\nMajority Floor Leader of the House;\nMinority Floor Leader of the Senate;\n..\nMinority Floor Leader of the House;\nk. Chairperson, Senate Committee on Foreign Relations;\n1. Chairperson, Senate Committee on National Defense and\nm. Chairperson, Senate Committee on Public Order and Illegal\nPOMA Outgoing • 05342\n\nChairperson, House Committee on Foreign Affairs;\n0. Chairperson, House Committee on National Defense;\nChairperson, House Committee on Public Order and Security;\n9. Executive Secretary;\nNational Security Adviser;\nSecretary of Foreign Affairs;\nSecretary of Justice;\nSecretary of National Defense;\nSecretary of the Interior and Local Government;\nSecretary of Labor and Employment;\nChief Presidential Legal Counsel;\nPresidential Spokesperson;\n2. Head, Presidential Legislative Liaison Office; and\naa. Past Presidents of the Philippines,\nand such other government officials and private citizens as the President\nmay appoint or designate from time to time.\nThe Director-General of the National Intelligence Coordinating\nAgency, the Chief of Staff of the Armed Forces of the Philippines, the\nChief of the Philippine National Police, the Director of the National\nBureau of Investigation and the Governor of the Bangko Sentral ng\nPilipinas shall attend the meetings of the Council as may be necessary to\nadvise and assist in the deliberations."}},{"id":"PH-H16819-A2","no":2,"noLabel":{"en":"SECTION 2"},"text":{"en":"The Executive Committee of the NSC is hereby\nreconstituted and shall be composed of the following:\nPresident as Chairperson;\nb. Vice-President;\nSenate President or his representative;\nSpeaker of the House of Representatives or his representative;\ne. Executive Secretary;\nNational Security Adviser;\ng. Secretary of Foreign Affairs;\nSecretary of Justice;\n!.\nSecretary of National Defense; and\nSecretary of the Interior and Local Government,\nand such other members or advisers as the President may designate\nfrom time to time.\nThe Executive Committee shall review national security issues and\nconcerns and formulate positions or solutions for consideration by the\nNSC. It shall determine the agenda and order of business of the NSC,\nand shall ensure that decisions of the NSC are clearly communicated to\nPOMA Outgoing • 05343\n\nthe agencies concerned.\nimplementation of decisions.\nIt shall advise the President on the\nTo carry out its functions, the Executive Committee may utilize the\nfacilities and expertise of any of the government agencies and\ninstrumentalities, and promulgate rules and regulations to govern its\noperations."}},{"id":"PH-H16819-A3","no":3,"noLabel":{"en":"SECTION 3"},"text":{"en":"The NSC shall be an advisory body to the President.\nThe National Security Adviser shall ensure that the policies formulated\nby the NSC and approved by the President are effectively and efficiently\nimplemented."}},{"id":"PH-H16819-A4","no":4,"noLabel":{"en":"SECTION 4"},"text":{"en":"Executive Order No. 33 dated November 18, 1992 is\nhereby modified accordingly. All other orders, rules, regulations and\nissuances, or parts thereof, which are inconsistent with this Executive\nOrder, are hereby repealed or likewise modified accordingly."}},{"id":"PH-H16819-A5","no":5,"noLabel":{"en":"SECTION 5"},"text":{"en":"This Executive Order shall take effect immediately\nupon approval.\nCity of Manila, September 17, 2001.\nBy the President:\nCither en. 6 G. Rommele\nALBERTO G. ROMULO\nExecutive Secretary\nPMS LIBRARY\nPGMA Outgoina • 05344 PMS LIBRARY BCODE002034\n3"}}],"pack":"ph-p157"};
  FT["PH-H16820"] = {"id":"PH-H16820","coverage":"full","language":"en","sourceName":"The LawPhil Project — Arellano Law Foundation","sourceUrl":"","fetchedAt":"2026-10-28","articleCount":4,"structureMode":"ARTICLE","title":{"zh":null,"en":"MALACANIaNI PALACE BY THE PRESIDENT OF THE PHILIPPINES THE OVERSEAS PREPAREDNESS AND RESPONSE THE PRESIDENTIAL MIDDLE EAST PREPAREDNESS","orig":"MALACANIaNI PALACE BY THE PRESIDENT OF THE PHILIPPINES THE OVERSEAS PREPAREDNESS AND RESPONSE THE PRESIDENTIAL MIDDLE EAST PREPAREDNESS"},"level":"law","status":"active","docNumber":"Executive Order No. 34","issuingBody":"President of the Philippines","completenessNote":"全文，共 4 条；逐字取自 LawPhil PDF 文本化成果（第三方 OCR，非机翻），原始文件 EO_00034_2011.txt","textQuality":"ocr-vendor","sourceFile":"菲律宾/法律原文/07_行政命令_EO/EO_00034_2011.txt","country":"PH","countryName":"菲律宾","layer":"intl","articles":[{"id":"PH-H16820-A2","no":2,"noLabel":{"en":"SECTION 2"},"text":{"en":"Functions - The following are the functions,\nresponsibilities\nSubject to the approval of the President,\nanticipate strategies and\nformulate policies and focus on appropriate\nnatural disasters, civil unrest, armed conflicts, and other similar\ncrises in foreign countries\naffecting overseas Filipinos;\nDevelop and adopt interactive operating arrangements among\nformulate strategies,\nand integrate\nagency plans to effect\nmaximum coordination\nand proper resolutiort\nof concerns that rnay\n@ffire o! tbe lFres&et al tte fitfl;qpillzs\nilililililllll\nlllllllllllilll\narise during crises;\n\nlmplement all policies, plans, strategies, and modes for\ncoordination\nthat are approved by the President,\nand monitor their\nimplementation\nReview and update the individual\ncontingency\nplans submitted\nthe Philippine Embassies and consurates General, undertake\ncontinuing assessment\nof the said plans, conduct threat and\nenvironmental\nscanning, and provide policy and operational\nguidance to ensure the safety and welfare of overseas Filipinos;\nFormulate contingency plans for the foilowing regions and\nreview/update\nthese plans every six (6) months:\nMiddle East and Africa;\nAsia, Australia,\nand the pacific;\n(0\nEstablish a pool of crisis management\nexperts, technibal experts,\nand trained personnel from the OPRT rnember-agencies\nrapid reaction teams;\nAuthorize the deployment\nof rapid reaction teams to crisis-hit\nwith a significant\nconcentration\nof Filipinos;\nAuthorize the dispatch of additional personnel to reinforce\nPhilippine\nand Consulates\nGeneral for a duration of up\nto three (3) months, subject to extension, to ensure systematic\nrepatriation\nand relocation\nactivities,\namong others;\nEstablish a monitoring mechanism that regularly gathers and\nupdates information on the identities and locations of overseas\nparticularly\nin crisis-prone\n0)\nCall upon, for assistance,\nany. department,\nbureau, office, or\nagency of the government,\nor private sector partners (such as\nemployment,\nrecruitment,\nor manning agencies),\nand coordinate\n-with and/or seek the assistance\nof bilateral\nand multilateral\nto formulate\nand/or implement\nplans, programs\nand policies;\nConduct regular workshops on risk reduction and crisis\nmanagement\namong concerned\ngovernment\nol tle $reri!r* ot gr glitippiner\nililflilil\n\nPrepare a comprehensive\ncommunication\nplan that will apprise the\npublic on government\nactions to ensure the safety of Filipinos in\ncrisis situations;\nDirect and conduct other preparedness\nand contingency\nas may be required\nby the crisis situation;\nExercise other functions and powers as may be assigned by the\n-\ncomposition - The opRT shall be composed of the\nExecutive Secretary\nPresidentialAdviser\non Overseas\nWorkers' (OFW) Concerns\nForeign Affairs Secretary\nLabor and Employment\n(\"),\nDefense Secretary\n(0\nJustice Secretary\nInterior and Local Government\nBudget Secretary\n- Chairperson"}},{"id":"PH-H16820-A4","no":4,"noLabel":{"en":"SECTION 4"},"text":{"en":"Secretariat - The OPRT Secretariat\nshall be cornposed\nofficials from the OPRT member-agencies.\nlt shall provide administrative\nrelated support services to the team.\n.\nThe Secretariat shall be headed by a senior official\nExecutive Secretary\ndesignated by the"}},{"id":"PH-H16820-A5","no":5,"noLabel":{"en":"SECTION 5"},"text":{"en":"Funding - The initial funding requirernent\nfor the operation\nof the OPRT shall be sourced from the Contingent Fund of the Office of the\nPresident and such other sources as may be identified by the Department\nBudget and Management. Annual funding requirements\nthereon of the OpRT\nshall be included\nin the general apprcpriations.\nThe remaining\nfunds, properties\nand other assets of the PMEPC are\nhereby transferred\n@Itu ot $e $r*i!af ol tle Swminer\nilililililillI\n\nsEcrloN Q. lepeating Gtause - Executive order No. 159 (s. 2002),\nOrder No.20 (s.2011) and all other issuances,\nrules and regulationi,\nor parts thereof, which are inconsistent\nwith this Executive Order, are hereby\nor modified accordingly."}},{"id":"PH-H16820-A7","no":7,"noLabel":{"en":"SECTION 7"},"text":{"en":"Separability Clause - lf any provision of this Executive\nOrder is declared invalid or unconstitutional,\nthe other provisions not affected\nshall remain valid and subsisting.\nEffectivity\nThis Executive Order shall take effect\nimmediately\nupon publication\nin a newspaper\ncirculation.\n_DO[E, in the City of Manila,\nthis 6th day of April\nin the year of Our\nLord, Two Thousand Eleven.\n\\ /\nBy the President\n@ltiill ol $e iprerilril Dl rt0 Srilipplut\nililtilIil"}}],"pack":"ph-p157"};
  FT["PH-H16821"] = {"id":"PH-H16821","coverage":"full","language":"en","sourceName":"The LawPhil Project — Arellano Law Foundation","sourceUrl":"","fetchedAt":"2026-10-28","articleCount":4,"structureMode":"ARTICLE","title":{"zh":null,"en":"MALACAÑAN PALACE BY THE PRESIDENT OF THE PHILIPPINES AMENDED, PRESCRIBING THE RULES AND PROCEDURES ON THE REVIEW AND APPROVAL OF ALL GOVERNMENT CONTRACTS, PURSUANT TO REPUBLIC ACT NO.","orig":"MALACAÑAN PALACE BY THE PRESIDENT OF THE PHILIPPINES AMENDED, PRESCRIBING THE RULES AND PROCEDURES ON THE REVIEW AND APPROVAL OF ALL GOVERNMENT CONTRACTS, PURSUANT TO REPUBLIC ACT NO."},"level":"law","status":"active","docNumber":"Executive Order No. 34","issuingBody":"President of the Philippines","completenessNote":"全文，共 4 条；逐字取自 LawPhil PDF 文本化成果（第三方 OCR，非机翻），原始文件 EO_00034_2017.txt","textQuality":"ocr-vendor","sourceFile":"菲律宾/法律原文/07_行政命令_EO/EO_00034_2017.txt","country":"PH","countryName":"菲律宾","layer":"intl","articles":[{"id":"PH-H16821-A1","no":1,"noLabel":{"en":"SECTION 1"},"text":{"en":"Section 4 of O No. 423, as amended, is hereby further\namended to read as follows:\n\"SECTION 4. Approval of Government Contracts Entered\nInto Through Alternative Methods of Procurement. Where the\nHead of the Procuring Entity has made a determination that a\nGovernment contract, including Government contracts required by law\nto be acted upon and/or approved by the President, regardless of\namount, falls under any of the exceptions from public bidding\ndescribed in Section 3 hereof, the Head of the Procuring Entity may\nproceed with the alternative methods of procurement according to the\nlaw and applicable rules and regulations; Provided, that for\nGovernment contracts involving an amount of at least P500 Million,\nthe Head of the Procuring Entity issues a certification under oath that\nthe contract falls within the exceptions from public bidding, is being\nentered into in faithful compliance with all applicable laws, rules and\nregulations, and is advantageous to the government.\nExcept for Government contracts required by law to be acted\nupon and/or approved by the President, the Head of the Procuring\nEntity shall have full authority to give final approval and/or enter into\nsaid Government contracts through alternative methods of\nprocurement allowed by law and applicable rules and regulations\nupon issuing the certificates mentioned in the immediately preceding\nparagraph, when applicable.\nThe Head of the Procuring Entity may delegate in writing this\nfull authority to give final approval and/or to enter into Government\ncontracts, through alternative methods of procurement allowed by law,\ninvolving such amount or threshold as he may deem appropriate, as\ncircumstances may warrant, subject to existing laws and such\nlimitations imposed by the Head of the Procuring Entity concerned\n(Section 5(j), Republic Act No. 9184). However, the Head of the\nProcuring Entity may not delegate the authority to certify under oath\nthat the contract falls within the exceptions from public bidding, is\nbeing entered into in faithful compliance with all applicable laws, rules\nand regulations, and is advantageous to the government.\""}},{"id":"PH-H16821-A2","no":2,"noLabel":{"en":"SECTION 2"},"text":{"en":"Section 6(b) of the same EO is also hereby amended to read as\n\"SECTION 6. Government Contracts Requiring Presidential\nAction and/or Approval.\nb. All Government contracts required by law to be acted upon\nand/or approved by the President, and any subsequent\namendments or supplements thereto, shall be submitted\nwith complete documentation to NEDA, through its Director-\n\nGeneral, within seven (7) days from approval by the Head\nof Procuring Entity concerned or his duly authorized\nrepresentative, as the case may be, for NDA's review and\nevaluation.\nGovernment contracts submitted hereunder shall be\naccompanied by a complete execution copy of the contract,\nrelated agreements, annexes, other approvals and permits,\nincluding a detailed summary of the pertinent laws, rules\nand regulations governing the processing and award of the\ncontract, and accompanied by the requirements of Section\n4 hereof where alternative methods of procurement were\nresorted to."}},{"id":"PH-H16821-A3","no":3,"noLabel":{"en":"SECTION 3"},"text":{"en":"Except for the foregoing amendments, all other provisions of EO\nNo. 423, as amended, shall remain unchanged."}},{"id":"PH-H16821-A4","no":4,"noLabel":{"en":"SECTION 4"},"text":{"en":"This Executive Order shall take effect immediately upon its\npublication in a national newspaper of general circulation.\nDONE, in the City of Manila this 17thday of July\nLord, Two Thousand and Seventeen.\nin the year of Our\nBy the President:\nSALVADOR C. MEDIALDEA\nExecutive Secretary A\nREPUBLIC OF THE PHILIPPINES\n~ 002881"}}],"pack":"ph-p157"};
  FT["PH-H16822"] = {"id":"PH-H16822","coverage":"full","language":"en","sourceName":"The LawPhil Project — Arellano Law Foundation","sourceUrl":"","fetchedAt":"2026-10-28","articleCount":13,"structureMode":"ARTICLE","title":{"zh":null,"en":"MALACANAN PALACE BY THE PRESIDENT OF THE PHILIPPINES DECLARING THE PAMBANSANG PABAHAY PARA SA PILIPINO PROGRAM AS A FLAGSHIP PROGRAM OF THE GOVERNMENT, AND DIRECTING ALL NATIONAL GOVERNMENT AGENCIES AND INSTRUMENTALITIES, INCLUDING GOVERNMENT-OWNED OR -CONTROLLED CORPORATIONS, AND LOCAL GOVERNMENT UNITS, TO SUBMIT A DETAILED INVENTORY OF ALL AVAILABLE AND SUITABLE LANDS FOR THE IMPLEMENTATION OF THE","orig":"MALACANAN PALACE BY THE PRESIDENT OF THE PHILIPPINES DECLARING THE PAMBANSANG PABAHAY PARA SA PILIPINO PROGRAM AS A FLAGSHIP PROGRAM OF THE GOVERNMENT, AND DIRECTING ALL NATIONAL GOVERNMENT AGENCIES AND INSTRUMENTALITIES, INCLUDING GOVERNMENT-OWNED OR -CONTROLLED CORPORATIONS, AND LOCAL GOVERNMENT UNITS, TO SUBMIT A DETAILED INVENTORY OF ALL AVAILABLE AND SUITABLE LANDS FOR THE IMPLEMENTATION OF THE"},"level":"law","status":"active","docNumber":"Executive Order No. 34","issuingBody":"President of the Philippines","completenessNote":"全文，共 13 条；逐字取自 LawPhil PDF 文本化成果（第三方 OCR，非机翻），原始文件 EO_00034_2023.txt","textQuality":"ocr-vendor","sourceFile":"菲律宾/法律原文/07_行政命令_EO/EO_00034_2023.txt","country":"PH","countryName":"菲律宾","layer":"intl","articles":[{"id":"PH-H16822-A1","no":1,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 1"},"text":{"en":"Declaration of the 4PH Program as a Flagship Program of the\nGovernment. The 4PH Program is hereby declared as a Flagship Program of the\nGovernment.\nThe DHSUD, as the primary government entity responsible for the management\nof housing and human settlements in the country, shall be the lead implementing\nagency of the Program.\nFor this purpose, all NGAs, LGUs, and other government entities are hereby\ndirected to provide full support to and cooperation with the DHSUD to ensure the\nsuccessful implementation of the Program."}},{"id":"PH-H16822-A2","no":2,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 2"},"text":{"en":"Identification of Lands for Housing and Human Settlements.\nThe DHSUD shall identify national and local government lands that are suitable for\nhousing and human settlements, including new townships and estates development,\nin coordination with concerned GAs and LGUs, and undertake the required activities\nto develop the same in an efficient manner.\nThe DHSUD shall likewise identify available public lands, and recommend to\nthe President, through the Department of Environment and Natural Resources, the\nissuance of Proclamations declaring said public lands as alienable and disposable,\nand reserving the same for housing and human settlement purposes, subject to\nexisting laws, rules and regulations."}},{"id":"PH-H16822-A3","no":3,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 3"},"text":{"en":"Mandatory Submission of Land Inventory by GAs and LGUs.\nNational Government departments, agencies, and instrumentalities, including GOCCs\nand their subsidiaries, as well as LGUs, shall conduct an inventory of the lands that\nthey own and administer, and submit the complete list to the DHSUD within sixty (60)\ncalendar days from the issuance of this Order.\nThe inventory of lands shall include government-owned idle lands or lands that\nhave not been used for the purpose for which they have been originally reserved or\nset aside for at least ten (10) years, and on which no improvements have been made\nby the owner as certified by the concerned LGU, pursuant to Section 8, Paragraph 2\nof RA No. 7279, as amended, and Sections 5. I|(d) and 24 of RA No. 11201\n2\n\nThe Land Registration Authority (LA) shall assist these agencies in the\npreparation of their respective inventories by providing a list of titles and the\ncorresponding certified true copies thereof that are registered in the name of said"}},{"id":"PH-H16822-A4","no":4,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 4"},"text":{"en":"Acquisition and Development of Identified Lands. Subject to\nlimitations under applicable laws, rules and regulations, the DHSUD shall acquire\nownership and/or administration of the identified lands of concerned agencies, for\nhousing and human settlement purposes, and shall carry out the immediate\ndevelopment of the aforementioned lands.\nThe LA shall cancel the titles of identified lands registered in the name of\nconcerned agencies, and re-issue new titles in the name of the DHSUD, subject to\nrelevant provisions of Presidential Decree No. 1529 or the \"Property Registration"}},{"id":"PH-H16822-A5","no":5,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 5"},"text":{"en":"Expropriation of Lands. In the exercise of its power of eminent\ndomain, the DHSUD, by itself or through the KSAs, shall initiate the expropriation of\nlands when necessary, subject to existing laws, rules, and regulations."}},{"id":"PH-H16822-A6","no":6,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 6"},"text":{"en":"Agency Support. All concerned GAs and instrumentalities,\nincluding GOCCs, and partner LGUs, are hereby directed to provide the necessary\nassistance and support to the DHSUD for the effective implementation of this Order."}},{"id":"PH-H16822-A7","no":7,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 7"},"text":{"en":"Reports. All GAs and instrumentalities, including GOCCs, are\nhereby directed, and all LGUs are hereby enjoined, to submit regular reports to the\nDHSUD on the status of the implementation of the Program and their compliance with\nthis Order. The DHSUD shall provide a summarized report to the President through\nthe Office of the Executive Secretary."}},{"id":"PH-H16822-A8","no":8,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 8"},"text":{"en":"Additional Manpower. The DHSUD shall determine the\nappropriate staffing pattern and corresponding qualification standards for the creation\nof additional positions necessary for the administration and operation of the Program,\nand submit to the Department of Budget and Management, for review and approval,\nthe proposed changes in the organizational structure and staffing pattern of the\nDHSUD, subject to compliance with relevant laws, rules, and regulations."}},{"id":"PH-H16822-A9","no":9,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 9"},"text":{"en":"Implementing Rules and Regulations. Within thirty (30) working\ndays from the effectivity of this Order, the DHSUD shall formulate the rules and\nregulations necessary to implement this Order."}},{"id":"PH-H16822-A10","no":10,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 10"},"text":{"en":"Funding. The funds necessary for the implementation of this Order\nshall be charged against current and available appropriations of concerned agencies,\nsubject to pertinent budgeting, accounting, and auditing laws, rules and regulations.\nThereafter, the funding requirements for succeeding years shall be included in the\nannual General Appropriations Act, subject to the usual budget preparation process."}},{"id":"PH-H16822-A11","no":11,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 11"},"text":{"en":"Separability. If any part or provision of this Order shall be held\ninvalid or unconstitutional, the provisions not affected thereby shall remain in full force\n3"}},{"id":"PH-H16822-A12","no":12,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 12"},"text":{"en":"Repeal. All orders, rules and regulations, and other issuances or\nparts thereof which are inconsistent with the provisions of this Order are hereby\nrepealed or modified accordingly."}},{"id":"PH-H16822-A13","no":13,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 13"},"text":{"en":"Effectivity. This Order shall take effect upon publication in the\nOfficial Gazette or in a newspaper of general circulation.\nDONE, in the City of Manila, this 17th day of July\nOur Lord, Two Thousand and Twenty-Three.\n, in the year of\nBy the President:\nLUCAS P. BERSAMIN\nExecutive Secretary\nOffice of the President\nMALACAÑANG RECORDS OFFICE\nATTY. CONCEPCION\nROLINO-ERAD\n9 719.2003\nDIRECTOR IV\nREPUBLIC OF THE PHILIPPINES"}}],"pack":"ph-p157"};
  FT["PH-H16823"] = {"id":"PH-H16823","coverage":"full","language":"en","sourceName":"The LawPhil Project — Arellano Law Foundation","sourceUrl":"LawPhil (HTML full text only)  |  https://lawphil.net/executive/execord/eo1936/eo_35_1936.html","fetchedAt":"2026-10-28","articleCount":1,"structureMode":"WHOLE","title":{"zh":null,"en":"Fixing Office Hours on Saturdays and During the Rainy Season in the City of Baguio","orig":"Fixing Office Hours on Saturdays and During the Rainy Season in the City of Baguio"},"level":"law","status":"active","docNumber":"Executive Order No. 35","issuingBody":"President of the Philippines","promulgatedDate":"1936-06-02","completenessNote":"全文，共 1 条；逐字取自 LawPhil PDF 文本化成果（第三方 OCR，非机翻），原始文件 EO_00035_1936_html.txt","textQuality":"ocr-vendor","sourceFile":"菲律宾/法律原文/07_行政命令_EO/EO_00035_1936_html.txt","country":"PH","countryName":"菲律宾","layer":"intl","articles":[{"id":"PH-H16823-A1","no":1,"noLabel":{},"text":{"en":"MALACAÑAN PALACE\nBY THE PRESIDENT OF THE PHILIPPINES\n[ EXECUTIVE ORDER NO. 35, June 02, 1936 ]\nFIXING OFFICE HOURS ON SATURDAYS AND DURING THE RAINY SEASON IN THE CITY OF\nPursuant to the provisions of section five hundred and sixty-four of the Administrative Code of nineteen\nhundred and seventeen, the office hours of all Government bureaus and offices (Insular, provincial and\nmunicipal) in the City of Baguio, during the period from July first to September fifteenth, nineteen hundred\nand thirty-six, both dates inclusive, are hereby reduced to five continuous hours which shall be from\nseven-thirty a.m. to twelve-thirty p.m.\nThis Order does not oblige the head of any department, bureau, or office so to reduce the hours of labor in his\nbranch of work, but leaves the same in his discretion subject to the requirements of the service.\nDone at the City of Manila, this second day of June, in the year of Our Lord, nineteen hundred and thirty-six,\nand of the Commonwealth of the Philippines, the first.\nMANUEL L. QUEZON\nPresident of the Philippines\nBy the President:\nELPIDIO QUIRINO\nSecretary of the Interior"}}],"pack":"ph-p157"};
  FT["PH-H16824"] = {"id":"PH-H16824","coverage":"full","language":"en","sourceName":"The LawPhil Project — Arellano Law Foundation","sourceUrl":"LawPhil (HTML full text only)  |  https://lawphil.net/executive/execord/eo1947/eo_35_1947.html","fetchedAt":"2026-10-28","articleCount":1,"structureMode":"WHOLE","title":{"zh":null,"en":"Prescribing the Fees for Milling Palay","orig":"Prescribing the Fees for Milling Palay"},"level":"law","status":"active","docNumber":"Executive Order No. 35","issuingBody":"President of the Philippines","promulgatedDate":"1947-01-03","completenessNote":"全文，共 1 条；逐字取自 LawPhil PDF 文本化成果（第三方 OCR，非机翻），原始文件 EO_00035_1947_html.txt","textQuality":"ocr-vendor","sourceFile":"菲律宾/法律原文/07_行政命令_EO/EO_00035_1947_html.txt","country":"PH","countryName":"菲律宾","layer":"intl","articles":[{"id":"PH-H16824-A1","no":1,"noLabel":{},"text":{"en":"MALACAÑAN PALACE\nBY THE PRESIDENT OF THE PHILIPPINES\n[ EXECUTIVE ORDER NO. 35, January 03, 1947 ]\nPRESCRIBING THE FEES FOR MILLING PALAY\nWHEREAS, it is necessary, because of the present emergency, that the fees for milling palay be fixed in order\nto prevent excessive charges for such service, thus increasing the price of this prime commodity to the\nultimate consumer:\nNOW, THEREFORE, I, MANUEL ROXAS, President of the Philippines, by virtue of the powers vested in\nme by the Constitution and pursuant to the provisions of the Emergency Powers Law, do hereby order that no\nowner of rice mills shall charge more than one peso (P1.00) for every cavan of rice milled, the by-products to\ngo to the owner of the palay milled.\nAny violation of the provisions of this Order shall be punished in accordance with the provisions of section 3\nof Commonwealth Act No. 600, as amended.\nDone at the City of Manila , this 3rd day of January, in the year of Our Lord nineteen hundred and\nforty-seven, and of the Independence of the Philippines, the first.\n(Sgd.) MANUEL ROXAS\nPresident of the Philippines\nBy the President:\n(Sgd.) EMILIO ABELLO\nChief of the Executive Office"}}],"pack":"ph-p157"};
  FT["PH-H16825"] = {"id":"PH-H16825","coverage":"full","language":"en","sourceName":"The LawPhil Project — Arellano Law Foundation","sourceUrl":"","fetchedAt":"2026-10-28","articleCount":3,"structureMode":"ARTICLE","title":{"zh":null,"en":"MALACANANG BY THE PRESIDENT OF THE PHILIPPINES EXPOUTIVE ORDER NO. 35 PROVIDING FOR AN EFFECTIVE ORGANIZATION FOR NATIONAL SECURITY AND TOR THE COORDINATION AND UNIFIED DIRECTION OF NATIONAL MOBILIZATION PLANS AND POLIGIES.","orig":"MALACANANG BY THE PRESIDENT OF THE PHILIPPINES EXPOUTIVE ORDER NO. 35 PROVIDING FOR AN EFFECTIVE ORGANIZATION FOR NATIONAL SECURITY AND TOR THE COORDINATION AND UNIFIED DIRECTION OF NATIONAL MOBILIZATION PLANS AND POLIGIES."},"level":"law","status":"active","docNumber":"Executive Order No. 35","issuingBody":"President of the Philippines","completenessNote":"全文，共 3 条；逐字取自 LawPhil PDF 文本化成果（第三方 OCR，非机翻），原始文件 EO_00035_1954.txt","textQuality":"ocr-vendor","sourceFile":"菲律宾/法律原文/07_行政命令_EO/EO_00035_1954.txt","country":"PH","countryName":"菲律宾","layer":"intl","articles":[{"id":"PH-H16825-A1","no":1,"noLabel":{"en":"SECTION 1"},"text":{"en":"National Security Council.- a. The Gound1l of\nNational Defonso ostablishod under Section 6 of the National\nDefonse Act, and as organizod by Executive Ordor No. 330, dated\nJuly 1, 1950, which named It as the National Security Counsil,\nhall have the following functions\n(1) To advise the Prosident with respect to the integra-\ntion of domostic, foreigs and military polioies rolating to\nthe national scurity so as to onablo the armed services and\nthe othor dopartments and agonies of the Goverrment to co.\noperato more affectively in matters involving the national\n(2) To assoss and appraise the objoctivos, commitments\nand risks of the Philippines in rolation to our actual and\npotential military power, In the intorost of national socurity,\nfor the purposo of making rocommendation to the Prosidont in\nconnection throwith;\n(3) To consider policios on matters of common interest\nto tho departments and agencies of the Government concerned\nwith the national security, and to maho recommendation to tho\nPresident in connection therowith;\n(4) To advise the Prosidont concolning the coordination\nof military, industrial and civilian mobilization, Including\n(a) policios concerning industrial ad civiliga\nmobilization in order to assuro the most effoctive\nmobilization and maximum utilization of the nation' a\nmanpowor in th event of war;\n\n- 2 -\n(b) programs for the effective use in tine of\nwar of the nation's natural and industrial resourceg\nfor military and civilian nods, for the maintenance\nand stabilization of tho civilian economy in time of\nwar, and for the adjustment of such aconcy to war\nneeds and conditiona;.\n(o) polioios for unifying, in timo of war, the\nactivities of Govermont agoncios and departments\nangagod in or concernod with production, procurement,\ndistribution, or transportation of military or civilian\nsupplies, materials and products;\n(a) the relationship botwoon potontial supplies\nof, and potential requiromonts for, manpower, resources\nand productive facilitios in time of war;\n(o) policies for establishing adequate roserves\nof' strategic and critioal material and for the conserva\ntion. of these resourcas;\n(r) the stratogie relocation of industries, serv-\nIces, and govorment and economic activities, the con\ntinuous operation of which la ossential to the nation's\nb. In addition to tho abovo functions, the Council shall, under\nthe direction and on behalf of the President\n(1) preparo and maintain at all times plans for the\noffective mobilization in time of war of the nation's finan-\ncial, industrial, economic and manpowor resources and forces;\n(2) direct, control and coordinate all mobilization\nactivitios and functions of the executive branch of the\nGovorament, Including but not limited to production, pro-\ncurement, manpower, stabilization, communications and trans\nport activities and functions;\n(3) direct and control the operational functions and\nsctivitias of the National Intelligonce Coordinating Agency;\n(4) perform such othor functions. and duties as the\nPresident may direct as necessary and proper for the na\ntional security.\nSt. 2. q. Tho Counoil shall have a permanent staff to assist.?\nit in the performance of its functions and duties.\nTho staff aball\nbo cemposod of the pormanent Secretary of the Council, as bead, and\n\nnot more than five Assistants who shall be permanently detailed\nthereto from such offices, branches or agencies of the Executivo\nDepartment as the Prosident may direct. Until otherwise provided\nby law and appropriations for this purpose, the Secretary and his\nAssistants shall continue to rocoivo their compensation from tho\noxecutive offico, bureau, or agony from which they are detailed.\nb. The Secretary of the Council is horeby authorized to apa\npoint and fix the salaries of such personnel as may be necessary\nto onable the staff to perform tho dutios and functions required\nby tho Council, subject to tho availability of funds for this pur\nc. In performing Its functions, the Council shall utilize to\nthe maximum extent the facilities and resourcos of the departments\nand agonciss of the Government.\nSC. 3. lational Intellionco Coordinating Agency. a. Tor\nthe purposo of coordinating tho intolligonce activitios of the\nsovoral Goverment dopartments and agencios in the interest of\nnational socurity, the National Intelligence Coordinating Agony,\nincluding the Coordinator of National Intelligonce, shall hereafter\nporform the following dutios and functions under tho operational\ndiroction and control of the National Security Counoil;\n(1) To adviso the National Socurity Council in matters\nconcorning such intelligenco activities of the Goverrment\ndepartmonts and agencies as relate to national security;\n(2) To make rocommondations to tho National Security\nCouncil for the coordination of such Intelligance activities\nof the dopartments and agoncios of the Goverrment as relate\nto the national socurity;\n(3) To correlate and ovaluate intelligence rolating to\nthe national scourity, and provido for the appropriate dissa-\nmination of such Intelligence within the Governent, using,\nwhere appropriato, existing agoncios and facilitioas Provided,\nThat the Agency or its personnol shall have no police, sub-\npoena, law-onforcoment powers, or internal-socurity functions:\nProvided, further, That tho dopartmonts, and other agencios of\nthe Government shall continue to collect, evaluate, correlato,\nand disseminate departmental intelligence: And provided, fur\nther, That the Coordinator of National Intelligones shall be.\nrosponsible for protecting intelligence sources and mathods\nfrom unauthorized disclosuro;\n\nfor the bonofit of the cristing intolli-\ngence agencics, suob additional sorvices of common concern\nas the National Socurity Council dotermines can be moro of-\nficiently accomplished contrally;\n.\n(5) To perform such other functions and duties rolated\nto intelligence affecting tho national security as tho Na-\ntional Sacurity Council may from time to time diroct, subject\nto the approval of the Prosidont.\nb. To the oxtent recommonded by the National Security Counci1\nand approved by the Prosident, such Intelligence of the departments\nand agencios of the Govornment as relatos to tha national security\nshall be open to the inspoction of the Coordinator of National In-\ntelligence; and such Intolligence as rolatos to tho national. socurity\nand is possessod by such dopartmonts and other agoncies of the Govern-\nment shall be made availablo to the Coordinator of National Into111-\ngonco for correlation, evaluation and dissemination.\nc. For administrativo purposos, the National Intelligonce Co.\nordinating Agoney, including the Coordinator of National Intelligenos,\nshall be diroctly under the Offico of the Prosident."}},{"id":"PH-H16825-A4","no":4,"noLabel":{"en":"SEC 4"},"text":{"en":"a. any commissioned officer of the Armed Forces of the\nPhilippines on active duty who is appointed as Secratary or Assistant\nSecrotary of the National Socurity Council, or as Coordinator of Na-\ntional Intelligenco, shall -\n(1) in tho porformance of his duties undor this Order,\nbo subject to no authority, control, supervision, rostriction\nor prohibition (nilitary or otherwise) other than would be\noperative with respoct to him 1f he woro a civilian in no way\nconnected with the Dopartment of National Dofense or the Armed\nForcos of the Philippinds or any component thereof;\n(2) not possoss or exerçise any authority, control,\nsuporvision, powors, functions or duties (otbor than such\nas he possessos, or is authorized or airacted to oxorciso,\nunder this Order) with respect to the Department of National\nDefonse or the Armed Forces of the Philippines or any com\nponent thereof.\nb. Except as provided in subsoction a, the appointmont and\nservico of a comissioned officer of the Armed Forces of the Phil-\nippines as Socretary or Assistant Secretary of the National Security\nCouncil, or as Coordinator of National Intelligence, shall in no\nway affoct the military status, office, rank or grade ho may occupy\nor hold in the military service, or any enolumonts, allowances,\n\n5 ∞\nright, privilege or bonefit incident to or arising out of his\nmilitary office or status. Any such commissioned officer hall,\nwhile sorving in any of the officos beroinabove provided, re-\ncoive ~ (1) from the appropriations for the Armed Forces, the\nmilitary pay and allowancos payable to him by virtue of his\nmilitary status; and (2) from funds appropriated for the ex-\npenses of the Council or the Agony, as the casa may bo, the\namount by which the monthly compensation which may now or\nhereafter be provided for the civilian position excoods bis\nmonthly military pay and allowances."}},{"id":"PH-H16825-A5","no":5,"noLabel":{"en":"SEC 5"},"text":{"en":"Funds for the operation of the National Security\nCouncil and the National Intelligonce Coordinating Agony shall\nheroafter be Includod in tho annual gonoral appropriations for\nthe Offico of the President.\n6. The provisions of Executive Order No. 235, dated\nJuly 1, 1949, which aro inconsistent with this Order, are hereby\nrepealed or modified accordingly.\nDone in the City of Manila this 20th day of\nthe joar of Our Lord, ninetoon hundred and fifty-four, and of\nthe Independence of tho Philippines, tho eighta.\nJustingers,\nBy the Prosidont:\nFRED RUIZ CASTRO\nExocutive Secratary"}}],"pack":"ph-p157"};
