  FT["PH-H16909"] = {"id":"PH-H16909","coverage":"full","language":"en","sourceName":"The LawPhil Project — Arellano Law Foundation","sourceUrl":"","fetchedAt":"2026-10-28","articleCount":5,"structureMode":"ARTICLE","title":{"zh":null,"en":"EXECunvE ORDER NO. -42","orig":"EXECunvE ORDER NO. -42"},"level":"law","status":"active","docNumber":"Executive Order No. 42","issuingBody":"President of the Philippines","completenessNote":"全文，共 5 条；逐字取自 LawPhil PDF 文本化成果（第三方 OCR，非机翻），原始文件 EO_00042_1998.txt","textQuality":"ocr-vendor","sourceFile":"菲律宾/法律原文/07_行政命令_EO/EO_00042_1998.txt","country":"PH","countryName":"菲律宾","layer":"intl","articles":[{"id":"PH-H16909-A1","no":1,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 1"},"text":{"en":"Section 1 of Executive Order No:-197 is hereby amended to read as\n\"Section 1. Name\nand Territorial\nPresidential\nCommission to plan for and develop a Growth Corridor shall be known as\nPresidential Commission on RIZLAQUE Growth Area, embracing the provinces\nRizal, LagWla, Aurora and Quezon\".\n197, series of 1994, created the Presidential\nto fast-track the implementation\nof programsthe\narea from the National Capital Region to\n\n.~\n~\n-2."}},{"id":"PH-H16909-A2","no":2,"noLabel":{"en":"Sec 2"},"text":{"en":"Sec1ion 2 of Executive Order No.follows:\n197 is hereby amended to read as\n\"Sec. 2 Composition. The Commission shall be chaired by the Chailman\nof the Presidential Committee on flagship Programs and Projects, with the\nChailman of the Public Estate Authority (PEA) as Co-Cbainnan, and the following\nas members: Chainnan of the Housing and Urban Development Coordinating\nCoWlCil, Deputy Director General, National Economic and Development\nAuthority; Undersecretaries of the Department of Public Works and Highways,\nDepal1ln!ent of Environment and Natural Resources, Depal1ln!ent of Agrarian\nRefOlm., Depat1ment of Trade and bldusay, Department of the blterior and Local\nGovernment; Head of the Presidential Management Staff; and Governors of Riza1,\nLaguna, Aurora and Quezon provinces\"."}},{"id":"PH-H16909-A3","no":3,"noLabel":{"en":"Sec 3"},"text":{"en":"In addition to the functions and responsibilities of the Commission as\npro\"\\fided in Execu1ive Order No. 197, the Commission shall have the following functions\nand re8pons1biJities:\n\"j. Provide overall direction, coordination, and supervision in the planning,\nimplementation, and monitoring of its projects under the MARll..AQUE\nFRAMEWORK and MASTER PLAN;\nk. Enter into any kind of aITangement or agreement with public and private\nentities in pW\"Suance\nof its objectives and in furtherance of its mandate;\n1. Act as coordinating body with respect to all plans, programs, and projects\nproposed by the local government units and national agencies, for\nimplementation within the growth area;\nm. Ensure that all projects and programs proposed to be Wldertaken by\nprivate entities mthin he Growth Area are in consonant mth the\nCommission's developmental frameworks.\"\n4. Section 4 of Executive Ordr No.\n197 is hereby amended to read as\n\"Sec. 4. Powers and Functions of the Executive Director. The\nExecutive Director, appointed by the President of the Philippines, shall sit as\nex-officio member of the Commission, and shall be its Chief Executive\nresponsible for the execution and administration of its approved policies and\nmeasures. He shall also perform the following functions:\n.~.\n\n\",\n-3-\na. Submit for consideration of the Commission the policies and measmes\nnecessary to carry out the mandate of the Commission;\nb. Execute and administer the policies, plans, programs and projects\napproved by the Commission;\n\\\nDirect and supernse the operation and internal administration of the\nCommission;\nd. Represent the Commission in all dealings Mth agencies and\nins1IUmentaJi1ies\nof the government, and Mth all other private entities,\ndomestic or foreign; and\ne. Exercise such other duties as may be vested by the Commission and\nauthorized by law.\""}},{"id":"PH-H16909-A5","no":5,"noLabel":{"en":"Sec 5"},"text":{"en":"Repealing Clause. The provisions of Executive Order No. 197 dated\nAugust 29, 1994, and Executive Order No. 232 dated March 29, 1995, to the extent that\nthey are inconsistent with this Executive Order, are hereby repealed or amended\naccordingly\n."}},{"id":"PH-H16909-A6","no":6,"noLabel":{"en":"Sec 6"},"text":{"en":"This Executive Order shall take effect immediately.\nDone in the City of Manila, this 01 !;-J!--\nin the year of Our Lord,\nnineteen hundred and ninety eight.\n..6\nBy the President:\nRONALDO B. ZAMORA\nExecutive Secretary"}}],"pack":"ph-p157"};
  FT["PH-H16910"] = {"id":"PH-H16910","coverage":"full","language":"en","sourceName":"The LawPhil Project — Arellano Law Foundation","sourceUrl":"","fetchedAt":"2026-10-28","articleCount":2,"structureMode":"ARTICLE","title":{"zh":null,"en":"MALACAÑANG TRANSFERRING THE PHILIPPINE CROP INSURANCE CORPORATION FROM THE DEPARTMENT OF AGRICULTURE TO THE DEPARTMENT OF FINANCE","orig":"MALACAÑANG TRANSFERRING THE PHILIPPINE CROP INSURANCE CORPORATION FROM THE DEPARTMENT OF AGRICULTURE TO THE DEPARTMENT OF FINANCE"},"level":"law","status":"active","docNumber":"Executive Order No. 42","issuingBody":"President of the Philippines","completenessNote":"全文，共 2 条；逐字取自 LawPhil PDF 文本化成果（第三方 OCR，非机翻），原始文件 EO_00042_2001.txt","textQuality":"ocr-vendor","sourceFile":"菲律宾/法律原文/07_行政命令_EO/EO_00042_2001.txt","country":"PH","countryName":"菲律宾","layer":"intl","articles":[{"id":"PH-H16910-A2","no":2,"noLabel":{"en":"SECTION 2"},"text":{"en":"Repealing Clause. All executive orders, rules and\nregulations and other issuances inconsistent with the provisions of this\nExecutive Order are hereby revoked or modified accordingly."}},{"id":"PH-H16910-A3","no":3,"noLabel":{"en":"SECTION 3"},"text":{"en":"Effectivity. This Executive Order shall take effect\nimmediately.\nCity of Manila, October 15, 2001\nPMS LIBRARY\nBy the President:\nALBERTO G. ROMULO\nExecutive Secretary\nPMS LIBRARY BCODE002068\n2"}}],"pack":"ph-p157"};
  FT["PH-H16911"] = {"id":"PH-H16911","coverage":"full","language":"en","sourceName":"The LawPhil Project — Arellano Law Foundation","sourceUrl":"","fetchedAt":"2026-10-28","articleCount":1,"structureMode":"WHOLE","title":{"zh":null,"en":"MALACAÑAN PALACE BY THE PRESIDENT OF THE PHILIPPINES PROVIDING THE PRESIDENTIAL COMMISSION ON GOOD GOVERNMENT WITH PROVISIONAL AUTHORITY TO REPLACE DIRECTORS IN SEQUESTERED OR SURRENDERED CORPORATIONS.","orig":"MALACAÑAN PALACE BY THE PRESIDENT OF THE PHILIPPINES PROVIDING THE PRESIDENTIAL COMMISSION ON GOOD GOVERNMENT WITH PROVISIONAL AUTHORITY TO REPLACE DIRECTORS IN SEQUESTERED OR SURRENDERED CORPORATIONS."},"level":"law","status":"active","docNumber":"Executive Order No. 42","issuingBody":"President of the Philippines","completenessNote":"全文，共 1 条；逐字取自 LawPhil PDF 文本化成果（第三方 OCR，非机翻），原始文件 EO_00042_2011.txt","textQuality":"ocr-vendor","sourceFile":"菲律宾/法律原文/07_行政命令_EO/EO_00042_2011.txt","country":"PH","countryName":"菲律宾","layer":"intl","articles":[{"id":"PH-H16911-A1","no":1,"noLabel":{"en":"SECTION 1"},"text":{"en":"Granting of Provisional Authority. The Presidential Commission\non Good Government (PCGG) in addition to its powers, functions and duties pursuant to\nexisting laws and executive issuances shall have the provisional authority to replace\nany of the nominee-directors currently holding positions in such capacity in any of the\ncorporations sequestered by or surrendered to it with up to two members of the PCGG.\nSECTION. 2. Validity. The provisional authority subject of this issuance shall be\nexercised by the PCGG Chairperson. The designation of any PCGG member as\nprovisional nominees will be valid until permanent replacements are made by the\nPresident. These permanent replacements shall be under the general supervision of the\nSECTION. 3. List of temporary nominees. The PCGG shall furnish the\nPresident, through the Executive Secretary, with a list of the temporary replacements to\nthe board of such corporations within a reasonable time from the moment they are\nSECTION. 4. Report. All nominee-directors shall be required to submit to the\nPCGG monthly reports or as often as may be required, on the affairs, developments\nand transactions affecting the respective corporations. The PCGG shall from time to\ntime submit a detailed summary of these reports to the President.\n@itice ofthe President of the Philioines\n\nSECTION. 5. Duration. Unless otherwise extended by the President, the\nprovisional authority granted to the PCGG shall be valid until 31 December 2011.\nSECTION. 6. Repealing Clause. All other rules, regulations and issuances or\nparts thereof which are inconsistent with this Executive Order are hereby repealed or\nmodified accordingly.\nSECTION. 7. Effectivity. This Order shall take effect immediately upon its\npublication in a national newspaper of general circulation.\nDONE in the City of Manila, this 9th day of\nour Lord, Two Thousand and Eleven.\n,in the year of\nBy the President:\nPAQUITO N. OCHOA, JR.\nExecutive Secretary\nCERTIFIED COPY:\n@ifice of the President of the Philipines\nMARIANITE M UIMAANDAL\nDIRECTOR IV\nC/S-1-201 Q812 -2011 MALACARANG RECORDS OFFICE"}}],"pack":"ph-p157"};
  FT["PH-H16912"] = {"id":"PH-H16912","coverage":"full","language":"en","sourceName":"The LawPhil Project — Arellano Law Foundation","sourceUrl":"","fetchedAt":"2026-10-28","articleCount":5,"structureMode":"ARTICLE","title":{"zh":null,"en":"MALACAÑAN PALACE BY THE PRESIDENT OF THE PHILIPPINES REPEALING EXECUTIVE ORDER (EO) NO. 340 (S. 2004) AND DEFINING THE POWERS, FUNCTIONS AND DUTIES OF THE BOARD OF DIRECTORS OF THE SUBIC BAY METROPOLITAN AUTHORITY (SBMA) AND THE SBMA ADMINISTRATOR","orig":"MALACAÑAN PALACE BY THE PRESIDENT OF THE PHILIPPINES REPEALING EXECUTIVE ORDER (EO) NO. 340 (S. 2004) AND DEFINING THE POWERS, FUNCTIONS AND DUTIES OF THE BOARD OF DIRECTORS OF THE SUBIC BAY METROPOLITAN AUTHORITY (SBMA) AND THE SBMA ADMINISTRATOR"},"level":"law","status":"active","docNumber":"Executive Order No. 42","issuingBody":"President of the Philippines","completenessNote":"全文，共 5 条；逐字取自 LawPhil PDF 文本化成果（第三方 OCR，非机翻），原始文件 EO_00042_2017.txt","textQuality":"ocr-vendor","sourceFile":"菲律宾/法律原文/07_行政命令_EO/EO_00042_2017.txt","country":"PH","countryName":"菲律宾","layer":"intl","articles":[{"id":"PH-H16912-A1","no":1,"noLabel":{"en":"SECTION 1"},"text":{"en":"Repeal. EO No. 340 (s. 2004) is hereby expressly repealed."}},{"id":"PH-H16912-A2","no":2,"noLabel":{"en":"SECTION 2"},"text":{"en":"Powers of the SBMA Board. The powers of the SBMA, as\ndefined under RA No. 7227, shall be exercised by the SBMA Board of Directors."}},{"id":"PH-H16912-A3","no":3,"noLabel":{"en":"SECTION 3"},"text":{"en":"SBMA Administrator and Chairman of the SBMA Board. The\nPresident shall appoint the Administrator of the SBMA, who shall be the ex officio\nChairman of the SBMA Board.\nSECTION. 4. Powers and Duties of the SBMA Administrator. The\nAdministrator, who shall be the Chief Executive Officer of the SBMA, shall have the\nfollowing powers, functions and duties:\na. To execute, administer and implement the policies and measures\napproved and adopted by the SBMA Board;\nb. To directly administer and supervise the operations and day-to-day\nbusiness activities of the SBMA:\nTo exercise the powers of control and supervision over decisions and\nactions of subordinate officers;\nd. To appoint, transfer, remove, suspend or otherwise discipline any\nemployee of the SBMA in accordance with law;\ne. To represent the SBMA in all dealings with offices, agencies and\ninstrumentalities of the Government and with all persons and entities,\npublic or private, domestic or foreign, unless otherwise directed by the\nPresident or by the SBMA Board;\nTo sign all permits, certificates, authorizations, and other official\ndocuments issued by the SBMA in the exercise of its governmental,\nregulatory, proprietary, and commercial powers;\ng. To execute, on behalf of the SBMA, all contracts, agreements and\nother instruments affecting the interests of the SBMA or where the\nSBMA is a contracting party, duly approved by the SBMA Board;\nh. To direct and supervise the preparation of the agenda for the\nmeetings of the SBMA Board;\n1. To preside at the meetings of the SBMA Board; and\n].\nTo perform such other functions and duties as the President may\ndirect, or as may be assigned to him/her by the SBMA Board."}},{"id":"PH-H16912-A5","no":5,"noLabel":{"en":"SECTION 5"},"text":{"en":"Separability. If any provision of this Order is held invalid or\nunconstitutional, the other provisions not otherwise affected shall remain in full force"}},{"id":"PH-H16912-A6","no":6,"noLabel":{"en":"SECTION 6"},"text":{"en":"Effectivity. This Order shall take effect immediately.\nDONE, in the City of Manila, this 25thdaySeptembein the year of Our Lord,\nTwo Thousand and Seventeen.\nBy the Président:\nSALVADOR C. MEDIALDEA\nExecutive Secretary\n1\nREPUBLIC OF THE PRILIPPINES\n- 003840"}}],"pack":"ph-p157"};
  FT["PH-H16913"] = {"id":"PH-H16913","coverage":"full","language":"en","sourceName":"The LawPhil Project — Arellano Law Foundation","sourceUrl":"","fetchedAt":"2026-10-28","articleCount":5,"structureMode":"ARTICLE","title":{"zh":null,"en":"MALACAÑAN PALACE BY THE PRESIDENT OF THE PHILIPPINES LIFTING THE MANDATED PRICE CEILINGS ON RICE UNDER","orig":"MALACAÑAN PALACE BY THE PRESIDENT OF THE PHILIPPINES LIFTING THE MANDATED PRICE CEILINGS ON RICE UNDER"},"level":"law","status":"active","docNumber":"Executive Order No. 42","issuingBody":"President of the Philippines","completenessNote":"全文，共 5 条；逐字取自 LawPhil PDF 文本化成果（第三方 OCR，非机翻），原始文件 EO_00042_2023.txt","textQuality":"ocr-vendor","sourceFile":"菲律宾/法律原文/07_行政命令_EO/EO_00042_2023.txt","country":"PH","countryName":"菲律宾","layer":"intl","articles":[{"id":"PH-H16913-A1","no":1,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 1"},"text":{"en":"Lifting of the Mandated Price Ceilings on Rice. Following the\nrecommendation of the DA and DTI, the mandated price ceilings on regular milled and\nwell-milled rice under EO No. 39 are hereby lifted."}},{"id":"PH-H16913-A2","no":2,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 2"},"text":{"en":"Directive to Other Agencies. To ensure stability of rice prices upon\nthe lifting of the mandated price ceilings, other concerned agencies, consistent with\ntheir respective mandates, shall fortify their existing programs and initiatives to provide\nsupport and assistance to farmers, retailers, and consumers."}},{"id":"PH-H16913-A3","no":3,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 3"},"text":{"en":"Separability. If any part or provision of this Order shall be held\ninvalid or unconstitutional, the provisions not affected thereby shall remain in full force"}},{"id":"PH-H16913-A4","no":4,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 4"},"text":{"en":"Repeal. EO No. 39 is hereby repealed. All other orders, rules and\nregulations, and issuances or parts thereof which are inconsistent with the provisions\nof this Order are hereby repealed or modified accordingly."}},{"id":"PH-H16913-A5","no":5,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 5"},"text":{"en":"Effectivity. This Order shall take effect immediately upon\npublication in the Official Gazette or in a newspaper of general circulation.\nDONE, in the City of Manila, this 4th day of\nof our Lord, Two Thousand and Twenty-Three.\nOctober , in the year\nBy the President:\nLUCAS P. BERSAMIN\nExecutive Sectetary\nOffice of the President\nMALACANANG RECORDS OFFICE\nATTY. CONCEPCION LENY E TERBOLINO-ENAD\n8 16-10-2029\nDIRECTOR IV\nREPUBLIC OF THE PHILIPPINES\n2"}}],"pack":"ph-p157"};
  FT["PH-H16914"] = {"id":"PH-H16914","coverage":"full","language":"en","sourceName":"The LawPhil Project — Arellano Law Foundation","sourceUrl":"","fetchedAt":"2026-10-28","articleCount":1,"structureMode":"WHOLE","title":{"zh":null,"en":"THE GOVERNMENT OF THE PHILIPPINE ISLANDS, EXECUTIVE BUREAU. MANILA, June 24, 1913. EXECUTIVE ORDER }","orig":"THE GOVERNMENT OF THE PHILIPPINE ISLANDS, EXECUTIVE BUREAU. MANILA, June 24, 1913. EXECUTIVE ORDER }"},"level":"law","status":"active","docNumber":"Executive Order No. 43","issuingBody":"President of the Philippines","completenessNote":"全文，共 1 条；逐字取自 LawPhil PDF 文本化成果（第三方 OCR，非机翻），原始文件 EO_00043_1913.txt","textQuality":"ocr-vendor","sourceFile":"菲律宾/法律原文/07_行政命令_EO/EO_00043_1913.txt","country":"PH","countryName":"菲律宾","layer":"intl","articles":[{"id":"PH-H16914-A1","no":1,"noLabel":{},"text":{"en":"18' W. 21.57 m. to point 32; N. 14° 30' W. 105.92 m. to\npoint 33; N. 7° 25' E. 30.08 m. to point 34; N. 27° 23' E.\n46.29 m. to point 35; N. 44° 47' E. 149.09 m. to point 36;\nN. 36° 44' W. 40.0 m. to point 37; N. 61° 57' W. 40.56 m.\nto point 38; N. 28° 38' W. 45.65 m. to point 39; N. 87° 26°\nE. 829.56 m. to point 40; S. 35° 03' W. 104.92 m. to point\n41; S. 47° 02 W. 37.05 m. to point 42; S. 50° 07° W. 97.02\nm. to point 43; S. 13° 15' W. 115.91 m. to point 44; S. 75°\n54' E. 71.0 m. to point 45; S. 34° 43' E. 10.41 m. to point\n46; S. 9° 30° W. 36.12 m. to point 47; S. 29° 52' W. 37.11\nm. to point 48; S. 3° 36' W. 55.52 m. to point 49; S. 36° 27'\nE. 103.62 m. to point 50; N. 61° 39 E. 121.09 m. to point 51;\nS. 78° 36' E. 43.91 m. to point 52; S. 38° 54' E. 121.41\nm. to point 58; S. 20° 13' W. 82.08 m. to point 54; S. 28°\n38' E. 78.00 m. to point 55; S. 7° 54' W. 90.11 m. to point\n56; S. 73° 44° W. 55.0 m. to point 57; S. 17° 23' W. 55.37\nm. to point 58; S. 78° 19 E. 61.43 m. to point 59; S. 55°\n31' W. 77.23 m. to point 1, point of beginning.\nContaining 728,110.32 square meters.\nAll points are on Laguna de Bay.\nBounded on north by public land; on all other sides by\nLaguna de Bay.\nBearings true.\nVariation, 0° 32 E.\nPoints referred to marked on plan In-104.\nSurveyed, January, 1912. Approved, June 13, 1913.\nW. CAMEROn FORBES,\nGovernor-General."}}],"pack":"ph-p157"};
  FT["PH-H16915"] = {"id":"PH-H16915","coverage":"full","language":"en","sourceName":"The LawPhil Project — Arellano Law Foundation","sourceUrl":"LawPhil (HTML full text only)  |  https://lawphil.net/executive/execord/eo1936/eo_43_1936.html","fetchedAt":"2026-10-28","articleCount":1,"structureMode":"WHOLE","title":{"zh":null,"en":"Transferring Certain Functions and Duties of the Bureau of Science to Other Entities Under the Commonwealth of the Philippines.","orig":"Transferring Certain Functions and Duties of the Bureau of Science to Other Entities Under the Commonwealth of the Philippines."},"level":"law","status":"active","docNumber":"Executive Order No. 43","issuingBody":"President of the Philippines","promulgatedDate":"1936-06-30","completenessNote":"全文，共 1 条；逐字取自 LawPhil PDF 文本化成果（第三方 OCR，非机翻），原始文件 EO_00043_1936_html.txt","textQuality":"ocr-vendor","sourceFile":"菲律宾/法律原文/07_行政命令_EO/EO_00043_1936_html.txt","country":"PH","countryName":"菲律宾","layer":"intl","articles":[{"id":"PH-H16915-A1","no":1,"noLabel":{},"text":{"en":"MALACAÑAN PALACE\nBY THE PRESIDENT OF THE PHILIPPINES\n[ EXECUTIVE ORDER NO. 43, June 13, 1936 ]\nTRANSFERRING CERTAIN FUNCTIONS AND DUTIES OF THE BUREAU OF SCIENCE TO OTHER\nENTITIES UNDER THE COMMONWEALTH OF THE PHILIPPINES\nWHEREAS, by virtue of the provisions of Commonwealth Act Numbered Five, a Government Survey Board\nhas been created for the purpose of recommending to the President needed reforms in the present organization\nof the Government; and\nWHEREAS, the said Government Survey Board has recommended the transfer of certain functions, duties,\npersonnel, appropriations, books, records, equipment, supplies, lands, buildings, and other property of the\nBureau of Science to other entities under the Commonwealth of the Philippines;\nNOW, THEREFORE, by virtue of the powers vested in me by the Constitution and existing laws and in\npursuance of the provisions of Commonwealth Act Numbered Five, it is hereby directed that—\n1. The following functions and duties heretofore performed by the Bureau of Science shall be transferred\ntherefrom to the Government organizations designated herein:\n(a) The analysis and inspection of foods and drugs in connection with the enforcement of the Food and Drugs\nAct, the Nutrition Laboratory, the Division of Biological Products, and the Alabang Vaccine and Serum\nLaboratory, to the School of Hygiene and Public Health of the University of the Philippines;\n(b) The Iloilo Biological Research Laboratory and Cebu Biological Research Laboratory, to the Bureau of\n(c) The anti-rabic treatment service now being performed by the Bureau of Science, to the Philippine General\n(d) The manufacture of tiki-tiki extract, to the College of Pharmacy of the University of the Philippines. This\ntransfer should be effected as soon as proper arrangements can be conveniently made for the installation of the\ntiki-tiki plant in the College of Pharmacy; and\n(e) The Home Economics Division, to the Bureau of Plant Industry and Education, as the Budget Commission\nmay find appropriate."}}],"pack":"ph-p157"};
