  FT["PH-H16940"] = {"id":"PH-H16940","coverage":"full","language":"en","sourceName":"The LawPhil Project — Arellano Law Foundation","sourceUrl":"","fetchedAt":"2026-10-28","articleCount":1,"structureMode":"WHOLE","title":{"zh":null,"en":"BXBCUi,I~ 1p~BR :!~O.1:~2--:-","orig":"BXBCUi,I~ 1p~BR :!~O.1:~2--:-"},"level":"law","status":"active","docNumber":"Executive Order No. 45","issuingBody":"President of the Philippines","completenessNote":"全文，共 1 条；逐字取自 LawPhil PDF 文本化成果（第三方 OCR，非机翻），原始文件 EO_00045_1993.txt","textQuality":"ocr-vendor","sourceFile":"菲律宾/法律原文/07_行政命令_EO/EO_00045_1993.txt","country":"PH","countryName":"菲律宾","layer":"intl","articles":[{"id":"PH-H16940-A4","no":4,"noLabel":{"en":"SECTION 4"},"text":{"en":"immediately.\nPhilippines,\n5th day of, January,\nin the year of our\ni andj,Ninet~:\n;\n!\n,\n\"'\"'\n,.\n~\n\\\n,\n,\"\n~\n11\n10\n\"\n!\n\"\n;\",\n,\n.,\n!\n1::\n{;\n:;\nPresidential"}}],"pack":"ph-p157"};
  FT["PH-H16941"] = {"id":"PH-H16941","coverage":"full","language":"en","sourceName":"The LawPhil Project — Arellano Law Foundation","sourceUrl":"","fetchedAt":"2026-10-28","articleCount":1,"structureMode":"WHOLE","title":{"zh":null,"en":"BY THE PRESIDENT OF THE PHILIPPINES EXECUTIVE ORDER NO.","orig":"BY THE PRESIDENT OF THE PHILIPPINES EXECUTIVE ORDER NO."},"level":"law","status":"active","docNumber":"Executive Order No. 45","issuingBody":"President of the Philippines","completenessNote":"全文，共 1 条；逐字取自 LawPhil PDF 文本化成果（第三方 OCR，非机翻），原始文件 EO_00045_1998.txt","textQuality":"ocr-vendor","sourceFile":"菲律宾/法律原文/07_行政命令_EO/EO_00045_1998.txt","country":"PH","countryName":"菲律宾","layer":"intl","articles":[{"id":"PH-H16941-A1","no":1,"noLabel":{"en":"SECTION 1"},"text":{"en":"CREATION\nOF TASK FORCE. -There\nis hereby created a\nPresidential Anti-Smuggling Task Force, hereinafter called the \"Task Force,\" under the\ncontrol and supervision of the Office of the President principally to combat smuggling,\nunlawful importations and other frauds upon customs committed in large scale or by\norganized and syndicated groups.\nCOMPOSITION.\n-The Task Force shall be composed of senior\nfrom the following agencies: The Office of the President, the Department of\nFinance, the Department of Justice, the Bureau of Customs, the Bureau of Internal\nRevenue, the Economic Intelligence and Investigation Bureau, the National Bureau of\nInvestigation, the Philippine National Police and the Intelligence Service of the Armed\nForces of the Philippines.\n...\"\nrrauaulent practIces against customs laws is one of the urgent concerns of the\nadministration;\n\n\" \" \" The. Task F 9:rce. shall be headed by a qualified senior law enforcement officer to\n\"be \"designated by the President.\" He shall be assisted\" by a: deputy who shall-likewise be\ndesignated by the President.\nPOWERS AND FUNCTIONS. -The Task Force shall have the\n.\nfollowing powers and functions:\nTo prepare and implement appropriate and effective measures to prevent and\nsuppress large-scale smuggling and other prohibited and unlawful\nimportations;\n2. To effect searches and seizures conformably with the provisions of the Tariff\nand Customs Code, as amended, and to cause or direct the immediate arrest,\ninvestigation and speedy prosecution of smugglers and illegal importers;\n3.\nTo conduct intelligence and counter-intelligence on smuggling and other\nunlawful importations, including the monitoring of situations, circumstances,\nactivities of individuals, groups and entities who are involved\nreasonably believed to be involved in smuggling activities;\n4. To select and recruit personnel from within the PNP and other law\nenforcement agencies for assignment to the Task Force with the conformity of\nthe office or agency concerned;\n5. To enlist the assistance of any department, bureau, office or agency or\ninstrumentality of the government, including government-owned or controlled\ncorporations to carry out its functions, including the use of their respective\npersonnel, facilities and resources;\n6. To perform such functions and carry out such activities as may be directed by\nthe President.\nOFFENSES COVERED. -\nauthority to take cognizance of the following crimes:\nTask Force shall have the\na) Smuggling and customs frauds committed by organized or syndicated groups\nor criminal enterprises.\nb) Smuggling and other false and fraudulent importations or violations of\ncustoms laws committed in large scale.\nc) Such other cases of violations of the Tariff and Customs Code, as amended, as\nthe President may determine from time to time.\n\nand other customs frauds and violations of customs laws shall be\ndeemed committed by: a syndicate i(cacried out by ~ .group of three (3:) or. more. pers:ons\nconspiring or confederating with or mutually helping one another in carrying out the\ncriminal acts. They shall be deemed committed in large scale if committed in connivance\nwith officials and employees of the Bureau of Customs or where the determinable value\nof importations exceeds PI Million.\nORGANIZATIONAL\nSUPPORT. -The\nTask Force shall\norganize technical, administrative and special staffs composed of personnel assigned or\ndetailed to the Task Force by the different agencies called to assist the Task Force. The\nhead of the Task Force shall delineate the respective responsibilities of the supporting\nSPECIAL TEAM OF PROSECUTORS. -To\nassist the Task\nForce in the expeditious prosecution of criminal and other cases involving syndicated and\nlarge scale smuggling and customs frauds, a Special Team of Prosecutors from the\nDepartment of Justice shall be assigned to the Task Force. The team shall have the\nfollowing powers and duties:\nTo evaluate evidence gathered by the Task Force and to determine whether or\nnot violations of the Tariff Code or Customs Code, as amended, and other\nrelated laws and regulations have been committed;\n12.\nTo initiate and conduct preliminary investigations and to file and prosecute\nthe appropriate administrative and criminal charges against person(s)\nresponsible for the violation of customs law;\n.\n3\nTo recommend the issuance of warrant of seizure and detention in appropriate\nThe Special Team of Prosecutors may be assisted by lawyers selected andrecruite\nby the Task Force from the National Bureau of Inves,tigation, the Bureau of\nCustoms and the Economic Intelligence and Investigation Bureau.\nSPECIAL POOL OF HEARING OFFICERS. -A Special Pool\nof Hearing Officers in the Bureau of Customs under the Deputy Commissioner for\nRevenue Collection and Monitoring Group is hereby created to specifically attend to or\nhear seizure cases arising from unlawful importations and violations of customs laws\nbeing investigated by the Task Force.\nIn addition to the powers granted under the Tariff and Customs Code, as amended\nand under customs rules and regulations issued pursuant thereto, the Hearing Officers\nshall have the authority to summon witnesses, administer oaths, or take testimony or\nevidence relevant to the investigation by subpoena ad testificandum and subpoena duces\n\n-\ntecum, to rule on motions and issues presented during the proceedings and to do such\nother acts necessary and incidental to the discharge of their functions.\n,\nThe Special Pool of Hearing Officers shall be composed of at least six (6)\nmembers to be selected from the various legal units of the Bureau of Customs.\nSUMMARY PROCEEDINGS. -The\nseizure proceedings shall\nbe terminated within a period of thirty (30) days from the date of commencement of\nhearing. Subject to the essential requirement of due process, the technicalities of law and\nprocedure and the rules governing the admissibilty and sufficiency of evidence obtaining\nin courts of law shall not strictly apply.\nThe decision on seizure proceedings shall be rendered by the Collector of\nCustoms within five (5) days from termination of the formal hearing.\nNon-compliance with the mandatory period for termination of the proceedings\nand rendition of decision shall subject the responsible officials to suspension or dismissal\nfrom the service as the circumstances shall warrant.\nAUTHORIZATIONS. -The Commissioner of Customs shall, if\nnecessary, issue such authorizations and orders required under the Tariff and Customs\nCode, as amended, for all purposes relevant to the exercise and performance of the\npowers and functions of the Task Force.\nFUNDING. -Subject to the usual audit, the Task Force shall be\nprovided with an initial annual allocation of ~\nMILLICN PF.sa> to be drawn from the\nPresident's Contingency Fund and from the government's savings.\nThereafter,\nappropriations for the succeeding years shall be incorporated in the budget proposal of\nthe Office of the President.\nOPERATING GUIDELINES.\nTask Force shall adopt, in\ncoordination with customs law enforcement agencies, such operating guidelines as may\nbe necessary to implement this Executive Order, subject to the approval of the President.\nIt shall submit to the President reports of its activities with appropriate recommendations\nfor the information and guidance of the President.\nCOORDINATING INSTRUCTIONS. -The\nobjective of this\nissuance is to focus and maximize the impact on organized and large-scale smuggling and\nrelated crimes to be addressed by the Task Force operating directly under the Office of\nthe President, while the Philippine National Police shall continue to be the primary\ngeneral law enforcement agency of the country pursuant to Republic Act No. 6875, as\namended. Accordingly, close coordination and cooperation shall be undertaken by the\nhead of the Task Force, the Chief of the PNP and other heads of customs law\nenforcement agencies, to insure effective and efficient prosecution of the anti-smuggling\n\nA1Y orders, issuallce~, rules and\nregulations, or parts thereof which are inconsistent with this Executive Order are hereby\nrepealed or modified accordingly.\nimmediately.\nEFFECTIVITY.\nThis Executive Order shall take effect\nDONE in the City of Manila, this\nOur Lord, Nineteen Hundred and Ninety-Eight.\nin the year of\n(===7-\nBy the President:\nRONALDO B. ZAMORA\nExecutive Secretary\n# 002028\n..\npr~1S LIBRARY.\n..-"}}],"pack":"ph-p157"};
  FT["PH-H16942"] = {"id":"PH-H16942","coverage":"full","language":"en","sourceName":"The LawPhil Project — Arellano Law Foundation","sourceUrl":"","fetchedAt":"2026-10-28","articleCount":8,"structureMode":"ARTICLE","title":{"zh":null,"en":"MALACANANG EXECUTIVE ORDER NO.","orig":"MALACANANG EXECUTIVE ORDER NO."},"level":"law","status":"active","docNumber":"Executive Order No. 45","issuingBody":"President of the Philippines","completenessNote":"全文，共 8 条；逐字取自 LawPhil PDF 文本化成果（第三方 OCR，非机翻），原始文件 EO_00045_2001.txt","textQuality":"ocr-vendor","sourceFile":"菲律宾/法律原文/07_行政命令_EO/EO_00045_2001.txt","country":"PH","countryName":"菲律宾","layer":"intl","articles":[{"id":"PH-H16942-A5","no":5,"noLabel":{"en":"SECTION 5"},"text":{"en":"Affidavit In Lieu of Certification, Clearance or Pennit.-\nWhere the responsible officer of the agencies concerned fails or refuses to\ndispose of the application\nthe period prescribed\napplicant may, unless expressly prohibited\nby law, submit an affidavit,\nsupporting\nindividuals,\nin lieu of the certification, clearance or permit."}},{"id":"PH-H16942-A6","no":6,"noLabel":{"en":"SECTION 6"},"text":{"en":"Time Periods.- The local government unit concerned\nand each of the officers and agencies listed below shall dispose of an\napplication\nfor housing-related\ncertification,\nclearance or permit within\nthe periods prescribed below:\nHousing and Land Use Regulatory Board (HLURB)\nHLURB Regional Director\nor the local zoning\nappropriate,\napplications\nCertification\nof Site Zoning Classification\nsubject of the application: Ten (10) days from receipt of\ncomplete application.\nThe HLURB Regional\nfor applications\nCertificate\nof Registration and License to Sell (L TS):\nTen (10) days from receipt of complete application and\ncomp.liance with the publication requirement.\nDepartmen t of Agrarian Reform\nDAR~: ..Secretary\napplications\nfor Conversion Order or Exemption Order\nunder Department of Justice Opinion No. 44, series of\n1990:\nof complete\napplication,\nincluding the DA Certificate of Eligibility\nReclassification\nof Agricultural\nHLURB Certification of Site Zoning Classification of the\nland subject of the application.\nMunicipal Agrarian Reform Officer (MARO)\napplications\nCertification:\ncomplete application.\n1)\n(2)\nCenter on Land Use Planning and Policy (CLUPP I) or\nRegional CLUPP I\nCLUPP I or the Regional CLUPP I, where\nappropriate:\n(3D) days from receipt of\ncomplete application.\n3\n\nDepartment of Environment and Natural Resources (DENR)\napplications\nfor Environmental\nCompliance Certificate\n(ECC): Forty five (45) days from receipt of complete\napplication.\napplications\nfor National\nIntegrated\nProtected Area\n(NIPAS) Certification\nproject area is within or outside the NIPAS: Fifteen (15)\ndays from receipt of complete application.\nThe DENR Assistant Regional Executive Director\nOperations\napplications\nverification\nof Survey Returns:\nreceipt of complete application.\nMines and Geosciences Bureau (MGB)\nMGB Director for applications\nfor approval\nEngineering\nGeological\nAssessment Report (EGGAR): Ten (10) days from\nreceipt of EGGAR.\n(2)\nLaguna Lake Development Authority (LLDA)\nLLDA Administrator\nfor applications\nissuance of LLDA Certification\nstating whether\nthe project area is within or outside the LLDA\narea:~~Fifteen (IS) days from receipt of complete\napplication.\nDepartment of Agriculture\nDA Secretary or Regional Director for applications\nfor Certification\nof Eligibility\nfor Reclassification\nAgricultural\nLand stating,\namong others,\nproject area is not covered by Strategic Agricultural\nDevelopment\n(SAFDZ) and/or\nNetwork of Protected Areas for Agricultural\nIndustrial\nDevelopment (NPAAAD): Thirty\napplication,\nClearance Certifications\nfrom NIA and PCA or SRA,\nwhere required.\n'-\n(1)\nNational Irrigation Administration\nNIA Regional Manager for applications\nIrrigation\nClearance Certification:\ndays from receipt of complete application.\n4\n\n(2)\nPhilippine Coconut Authority (PCA)\nPCA Administrator\nfor applications\nClearance Certification:\nFifteen (15) days from\nreceipt of complete application.\n(3)\nSugar Regulatory Administration\nSRA Administrator\nfor applications\nClearance Certification:\nFifteen (15) days from\nreceipt of complete application.\nLocal Government Units\n(30) days from receipt of complete application to\nissue Development Permits"}},{"id":"PH-H16942-A7","no":7,"noLabel":{"en":"SECTION 7"},"text":{"en":"Sanctions.-In\ncase the responsible officers of the\nagencies concerned fail or refuse to dispose of the application within the\nperiods prescribed above, said officers shall, in accordance with civil\nservice laws, rules and regulations\nincluding Civil Service Commission\nResolution No. 99-1936, be liable for administrative\nsanctions as may be\nprovided in the implementing\nrules and regulations\nof this Executive"}},{"id":"PH-H16942-A8","no":8,"noLabel":{"en":"SECTION 8"},"text":{"en":"Implementing Rules and Regulations.-Within\n(30) days from issuance of this Executive Order, the Chairman\n...,\nDevelopment\nCoordinating\nSecretaries of the Department\nof Agrarian Reform, the Department\nEnvironment\nand Natural Resources, and the Department of Agriculture\nshall issue the rules and regulations for the effective implementation\nfast-tracking\nimplementation\nof housing projects."}},{"id":"PH-H16942-A9","no":9,"noLabel":{"en":"SECTION 9"},"text":{"en":"Pending Applications.-\nWithin thirty (30) days from\nissuance of this Execu tive Order, the Department of Agrarian Reform, the\nDepartment of Environment and Natural Resources, and the Department\nof Agriculture\nshall complete the inventory of pending applications\nhousing-related\ncertifications,\nclearances or permits and submit a plan\nfor the prompt disposition of the same in the light of the objectives of this\nExecu tive Order.\n'-"}},{"id":"PH-H16942-A10","no":10,"noLabel":{"en":"SECTION 10"},"text":{"en":"Proposed Legislation.-Within\nthirty (30) days from\nissuance of this Executive Order, said agencies shall submit\nPresident a draft bill\nfor legislative measures to fast-track"}},{"id":"PH-H16942-A11","no":11,"noLabel":{"en":"SECTION 11"},"text":{"en":"Repealing Clause.-AII\nexecutive orders, rules, and\nregulations\ninconsistent\nwith any provision of this Executive Order shall\nbe deemed revoked, amended or modified accordingly."}},{"id":"PH-H16942-A12","no":12,"noLabel":{"en":"SECTION 12"},"text":{"en":"Effectivity.\nimmediately.\nExecu tive Order shall. take effect\nCity of Manila, October\n,2001.\n~ 7\nPMS LIBRARY"}}],"pack":"ph-p157"};
  FT["PH-H16943"] = {"id":"PH-H16943","coverage":"full","language":"en","sourceName":"The LawPhil Project — Arellano Law Foundation","sourceUrl":"","fetchedAt":"2026-10-28","articleCount":5,"structureMode":"ARTICLE","title":{"zh":null,"en":"MALA CANAN PALACE BY THE PRESIDENT OF THE PHILIPPINES EXECUTIVE ORDER NO.","orig":"MALA CANAN PALACE BY THE PRESIDENT OF THE PHILIPPINES EXECUTIVE ORDER NO."},"level":"law","status":"active","docNumber":"Executive Order No. 45","issuingBody":"President of the Philippines","completenessNote":"全文，共 5 条；逐字取自 LawPhil PDF 文本化成果（第三方 OCR，非机翻），原始文件 EO_00045_2011.txt","textQuality":"ocr-vendor","sourceFile":"菲律宾/法律原文/07_行政命令_EO/EO_00045_2011.txt","country":"PH","countryName":"菲律宾","layer":"intl","articles":[{"id":"PH-H16943-A1","no":1,"noLabel":{"en":"SECTION 1"},"text":{"en":"Designation of Competition Authority. The DOJ is hereby\ndesignated as the Competition Authority with the following duties and\nresponsibilities:\nInvestigate all cases involving violations of competition laws and\nprosecute violators to prevent, restrain and punish monopolization, cartels\nand co\"mbinations in restraint of trade;\n.\nEnforce competition policies and laws to protect consumers from abusive,\nfraudulent, or harmful corrupt business practices;\nSupervise competition in markets by ens Wing that prohibitions and\nrequirements of competition laws are adhered to, and to this end, call on\nother government agencies and/or entities for submission of reports and\nprovision for assistance;\nimplement measures to\npromote transparency and\naccountability in markets;\nPrepare, publish and disseminate studies and reports on competition to\ninform and guide the industry and consumers; and\nPromote international cooperation and strengthen\nPhilippine · trade\nrelations with other countries, economies, and institutions in trade\nagreements."}},{"id":"PH-H16943-A2","no":2,"noLabel":{"en":"SECTION 2"},"text":{"en":"Office for Competition. There is hereby created the Office\nfor Competition under the Office of the Secretary of Justice to carry out the duties\nand responsibilities set forth in Section 1. The Office shall be manned by such\nnumber of staff including legal and technical experts, consultants and resource\npersons to effectively and efficiently pursue its mandate. The Secretary of Justice\nshall designate the Chief/Head and members of the said Office.\n0Uitt oll!Jt ~mil1~111 o! I!Jt ~bilippin2g\n111111111111111111111111111111111111111111111111111111111111\n2"}},{"id":"PH-H16943-A3","no":3,"noLabel":{"en":"SECTION 3"},"text":{"en":"Funding. To carry out the provisions of this Order, initial\nfunds for the operations of the .office for Competition shall be .taken from the\navailable funds of the DOJ. Thereafter, such amount as may be deemed\nnecessary for the annual operations of said Office, shall be incorporated and\nincluded in the annual budgetary appropriations of the DOJ."}},{"id":"PH-H16943-A4","no":4,"noLabel":{"en":"SECTION 4"},"text":{"en":"Separability Clause. If any provision of this Executive Order\nis declared invalid or unconstitutional, the other provisions not affected thereby\nshall remain valid and subsisting."}},{"id":"PH-H16943-A5","no":5,"noLabel":{"en":"SECTION 5"},"text":{"en":"Repealing Clause. All orders, rules, regulations, and\nissuances, or part thereof, which are inconsistent with this Executive Order, are\nhereby repealed, amended, or modified accordingly.\nEffectivity. This Executive Order shall take effect\nimmediately upon publication in a newspaper of general circulation.\nDONE, in the City of Manila, this 9th day of\nof our Lord, Two Thousand Eleven.\n@flit20! tlj2 3:§r2.rib~nt o! tlj2\n111111111111111111111111111111111111111111\nCERTIFIED COPY:\nMA1H/.H-llTn M. DIM\nUIHECTOR IV\n.\n~\n,MAlACANANG RECORDS OFFICE,\n3"}}],"pack":"ph-p157"};
  FT["PH-H16944"] = {"id":"PH-H16944","coverage":"full","language":"en","sourceName":"The LawPhil Project — Arellano Law Foundation","sourceUrl":"","fetchedAt":"2026-10-28","articleCount":13,"structureMode":"ARTICLE","title":{"zh":null,"en":"MALACAÑAN PALACE BY THE PRESIDENT OF THE PHILIPPINES PROVIDING FOR THE REORGANIZATION OF THE FIELD OFFICES OF THE OFFICE OF CONSULAR AFFAIRS OF THE DEPARTMENT OF FOREIGN","orig":"MALACAÑAN PALACE BY THE PRESIDENT OF THE PHILIPPINES PROVIDING FOR THE REORGANIZATION OF THE FIELD OFFICES OF THE OFFICE OF CONSULAR AFFAIRS OF THE DEPARTMENT OF FOREIGN"},"level":"law","status":"active","docNumber":"Executive Order No. 45","issuingBody":"President of the Philippines","completenessNote":"全文，共 13 条；逐字取自 LawPhil PDF 文本化成果（第三方 OCR，非机翻），原始文件 EO_00045_2017.txt","textQuality":"ocr-vendor","sourceFile":"菲律宾/法律原文/07_行政命令_EO/EO_00045_2017.txt","country":"PH","countryName":"菲律宾","layer":"intl","articles":[{"id":"PH-H16944-A1","no":1,"noLabel":{"en":"SECTION 1"},"text":{"en":"DA Consular Offices. The Field Offices of the DFA-OCA shall be\nreorganized to form the DFA Consular Offices (DA COs). The DA COs shall perform the\nfollowing functions:\nTHE PRESIDENT OF THE PHILIPPINES\n\na. Issue passports to Filipino nationals;\nb. Provide authentication services;\nc. Issue verification for consular record documents and accept applications for delayed\nregistration of report of birth, marriage or death abroad and other civil registry\ndocuments in coordination with relevant Philippine Foreign Service Posts;\nd. Provide assistance-to-nationals (AT) services to Filipinos; and\ne. Perform such other functions as may be assigned by the DFA-OCA, in accordance\nwith existing laws, rules and regulations.\nAll DA COs shall be under the supervision of the Assistant Secretary for the DFA-OCA.\nEach DFA CO shall be headed by a Foreign Service Officer (FO), Foreign Service Staff Officer\n(FSSO), or other qualified competent personnel duly designated by the SFA."}},{"id":"PH-H16944-A2","no":2,"noLabel":{"en":"SECTION 2"},"text":{"en":"DFA Consular Offices. The current SOs and RCOs shall be renamed as\nDA COs. Each DFA CO shall be individually referred to as \"DA Consular Office [name of\ncity/municipality/location.\" The DA COs are as follows\n1. DFA CO NCR-East at Mandaluyong City;\n2. DA CO NCR-Central at Pasig City;\n3. DA CO NCR-West at Manila;\n4. DFA CO NCR-South at Muntinlupa City;\n5. DFA CO NCR-Northeast at Quezon City;\n6. DFA CO NCR-North at Novaliches;\n7. DA CO Angeles at Angeles City;\n8. DFA CO Bacolod at Bacolod City;\n9. DA CO Baguio at Baguio City;\n10. DFA CO Butuan at Butuan City;\n11. DA CO Cagayan de Oro at Cagayan de Oro City;\n12. DA CO Calasiao at Calasiao, Pangasinan;\n13. DFA CO Mandaue at Mandaue City, Cebu;\n14. DFA CO Cotabato at Cotabato City;\n15. DA CO Davao at Davao City;\n16. DFA CO Dumaguete at Dumaguete City;\n17. DFA CO General Santos at General Santos City;\n18. DFA CO Iloilo at Iloilo City;\n19. DA CO La Union at San Fernando City, La Union;\n20. DFA CO Legazpi at Legazpi City;\n21. DFA CO Lipa at Lipa City;\n22 DFA CO Lucena at Lucena City;\n23. DA CO Pampanga at San Fernando City, Pampanga;\n24. DA CO Puerto Princesa at Puerto Princesa City;\n25. DFA CO Tacloban at Tacloban City;\n26. DFA CO Tuguegarao at Tuguegarao City; and\n27. DFA CO Zamboanga at Zamboanga City."}},{"id":"PH-H16944-A3","no":3,"noLabel":{"en":"SECTION 3"},"text":{"en":"Additional DA Consular Offices. Other DA COs may be subsequently\ncreated, provided all the following criteria are met:\n\na. When the projected number of clientele of the proposed DA CO is seventy-five\nthousand (75,000) or more, if outside NCR, or three hundred thousand (300,000) or\nmore, if within NCR, in any given year;\nb. When the projected number of passports, authenticated documents or consular\nrecords to be accepted, issued and released annually by the proposed DA CO for\nthe first year is one hundred thousand (100,000) or more; and\nc. When the projected amount of consular collection of the proposed DA CO is at least\nseventy-one million two hundred fifty thousand Philippine pesos (PhP71,250,000.00)\nin any given year.\nThe SFA may propose the establishment of additional COs by submitting a cost-benefit\nanalysis to the Department of Budget and Management (DBM) for review and recommendation\nto the Office of the President. The opening of more DA COs shall be subject to the approval of\nthe President and the availability of funds, as recommended by the DBM. The creation of DFA\nCOs that do not strictly comply with the above stated criteria may nonetheless be approved,\nprovided that the DA submits sufficient justification with the concurrence of the DBM"}},{"id":"PH-H16944-A4","no":4,"noLabel":{"en":"SECTION 4"},"text":{"en":"Closure of Existing DA Consular Offices. The SFA is authorized to close\nexisting DA COs whenever any of the following circumstances is present:\na. When the demand for consular services from the DA CO becomes chronically low or\nhas experienced a fifty percent (50%) decline over the last five (5) years;\nb. When a newly opened DA CO in a nearby city or province can adequately serve the\nclients of the existing office;\nc. Whenever warranted by the prevailing circumstances in the area where the existing\nDA CO is located, for security reasons, or due to natural or man-made calamities; or\nd. Other analogous circumstances that warrant closure of the office.\nThe SFA shall give written notice to the DBM and the Office of the President within thirty\n(30) days from the closure of any existing DA CO."}},{"id":"PH-H16944-A5","no":5,"noLabel":{"en":"SECTION 5"},"text":{"en":"Personnel. Home-based plantilla positions for the DA COs shall be created\nin coordination with the DBM."}},{"id":"PH-H16944-A6","no":6,"noLabel":{"en":"SECTION 6"},"text":{"en":"Housing Benefits of Heads of DA Consular Offices. Heads of DA COs\nwho are assigned or transferred to an area other than their domicile and do not have their own\nhouses or rooms in that area shall be provided with quarters at government expense, subject to\nthe limits prescribed by the DBM and other existing laws, rules and regulations, including National\nBudget Circular No. 456 (s. 1996).\nThose who prefer other dwelling areas shall pay the difference in case the prevailing rental\nin their chosen areas is higher than the ceiling prescribed by the DBM and other existing laws,\nrules and regulations.\n\nWhen there are existing government-owned/leased residential quarters at the time and in\nthe place of assignment, the Head of the DA CO may opt to stay in other preferred dwelling\nareas but at his/her own expense."}},{"id":"PH-H16944-A7","no":7,"noLabel":{"en":"SECTION 7"},"text":{"en":"Transport of Personal Effects at Government Expense. The Heads of\nDA COs covered by the preceding section shall be entitled to bring, by any available means of\ntransportation, such personal effects as may be considered necessary in the performance of\nofficial duties, not to exceed 500 kilograms, at the expense of the DA. Any excess shall be for\nthe personal account of the concerned Head of the DA CO."}},{"id":"PH-H16944-A8","no":8,"noLabel":{"en":"SECTION 8"},"text":{"en":"Representation and Transportation Allowances. All Heads of DA COs\nshall be entitled to monthly commutable representation and transportation allowances which shall\nnot exceed the ceiling provided in relevant laws, rules and regulations."}},{"id":"PH-H16944-A9","no":9,"noLabel":{"en":"SECTION 9"},"text":{"en":"Funding Source. All expenditures of DA COs shall be chargeable to the\nannual appropriations of the DA and the Passport Revolving Fund created under RA No. 8239.\nIn case of insufficiency of funds, such amount needed for the creation of new positions\nmay be charged against the Miscellaneous Personnel Benefits Fund. Thereafter, such amount\nneeded shall be included in the budget of the DA under the General Appropriations Act."}},{"id":"PH-H16944-A10","no":10,"noLabel":{"en":"SECTION 10"},"text":{"en":"Implementing. Rules and Regulations. The SFA may issue such rules\nand regulations as may be necessary to implement this Order; provided, that all provisions and\nguidelines that have organizational, staffing and financial implications shall properly be\ncoordinated with the DBM."}},{"id":"PH-H16944-A11","no":11,"noLabel":{"en":"SECTION 11"},"text":{"en":"Repeal. All issuances, orders, rules, and regulations or parts thereof, which\nare inconsistent with any of the provisions of this Order, are hereby repealed or modified\naccordingly."}},{"id":"PH-H16944-A12","no":12,"noLabel":{"en":"SECTION 12"},"text":{"en":"Separability. Should any provision of this Order be declared invalid or\nunconstitutional, the other provisions unaffected thereby shall remain valid and subsisting."}},{"id":"PH-H16944-A13","no":13,"noLabel":{"en":"SECTION 13"},"text":{"en":"Effectivity. This Executive Order shall take effect fifteen (15) days after\npublication in a newspaper of general circulation.\nDone in the City of Manila this 20th day of\nTwo Thousand and Seventeen.\nin the year of our Lord,\nBy the President:\n81.\nSALVADOR C. MEDIALDEA\nExecutive Secretary\nREPUBIIC OF THE PHILIPPINES\nOffice of the President\nMALACAÑANG RECORDS OFFICE\nCERTITED COPY\nATTY. CONCEPCION ZENY E. FERROLINO-ENAD\n$10-24-207 DIRECTOR III - ACTING HEAD"}}],"pack":"ph-p157"};
  FT["PH-H16945"] = {"id":"PH-H16945","coverage":"full","language":"en","sourceName":"The LawPhil Project — Arellano Law Foundation","sourceUrl":"","fetchedAt":"2026-10-28","articleCount":4,"structureMode":"ARTICLE","title":{"zh":null,"en":"MALACANAN PALACE BY THE PRESIDENT OF THE PHILIPPINES TRANSFERRING THE ATTACHMENT OF THE DEVELOPMENT ACADEMY OF THE PHILIPPINES TO THE NATIONAL ECONOMIC AND DEVELOPMENT AUTHORITY","orig":"MALACANAN PALACE BY THE PRESIDENT OF THE PHILIPPINES TRANSFERRING THE ATTACHMENT OF THE DEVELOPMENT ACADEMY OF THE PHILIPPINES TO THE NATIONAL ECONOMIC AND DEVELOPMENT AUTHORITY"},"level":"law","status":"active","docNumber":"Executive Order No. 45","issuingBody":"President of the Philippines","completenessNote":"全文，共 4 条；逐字取自 LawPhil PDF 文本化成果（第三方 OCR，非机翻），原始文件 EO_00045_2023.txt","textQuality":"ocr-vendor","sourceFile":"菲律宾/法律原文/07_行政命令_EO/EO_00045_2023.txt","country":"PH","countryName":"菲律宾","layer":"intl","articles":[{"id":"PH-H16945-A1","no":1,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 1"},"text":{"en":"Attachment. The DAP is hereby attached to the NEDA for policy\nand program coordination."}},{"id":"PH-H16945-A2","no":2,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 2"},"text":{"en":"Separability. If any part or provision of this Order shall be held\ninvalid, or unconstitutional, the provisions not affected thereby shall remain in full force"}},{"id":"PH-H16945-A3","no":3,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 3"},"text":{"en":"Repeal. All orders, rules and regulations, and other issuances or\nparts thereof which are inconsistent with the provisions of this Order are hereby\nrepealed or modified accordingly."}},{"id":"PH-H16945-A4","no":4,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 4"},"text":{"en":"Effectivity. This Order shall take effect immediately upon publication\nin the Official Gazette or in a newspaper of general circulation.\nDONE, in the City of Manila, this 25 *ay of October, in the year of our Lord,\nTwo Thousand and Twenty-Three.\nBy the President:\nLUCAS P. BERSAMIN\nExecutive Secretary\nREPUBLIC OF THE PHILIPPINES\n2\nOffice of the President\nMALACANANG RECORDS OFFICE\nATTY. CONCEPCION ZEN/ E. PETROLINO-ENAD\n10-26 -2023 DIRECTOR IV"}}],"pack":"ph-p157"};
  FT["PH-H16946"] = {"id":"PH-H16946","coverage":"full","language":"en","sourceName":"The LawPhil Project — Arellano Law Foundation","sourceUrl":"","fetchedAt":"2026-10-28","articleCount":1,"structureMode":"WHOLE","title":{"zh":null,"en":"THE GOVERNMENT OF THE PHILIPPINE ISLANDS, EXECUTIVE BUREAU. MANILA, June 26, 1913. EXECUTIVE ORDER \\","orig":"THE GOVERNMENT OF THE PHILIPPINE ISLANDS, EXECUTIVE BUREAU. MANILA, June 26, 1913. EXECUTIVE ORDER \\"},"level":"law","status":"active","docNumber":"Executive Order No. 46","issuingBody":"President of the Philippines","completenessNote":"全文，共 1 条；逐字取自 LawPhil PDF 文本化成果（第三方 OCR，非机翻），原始文件 EO_00046_1913.txt","textQuality":"ocr-vendor","sourceFile":"菲律宾/法律原文/07_行政命令_EO/EO_00046_1913.txt","country":"PH","countryName":"菲律宾","layer":"intl","articles":[{"id":"PH-H16946-A1","no":1,"noLabel":{},"text":{"en":"sale in the Philippine Islands than by export as herein pro-\nvided, said committee is hereby authorized to sell said drugs\nto responsible persons duly authorized by law to deal in such\ncommodities in the Philippine Islands.\nThe Opium Committee will make certified reports in trip-\nlicate of all drugs destroyed or otherwise disposed of by it,\nand one copy of each such report shall be delivered to the\nInsular Auditor, one to the Insular Collector of Customs, and\n- one to the Collector of Internal Revenue.\n\"Mr. Easthagen will serve as chairman and Mr. Brown\nas recorder of this committee.\"\nW. CAMERON FORBES,\nGovernor-General."}}],"pack":"ph-p157"};
  FT["PH-H16947"] = {"id":"PH-H16947","coverage":"full","language":"en","sourceName":"The LawPhil Project — Arellano Law Foundation","sourceUrl":"LawPhil (HTML full text only)  |  https://lawphil.net/executive/execord/eo1936/eo_46_1936.html","fetchedAt":"2026-10-28","articleCount":1,"structureMode":"WHOLE","title":{"zh":null,"en":"Designation of Officers and Employees Who May Be Granted Deferment of Their Trainee Instruction for a Period Not to Exceed Three Years.","orig":"Designation of Officers and Employees Who May Be Granted Deferment of Their Trainee Instruction for a Period Not to Exceed Three Years."},"level":"law","status":"active","docNumber":"Executive Order No. 46","issuingBody":"President of the Philippines","promulgatedDate":"1936-07-07","completenessNote":"全文，共 1 条；逐字取自 LawPhil PDF 文本化成果（第三方 OCR，非机翻），原始文件 EO_00046_1936_html.txt","textQuality":"ocr-vendor","sourceFile":"菲律宾/法律原文/07_行政命令_EO/EO_00046_1936_html.txt","country":"PH","countryName":"菲律宾","layer":"intl","articles":[{"id":"PH-H16947-A1","no":1,"noLabel":{},"text":{"en":"MALACAÑAN PALACE\nBY THE PRESIDENT OF THE PHILIPPINES\n[ EXECUTIVE ORDER NO. 46, July 07, 1936 ]\nDESIGNATION OF OFFICERS AND EMPLOYEES WHO MAY BE GRANTED DEFERMENT OF\nTHEIR TRAINEE INSTRUCTION FOR A PERIOD NOT TO EXCEED THREE YEARS\nUpon the recommendation of the Chief of Staff, Army of the Philippines, and pursuant to the provisions of\nsection sixty-four (a) of Commonwealth Act Numbered One, I hereby designate the following officers and\nemployees who may be granted deferment of their trainee instruction for not to exceed three years:\nMunicipal treasurers, school teachers, postmasters, telegraph operators, weather observers, and such other\nofficers and employees of the Insular, provincial, municipal, and municipal district governments who may\npresent certificates from their respective bureau chiefs to the acceptance boards to the effect that they cannot\nbe relieved without detriment to the service.\nDone at the City of Manila, this seventh day of July, in the year of Our Lord, nineteen hundred and thirty-six,\nand of the Commonwealth of the Philippines, the first.\nMANUEL L. QUEZON\nPresident of the Philippines\nBy the President:\nELPIDIO QUIRINO\nSecretary of the Interior"}}],"pack":"ph-p157"};
  FT["PH-H16948"] = {"id":"PH-H16948","coverage":"full","language":"en","sourceName":"The LawPhil Project — Arellano Law Foundation","sourceUrl":"","fetchedAt":"2026-10-28","articleCount":1,"structureMode":"WHOLE","title":{"zh":null,"en":"•MALACAÑAN PALACE BY THE PRESIDENT OF THE PHILIPPINES AMENDING EXECUTIVE ORDER NUMBERED TWENTY-FIVE, ENTITLED PROMULGATING RULES AND REGULATIONS CONCERNING CUR- , BOOKS AND ACCOUNTS OF BANKS AND THEIR BRANCHES AND AGENCIES IN TIE PROVINCES, PROVINCIAL, CITY AND MUNICIPAL TREASURIES AND OTHER GOVERNENT ACCOUNTABLE OFFICERS AND DEBT MORATORIUM. I","orig":"•MALACAÑAN PALACE BY THE PRESIDENT OF THE PHILIPPINES AMENDING EXECUTIVE ORDER NUMBERED TWENTY-FIVE, ENTITLED PROMULGATING RULES AND REGULATIONS CONCERNING CUR- , BOOKS AND ACCOUNTS OF BANKS AND THEIR BRANCHES AND AGENCIES IN TIE PROVINCES, PROVINCIAL, CITY AND MUNICIPAL TREASURIES AND OTHER GOVERNENT ACCOUNTABLE OFFICERS AND DEBT MORATORIUM. I"},"level":"law","status":"active","docNumber":"Executive Order No. 46","issuingBody":"President of the Philippines","completenessNote":"全文，共 1 条；逐字取自 LawPhil PDF 文本化成果（第三方 OCR，非机翻），原始文件 EO_00046_1945.txt","textQuality":"ocr-vendor","sourceFile":"菲律宾/法律原文/07_行政命令_EO/EO_00046_1945.txt","country":"PH","countryName":"菲律宾","layer":"intl","articles":[{"id":"PH-H16948-A1","no":1,"noLabel":{},"text":{"en":"2\na given province more emergency currencies were in\ncirculation than the amount actually authorized to\nbe issued, the Committee will recommend what action\nshall be taken: Provided, however, That counterfeit\nemergency currencies will not be redeemed.\"\nDone in the city of Manila, this 6th day of June, in\nthe year of our Lord, nineteen hundred and forty-five, and\nof the Commonwealth of the Philippines, the tenth.\nPresident offthe Philippines\nBy the President:\nSecretary to the President"}}],"pack":"ph-p157"};
