  FT["PH-H17064"] = {"id":"PH-H17064","coverage":"full","language":"en","sourceName":"The LawPhil Project — Arellano Law Foundation","sourceUrl":"","fetchedAt":"2026-10-28","articleCount":8,"structureMode":"ARTICLE","title":{"zh":null,"en":"CREATING A SPECIAL HEARING DIVISION AND A TEAM OF PROSECUTORS IN THE BUREAU OF CUSTOMS TO EXPEDITE SEIZURE PROCEEDINGS AND PROSECUTE OFFENDERS","orig":"CREATING A SPECIAL HEARING DIVISION AND A TEAM OF PROSECUTORS IN THE BUREAU OF CUSTOMS TO EXPEDITE SEIZURE PROCEEDINGS AND PROSECUTE OFFENDERS"},"level":"law","status":"active","docNumber":"Executive Order No. 57","issuingBody":"President of the Philippines","completenessNote":"全文，共 8 条；逐字取自 LawPhil PDF 文本化成果（第三方 OCR，非机翻），原始文件 EO_00057_1999.txt","textQuality":"ocr-vendor","sourceFile":"菲律宾/法律原文/07_行政命令_EO/EO_00057_1999.txt","country":"PH","countryName":"菲律宾","layer":"intl","articles":[{"id":"PH-H17064-A1","no":1,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 1"},"text":{"en":"Declaration\nIt shall be the policy of the state to\nprotect and develop the national economy and general welfare by increasing the\ncollection of government revenues, particularly\nimport 9uties and taxes, and\nthe suppression of all forms of fraudulent\npractices and other violations of the\nTariff and Customs Code and other laws being enforced by the Bureau of"}},{"id":"PH-H17064-A2","no":2,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 2"},"text":{"en":"Prosecutors.\nThe Special\nand Special\nIn order to carty out the foregoing policy, a Special Hearing Division\nCommissioner\nfor Revenue Collection\nMonitoring is hereby created with the following objectives:\nTo institute\nproceedings,\nparticularly,\nwhen they involve sensitive articles,\nthe appraised\nof the seized articles\n.,;.,,~\n.~\"\n1\\1~lmlll\\\\II\\lllm~1\nPJEEHOIOQ\"m'264°A-\n\n2,: J-G.establishand m~~nthe-l~g~ity.at:ld\n:iI!tegri~.of the- ~izur~\nproceedings: and\n'A Special Team of Prosecutors under the Deputy Commissioner for\nIntelligence\nand Enforcement\nGroup is likewise created with the\nfollowing objectives:\n1\n-\nTo act as legal consultants to the Presidential Task Force\nAgain~t Smuggling;\n2.\nTo evaluate evidence gathered by the task force and make a\ndetermination\nof whether or not an infringement\nof the Tariff\nand Customs Code or related laws and regulation\n3.\nTo recommend\nfor the issuance\nof Seizure and\nin appropriate\ncases and coordinate\nprosecuting\narms (of the government\nin filing the appropriate\nadministrative\nand criminal charges against persons responsible\nfor the violation of the Tariff and Customs Code or other laws\nimplemented/ enforced by the Bureau of Customs.\n,"}},{"id":"PH-H17064-A3","no":3,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 3"},"text":{"en":"Powers. Functions\nand ResRQnsibilities\nThe Special Hearing Division shall have the following powers and\n1.\nTo call the parties\nto a pre-trial\nconference\nto enter into\nstipulations\nof facts and determine the issues involved in the\ncontroversy;\n2.\nTo rule on motions\nmade by either or both parties\nproceedings;\n3.\nTo issue interlocutory orders and subpoena duces tecum and\nsubpoena ad testificandum;\n4.\nTo conduct expeditious, and if\"warranted,\nmarathon hearings,\nthe period of which shall not exceed thirty (30) days;\n5.\nTo recommend to the Collector of Customs a decision within\nten (10) days from the completion or termination of the formal\nhearing. which decision shall be submitted to the Collector of\nCustoms concerned for his signature;.\n6.\nIf the hearing officer deems it unnecessary to conduct a full\ntrial on the controversy, he may require ~he parties to submit\ntheir memoranda within a period of five (5) days and he shall\n2\n\na deci$ibnto\nthe Collectorof\"Customs\n'.\n..'\n,.\n(10) days frorp the submission\nof the pleadings.\nextension of time to submit memoranda shall not be allowed\n\\\nand sh'all.be considered a prohibited motion.\n\\\nThe Special Team of Prosecutors shall likewise have the following\npowers and functions:\n1\nTo conduct preliminary\ninvestigation\nand issue the necessary\nsubpoenas to concerned persons who may be potential\nwitnesses in the Seizure Proceedings to be instituted\nthe articles or goods involved in the unlawful\nimportation\nexportation;\n2.\nwith the Legal Service, Bureau of Customs\nmatters involving appreciation\nand evaluation of evidences as\nwell as in the formulation\nof legal strategies to be used during\nthe actual hearing;\n3.\nTo recommend for the fIling of appropriate administrative\ncharges against those individuals\ninvolved in the\nunlawful importation."}},{"id":"PH-H17064-A4","no":4,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 4"},"text":{"en":"Comoosition\nand O:gerational Control\nThe Special Hearing Division shall be under the direct control of the\nDeputy Commissioner for Revenue Collection and Monitoring and\nshall be composed of at least six (6) members to be selected from the\nLaw Divisions of paM, NAJA and MICP upon the recommendation of\nthe respective Division Chiefs thereat.\nAll cases shall be assigned to each member on a rotation basis.\nThe Special Team of Prosecutors shall be directly under the Deputy\nCommissioner for Intelligence and Enforcement Group who shall be\ncomposed of as many members depending upon the volume of work\nand the discretion of the said Deputy Commissioner.\nThe (Special Team of Prosecutors) shall be selected from the\nlawyers presently assigned at the ESS, CISS and Legal Service.\nof the Necessary\nCPO's and Travel Order.\nresponsibility.\nCommissioner\nfor Internal\nAdministration\nGroup to issue the required CPO's and/or Travel Order to the\nmembers of both the Special Hearing Division and Special Team of Prosecutors\nsubject to approval of the Secretary of Finance in accordance with Executive\nOrder No.4 7 dated December 8. 1998.\n~\n3\nIIIIIIII~IIIIIIIIIII~~IIII\n! 2642\n\n.: \" Section .6... Rig~ts. and PrlVileies.\nIn view of-the sensitive.natute.-of\ntheir functions as herein before provided, the members of the Special Hearing\nDivision and Special Team of Prosecutors\nshall be entitled to'the\n..,\n.'\n,.\n..'.\n-\\\n.\nFree transportation\nand hotel accommodation\nin cases where the\nhearing is to be held outside Metro Manila;\nPer diems at the rate authorized under existing regulations;\nHazard Pay and a monthly allowance of f)5,OOO.OO to be drawn fromthe\nbudget appropriated for this purpose by the Bureau of Customs;"}},{"id":"PH-H17064-A7","no":7,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 7"},"text":{"en":"Adoption\nof Customs Administrative\nprovision of Customs Administrative\nis hereby adopted."}},{"id":"PH-H17064-A8","no":8,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 8"},"text":{"en":"ReDeal bI Modification.\nAny provision of administrative\norders, memorandum\norders or other issuances inconsistent\nhereby repealed or modified accordingly."}},{"id":"PH-H17064-A9","no":9,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 9"},"text":{"en":"Se~arabiUty Clause. If any provision of this Executive Order\nshall be held unconstitutional,\nthe other provisions shall not be affected."}},{"id":"PH-H17064-A10","no":10,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 10"},"text":{"en":"Effectivity.\nThis Executive Order shall take effect after\nfifteen (15) days following the completion\nof its publication\nin the Offic~al\nGazette or any newspaper of general circulation.\nDone in the City of Manila this.\nof Our Lord, Nineteen Hundred and Ninety-Nine.\n/-~-~\n\" \"~~\nPMS LIBRARY\nBy the President:\n~\nRAMON B. CARDENAS\nExecutive Secretary\ni\\\\iillillilllllllllllllll\\lllllll\\\nPM' LIBRARY BCOOEO04202\n4"}}],"pack":"ph-p157"};
  FT["PH-H17065"] = {"id":"PH-H17065","coverage":"full","language":"en","sourceName":"The LawPhil Project — Arellano Law Foundation","sourceUrl":"","fetchedAt":"2026-10-28","articleCount":7,"structureMode":"ARTICLE","title":{"zh":null,"en":"MALACAÑANG PMS LIBRARY BY THE PRESIDENT OF THE PHILIPPINES MN 10281 CREATING A CABINET COMMITTEE ON THE MUTUAL LOGISTICS SUPPORT AGREEMENT (MLSA)","orig":"MALACAÑANG PMS LIBRARY BY THE PRESIDENT OF THE PHILIPPINES MN 10281 CREATING A CABINET COMMITTEE ON THE MUTUAL LOGISTICS SUPPORT AGREEMENT (MLSA)"},"level":"law","status":"active","docNumber":"Executive Order No. 57","issuingBody":"President of the Philippines","completenessNote":"全文，共 7 条；逐字取自 LawPhil PDF 文本化成果（第三方 OCR，非机翻），原始文件 EO_00057_2001.txt","textQuality":"ocr-vendor","sourceFile":"菲律宾/法律原文/07_行政命令_EO/EO_00057_2001.txt","country":"PH","countryName":"菲律宾","layer":"intl","articles":[{"id":"PH-H17065-A1","no":1,"noLabel":{"en":"SECTION 1"},"text":{"en":"Creation of a Cabinet Committee on the RP-US Mutual\nLogistics Support Agreement (MLS). - A Cabinet Committee on the RP-US\nMLSA (CC-MLSA) is hereby constituted cor posed of the following:\nSecretary of National Defense\nSecretary of Foreign Affairs\nSecretary of Justice\n-\nPOMA Outgoing r 07045"}},{"id":"PH-H17065-A2","no":2,"noLabel":{"en":"SEC 2"},"text":{"en":"Functions and Responsibilities. - The Cabinet Committee on the\na. Oversee and provide direction in the formulation of the Philippine draft\nof the MLSA, taking into account pertinent constitutional provisions,\nthe country's commitments under existing mutual defense agreements\nand its obligations as member of the United Nations;\nb. Provide guidance and supervision to a Technical Working Group in the\ndiscussion of the MLSA with its US counterpart and the eventual\ndrafting of the MLSA;\nc. Review and submit the final draft of the MLSA to the President for\napproval not later than December 31, 2001;\nd. Undertake such other functions as may be necessary or as may be\ndirected by the President for the attainment of its mandate."}},{"id":"PH-H17065-A3","no":3,"noLabel":{"en":"SEC 3"},"text":{"en":"Technical Working Group. - To provide technical support to the\nCC-MLSA, there is hereby established a Technical Working Group (TWG) to be\ncomposed of a representative each from the Department of National Defense\n(DND), Department of Foreign Affairs (DA) and the Department of Justice\n(DOJ, with the DND representative as chairman. Each representative, to be\ndesignated by their respective departments heads, shall have the rank not lower\nthan an assistant secretary or his equivalent.\nThe TWG on the MLSA shall formulate the draft Philippine MLSA and\nundertake the discussions with the US panel towards arriving at a mutually\nacceptable MLSA. It shall perform such functions as the Cabinet Committee on\nthe MLSA may from time to time assign."}},{"id":"PH-H17065-A4","no":4,"noLabel":{"en":"SEC 4"},"text":{"en":"Administrative Support. - The Cabinet Committee and TWG on\nthe MLSA shall be provided with secretarial and administrative support from any\nof its member departments as the Cabinet Committee may designate."}},{"id":"PH-H17065-A5","no":5,"noLabel":{"en":"SEC 5"},"text":{"en":"Assistance From Other Government Entities. - All government\ndepartments, agencies and instrumentalities are hereby directed to extend full\nsupport and cooperation to the Cabinet Committee and the TWG on the RP-US\nMLSA and their secretariat and to grant them access to such information, data and\nrecords as are necessary for the fulfillment of their objectives."}},{"id":"PH-H17065-A6","no":6,"noLabel":{"en":"SEC 6"},"text":{"en":"Repealing Clause. - All issuances, orders, rules and regulations,\nor parts thereof which are inconsistent with the provisions of this Order are hereby\nrepealed or modified accordingly.\n21\nPOMA Outgoing * 07046"}},{"id":"PH-H17065-A7","no":7,"noLabel":{"en":"SEC 7"},"text":{"en":"Effectivity. - This Executive Order shall take effect immediately.\nDONE in the City of Manila this 3rd day of December- in the year of\nour Lord, two thousand and one.\nBy the President:\nALBERTO G. ROMULO\nExecutive Secretary\nPMS LIBRARY\nPOMA Outgoing * 07047\nPMS LIBRARY BCODE002101\n31"}}],"pack":"ph-p157"};
  FT["PH-H17066"] = {"id":"PH-H17066","coverage":"full","language":"en","sourceName":"The LawPhil Project — Arellano Law Foundation","sourceUrl":"","fetchedAt":"2026-10-28","articleCount":14,"structureMode":"ARTICLE","title":{"zh":null,"en":"MALACAÑAN PALACE BY THE PRESIDENT OF THE PHILIPPINES ESTABLISHING A NATIONAL COAST WATCH SYSTEM, PROVIDING FOR ITS STRUCTURE AND DEFINING THE ROLES AND RESPONSIBILITIES OF MEMBER AGENCIES IN PROVIDING COORDINATED INTER-AGENCY MARITIME SECURITY OPERATIONS AND FOR OTHER PURPOSES","orig":"MALACAÑAN PALACE BY THE PRESIDENT OF THE PHILIPPINES ESTABLISHING A NATIONAL COAST WATCH SYSTEM, PROVIDING FOR ITS STRUCTURE AND DEFINING THE ROLES AND RESPONSIBILITIES OF MEMBER AGENCIES IN PROVIDING COORDINATED INTER-AGENCY MARITIME SECURITY OPERATIONS AND FOR OTHER PURPOSES"},"level":"law","status":"active","docNumber":"Executive Order No. 57","issuingBody":"President of the Philippines","completenessNote":"全文，共 14 条；逐字取自 LawPhil PDF 文本化成果（第三方 OCR，非机翻），原始文件 EO_00057_2011.txt","textQuality":"ocr-vendor","sourceFile":"菲律宾/法律原文/07_行政命令_EO/EO_00057_2011.txt","country":"PH","countryName":"菲律宾","layer":"intl","articles":[{"id":"PH-H17066-A1","no":1,"noLabel":{"en":"SECTION 1"},"text":{"en":"Establishment of the National Coast Watch System. There is\nhereby established a National Coast Watch System (NCWS) as the central inter-agency\nmechanism for a coordinated and coherent approach on maritime issues and maritime\nsecurity operations towards enhancing governance in the country's maritime domain."}},{"id":"PH-H17066-A2","no":2,"noLabel":{"en":"SECTION 2"},"text":{"en":"Establishment of the National Coast Watch Council. There is\nhereby established a National Coast Watch Council, hereinafter referred to as the\n\"Council.\" which shall be composed of the following:\nChairperson\nExecutive Secretary\nSecretary of Transportation and Communications\nSecretary of National Defense\nSecretary of Foreign Affairs\nSecretary of the Interior and Local Government\nSecretary of Justice\nSecretary of Energy\nSecretary of Finance\nSecretary of Environment and Natural Resources\nSecretary of Agriculture\nThe Council shall meet at least twice every year, and at such other times as the\nChairperson may deem necessary or appropriate.\n2\nOffice ofthe President ofthe ?Chilippines"}},{"id":"PH-H17066-A3","no":3,"noLabel":{"en":"SECTION 3"},"text":{"en":"Powers and Functions of the Council. The Council shall be the\ncentral inter-agency body which shall be in charge of formulating strategic direction and\npolicy guidance for the NCWS. The Council shall further have the following powers and\nProvide strategic direction and policy guidelines for CVS maritime security\noperations, and multinational and cross-border cooperation on maritime security;\nConduct periodic review of maritime security operations and render periodic\nreports to the President and the National Security Council (NSC);\nRecommend to the President policies and procedures in managing and securing\nthe countrv's maritime domain, as well as the issuance of administrative rules\nand regulations to enhance maritime security in the Philippines;\nHarmonize capability plans and fund requirements relative to maritime security\nHarmonize and coordinate the roles and relationships of different government\nagencies, pursuant to their mandates, relative to the policy direction of maritime\nsecurity and governance framework as may be determined by the Council;\nConvene or dissolve, as the need arises, inter-agency committees and/or\nworking groups to assist the Council in the performance of its functions;\nExercise overall iurisdiction and direction over policy-formulation, implementation\nand coordination with other government agencies, experts and organizations,\nboth foreign and local, on all maritime issues affecting the country;\nEnlist and/or require the support and/or assistance of any department, bureau or\nagency of the government in the pursuit of its mandates and functions;\nPromulgate rules and regulations as may be necessary for the Council to perform\nits mandate under this Executive Order; and\nPerform such other functions as may be deemed necessary by the Chairperson\nfor the effective discharge of its mandate or as may be directed by the President."}},{"id":"PH-H17066-A4","no":4,"noLabel":{"en":"SECTION 4"},"text":{"en":"The Coast Watch Council Secretariat. The Coast Watch Council\nSecretariat. hereinafter referred to as the \"Secretariat.\" is hereby established to provide\ntechnical and administrative support to the Council. The Secretariat shall also have the\nfollowing functions:\nProvide consultative research and administrative services to the Council;\n@flice ofthp resident of the Philionines\n\nAssist the Council in proposing and reviewing legislative and administrative\nissuances on maritime security;\nAssist inter-agency committees and working groups created by the Council in the\nperformance of their respective mandates, including the provision of\nadministrative, technical and secretariat support; and\nPerform such other functions and tasks as the Council may direct.\nThe Secretariat shall be headed by an Executive Director, who shall be\nappointed by the Chairperson, upon the recommendation of the Council. The Council\nshall determine the personnel requirements of the Secretariat in accordance with\napplicable laws, rules and regulations."}},{"id":"PH-H17066-A5","no":5,"noLabel":{"en":"SECTION 5"},"text":{"en":"National Coast Watch Center. The National Coast Watch Center,\nhereinafter referred to as the \"Center,\" in accordance with the strategic direction and\npolicy guidance issued by the Council, shall implement and coordinate maritime security\noperations. It shall further have the following functions:\nGather, consolidate, synthesize and disseminate information relevant to maritime\nDevelop and maintain effective communications and information systems to\nenhance inter-agency coordination in maritime security operations;\nCoordinate the conduct of maritime surveillance or response operations upon the\nrequest of a member agency or when an exigency arises;\nPlan, coordinate, monitor, evaluate, document and report on the conduct of\nmaritime security operations;\nWhen so authorized by the Council, coordinate cross-border and multinational\nmaritime security cooperation;\nCoordinate support for the prosecution of apprehended violators;\nDevelop a common operating picture to enhance maritime situational awareness;\nConduct periodic assessments on maritime security;\nWhen so authorized by the Council, and in coordination with the Department of\nForeign Affairs, initiate cross-border and multinational maritime security\ncooperation; and\nPerform such other functions as may be directed by the Council.\n4\n@flice ofthe resident of the Chilivines\n\nThe Center shall be established in and headed by the Philippine Coast Guard"}},{"id":"PH-H17066-A6","no":6,"noLabel":{"en":"SECTION 6"},"text":{"en":"Support Agencies. Subject to such rules and regulations, which\nthe Council shall promulgate, the following agencies shall provide manpower,\nequipment and material support to the Center and its operations:\nPhilippine Navy;\nPhilippine Coast Guard;\nPhilippine National Police Maritime Group;\nNational Prosecution Service of the Department of Justice;\nBureau of Customs;\nBureau of Immigration;\nNational Bureau of Investigation;\nBureau of Fisheries and Aquatic Resources; and\nPhilippine Center on Transnational Crime.\nThe roles and responsibilities of each of the support agencies in the conduct of\nmaritime security and enforcement operations shall be set forth in the rules and\nregulations to be promulgated by the Council.\nAll other government agencies are hereby directed to actively coordinate and\ncooperate with the Council and support the maritime security operations of the\ngovernment. For this purpose, the Chairperson may call upon the heads of government\nagencies for assistance, as may be necessary."}},{"id":"PH-H17066-A7","no":7,"noLabel":{"en":"SECTION 7"},"text":{"en":"Abolition of the Commission on Maritime and Ocean Affairs.\nIn line with the continuing efforts to streamline and rationalize the functions of\ngovernment offices, the Commission on Maritime and Ocean Affairs (CMO) created\nunder Executive Order No. 612 (s. 2007), as amended, is hereby abolished. The\nmandate and functions of the CMOA shall now be performed by the Council"}},{"id":"PH-H17066-A8","no":8,"noLabel":{"en":"SECTION 8"},"text":{"en":"Non-Diminution of Mandates. Nothing in this Executive Order\nshall diminish the mandates, functions and responsibilities of the support agencies\nexcept under Section 7 hereof."}},{"id":"PH-H17066-A9","no":9,"noLabel":{"en":"SECTION 9"},"text":{"en":"Funding. The initial funding requirement of Twenty Million Pesos\n(Php 20,000,000.00) shall be sourced from the Special Account in the General Fund\n(SAGF) of the Department of Energy under Fund 151, to be released by the Department\nof Budget and Management (DBM), subject to the submission of the Bureau of Treasury\n(BTr) Certification on the availability of deposited collections with the SAG of the DOE\nand to existing laws and the usual government budgetary, accounting and auditing rules\nand regulations.\nThereafter, appropriations for the succeeding fiscal years shall be incorporated in\nthe General Appropriations Act.\n5\n@flice ofthe Bresident of the Philippines"}},{"id":"PH-H17066-A10","no":10,"noLabel":{"en":"SECTION 10"},"text":{"en":"Authority to Accept Assistance and/or Donations. The Council\nand the Center are hereby authorized to accept donations, contributions, grants,\nbequests or gifts from domestic or foreign sources, for purposes relevant to their\nmandates and functions, in accordance with applicable laws and rules and subject to\ngovernment accounting and auditing rules and regulations."}},{"id":"PH-H17066-A11","no":11,"noLabel":{"en":"SECTION 11"},"text":{"en":"Reports. The Council shall, within ninety (90) days from the\nissuance of this Executive Order, submit a report to the President on the implementation\nhereof. Thereafter, the Council shall submit annual reports to the President on the\noperations of both the Council and the Center."}},{"id":"PH-H17066-A12","no":12,"noLabel":{"en":"SECTION 12"},"text":{"en":"Separability. If any provision of this Executive Order is declared\ninvalid or unconstitutional, the other provisions unaffected shall remain valid and\nsubsisting."}},{"id":"PH-H17066-A13","no":13,"noLabel":{"en":"SECTION 13"},"text":{"en":"Repealing Clause. With the exception of Proclamation No. 72 (s.\n2001) and subiect to Section 3 hereof, all issuances, rules and regulations or parts\nthereof inconsistent with this Executive Order are hereby revoked, amended or modified\naccordingly."}},{"id":"PH-H17066-A14","no":14,"noLabel":{"en":"SECTION 14"},"text":{"en":"Effectivity. This Executive Order shall take effect immediately\nupon publication in a newspaper of general circulation.\nDONE, in the City of Manila, this 6th day of September\nof Our Lord, Two Thousand and Eleven.\n12\nBy the President:\nPAQUITO N. OCHOA, JR.\nExecutive Secretary\nOffice of the President of the Philippines\n6\nMARIANITO M. DIMAANDAL\nDIRECTOR IV\n44: 9.9. 11 499-9. 204 MALACARANG RECORDS OFFILE"}}],"pack":"ph-p157"};
  FT["PH-H17067"] = {"id":"PH-H17067","coverage":"full","language":"en","sourceName":"The LawPhil Project — Arellano Law Foundation","sourceUrl":"","fetchedAt":"2026-10-28","articleCount":7,"structureMode":"ARTICLE","title":{"zh":null,"en":"MALACAÑAN PALACE BY THE PRESIDENT OF THE PHILIPPINES REDUCING THE RATES OF DUTY ON CAPITAL EQUIPMENT, SPARE PARTS AND ACCESSORIES IMPORTED BY BOARD OF INVESTMENTS - REGISTERED NEW AND EXPANDING ENTERPRISES","orig":"MALACAÑAN PALACE BY THE PRESIDENT OF THE PHILIPPINES REDUCING THE RATES OF DUTY ON CAPITAL EQUIPMENT, SPARE PARTS AND ACCESSORIES IMPORTED BY BOARD OF INVESTMENTS - REGISTERED NEW AND EXPANDING ENTERPRISES"},"level":"law","status":"active","docNumber":"Executive Order No. 57","issuingBody":"President of the Philippines","completenessNote":"全文，共 7 条；逐字取自 LawPhil PDF 文本化成果（第三方 OCR，非机翻），原始文件 EO_00057_2018.txt","textQuality":"ocr-vendor","sourceFile":"菲律宾/法律原文/07_行政命令_EO/EO_00057_2018.txt","country":"PH","countryName":"菲律宾","layer":"intl","articles":[{"id":"PH-H17067-A1","no":1,"noLabel":{"en":"SECTION 1"},"text":{"en":"Zero Percent Duty. Any importation of capital equipment, spare\nparts and accessories by BOl-registered enterprises shall be subjected to zero percent\nduty, as indicated in Section 2 hereof.\n'THE PRESIDENT OF THE PHILIPPINES"}},{"id":"PH-H17067-A2","no":2,"noLabel":{"en":"SECTION 2"},"text":{"en":"Coverage. The zero percent duty shall be applied to importations by\nBOl-registered new and expanding enterprises of capital equipment, spare parts and\naccessories classified under Chapters 40, 59, 68, 69, 70, 73, 76, 82, 83, 84, 85, 86, 87,\n89, 90 and 96 of the CMTA, upon issuance by the BOl of a Certificate of Authority,\nprovided that such imported capital equipment, spare parts and accessories comply with\nthe following conditions\na. They are not manufactured domestically in sufficient quantity, of comparable\nquality, and at reasonable prices; and\nb. They are reasonably needed and will be used exclusively by the enterprise in its\nregistered activity."}},{"id":"PH-H17067-A3","no":3,"noLabel":{"en":"SECTION 3"},"text":{"en":"Prohibition to Sell, Transfer, or Dispose. The BOl-registered\nenterprise cannot sell, transfer or dispose of the aforementioned capital equipment,\nmachinery, spare parts and accessories, without prior BOI approval, within five (5) years\nfrom the date of importation; otherwise, the BOl-registered enterprise will be solidarily\nliable to pay twice the amount of the duty foregone or five hundred thousand pesos (Php\n500,000.00), whichever is higher, without prejudice to other applicable penalties under"}},{"id":"PH-H17067-A4","no":4,"noLabel":{"en":"SECTION 4"},"text":{"en":"Implementing Rules and Regulations (IRR). The BOI, in\ncoordination with the Tariff Commission, shall promulgate the IRR governing the\nimplementation of this Order."}},{"id":"PH-H17067-A5","no":5,"noLabel":{"en":"SECTION 5"},"text":{"en":"Repealing Clause. All issuances, orders, rules and regulations, or\nparts thereof, which are inconsistent with this Order are hereby repealed, amended or\nmodified accordingly."}},{"id":"PH-H17067-A6","no":6,"noLabel":{"en":"SECTION 6"},"text":{"en":"Separability Clause. If any provision of this Order is declared invalid\nor unconstitutional, the other provisions not affected thereby shall remain valid and\nsubsisting."}},{"id":"PH-H17067-A7","no":7,"noLabel":{"en":"SECTION 7"},"text":{"en":"Effectivity Clause. This Order shall take effect immediately after its\ncomplete publication in a newspaper of general circulation in the Philippines, and shall\nbe valid for a period of one (1) year or until a law amending EO No. 226 is enacted,\nwhichever comes earlier.\nDONE, in the City of Manila, this22nd of June\nThousand and Eighteen.\n, in the year of our Lord, Two\nBy the President:\nMICHAEL P. ONG\nActing Executive Secretary.\nREPUBLIC OF THE\nPHILIPPINES\nOffice of the President\nMALACAÑANG RECORDS OFFICE\nCENTIRIED COPS\nATTY. CONCEPCO MORT E: FERROUINO-OKAC\n078-28\nDIRECTOR NO"}}],"pack":"ph-p157"};
  FT["PH-H17068"] = {"id":"PH-H17068","coverage":"full","language":"en","sourceName":"The LawPhil Project — Arellano Law Foundation","sourceUrl":"","fetchedAt":"2026-10-28","articleCount":14,"structureMode":"ARTICLE","title":{"zh":null,"en":"MALACAÑAN PALACE BY THE PRESIDENT OF THE PHILIPPINES STRENGTHENING THE PHILIPPINES' MARITIME SECURITY AND MARITIME DOMAIN AWARENESS","orig":"MALACAÑAN PALACE BY THE PRESIDENT OF THE PHILIPPINES STRENGTHENING THE PHILIPPINES' MARITIME SECURITY AND MARITIME DOMAIN AWARENESS"},"level":"law","status":"active","docNumber":"Executive Order No. 57","issuingBody":"President of the Philippines","completenessNote":"全文，共 14 条；逐字取自 LawPhil PDF 文本化成果（第三方 OCR，非机翻），原始文件 EO_00057_2024.txt","textQuality":"ocr-vendor","sourceFile":"菲律宾/法律原文/07_行政命令_EO/EO_00057_2024.txt","country":"PH","countryName":"菲律宾","layer":"intl","articles":[{"id":"PH-H17068-A1","no":1,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 1"},"text":{"en":"Coverage. Subject to existing laws, rules and regulations, and except as\nprovided in relevant Presidential issuances, this Order shall cover the following areas:\na. \"Maritime Domain\" - all areas and things of, on, under, relating to, adjacent to, or\nbordering on an ocean, sea, or other bodies of water, including all maritime related\nactivities, infrastructure, people, cargo and vessels and other conveyances. It includes\nthe maritime zones such as internal waters, territorial sea, contiguous zone, exclusive\neconomic zone and continental shelves:\nb. 'Maritime Security\" - protection and conservation of the country's marine assets,\nmaritime practices, territorial integrity, and coastal peace and order. The concept of\nmaritime security is all encompassing to include military, socio-economic,\nenvironmental, and political concerns, among others; and\nc. \"Maritime Domain Awareness\" - effective understanding of anything associated with\nthe maritime domain that could impact the sovereignty and sovereign rights, security,\nsafety, economy, or environment of the country."}},{"id":"PH-H17068-A2","no":2,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 2"},"text":{"en":"National Maritime Council. The National Coast Watch Council is hereby\nrenamed and reorganized as the National Maritime Council (\"Council\"). The Council shall\nbe composed of the following:\nChairperson\nExecutive Secretary\nSecretary, Department of National Defense\nSecretary and National Security Adviser, National Security Council;\nSecretary, Department of Agriculture;\nSecretary, Department of Energy;\nSecretary, Department of Environment and Natural Resources;\nSecretary, Department of Foreign Affairs (DFA);\n2\n\nSecretary, Department of Finance;\nSecretary, Department of the Interior and Local Government;\nSecretary, Department of Justice (DOJ);\nSecretary, Department of Transportation;\nSolicitor General, Office of the Solicitor General; and\nDirector-General, National Intelligence Coordinating Agency.\nThe Council shall meet quarterly, and at such other times as the Chairperson may deem\nnecessary or appropriate."}},{"id":"PH-H17068-A3","no":3,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 3"},"text":{"en":"Powers and Functions of the Council. The Council shall replace the\nNCWC under EO No. 57 as the central body in-charge of formulating policies and strategies\nto ensure a unified, coordinated and effective governance framework for the country's\nmaritime security and domain awareness. Towards this end, the Council shall have the\nfollowing powers and functions:\na. Exercise overall jurisdiction and direction on policy-formulation, implementation and\ncoordination with other government agencies, experts and organizations, both foreign\nand local, on all issues affecting the country's maritime security and domain awareness;\nb. Provide strategic direction and policy guidance for maritime security operations of the\nNational Maritime Center and its support agencies, and multinational and cross-border\ncooperation on maritime security and domain awareness;\nc. Recommend to the President policies and procedures in managing and securing the\ncountry's maritime domain, as well as the issuance of administrative rules and regulations\nto enhance and strengthen maritime security and domain awareness;\nd. Formulate and adopt national strategies for specific maritime concerns within the\njurisdiction of the Council;\ne. Coordinate and oversee the implementation of the National Marine Polic. which shall\nhenceforth be referred to as the \"National Maritime Security Policy and Strategy,\" and\nperiodically review and update the same as may be necessary in light of national and\ninternational developments;\nf. Harmonize capability plans and fund requirements relative to maritime security and\ndomain awareness;\ng. Harmonize and coordinate the roles and relationships of different government agencies,\npursuant to their mandates, on maritime security, domain awareness and governance\nframework as may be determined by the Council;\nh. As may be necessary, create, convene and reorganize committees, national and area\ntask forces, and/or working groups to assist in the performance of its functions, subject\nto existing laws, rules and regulations; and\ni. Perform such other functions as may be deemed necessary by the Chairperson for the\neffective discharge of its mandate or as may be directed by the President.\n3"}},{"id":"PH-H17068-A4","no":4,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 4"},"text":{"en":"Presidential Office for Maritime Concerns. The NCWC Secretariat\nshall be renamed as the Presidential Office for Maritime Concerns (POMC). The POMC\nshall perform the following functions:\na. Provide consultative, research, administrative and technical services to the Council, and\nensure the efficient and effective implementation of the policies of the Council;\nb. Assist the Council in proposing and reviewing legislative and administrative issuances on\nmaritime security and domain awareness;\nc. Provide assistance to the committees, national and area task forces, and working groups\ncreated by the Council, including the provision for administrative, technical and\nsecretariat support;\nd. Coordinate with the National Maritime Center, through the Philippine Coast Guard (PCG),\nregarding the implementation of this Order, as well as any directive, instruction, or policy\nguidance on maritime security and domain awareness issued by the President, Executive\nSecretary, or the Council; and\ne. Perform such other functions and tasks as the Council and/or the President may direct.\nThe Presidential Assistant for Maritime Concerns (PAMC) may report directly to the\nPresident on critical and urgent matters and issues affecting the country's maritime security\nand domain awareness.\nThe PAMC shall replace the Executive Director as Head of the NCWC Secretariat.\nIn this regard, the PAMC shall utilize the existing office and organizational structure and\nstaffing pattern of the NCWC Secretariat as the new POMC."}},{"id":"PH-H17068-A5","no":5,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 5"},"text":{"en":"National Maritime Center. In accordance with the strategic direction and\npolicy guidance issued by the Council, the National Coast Watch Center, which is hereby\nrenamed as the National Maritime Center, shall implement and coordinate maritime security\noperations. It shall further perform the following functions:\na. Gather, consolidate, synthesize and disseminate information relevant to the countrv's\nmaritime security and domain awareness;\nb. Develop and maintain effective communications and information systems to enhance\ninter-agency coordination on maritime security and domain awareness;\nc. Coordinate the conduct of maritime surveillance upon the request of a member-agency\nor when an exigency arises;\nd. Monitor, evaluate, document and report on the conduct of maritime security operations;\ne. When so authorized by the Council, and in coordination with the DA, coordinate and\ninitiate cross-border and multinational maritime security cooperation;\nf. Coordinate support for the prosecution of apprehended violators;\n\ng. Conduct periodic assessments on maritime security and domain awareness, and develop\na common operating picture to enhance maritime situational awareness; and\nh. Perform such other functions as may be directed by the Executive Secretary or the\nThe National Maritime Center shall remain under the leadership of the PCG."}},{"id":"PH-H17068-A6","no":6,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 6"},"text":{"en":"Support Agencies. The following agencies are hereby directed to render\nfull support and assistance to the Council, POMC and the National Maritime Center, in\naccordance with the policy direction of the Council:\nb. Armed Forces of the Philippines;\nc. Philippine National Police;\nd. DOJ-National Prosecution Service;\ne. Bureau of Customs;\nf. Bureau of Immigration;\ng. National Bureau of Investigation;\nh. Bureau of Fisheries and Aquatic Resources;\ni. Philippine Center on Transnational Crime;\nj. Philippine Drug Enforcement Agency;\nk. National Mapping and Resource Information Authority;\n1. Philippine Space Agency; and\nm. University of the Philippines - Institute for Maritime Affairs and Law of the Sea.\nFor this purpose, the Executive Secretary or the Council may, through the PAMC, direct,\norder and mobilize the support and assistance of government agencies as may be deemed\nThe roles and responsibilities of each of the support agencies in the conduct of\nmaritime security and enforcement operations, as well as provision of manpower,\nequipment and material support, shall be set forth in the rules and regulations to be\npromulgated by the Council: Provided, that, nothing in this Order shall diminish the\nmandates, functions and responsibilities of the above support agencies under their\nrespective charters.\nAll other government agencies are directed to actively coordinate and cooperate with\nthe Council and support the operations of the National Government to ensure the country's\nmaritime security and domain awareness."}},{"id":"PH-H17068-A7","no":7,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 7"},"text":{"en":"Authority to Accept Assistance and/or Donations. The National\nMaritime Center is hereby authorized to accept donations, contributions, grants, bequests\nor gifts from domestic or foreign sources, for purposes relevant to their mandates and\nfunctions, subject to existing laws, rules and regulations."}},{"id":"PH-H17068-A8","no":8,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 8"},"text":{"en":"NTF-WPS. Subject to Section 3 hereof, the NTF-WPS, created under MC\nNo. 94, shall be attached to the Council and shall receive policy guidance from the President\nthrough the Council. The PAMC shall be included as an additional Member of the NTF-WPS\nas the representative of the Council.\n5\n\nThe NTF-WPS shall orchestrate, synchronize, and operationalize the employment of\nthe capabilities of different government agencies to achieve unified action in the WPS."}},{"id":"PH-H17068-A9","no":9,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 9"},"text":{"en":"Funding. The funds necessary for the implementation of this Order shall\nbe charged against current and available appropriations of concerned agencies, subject to\npertinent budgeting, accounting, and auditing laws, rules and regulations. Thereafter. the\nfunding requirements for succeeding years shall be included in the annual General\nAppropriations Act, subject to the usual budget preparation process."}},{"id":"PH-H17068-A10","no":10,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 10"},"text":{"en":"Implementing Guidelines. Within sixty (60) days from the effectivity of\nthis Order, the Council shall formulate and issue guidelines for the effective implementation\nof this Order. The Implementing Guidelines shall include a transition plan for the transfer\nand administration of properties, equipment and facilities from the NCWC, NCWC\nSecretariat, National Coast Watch Center, and its regional offices, to the National Maritime\nCouncil, POMC and National Maritime Center, as may be applicable."}},{"id":"PH-H17068-A11","no":11,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 11"},"text":{"en":"Report. The POMC shall submit an annual report to the Office of the\nPresident, through the Office of the Executive Secretary, on the implementation of this\nOrder, as well as the operations of both the Council and the National Maritime Center."}},{"id":"PH-H17068-A12","no":12,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 12"},"text":{"en":"Separability. If any part or provision of this Order shall be held invalid\nor unconstitutional, the provisions not affected thereby shall remain in full force and effect."}},{"id":"PH-H17068-A13","no":13,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 13"},"text":{"en":"Repeal. With the exception of Proclamation No. 72 (s. 2001), this Order\nhereby repeals EO No. 57, and amends relevant provisions of MC No. 94. All other\nissuances, orders, rules and regulations, or parts thereof, that are inconsistent with this\nOrder, are hereby repealed or modified accordingly."}},{"id":"PH-H17068-A14","no":14,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 14"},"text":{"en":"Effectivity. This Order shall take effect immediately upon its publication\nin the Official Gazette or a newspaper of general circulation.\nDONE, in the City of Manila, this 25th\nyear of Our Lord, Two Thousand and Twenty-Four.\nday of March\nBy the President:\nLUCAS P. BERSAMIN\nExeçutive Secretaty\n6\nREPUBLIC ONTOHE HILIPPINES ent\nNIEmAs|2124ACTING DIRECTOR I"}}],"pack":"ph-p157"};
  FT["PH-H17069"] = {"id":"PH-H17069","coverage":"full","language":"en","sourceName":"The LawPhil Project — Arellano Law Foundation","sourceUrl":"LawPhil (HTML full text only)  |  https://lawphil.net/executive/execord/eo1936/eo_58_1936.html","fetchedAt":"2026-10-28","articleCount":1,"structureMode":"WHOLE","title":{"zh":null,"en":"Recognizing Reserve Officers Training in the Collegiate Department of San Juan De Letran College","orig":"Recognizing Reserve Officers Training in the Collegiate Department of San Juan De Letran College"},"level":"law","status":"active","docNumber":"Executive Order No. 58","issuingBody":"President of the Philippines","promulgatedDate":"1936-10-14","completenessNote":"全文，共 1 条；逐字取自 LawPhil PDF 文本化成果（第三方 OCR，非机翻），原始文件 EO_00058_1936_html.txt","textQuality":"ocr-vendor","sourceFile":"菲律宾/法律原文/07_行政命令_EO/EO_00058_1936_html.txt","country":"PH","countryName":"菲律宾","layer":"intl","articles":[{"id":"PH-H17069-A1","no":1,"noLabel":{},"text":{"en":"MALACAÑAN PALACE\nBY THE PRESIDENT OF THE PHILIPPINES\n[ EXECUTIVE ORDER NO. 58, October 14, 1936 ]\nRECOGNIZING RESERVE OFFICERS’ TRAINING IN THE COLLEGIATE DEPARTMENT OF SAN\nJUAN DE LETRAN COLLEGE\nBy virtue of the powers vested in me by the National Defense Act, I, Manuel L. Quezon, President of the\nPhilippines, hereby recognize the high standard of training in the Reserve Officers’ Training Corps in the\nCollegiate Department of San Juan de Letran College.\nSince every physically fit male student of collegiate standing in this institution is now being required to pursue\na course of at least two years of military instruction, such student shall upon completion of such training be\nexempted from trainee instruction. It shall not exempt him from registration.\nDone at the City of Manila, this fourteenth day of October, in the year of Our Lord, nineteen hundred and\nthirty-six, and of the Commonwealth of the Philippines, the first.\nMANUEL L. QUEZON\nPresident of the Philippines\nBy the President:\nELPIDIO QUIRINO\nSecretary of the Interior"}}],"pack":"ph-p157"};
  FT["PH-H17070"] = {"id":"PH-H17070","coverage":"full","language":"en","sourceName":"The LawPhil Project — Arellano Law Foundation","sourceUrl":"","fetchedAt":"2026-10-28","articleCount":1,"structureMode":"WHOLE","title":{"zh":null,"en":"MAL AC AÑTANG RESIDENCE OF THE PRESIDENT OF THE PHILIFFINES BY THE PRESIDENT OF THE PHILIFF INES DECLARING CORREGIDOR AND BATAAT NATIONAL SHRINES, OFENING THEM TO THE TUBLIC AND MAKING THE!! ACCESSIBLE AS TOURIST ATTRACTIONS AND SCENES OF FO: ULAR FILGRIM AGES, AND CREATING & COIT'ISSION FOR THEIR DEVELOP- MENT AND MAIITENANCE,","orig":"MAL AC AÑTANG RESIDENCE OF THE PRESIDENT OF THE PHILIFFINES BY THE PRESIDENT OF THE PHILIFF INES DECLARING CORREGIDOR AND BATAAT NATIONAL SHRINES, OFENING THEM TO THE TUBLIC AND MAKING THE!! ACCESSIBLE AS TOURIST ATTRACTIONS AND SCENES OF FO: ULAR FILGRIM AGES, AND CREATING & COIT'ISSION FOR THEIR DEVELOP- MENT AND MAIITENANCE,"},"level":"law","status":"active","docNumber":"Executive Order No. 58","issuingBody":"President of the Philippines","completenessNote":"全文，共 1 条；逐字取自 LawPhil PDF 文本化成果（第三方 OCR，非机翻），原始文件 EO_00058_1954.txt","textQuality":"ocr-vendor","sourceFile":"菲律宾/法律原文/07_行政命令_EO/EO_00058_1954.txt","country":"PH","countryName":"菲律宾","layer":"intl","articles":[{"id":"PH-H17070-A1","no":1,"noLabel":{},"text":{"en":"exclusively for temporary military uses, at the same time taking 1m-\nmediate steps to romovo military stores and other dengerous objects,\nespecially unexploded mines, bombs and shells alone the road leading\nto or within the historic sites,\n5. The Commission shall conduct\n- 2 -\n5. The Commission shall conduct studies and prepare a veneral\nprogram for the levelopment of national parks embracing all the his-\ntoric areas and recommend to the President a plan for appropriate\nmemorials or monuments wherever they are deemed desirable, taking into\nscount the topography, vegetation and historical backround of the places\nselected for the purpose.\n6. The Commission shall also immediately take steps towards the re-\nconditicning of the air-strip in Corregidor and the construction of another\nat a convenient site in Bataan as well as the construction of suitable rest-\nhouses for tourists and visitors in convenient locations in both places. For\nrest-house purposes, preference shall be given to the reconstruction and\nrestoration to as nearly like the original as possible of the cottage occupied\nby General Macarthur in Corregidor and of any building in Bataan which has\nhistoric background connected with the last war,\n7. The Secretary of Public Works and Communicatins, the Armed Forces\nof the Philippines and the Civil Aeronautics Administration are hereby\ndirected to give priority to these improvements and to make available for\ntheir immediate realization such funds as they may be in a position to dish\npose of out of their respective current appropriations for similar projects.\n8. The Commission may cooperate with the U.S. Bataan- Correridor Memorial\nCommission and, if it so deems proper, endeavor to bring bout an integration\nof the plans of both bodies into a common project,\n9. The Commission may call on any department, bureau, office, agency\nor instrumentality of the government for such assistance as it may need in\nthe preparation and execution of its plans or in the maintenance of the\nservices to be established.\n10. All executive orders, administrative orders and proclamations or\nparts thereof inconsistent with any of the provisions and purposes of this\nOrder are hereby repealed or modified accordingly,\n11, This Order shall take effect immediately.\nDone in the City of Manila, this I6th day of August, in year of\nOur Lord, nineteen hundred and fifty-four, and of the Independence of the\nThilippines, the ninth.\n(SGD.) RAMON MAGSAYSAY\nPresident of the Philippines\nBy the President:\n(SGD.) FRED RUIZ CASTRO\nExecutive Secretary"}}],"pack":"ph-p157"};
  FT["PH-H17071"] = {"id":"PH-H17071","coverage":"full","language":"en","sourceName":"The LawPhil Project — Arellano Law Foundation","sourceUrl":"LawPhil (source has HTML full text only)","fetchedAt":"2026-10-28","articleCount":4,"structureMode":"ARTICLE","title":{"zh":null,"en":"Rationalizing Fees and Other Charges on Firearms, Explosives and Explosives Ingredients, Security Agencies and Security Guards","orig":"Rationalizing Fees and Other Charges on Firearms, Explosives and Explosives Ingredients, Security Agencies and Security Guards"},"level":"law","status":"active","docNumber":"Executive Order No. 58","issuingBody":"President of the Philippines","promulgatedDate":"1987-01-01","completenessNote":"全文，共 4 条；逐字取自 LawPhil PDF 文本化成果（第三方 OCR，非机翻），原始文件 EO_00058_1987_html.txt","textQuality":"ocr-vendor","sourceFile":"菲律宾/法律原文/07_行政命令_EO/EO_00058_1987_html.txt","country":"PH","countryName":"菲律宾","layer":"intl","articles":[{"id":"PH-H17071-A1","no":1,"noLabel":{"en":"Sec 1"},"text":{"en":"The provisions of Batas Pambansa Blg. 325 and its implementing rules and regulations and other laws\nto the contrary notwithstanding, the rates of license/registration/permit fees, other charges, and\nPenal/administrative fines relative to firearms, explosives and explosives ingredients, security agencies and\nsecurity guards shall be as follows:\n1.\nAnnual Firearm License Fee\n(b) Shotgun (all gauges)\n120.00\n(c) Pist/Rev Cal. .22 (Ord)\n150.00\n(d) Pist/Rev Cal. .25; 32; .38; 380; 9MM; 65; 6.35 and Magnum .22 rimfire\n130.00\n(e) Pist/Rev Cal .45; Magnum Cal .22 centerfire, .357;41 and .44\n200.00\n200.00\n2.\nPermit to Purchase Explosives/Explosives Ingredients:\n(a) Explosives\n100.00\n\n(b) Explosives Ingredients\n50.00\n3.\nStorage Fee (Annual)\n500.00\n4.\nStorage to Import Explosives and its Ingredients\n200.00\n5.\nPermit to Unload Explosives and its Ingredients\n100.00\n6.\nAnnual Private Security License/Registration:\n(a) Scty Offr/Pvt Det/Consultant\n500.00\n(b) Pvt Scty Gd/Supervisor\n25.00\n(c) Pvt Scty Agcy and Coy Gd Forces\n1,000.00\n(d) Registration Fees of Scty Guards by Scty Agencies\n10.00\n7.\nPenal/Administrative Fines:\n(b) Shotgun (all gauges)\n700.00\n(c) Pist/Rev Cal. .25 (Ord)\n800.00\n(d) Pist/Rev Cal. .25; 32; .38; .380; 9MM; 7.65; 6.35 and Magnum .22 rimfire\n900.00\n(e) Pist/Rev Cal .45; Magnum Cal .22 centerfire, .357; .41 and .44\n1,000.00\n1,000.00"}},{"id":"PH-H17071-A2","no":2,"noLabel":{"en":"Sec 2"},"text":{"en":"The Philippine Constabulary/Integrated National Police is hereby authorizing to impose the following\nfees for licenses issued in connection with explosives/explosives ingredients:\n\nLicense (Annual)\nDealer's License\nLicense authorizing the importation, purchase, possession, sale, transfer and general business handling\ngunpowder dynamite, explosives or their ingredients.\nManufacturer's License\nLicense authorizing the manufacturer of gunpowder, dynamite, explosives or their ingredients.\n1,000.00\nPurchaser's License\nLicense authorizing the purchase and possession of dynamite, explosives or ingredients for use of mines,\nquarries, road construction, wrecking and for use in any other legal and lawful occupation.\n200.00\nForeman's License\nLicense authorizing the purchase and possession of dynamite, explosives or their ingredients by workmen in\nmines, quarries, road construction, wrecking or for use in any other legal and lawful public or private works.\nLicense must be qualified blaster or must technically qualified to handle explosives.\n100.00"}},{"id":"PH-H17071-A3","no":3,"noLabel":{"en":"Sec 3"},"text":{"en":"The rates of fees and charges provided under this Executive Order shall take effect on January 1, 1987."}},{"id":"PH-H17071-A4","no":4,"noLabel":{"en":"Sec 4"},"text":{"en":"All laws, orders, issuances, and rules and regulations or parts thereof inconsistent with this Executive\nOrder are hereby repealed or modified accordingly.\nDone in the City of Manila, this 7th day of November, in the year of Our Lord, nineteen hundred and"}}],"pack":"ph-p157"};
  FT["PH-H17072"] = {"id":"PH-H17072","coverage":"full","language":"en","sourceName":"The LawPhil Project — Arellano Law Foundation","sourceUrl":"","fetchedAt":"2026-10-28","articleCount":1,"structureMode":"WHOLE","title":{"zh":null,"en":"EXECUTIVE ORDER NO. CREATING AN INTER-AGENCY E1{ECUTIVE COMMITTEE TO COMI'REHENSIVE DEVELOPMENT HOUSING AUTHORITY PROPERTY IN NORTHTRIANGLE, QUEZON CITY","orig":"EXECUTIVE ORDER NO. CREATING AN INTER-AGENCY E1{ECUTIVE COMMITTEE TO COMI'REHENSIVE DEVELOPMENT HOUSING AUTHORITY PROPERTY IN NORTHTRIANGLE, QUEZON CITY"},"level":"law","status":"active","docNumber":"Executive Order No. 58","issuingBody":"President of the Philippines","completenessNote":"全文，共 1 条；逐字取自 LawPhil PDF 文本化成果（第三方 OCR，非机翻），原始文件 EO_00058_1993.txt","textQuality":"ocr-vendor","sourceFile":"菲律宾/法律原文/07_行政命令_EO/EO_00058_1993.txt","country":"PH","countryName":"菲律宾","layer":"intl","articles":[{"id":"PH-H17072-A8","no":8,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 8"},"text":{"en":"immediately.\nHundred and Ninety\n~\nBy the President:\n-~ -\nPresidential"}}],"pack":"ph-p157"};
  FT["PH-H17073"] = {"id":"PH-H17073","coverage":"full","language":"en","sourceName":"The LawPhil Project — Arellano Law Foundation","sourceUrl":"","fetchedAt":"2026-10-28","articleCount":4,"structureMode":"ARTICLE","title":{"zh":null,"en":". ~ PMS LiBRARY' \" EXECUTIVE ~~DER NO. -~ Creating a Domestic Trade Development Defining its Composition, Powers and Functions it is a standing policy of the government development of business that are crucial to the delivery of basicservices, and directly affect the livelihood and \\\"Ielfare of our people; WHEREAS, the government recognizes the need to boost efforts to promote the domestic trade sector in view of its increasing importance to job generation, sustainable economic growth and countryside development; current economic a vibrantly f4nctioning domestic trade sector to ensure sustained economic growth and correspondingly address the economic goals of productivity in business. employment systematic countrywide enterprise developmerlt and enhanced income-generating capabilities for our people; there is a need to integrate government and private sector that 'vvill foster the growtrl trade as foundation for sound and equitable","orig":". ~ PMS LiBRARY' \" EXECUTIVE ~~DER NO. -~ Creating a Domestic Trade Development Defining its Composition, Powers and Functions it is a standing policy of the government development of business that are crucial to the delivery of basicservices, and directly affect the livelihood and \\\"Ielfare of our people; WHEREAS, the government recognizes the need to boost efforts to promote the domestic trade sector in view of its increasing importance to job generation, sustainable economic growth and countryside development; current economic a vibrantly f4nctioning domestic trade sector to ensure sustained economic growth and correspondingly address the economic goals of productivity in business. employment systematic countrywide enterprise developmerlt and enhanced income-generating capabilities for our people; there is a need to integrate government and private sector that 'vvill foster the growtrl trade as foundation for sound and equitable"},"level":"law","status":"active","docNumber":"Executive Order No. 58","issuingBody":"President of the Philippines","completenessNote":"全文，共 4 条；逐字取自 LawPhil PDF 文本化成果（第三方 OCR，非机翻），原始文件 EO_00058_1998.txt","textQuality":"ocr-vendor","sourceFile":"菲律宾/法律原文/07_行政命令_EO/EO_00058_1998.txt","country":"PH","countryName":"菲律宾","layer":"intl","articles":[{"id":"PH-H17073-A3","no":3,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 3"},"text":{"en":"Secretariat.\nThe Council shall be assisted by a Secretariat\nbased in the Department\nof Trade and Industry, headed by an official\ndesignated\nby the Chairman of the Council, together with personnel from\ngovernment agencies and private sectors represented in the Council who\nshall be assigned to the Secretaria.t.\n\n\"\n\\\\\n\","}},{"id":"PH-H17073-A4","no":4,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 4"},"text":{"en":"Meetings.\nThe Council shall meet once a month, and at\nleast once- every 1:tuarter with the President: provided, that whenever\nPresident and/or the Chairman deem it necessa~. either the President or the\nmay convene the Council."}},{"id":"PH-H17073-A5","no":5,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 5"},"text":{"en":"Funding.\nFunding of activities and operational expenses of\nthe Council shall be supported by contributions from the government and the\nprivate sector.\nThe seed capital\nin an amount recommended\nDepartment of Trade and Industry, upon consultation with the Department of\nBudget and Management, and approved by the President shall be taken from\nthe Contingent Fund of the President. Thereafter, the annual contributions of\nthe government shall be included in the annual General Appropriations\nafter consultations with the Department of Budget and Management."}},{"id":"PH-H17073-A6","no":6,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 6"},"text":{"en":"Effectivity.\nThis Order shall take effect immediately.\nDone in the Ci~ of Manila, this!;(Y K\nnineteen hundred and ninety-eight.\n/\nBy the President:\n~-:>-~\n/~"}}],"pack":"ph-p157"};
  FT["PH-H17074"] = {"id":"PH-H17074","coverage":"full","language":"en","sourceName":"The LawPhil Project — Arellano Law Foundation","sourceUrl":"","fetchedAt":"2026-10-28","articleCount":1,"structureMode":"WHOLE","title":{"zh":null,"en":"MALACAÑANG BY THE PRESIDENT OF THE PHILIPPINES AUTHORIZING THE NATIONAL POWER CORPORATION TO DISPOSE OF ITS 1.6-HECTARE PROPERTY LOCATED IN SITIO PAJO, BAESA, QUEZON CITY TO ITS BONAFIDE OCCUPANTS","orig":"MALACAÑANG BY THE PRESIDENT OF THE PHILIPPINES AUTHORIZING THE NATIONAL POWER CORPORATION TO DISPOSE OF ITS 1.6-HECTARE PROPERTY LOCATED IN SITIO PAJO, BAESA, QUEZON CITY TO ITS BONAFIDE OCCUPANTS"},"level":"law","status":"active","docNumber":"Executive Order No. 58","issuingBody":"President of the Philippines","completenessNote":"全文，共 1 条；逐字取自 LawPhil PDF 文本化成果（第三方 OCR，非机翻），原始文件 EO_00058_2001.txt","textQuality":"ocr-vendor","sourceFile":"菲律宾/法律原文/07_行政命令_EO/EO_00058_2001.txt","country":"PH","countryName":"菲律宾","layer":"intl","articles":[{"id":"PH-H17074-A1","no":1,"noLabel":{},"text":{"en":"2\nDone in the City of Manila, this 5th day of\nyear of Our Lord, two thousand and one.\nBy the President:\nALBERTO G. ROMULO\nExecutive Secretary\nPMS LIBRARY\nPOMA Outgoing , 07086\nPMS LIBRARY BCODE002103"}}],"pack":"ph-p157"};
  FT["PH-H17075"] = {"id":"PH-H17075","coverage":"full","language":"en","sourceName":"The LawPhil Project — Arellano Law Foundation","sourceUrl":"","fetchedAt":"2026-10-28","articleCount":1,"structureMode":"WHOLE","title":{"zh":null,"en":"MALACAÑAN PALACE BY THE PRESIDENT OF THE PHILIPPINES MANDATING THE TRANSFER OF NAYONG PILIPINO FOUNDATION'S PASAY PROPERTY TO THE MANILA INTERNATIONAL AIRPORT","orig":"MALACAÑAN PALACE BY THE PRESIDENT OF THE PHILIPPINES MANDATING THE TRANSFER OF NAYONG PILIPINO FOUNDATION'S PASAY PROPERTY TO THE MANILA INTERNATIONAL AIRPORT"},"level":"law","status":"active","docNumber":"Executive Order No. 58","issuingBody":"President of the Philippines","completenessNote":"全文，共 1 条；逐字取自 LawPhil PDF 文本化成果（第三方 OCR，非机翻），原始文件 EO_00058_2011.txt","textQuality":"ocr-vendor","sourceFile":"菲律宾/法律原文/07_行政命令_EO/EO_00058_2011.txt","country":"PH","countryName":"菲律宾","layer":"intl","articles":[{"id":"PH-H17075-A1","no":1,"noLabel":{},"text":{"en":"person or entity without previous authorization by the President of the\nPhilippines.\nNOW, THEREFORE, I, BENIGN S. AQUINO III, President of the\nPhilippines, by virtue of the powers vested in me by law, do hereby order the\nNayong Pilipino Foundation, Inc. to transfer its remaining land with an area of\n22.3 hectares in Pasay City to the Manila International Airport Authority.\nThis Executive Order shall take effect immediately upon publication in\na newspaper of general circulation.\nDONE in the City of Manila, this 29th day of Septemh™the year of Our\nLord, Two Thousand and Eleven.\nBy the President:\nP/AQUITO N. OCHOA, JR.\nExecutive Secretary\n@flice of the Brasient otthe 3hiliopines\nCERTIFIED COPY:\nMARIANITE M DIMAANDAL\nDIRECTOR IV\n83 10-5-201 9 10 8•204 MALACANANG RECORDS OFFICE"}}],"pack":"ph-p157"};
  FT["PH-H17076"] = {"id":"PH-H17076","coverage":"full","language":"en","sourceName":"The LawPhil Project — Arellano Law Foundation","sourceUrl":"","fetchedAt":"2026-10-28","articleCount":10,"structureMode":"ARTICLE","title":{"zh":null,"en":"MALACANAN PALACE BY THE PRESIDENT OF THE PHILIPPINES APPROVING THE MERGER OF THE HOME GUARANTY CORPORATION AND THE PHILIPPINE EXPORT-IMPORT CREDIT AGENCY (PHILEXIM), TRANSFERRING THE GUARANTEE FUNCTIONS, PROGRAMS AND FUNDS OF THE SMALL BUSINESS CORPORATION, AND THE ADMINISTRATION OF THE AGRICULTURAL GUARANTEE FUND POOL AND THE INDUSTRIAL GUARANTEE AND LOAN FUND TO THE PHILEXIM, AND RENAMING THE PHILEXIM AS THE PHILIPPINE GUARANTEE CORPORATION","orig":"MALACANAN PALACE BY THE PRESIDENT OF THE PHILIPPINES APPROVING THE MERGER OF THE HOME GUARANTY CORPORATION AND THE PHILIPPINE EXPORT-IMPORT CREDIT AGENCY (PHILEXIM), TRANSFERRING THE GUARANTEE FUNCTIONS, PROGRAMS AND FUNDS OF THE SMALL BUSINESS CORPORATION, AND THE ADMINISTRATION OF THE AGRICULTURAL GUARANTEE FUND POOL AND THE INDUSTRIAL GUARANTEE AND LOAN FUND TO THE PHILEXIM, AND RENAMING THE PHILEXIM AS THE PHILIPPINE GUARANTEE CORPORATION"},"level":"law","status":"active","docNumber":"Executive Order No. 58","issuingBody":"President of the Philippines","completenessNote":"全文，共 10 条；逐字取自 LawPhil PDF 文本化成果（第三方 OCR，非机翻），原始文件 EO_00058_2018.txt","textQuality":"ocr-vendor","sourceFile":"菲律宾/法律原文/07_行政命令_EO/EO_00058_2018.txt","country":"PH","countryName":"菲律宾","layer":"intl","articles":[{"id":"PH-H17076-A1","no":1,"noLabel":{"en":"SECTION 1"},"text":{"en":"Transfer of Guarantee Functions, Programs and Funds; Merger. - The\nHGC shall be merged with the PhilEXIM, including all its guarantee functions, programs,\npersonnel, assets and liabilities. The PhilEXIM shall be the surviving entity in the merger.\nMoreover, all the guarantee-related functions, programs, funds, assets and liabilities of the SBC\nshall be transferred to the PhilEXIM.\n2\n\nThe administration of the AGP shall also be transferred to the PhilEXIM, including the\npenalties pertaining to the AGP pursuant to Section 10 of RA No. 10000, otherwise known as\nthe \"Agri-Agra Reform Credit Act of 2009,\" and its implementing rules and regulations, which\nwill be held in a separate account, and allocated for the needs of the agricultural and agrarian\nreform sector, subject to applicable laws and regulations.\nThe IGLF shall be transferred to the PhilEXIM, subject to the provisions of the existing\nLoan Agreement with the Asian Development Bank, and applicable laws and regulations."}},{"id":"PH-H17076-A2","no":2,"noLabel":{"en":"SECTION 2"},"text":{"en":"Implementation of the Merger and Transfer of the Guarantee\nFunctions, Programs and Funds. - The DOF shall implement the merger and transfer of the\nguarantee functions, programs and funds, and, in consultation with the LBP, DBP, DA, HUDCC\nand DTI, determine the extent and modes by which the guarantee functions, programs, funds,\nassets and liabilities will be transferred to the PhilEXIM.\nAll other government offices and agencies are hereby directed to promptly take such\nactions as may be necessary, subject to applicable laws and regulations, to fully implement the\nprovisions of this Order within one (1) year from its effectivity."}},{"id":"PH-H17076-A3","no":3,"noLabel":{"en":"SECTION 3"},"text":{"en":"Increase in the Authorized Capital Stock of PhilEXIM. - The authorized\ncapital stock of the PhilEXIM is hereby increased from Ten Billion Pesos (₽ 10,000,000,000.00)\nto Fifty Billion Pesos (₽ 50,000,000,000.00). The equity contributions of the National\nGovernment to the HGC, IGLF and AGP shall be transferred to the PhilEXIM to form part of\nits paid-up capital. Subject to prior coordination with the Department of Budget and\nManagement (DBM), any balance in the required paid-up capital shall be charged as capital\ninfusion from the National Government to be sourced from the annual General Appropriations"}},{"id":"PH-H17076-A4","no":4,"noLabel":{"en":"SECTION 4"},"text":{"en":"Reorganization of PhilEXIM and SBC. - The PhilEXIM and SBC are\nhereby directed to submit its proposed Restructuring Plan within one (1) year from the effectivity\nof this Order, for review, evaluation and approval of the GG. The proposed PhilEXIM and\nSBC Restructuring Plans shall be prepared in accordance with the existing rules and\nregulations of the GCG."}},{"id":"PH-H17076-A5","no":5,"noLabel":{"en":"SECTION 5"},"text":{"en":"Separation Incentive Pay. - All qualified officers and employees affected\nby the merger may avail of the separation pay below, in addition to retirement or separation\nbenefits allowed under existing laws and regulations:\nLENGTH OF SERVICE\nFirst 20 years\nRemaining years\n1.00 x Basic Monthly Pay (BMP) x No. of years\n1.25 x BMP × No. of years\n1.50 × BMP x No. of years\nFunding for the separation pay and other benefits of the affected officers and employees\nshall be sourced from the corporate funds of the concerned GOCCs. The DBM shall ensure\nthat there are sufficient funds to cover the compensation of affected officers and employees."}},{"id":"PH-H17076-A6","no":6,"noLabel":{"en":"SECTION 6"},"text":{"en":"Establishment of PhilEXIM Board of Liquidators as a Subsidiary of\nPhilEXIM. - To clean up its balance sheet through the spin-off of its non-performing assets\nand outstanding loans, the PhilEXIM is hereby authorized, through registration with the SEC,\nto establish its own subsidiary corporation, functioning as board of liquidators to manage its\nnon-performing assets, collect its receivables, recover and dispose of its acquired assets,\nmanage and settle its outstanding loans and administer its default contingent accounts.\n3"}},{"id":"PH-H17076-A7","no":7,"noLabel":{"en":"SECTION 7"},"text":{"en":"Renaming of Surviving Entity. - To reflect the centralized nature of the\nmerged guarantee functions that will be discharged by the PhilEXIM, it shall be renamed as\nthe \"Philippine Guarantee Corporation\" (PHILGUARANTEE)."}},{"id":"PH-H17076-A8","no":8,"noLabel":{"en":"SECTION 8"},"text":{"en":"Repeal. - All executive orders, rules and regulations, and other issuances\nor parts thereof which are inconsistent with this Order are hereby repealed, amended or\nmodified accordingly."}},{"id":"PH-H17076-A9","no":9,"noLabel":{"en":"SECTION 9"},"text":{"en":"Separability. - If any provision of this Order is declared invalid or\nunconstitutional, the other provisions not affected thereby shall remain valid and subsisting."}},{"id":"PH-H17076-A10","no":10,"noLabel":{"en":"SECTION 10"},"text":{"en":"Effectivity. - This Order shall take effect immediately upon publication\nin the Official Gazette or in a newspaper of general circulation.\nDONE, in the City of Manila, this23rdday of\nThousand and Eighteen.\nin the year of Our Lord, Two\nBy the President:\nSALVADOR C. MEDIALDEA\nExecutive Secretary A\nREPUBLIC OF THE PHILIPPINES\nOffice of the President\nMALACANANG RECORDS OFFICE\nIVY. CONCERCI\n97-24-204\n• TERROLING SHAD"}}],"pack":"ph-p157"};
  FT["PH-H17077"] = {"id":"PH-H17077","coverage":"full","language":"en","sourceName":"The LawPhil Project — Arellano Law Foundation","sourceUrl":"","fetchedAt":"2026-10-28","articleCount":6,"structureMode":"ARTICLE","title":{"zh":null,"en":"MALACAÑAN PALACE BY THE PRESIDENT OF THE PHILIPPINES ADOPTING THE NATIONAL CYBERSECURITY PLAN 2023-2028, AND DIRECTING THE IMPLEMENTATION THEREOF","orig":"MALACAÑAN PALACE BY THE PRESIDENT OF THE PHILIPPINES ADOPTING THE NATIONAL CYBERSECURITY PLAN 2023-2028, AND DIRECTING THE IMPLEMENTATION THEREOF"},"level":"law","status":"active","docNumber":"Executive Order No. 58","issuingBody":"President of the Philippines","completenessNote":"全文，共 6 条；逐字取自 LawPhil PDF 文本化成果（第三方 OCR，非机翻），原始文件 EO_00058_2024.txt","textQuality":"ocr-vendor","sourceFile":"菲律宾/法律原文/07_行政命令_EO/EO_00058_2024.txt","country":"PH","countryName":"菲律宾","layer":"intl","articles":[{"id":"PH-H17077-A1","no":1,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 1"},"text":{"en":"Adoption, Alignment, and Implementation of the NCSP 2023-2028.\nThe NCSP 2023-2028 is hereby adopted as the whole-of-nation roadmap for the integrated\ndevelopment and strategic direction of the country's cybersecurity.\nAIL national government agencies and instrumentalities, including\ngovernment-owned or -controlled corporations are hereby directed, and all LGUs are hereby\nencouraged, to formulate, adopt and implement their cybersecurity plans and strategies,\nwhich are relevant to their respective mandates, in accordance with the NCSP 2023-2028.\nThe DICT shall adopt a system for the effective implementation, monitoring, and\nreview of the NCSP 2023-2028, subject to existing laws, rules and regulations. As may be\nnecessary, the DICT, in cooperation with the private sector, shall provide technical\nassistance to other government agencies and offices relative to the implementation of the"}},{"id":"PH-H17077-A2","no":2,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 2"},"text":{"en":"Reporting. The DICT shall submit to the President, through the Office of\nthe Executive Secretary and NCIAC, a bi-annual report on the status and progress of the\nimplementation of the NCSP 2023-2028."}},{"id":"PH-H17077-A3","no":3,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 3"},"text":{"en":"Funding. The funding requirements for the implementation of this Order\nshall be charged against current and available appropriations of concerned agencies,\nsubject to pertinent budgeting, accounting, and auditing laws, rules and regulations.\nThereafter, the funding requirements necessary for the continued implementation of this\nOrder shall be included in the General Appropriations Act, subject to the usual budget\npreparation process."}},{"id":"PH-H17077-A4","no":4,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 4"},"text":{"en":"Separability. If any section or part of this Order is declared\nunconstitutional or invalid, the other sections or provisions not otherwise affected shall\nremain in full force and effect."}},{"id":"PH-H17077-A5","no":5,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 5"},"text":{"en":"Repeal. All other orders, guidelines, rules, regulations, and issuances or\nparts thereof, which are inconsistent with the provisions of this Order, are hereby repealed\nor modified accordingly."}},{"id":"PH-H17077-A6","no":6,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 6"},"text":{"en":"Effectivity. This Order shall take effect immediately upon publication in\nthe Official Gazette or a newspaper of general circulation.\nDONE, in the City of Manila, this 4th\nof our Lord, Two Thousand and Twenty Four.\nBy the President:\nVUÇAS P. BERSAMIN\nExecutive Secretary\n2\nMALACANAIBB004350 L\nCERTIFIED COPY\n14-8-204 ACTING DIRECTOR IV"}}],"pack":"ph-p157"};
  FT["PH-H17078"] = {"id":"PH-H17078","coverage":"full","language":"en","sourceName":"The LawPhil Project — Arellano Law Foundation","sourceUrl":"LawPhil (HTML full text only)  |  https://lawphil.net/executive/execord/eo1936/eo_59_1936.html","fetchedAt":"2026-10-28","articleCount":1,"structureMode":"WHOLE","title":{"zh":null,"en":"Transferring the Seat of Government of the Municipal District of Kabasalan, Zamboanga, From Its Present Location At the Barrio of Naga to the Barrio of","orig":"Transferring the Seat of Government of the Municipal District of Kabasalan, Zamboanga, From Its Present Location At the Barrio of Naga to the Barrio of"},"level":"law","status":"active","docNumber":"Executive Order No. 59","issuingBody":"President of the Philippines","promulgatedDate":"1936-10-21","completenessNote":"全文，共 1 条；逐字取自 LawPhil PDF 文本化成果（第三方 OCR，非机翻），原始文件 EO_00059_1936_html.txt","textQuality":"ocr-vendor","sourceFile":"菲律宾/法律原文/07_行政命令_EO/EO_00059_1936_html.txt","country":"PH","countryName":"菲律宾","layer":"intl","articles":[{"id":"PH-H17078-A1","no":1,"noLabel":{},"text":{"en":"MALACAÑAN PALACE\nBY THE PRESIDENT OF THE PHILIPPINES\n[ EXECUTIVE ORDER NO. 59, October 21, 1936 ]\nTRANSFERRING THE SEAT OF GOVERNMENT OF THE MUNICIPAL DISTRICT OF KABASALAN,\nZAMBOANGA, FROM ITS PRESENT LOCATION AT THE BARRIO OF NAGA TO THE BARRIO OF\nUpon the recommendation of the provincial board of Zamboanga, concurred in by the Director of the Bureau\nof non-Christian Tribes and the Honorable, the Secretary of the Interior, and pursuant to the provisions of\nsection sixty-eight of the Revised Administrative Code, the seat of government of the Municipal District of\nKabasalan, Province of Zamboanga, as organized under Executive Order Numbered One hundred thirty-five,\nseries of nineteen hundred and twenty-eight, of the Governor-General, is hereby transferred from its present\nlocation at Naga to the Barrio of Kabasalan, said municipal district.\nThe transfer herein made shall take effect on November fifteenth, nineteen hundred and thirty-six.\nDone at the City of Manila, this twenty-first day of October, in the year of Our Lord, nineteen hundred and\nthirty-six, and of the Commonwealth of the Philippines, the first.\nMANUEL L. QUEZON\nPresident of the Philippines\nBy the President:\nELPIDIO QUIRINO\nSecretary of the Interior"}}],"pack":"ph-p157"};
  FT["PH-H17079"] = {"id":"PH-H17079","coverage":"full","language":"en","sourceName":"The LawPhil Project — Arellano Law Foundation","sourceUrl":"","fetchedAt":"2026-10-28","articleCount":1,"structureMode":"WHOLE","title":{"zh":null,"en":"MALACANAN PALACE BY THE PRESIDENT OF THE PHILIPPINES CREATING THE METROPOLITAN TRANSPORTATION SERVICE (METRAN)","orig":"MALACANAN PALACE BY THE PRESIDENT OF THE PHILIPPINES CREATING THE METROPOLITAN TRANSPORTATION SERVICE (METRAN)"},"level":"law","status":"active","docNumber":"Executive Order No. 59","issuingBody":"President of the Philippines","completenessNote":"全文，共 1 条；逐字取自 LawPhil PDF 文本化成果（第三方 OCR，非机翻），原始文件 EO_00059_1945.txt","textQuality":"ocr-vendor","sourceFile":"菲律宾/法律原文/07_行政命令_EO/EO_00059_1945.txt","country":"PH","countryName":"菲律宾","layer":"intl","articles":[{"id":"PH-H17079-A1","no":1,"noLabel":{},"text":{"en":"All facilities of the Ord-\nnance Commercial Vehicle Unit of the United States Army,\n- 2 -\nAno was on went on st and Partiothes, may we turn to velviran\npersonnel now forming part of said unit, shall. likewise\nbe transferred to the METROPOLITAN TRANSPORTATION SERVICE\nAdministrative Order No. 2, dated June 25, 1945, is-\nsued by the Energency Controi Administrator and all other\norders inconsistent with the provisions of this Order are\nhereby repealed.\nThis Order shall take effect immediatelv.\nDone at the vity of Manila, this 27th day of July,\nin the year of Our Lord, nineteen hundred and forty-five,\nand of the Commonwealth of the Philippines, the tenth.\nSIRGIO OSMENA\nPresident or the Philippines\nBy the President:\nSecretary to the"}}],"pack":"ph-p157"};
  FT["PH-H17080"] = {"id":"PH-H17080","coverage":"full","language":"en","sourceName":"The LawPhil Project — Arellano Law Foundation","sourceUrl":"","fetchedAt":"2026-10-28","articleCount":1,"structureMode":"WHOLE","title":{"zh":null,"en":"MALAGAÑANG BY THE PRESIDENT OF THE PHILIPPINES PROVIDING FOR FACILITIES NECESSARY TO DECIARE EFFECTIVITY OF REPUBLIC ACT NC. 832 IN ALL PROVINCES AND CHARTERED CITIES OF THE PHILIPPINES ACCORDING TO A DEFINITE SCHEDTLE OF DATES.","orig":"MALAGAÑANG BY THE PRESIDENT OF THE PHILIPPINES PROVIDING FOR FACILITIES NECESSARY TO DECIARE EFFECTIVITY OF REPUBLIC ACT NC. 832 IN ALL PROVINCES AND CHARTERED CITIES OF THE PHILIPPINES ACCORDING TO A DEFINITE SCHEDTLE OF DATES."},"level":"law","status":"active","docNumber":"Executive Order No. 59","issuingBody":"President of the Philippines","completenessNote":"全文，共 1 条；逐字取自 LawPhil PDF 文本化成果（第三方 OCR，非机翻），原始文件 EO_00059_1954.txt","textQuality":"ocr-vendor","sourceFile":"菲律宾/法律原文/07_行政命令_EO/EO_00059_1954.txt","country":"PH","countryName":"菲律宾","layer":"intl","articles":[{"id":"PH-H17080-A1","no":1,"noLabel":{},"text":{"en":"- 2 -\nthe schedule of dates attached hereto as Appendix A, when the\nfacilities necessary to implement the law will have already been\nestahlished;\nNOW, THERETORE, I, RAMON MACSAYSAY, President of the Philip-\npines, by virtue of the powers vested in me by law, do hereby or'er:\n1. That the business of manufacturine, distributing and sell-\nine Premix Rice now being undertaken by the National Rice and Corn\nCorporation shall be transferred and entmisted to private enterprises.\n/\n2. That the NAPIC Premix Plant facilities shall he leased im-\nmediately by the National Rice and Corn Corporation under reasonahle\nterms not later than Movem'er 30, 1954, to a competent private party\nwho, in the opinion of the Secretary of Health, can satisfactorily\ncarmr out the commercial phase involved for the successful imnle-\nmentation of the law, and who will cooperate with the Department'\nof Health in the promotion of Rice Enrichment in the Philippines.\n3. That dollar allocation for the importation of the vitamins\nand chemicals needed for the manufacture of the Premix' Rice shall\nhe set aside yearly in such amounts as may he required, and assigned\nto bona-fide manufacturers of Premix Rice as certified by the Sec-\nretary of Health, to be used exclusively by said manufacturers for\nthe manufacture of Premix Rice only.\n4. That the amount, of P100, 000 shall be immediately released\nfrom the balance of the appropriation in Republic Act No. 832 to\nthe Institute of Nutrition, Department of Health, to be used for\nthe purchase, , transportation, sales and installation of approved\nfeeders as facility required by Republic Act No.\nimplementation.\n5. That the National Shipyards and Steel Corporation shall\nmanufacture and deliver the tie of feeders as approved by the\nDepartment of Health accordin to purchase orders issued to it\nhy the Institute of Nutrition, Department of Health, in Quantities\nup to 500 units per, month, and that at least 505 of the invoice\nvalue shall he parable to the MASSCO in advance, and fuls payment\nof the balance thereof shall be made within ninety (90) days after\ndelivery of each order.\n6. That the Denartment of Health shall encourare the man-\nfacture and sale of approved feeders by private firms, provided\nthat, the prices are comnetitive with those of the National. Ship-\nyards and Steel.\nCorporation.\n7. That the Department, of Health and its agencies shall\nundertake the distribution and sale of approved feeders to each\nand every rice miller in the Philippines at actual cost under\n- 3 -\nsuch a system as to allow rice millers to readily procure and\ninstall them not later than thirty (30) days before the dates\nof effectivity of the law in their resnective localities.\n9. That each rice miller shall, on his account and respon-\nsihility, procure and install the feeder in his rice mill not\nlater than thirty (30) days before the date of effectivity of\nthe law in the locality where his rice mill is erected.\n9. That the Department of Health is hereby empowered to\nissue such orders, males and regulations as are necessary to\nimnlement this Order and to control. and supervise the price and\ncuality of the Premix Rice manufactured and distributed by the\nprivate firms.\n10. That the balance of the original appropriation of\n1300,000 in Repuhlic Act No. 832 shall be immediately released\nfor the implementation of this Order.\n11. That the Decartment of Health shall encourare competi-\ntion in the production and distrihution of Premix Rice, provided\nthat such competition will not adversely affect the wiversal an-\nplication of the Act.\nThis Executive Order shall take effect immediately.\nDone in the City of Manila, this 24th daw of Aumist, in the\nyear of Our lord, nineteen hundred and fifty-four, and of the\nIndependence of the Philippines, the ninth.\n(Sea.) RAMON MAGSAYSAY\nPresident, of the Fhilippines\nBy the President:\n(Sad.) FRED RUIZ CASTRO\n#59\n(Appendix to Fixecutive\nAPPENDIX MAI\nRepublic of the Philionines\nDEPARTMENT OF HEALTH\nOFFICE OF THE SECRETARY\nThe President of the Fhilipoines\nMalacañang\nI hereby certify that all provinces and cities in the\nPhilippines where Republic Act No. 832 is not yet declared\neffective will have already had the necessary facilities\nto implement said Act thirty (30) days after the dates, in-\ndicated hereunder:\n1955\n1\n- City of Manila\nProvince of Rizal\nQuezon City\nDarupan City\n- Province of:\nNueva Eci.ja\nNueva Mizcava\nMindoro Oriental\nMindoro Occidental\nCabanatuan\n- Province of:\nMarinduque\nMountain Province\n- 2 _\n- Province of:\nIlocos Norte\n1956\n- Province of:\nCamarines Norte\nCamarines Sur\nCatanduanes\n_ Province of:\nNegros Oriental\nOriental Misamis\nOccidental Misamis\n- Province of:\n7 3 -\n- Province of:\nZamboanga del Norte\nZamboanga del Sur\nVery respectfully,\n(Sed.) PAULINO J. GARCIA, M,D.\nSecretary of Health"}}],"pack":"ph-p157"};
  FT["PH-H17081"] = {"id":"PH-H17081","coverage":"full","language":"en","sourceName":"The LawPhil Project — Arellano Law Foundation","sourceUrl":"","fetchedAt":"2026-10-28","articleCount":1,"structureMode":"WHOLE","title":{"zh":null,"en":"MALACANANG RESIDENCE OF THE PRESIDENT OI<' THE PHILIPPINES BY THE PRESIDENT OF 'l'HE PHILIPPINES 1955, ESTABLISHING THE CLASSIFICATION OF","orig":"MALACANANG RESIDENCE OF THE PRESIDENT OI<' THE PHILIPPINES BY THE PRESIDENT OF 'l'HE PHILIPPINES 1955, ESTABLISHING THE CLASSIFICATION OF"},"level":"law","status":"active","docNumber":"Executive Order No. 59","issuingBody":"President of the Philippines","completenessNote":"全文，共 1 条；逐字取自 LawPhil PDF 文本化成果（第三方 OCR，非机翻），原始文件 EO_00059_1963.txt","textQuality":"ocr-vendor","sourceFile":"菲律宾/法律原文/07_行政命令_EO/EO_00059_1963.txt","country":"PH","countryName":"菲律宾","layer":"intl","articles":[{"id":"PH-H17081-A1","no":1,"noLabel":{},"text":{"en":"ing Quezon Boulevard, Davao City, from Km. 364.306 to\nRm. 366.481, a distance of 2.175 kilometers, as a na-\ntional secondary road.\nDone in the City of Manila, this 19th day of December,\nin the year of Our Lord, nineteen hundred and sb..1.y-\nBy the President:\nSALVADOR L. MARINO\nDIOSDADO MACAPAGAL\nPresident of tll e Phil'ilJ1Jines\nActin9 E:cecntille SeCl'eta1'Y"}}],"pack":"ph-p157"};
  FT["PH-H17082"] = {"id":"PH-H17082","coverage":"full","language":"en","sourceName":"The LawPhil Project — Arellano Law Foundation","sourceUrl":"","fetchedAt":"2026-10-28","articleCount":1,"structureMode":"WHOLE","title":{"zh":null,"en":"MALACAITA!O RESIDENCE OF DID PRESIDEITT OF ME PITLIPPINES BY THD PRESIDENT OF THE PHILIPPINES IXECUTIVE ORDER NO. 59 REQUIRING THE ESTABLISHMBIT OF ROTC UINTS IN COLLEGES AID UNIVERSITIES..","orig":"MALACAITA!O RESIDENCE OF DID PRESIDEITT OF ME PITLIPPINES BY THD PRESIDENT OF THE PHILIPPINES IXECUTIVE ORDER NO. 59 REQUIRING THE ESTABLISHMBIT OF ROTC UINTS IN COLLEGES AID UNIVERSITIES.."},"level":"law","status":"active","docNumber":"Executive Order No. 59","issuingBody":"President of the Philippines","completenessNote":"全文，共 1 条；逐字取自 LawPhil PDF 文本化成果（第三方 OCR，非机翻），原始文件 EO_00059_1967.txt","textQuality":"ocr-vendor","sourceFile":"菲律宾/法律原文/07_行政命令_EO/EO_00059_1967.txt","country":"PH","countryName":"菲律宾","layer":"intl","articles":[{"id":"PH-H17082-A1","no":1,"noLabel":{},"text":{"en":"3. A11 ROTO/WATC fees and contributions collected\nby the colloges and univorsities concerned shall bo\nexponded exclusively in the operation and maintenance\nof the ROTC/WATC Units established therein except as\nprovided in paragrach 2 hereof in accordance with the\npolicies and regulations to be prescribed jointly by\nthe Secretary of National Defense, Secretary of Edu-\ncation and the President of the State Colloge or Uni-\nversity concerned, and approved by the residont of\nthe Philippines,\n4. ROTO instruction shall be scheduled at such\nhours and on such days of the work, including Satur-\ndays and Sundays, as shall be necessary to complete\nthe ROTC requirements.\nThe Secretery of National\nDefenso, Secretary of ducation and the President of\nthe State College or University concerned shall jointly\nprescribe the regulations for this purpose.\n5. By authority of lot lunbered twenty- seven\nhundred and six, as amended by Comnonwealth Act Nun-\nbered one hundred eighty, failure on the part of\nany institution herein before mentioned, now recog-\nnized by the Government, to comply with che Order\nor the milos and regulations prescribed pursuant\nthereto, shall be sufficient cause for the Secretary\nof Education to have such recognition withdraw.\n6. Tailure on the vart of State Colleges and\nUniversities to comply with this Order shall subject\nthe responsible officials thoreof to administrative\n7. Mo institution of learning required to os-\ntablish an ROTC course under this Ordor shall be\ngranted Government rocomition unless its curricula\ninclude the prescribed course of military instruc-\n8, No exemption of this Order shall be granted\nexcept by spccific direction of the President of the\nPhilippines upon the favorable recommendation of the\nSecrotary of Education through the Secretary of\nNational Defense.\n119\n9. The Secretary of Mational Defense shall in-\nclude in the ROTC Course herein provided instruction\nand training to prepare the fenale students for en-\nlisted and/or commissioned service in the Women's\nAuxiliary Corps.\nHowever, tho establishment of such\nWomen's Auxiliary Corps courses, shall be optional on\nthe part of the institution of learning, and enroll-\nment therein shall be voluntary on the part of the\n10, Executive Order No. 207, dated June 15, 1939,\nand rules and regulations inconsistont with this Order,\nare hereby repealed,\n11. This Order shall take effect upon approval.\nDone in the City of Manila, this 8th day of Feb-\nruary in the year of Our Lord, nineteen hundred and\nsixty-seven.\n(SOD.) FERDINAND D.\nFresident of the Philippines\nBy the President:\n(SOD.) RAFAEL M. SALAS\nExecutive Secretary\n120"}}],"pack":"ph-p157"};
