  FT["PH-H17085"] = {"id":"PH-H17085","coverage":"full","language":"en","sourceName":"The LawPhil Project — Arellano Law Foundation","sourceUrl":"","fetchedAt":"2026-10-28","articleCount":4,"structureMode":"ARTICLE","title":{"zh":null,"en":"PM.S II BRARY BY mEPR:ESIDE~OF THE PillLIPPlNES THE PHILIPPINE PORTS AUTHORITY IMPLEMENT A PROGRAM FOR FURTHER RATIONALIZATION, MODERNIZATION AND IMPROVEMENT OF PORT SERVICES AND FACILITIES IN GOVERNMENT PORTS","orig":"PM.S II BRARY BY mEPR:ESIDE~OF THE PillLIPPlNES THE PHILIPPINE PORTS AUTHORITY IMPLEMENT A PROGRAM FOR FURTHER RATIONALIZATION, MODERNIZATION AND IMPROVEMENT OF PORT SERVICES AND FACILITIES IN GOVERNMENT PORTS"},"level":"law","status":"active","docNumber":"Executive Order No. 59","issuingBody":"President of the Philippines","completenessNote":"全文，共 4 条；逐字取自 LawPhil PDF 文本化成果（第三方 OCR，非机翻），原始文件 EO_00059_1998.txt","textQuality":"ocr-vendor","sourceFile":"菲律宾/法律原文/07_行政命令_EO/EO_00059_1998.txt","country":"PH","countryName":"菲律宾","layer":"intl","articles":[{"id":"PH-H17085-A2","no":2,"noLabel":{"en":"SEC 2"},"text":{"en":"Unification and rationalization\nof all facility operators and\nservice providers.\nPursuant to the policy above stated, the PPA shall immediately\nfor integration,\nunification\nrationalization\nof all facility operators and service providers in ports\nwith high passenger and cargo volume, including\nHarbor in the Port of Manila. Toward this end, the PPA shall:\nproviders such as cargo handling operators, shipping companies\nand port workers and labor to unify into one corporation\nmerger, consolidation,\nor by any other\nsimilar means;\nother qualified\nproviders to invest in and join the unified contra,ctor, provided that\n(i) these other contractors\nshall provide needed technical\nmanagement\ncontribute\nresources for the operation and development of port\nservices and facilities or generate significant transhipment\nand (ii) no single corporation shall be allowed to own more than\n30% of the outstanding capital stock of a unified operator in a port,\nexcept in the port where such corporation has an existing permit,\ncargo handling\nlicense, or operating\ncontract from the PPA or\nwhere the vessels of the investor shipping company regularly call;\n(c) Exercise its authority\nunder its charter to grant the\nunified contractor a contract to manage, operate and develop the\nentire government port \\vithout need of a public bidding;\n,\n~\nIEEHologram;\n2\n\n...(d).Re,q~~e. th,e unified ~o~tractor tQ adopt and ~prove :the.\ntenns and conditions of a stock option plan which shall reserve for\nlabor. and employees of the unified contractor, including those who\nmay be retrenched due to redundancy five p~rcent (5%) 'of its total\noutstanding capital stock;\nNot later than the beginning of the fifth year of its contract,\nthe unified contractor shall start a divestment program offering at\nleast 30% of its authorized capital stock to the public.\n(e) Complete the unification\nof facility operators and service\nproviders as set forth in this executive order within twelve (12)\nmodernization;"}},{"id":"PH-H17085-A3","no":3,"noLabel":{"en":"SEC 3"},"text":{"en":"Functions and responsibilities\nof the unified contractor.\nThe unified\ncontractor\nshall have, among others, the following\nfunctions and responsibilities\nunder its contract to manage, operate and\ndevelop an entire government port:\n(a) Provide all the port services such as the allocation ofberth\nto vessels and the management of berths, tug assistance,.\ncargo and passenger handling,\ncranage, marshalling,\ntransit storage, warehousing,\nweighing, checking and surveying,\nporterage, port security,\nsupply of fuel and water, bunker and\nchandling supply, and others required by the users and clients of\nof necessary\nmaterials, and collect such corresponding fees and charges as may\nbe approved by PPA.\n(b) Grant subleases of port areas and buildings to various\nport users, clients and service companies or in general, undertake\noverall management of the port real estate and other port facilities,\nand collect rents due therefrom.\nmaintenance\nmaintenance dredging of its immediate berthing areas and turning\nbasin) of all existing and future facilities, fIXtures and equipment at\nits own account.\n111~11111111111111~11111111\n\n.-physically\ndevelbp,s:ubj.ect.\nto ?-PP-foval by\nthe authority,\nthe horizontal\nvertical infrastructure\ncapital dredging ~t its own account.\nIn every case where PPA determines a -need for\nterminal facilities, construction\nthereof shall commence withm six\nfrom the effectivity\nof its contract\noperational within the second year of said contract.\n(e) Undertake\nactivities\nnew port clients\npromote additional business for the port.\n(f) Provide personnel, equipment and systems for the security\nof cargoes, equipment and facilities, as well as control the entry\nand e~t of vehicles and persons in its delineated operational area."}},{"id":"PH-H17085-A4","no":4,"noLabel":{"en":"SEC 4"},"text":{"en":"Functions retained by PPA.\nNotwithstanding\nmanagement,\ndevelopment of the port to the unified contractor, the PPA shall continue\nto perform therein its regulatory functions\nand exercise the following\ninherent duties:\n(a) Approve the master and development plan of the ports in\nsupport to the national port planning and development thrusts;\n:\nservice and\n(c) Maintain its tariff setting functions;\n(d) Be responsible for harbor traffic management and the\nregulation of pilotage services;\n(e) Collect port and vessel charges due to the government;\n(f) Conduct periodic audit of the operations of the operator;\ncompliance\nwith the terms and conditions\n(h) Maintain its police functions.\n4\n\nMinimum:terms\nand conditions of the contract.\ncontract shall- contain the following\nconditions:\n.'\n(a) Notwithstanding\nthe award of its management, operation\nand the development to the unified\ncontractor,\nthe port shall\n.\ncontinue to be operated as common user, m:ulti'-purpose facility.\n-'(b) The unified contractor shall pay to the PPA a government\nshare -,. or a fIXed contr~ct fee with an escalation rate for the\nsucceeding years.\nIn addition,\napd in order for government to\nshare in the growth and development of fue port, the unified\ncontractor shall pay a variable fee to PPA which shall be a certain\npercentage' of its revenue from operations based on cargo ton,\ngross revenue or some other parameters.\n(c) The PPA shall collect vessel and port charges from port\nusers at private port rates.\n(d) The unified contractor shall be jointly and severally liable\nfor the payment of vessel and port charges due to the PPA from its\nport users and clients.\n(e) Upon expiration of the initial terms of the contract or in\nthe event of its termination or cancellation prior to its expiration by\nthe unified contractor,\nall existing permanent or semi-permanent\nimprovements,\nstructures,\nbuildings and facilities constructed\nor belonging to the unified contractor and situated in its delineated\noperational\narea shall automatically\nbecome the property of the\ngovernment without any obligation to reimburse, free from any lien\nor encumbrances.\n(f) The unified contractor shall comply with all laws, rules\nand regulations, and issuances.\nProtection of labor.\nIn implementing the foregoing mandate, the PPA shall ensure the\nprotection of labor and their legitimate rights under the law. The existing\ncargo handling or other service operators shall be primarily responsible\nfor the past service benefits and retirement/ separation benefits of their\nemployees and contractual\nIn the event the operator is\n\nmsolvent, fue linified\nconti-actor shall assume the- obligation of paying\nbenefi~s, without\nprej1.1diceto its right--of recourse a-gainsrthe\ninsolvent operator.\n\\\n7.\nAbsorption of labor.\nSubject to its own qualification\nstandards, the unified contractor\nshall absorb into its operations and manpower pool the labor force of the\nexisting operators whose contracts and services shall have been taken\nover. If the actual operational requirements\nshow a need to reduce the\nlabor force, the unified contractor,\nbefore resorting to any other legal\nremedy or action, shall offer to the employees concerned (a) a voluntary\nretirement program, (b) a viable skills training\nor retraining program to\nallow them to be assigned in any vacant positions\nin the company,\nand/ or other post-employment\nassistance programs\nupon such terms\nand conditions consistent with labor laws or the provisions of applicable\ncollective bargaining agreements, whichever shall be more favorable to\nthe employees seeking voluntary retirement.\nThe unified\ncontractor\nbe required\nto respect existing\ncollective bargaining agreements to provide contractual\nbenefits under\nsuch collective bargaining agreements as well as those found in existing\nSocial amelioration fund.\nThe PPA, under such terms and conditions it may prescribe, shall\nthe unified\ncontractor\nimmediately\ncommencement\nof its operations,\na social atnelioration\nfund for the\nbenefit of legitimate port labor.\n9.\nInter-modal\ntransportation\nThe DOTC shall prepare, in coordination with the Department of\nPublic Works and Highways, the Philippine National Railways, the Light\nRail Transit Authority,\nthe PPA and other relevant agencies, a master\nplan to develop an inter-modal\ntransportation\nsystem which would\nconnect high passenger and carg~ volume ports to mass transport\nsystems and facilities such as the rail system, to facilitate the efficient\nand safe movement of passenger and cargo.\n-\nI~IIIIIIIIIII!IIIIIIIIIIIII\n6\n\nOther agencies support.\n:All government departments,\noffices, agencies, instrumentalities,\ngovernment-owned\nand cQntrolled corporations -are hereby\nordered to support and assist ilie PPA in the implementati~n\nexecutive order.\n.'"}},{"id":"PH-H17085-A11","no":11,"noLabel":{"en":"SEC 11"},"text":{"en":"Implementing Rules_,\nThe PPA shall issue the necessary rules and regulations\nimplement this executive order, except for the implementation of Sections\n8 and 9 of this Executive Order which shall be handled by the DOTC.\nRepealing Clause.\nThis executive order repeals or amends all executive, department\nagency issuances\nor any provision\nthereof inconsistent\nSeparability .\nIf any provision of this executive order is declared invalid by a\ncourt of competent jurisdiction,\nit shall not adversely affect any other\nprovision of this executive order.\nEffectivity .\nThis executive order shall take effect fifteen (15) days after its\npublication in a newspaper of general circulation.\nDONE in the City of Manila this 28th day of December in the year of\nOur Lord, Nineteen Hundred and Ninety Eight.\n-6 \"\"'(~~~:~~\n~\n(====::::~\"\".-\nBy the President:\nrr.-iS LIBRARY\nExecutive Secretary\n\\\\\\\\\\\\1\\\\1\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"}}],"pack":"ph-p157"};
  FT["PH-H17086"] = {"id":"PH-H17086","coverage":"full","language":"en","sourceName":"The LawPhil Project — Arellano Law Foundation","sourceUrl":"","fetchedAt":"2026-10-28","articleCount":1,"structureMode":"WHOLE","title":{"zh":null,"en":"MALACAÑANG BY THE PRESIDENT OF THE PHILIPPINES AUTHORIZING THE FILOIL DEVELOPMENT AND MANAGEMENT CORPORATION TO SEGREGATE AND DISPOSE OF ITS PROPERTIES IN NOVELETA AND ROSARIO, CAVITE TO ITS BONAFIDE","orig":"MALACAÑANG BY THE PRESIDENT OF THE PHILIPPINES AUTHORIZING THE FILOIL DEVELOPMENT AND MANAGEMENT CORPORATION TO SEGREGATE AND DISPOSE OF ITS PROPERTIES IN NOVELETA AND ROSARIO, CAVITE TO ITS BONAFIDE"},"level":"law","status":"active","docNumber":"Executive Order No. 59","issuingBody":"President of the Philippines","completenessNote":"全文，共 1 条；逐字取自 LawPhil PDF 文本化成果（第三方 OCR，非机翻），原始文件 EO_00059_2001.txt","textQuality":"ocr-vendor","sourceFile":"菲律宾/法律原文/07_行政命令_EO/EO_00059_2001.txt","country":"PH","countryName":"菲律宾","layer":"intl","articles":[{"id":"PH-H17086-A1","no":1,"noLabel":{},"text":{"en":"24,746\nRosario, Cavite\nRosario, Cavite\nRosario, Cavite\nRosario, Cavite\nRosario, Cavite\nNoveleta, Cavite\nNoveleta, Cavite\nRosario, Cavite\nRosario, Cavite\nRosario, Cavite\nPOMA Outgoing * 07130\n2\n610\n.\n727\n728\n633\n687\n686\n691\n662\n765\n632\n634\n689\n688\n19,162\n1,575\n345\n398\n229\n3,149\n4,259\n1,155\n5,104\n26,830\n1,728\n1,218\n6,985\n3,939\n6,400\n5,044\n5,260\n6,486\nRosario, Cavite\nRosario, Cavite\nRosario, Cavite\nRosario, Cavite\nRosario, Cavite\nRosario, Cavite\nRosario, Cavite\nRosario, Cavite\nRosario, Cavite\nRosario, Cavite\nRosario, Cavite\nRosario, Cavite\nRosario, Cavite\nRosario, Cavite\nRosario, Cavite\nRosario, Cavite\nRosario, Cavite\nRosario, Cavite\nIt is also hereby ordered that an inter-agency committee be formed to formulate\nthe Master Development Plan and the implementing guidelines for the proper disposition\nof these properties. The Inter-Agency Committee shall be chaired by FDMC and co-\nchaired by HUDCC, with the following as members: Presidential Commission for the\nUrban Poor (CUP); the local government of Rosario and Noveleta, Cavite; and People's\nOrganizations and Non-government Organizations (POs and NGOs) as may be identified\nby the Chair and Co-Chair.\nIN WITNESS WHEREOF, I have hereunto set my hand and caused the seal of\nthe Republic of the Philippines to be affixed.\nDone in the City of Manila, this 10th day of December\nyear of Our Lord, two thousand and one.\nBy the President:\nALBERTO G. ROMULO\nExecutive Secretary\nPMS LIBRARY\nPOMA Outgoing * 07131\nPMS LIBRARY BCODE002105"}}],"pack":"ph-p157"};
  FT["PH-H17087"] = {"id":"PH-H17087","coverage":"full","language":"en","sourceName":"The LawPhil Project — Arellano Law Foundation","sourceUrl":"","fetchedAt":"2026-10-28","articleCount":4,"structureMode":"ARTICLE","title":{"zh":null,"en":"MALACAÑAN PALACE BY THE PRESIDENT OF THE PHILIPPINES PROVIDING FOR THE AMENDMENT OF EXECUTIVE ORDER (EO) NO. 309 (S. 2004) FOR THE INCLUSION OF OTHER GRAINS IN THE COVERAGE OF THE PHILIPPINE RICE POSTPRODUCTION CONSORTIUM (PRPC) AND CHANGING OF THE NAME OF PRPC INTO \"PHILIPPINE GRAINS POSTPRODUCTION CONSORTIUM","orig":"MALACAÑAN PALACE BY THE PRESIDENT OF THE PHILIPPINES PROVIDING FOR THE AMENDMENT OF EXECUTIVE ORDER (EO) NO. 309 (S. 2004) FOR THE INCLUSION OF OTHER GRAINS IN THE COVERAGE OF THE PHILIPPINE RICE POSTPRODUCTION CONSORTIUM (PRPC) AND CHANGING OF THE NAME OF PRPC INTO \"PHILIPPINE GRAINS POSTPRODUCTION CONSORTIUM"},"level":"law","status":"active","docNumber":"Executive Order No. 59","issuingBody":"President of the Philippines","completenessNote":"全文，共 4 条；逐字取自 LawPhil PDF 文本化成果（第三方 OCR，非机翻），原始文件 EO_00059_2011.txt","textQuality":"ocr-vendor","sourceFile":"菲律宾/法律原文/07_行政命令_EO/EO_00059_2011.txt","country":"PH","countryName":"菲律宾","layer":"intl","articles":[{"id":"PH-H17087-A2","no":2,"noLabel":{"en":"SECTION 2"},"text":{"en":"Functions of PGPC. The PGPC shall identify, coordinate and\npursue priority areas of collaboration among its member institutions, in the area of\nresearch and development and extension to enhance the development of the rice and\nother grains postproduction industry in the Philippines.\nIt shall likewise extend its collaboration with relevant government agencies, State\nUniversities and Colleges (SUCs), Local Government Units (LGUs), and the private\nsector, including foreign counterpart or donor institutions."}},{"id":"PH-H17087-A3","no":3,"noLabel":{"en":"SECTION 3"},"text":{"en":"Repealing Clause. All executive issuances or portions thereof\nwhich are inconsistent with this Executive Order are hereby revoked, amended, or\nmodified accordingly."}},{"id":"PH-H17087-A4","no":4,"noLabel":{"en":"SECTION 4"},"text":{"en":"Separability. If any provision of this Executive Order is declared\ninvalid or unconstitutional, the other provisions unaffected shall remain valid and\nsubsisting."}},{"id":"PH-H17087-A5","no":5,"noLabel":{"en":"SECTION 5"},"text":{"en":"Effectivity. This Executive Order shall take effect immediately upon\npublication in a newspaper of general circulation.\nDONE, in the City of Manila, this 30th day of September\nour Lord, Two Thousand and Eleven.\n, in the year of\nBy the President:\nPAQUITO N. OCHOA, JR.\nExecutive Secretary\nCERTIFIED COPY:\n@tice of the President of the Philionines\nMARIANITU M DIMAANDAL\nDIRECTOR IV\nSO AS 20M GRID V, 204 MALACANANG RECORDS OFFICE"}}],"pack":"ph-p157"};
  FT["PH-H17088"] = {"id":"PH-H17088","coverage":"full","language":"en","sourceName":"The LawPhil Project — Arellano Law Foundation","sourceUrl":"","fetchedAt":"2026-10-28","articleCount":3,"structureMode":"ARTICLE","title":{"zh":null,"en":"MALACAÑAN PALACE BY THE PRESIDENT OF THE PHILIPPINES ADJUSTING THE DIVIDEND RATE OF THE POWER SECTOR ASSETS AND LIABILITIES MANAGEMENT CORPORATION","orig":"MALACAÑAN PALACE BY THE PRESIDENT OF THE PHILIPPINES ADJUSTING THE DIVIDEND RATE OF THE POWER SECTOR ASSETS AND LIABILITIES MANAGEMENT CORPORATION"},"level":"law","status":"active","docNumber":"Executive Order No. 59","issuingBody":"President of the Philippines","completenessNote":"全文，共 3 条；逐字取自 LawPhil PDF 文本化成果（第三方 OCR，非机翻），原始文件 EO_00059_2018.txt","textQuality":"ocr-vendor","sourceFile":"菲律宾/法律原文/07_行政命令_EO/EO_00059_2018.txt","country":"PH","countryName":"菲律宾","layer":"intl","articles":[{"id":"PH-H17088-A1","no":1,"noLabel":{"en":"SECTION 1"},"text":{"en":"Pursuant to Section 5 of RA No. 7656, the percentage of net\nearnings to be declared and remitted by the PSALM as dividends to the National\nGovernment is adiusted from at least fifty percent (50%) of their annual net earnings\nto 3.3030407%, or an estimated amount of P2.11 Billion, for calendar years 2004,\nTHE PRESIDENT OF THE PHILIPPINES"}},{"id":"PH-H17088-A2","no":2,"noLabel":{"en":"SECTION 2"},"text":{"en":"The adjusted dividend rate set forth in Section 1 of this Order is\nonly applicable to the net earnings of the PSALM for the years stated above."}},{"id":"PH-H17088-A3","no":3,"noLabel":{"en":"SECTION 3"},"text":{"en":"This Order shall take effect immediately.\nDONE, in the City of Manila, this 25th day of\nOur Lord, Two Thousand and Eighteen.\nin the vear of\nBy the President:\nSALVADOR C. MEDIALDEA\nExecutive Secretary\nOffice of the President\nMALACAÑANG RECORDS OFFICE\nCERTIFIED COPY\nREPUBLIC OF THE PHILIPPINES\n007043\n97-24-2028"}}],"pack":"ph-p157"};
  FT["PH-H17089"] = {"id":"PH-H17089","coverage":"full","language":"en","sourceName":"The LawPhil Project — Arellano Law Foundation","sourceUrl":"","fetchedAt":"2026-10-28","articleCount":13,"structureMode":"ARTICLE","title":{"zh":null,"en":"MALACANAN PALACE BY THE PRESIDENT OF THE PHILIPPINES STREAMLINING THE PERMITTING PROCESS FOR INFRASTRUCTURE FLAGSHIP PROJECTS","orig":"MALACANAN PALACE BY THE PRESIDENT OF THE PHILIPPINES STREAMLINING THE PERMITTING PROCESS FOR INFRASTRUCTURE FLAGSHIP PROJECTS"},"level":"law","status":"active","docNumber":"Executive Order No. 59","issuingBody":"President of the Philippines","completenessNote":"全文，共 13 条；逐字取自 LawPhil PDF 文本化成果（第三方 OCR，非机翻），原始文件 EO_00059_2024.txt","textQuality":"ocr-vendor","sourceFile":"菲律宾/法律原文/07_行政命令_EO/EO_00059_2024.txt","country":"PH","countryName":"菲律宾","layer":"intl","articles":[{"id":"PH-H17089-A1","no":1,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 1"},"text":{"en":"Coverage. Pursuant to Section 3 of RA No. 9485, as amended, this Order\nshall apply to all GAs, including government-owned or -controlled corporations and other\ngovernment instrumentalities, as well as LGUs, involved in the issuance of licenses,\nclearances, permits, certifications or authorizations that are required for projects included in\nthe NEDA Board-approved list of IFPs."}},{"id":"PH-H17089-A2","no":2,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 2"},"text":{"en":"Streamlined Requirements for IPs. No other national or local permit\nor clearance shall be required in the construction, installation, repair, operation, and/or\nmaintenance of IPs except for the following:\na. Environmental Compliance Certificate/Certificate of Non-Coverage issued by the\nDepartment of Environment and Natural Resources;\nb. Building Permit/Occupational Permit/Certificate of Occupancy issued by the\nCity/Municipal Building Official;\nc. Excavation Permit issued by the concerned LGU, National Commission for Culture and\nthe Arts, Metropolitan Manila Development Authority, Department of Public Works and\nHighways (DPWH), and/or the Bases Conversion and Development Authority; and\nd. Other requirements as mandated by the Constitution and existing laws.\nThe streamlined reguirements shall apply to all pending and new applications\nsubmitted by GAs and LGUs for projects included in the NEDA Board-approved list of"}},{"id":"PH-H17089-A3","no":3,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 3"},"text":{"en":"Simplification and Streamlining Process. All GAs and LGUs are\nhereby directed to comply with the provisions of RA No. 9485, as amended, and its\nImplementing Rules and Regulations (IRR). To this end, all GAs and LGUs involved in the\nissuance of licenses, clearances, permits, certifications or authorizations for IFPS shall\nreview their respective Citizen's Charters in order to remove redundant and burdensome\nprocedures and requirements, and ensure that the revised procedures and requirements\nare accessible to the transacting public, in accordance with existing laws, rules and\nregulations.\nConsistent with Section 9 of RA No. 9485, as amended, the number of signatories in\nany document shall be limited to a maximum of three (3) signatures pertaining to the officers\ndirectly supervising the office or department responsible. When applicable, GAs and LGUs\nare encouraged to apply and utilize the Philippine National Public Key Infrastructure service\nof the Department of Information and Communications Technology (DICT)."}},{"id":"PH-H17089-A4","no":4,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 4"},"text":{"en":"Online and/or Electronic Submission and Acceptance. Pursuant to\nthe Zero-Contact Policy under RA No. 9485, as amended, all GAs and LGUs are hereby\ndirected to adopt a system for online and/or electronic submission and acceptance of\napplications for, and issuance of licenses, clearances, permits, certifications or\nauthorizations relative to the implementation of IPs.\nFurther, GAs and LGUs shall accept electronic copies of documentary\nrequirements needed for applications for licenses, clearances, permits, certifications or\nauthorizations for IFPS, and recognize electronic or digital signatures, subject to RA No.\n8792 and other existing laws, rules and regulations.\n2"}},{"id":"PH-H17089-A5","no":5,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 5"},"text":{"en":"Simultaneous Processing of Applications. All GAs and LGUs\ninvolved in the issuance of licenses, clearances, permits, certifications or authorizations for\nimplementation of IPs shall process the same with the presumption that relevant\ndocuments from other agencies have already been issued consistent with Rule VII Section\n3(c) of the IRR of RA No. 9485, as amended. The applicant shall execute an Affidavit of\nUndertaking, stating that it has secured all relevant documents from specific GAs or LGUs\nand/or that it shall submit the complete documentary requirements within thirty (30) working\ndays. For this purpose, the NGA or LGU may coordinate with other relevant offices or\nagencies to check or verify the status of applications pending with them. The concerned\nagency shall then issue the corresponding permits or licenses, with an annotation that it\nshall be subject to the completion of requirements covered by the undertaking."}},{"id":"PH-H17089-A6","no":6,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 6"},"text":{"en":"Digital Payment of Fees. To supplement over-the-counter payments, all\nGAs are directed, and all LGUs are encouraged to set up a payment gateway for\nacceptance of digital payments relative to applications for licenses, clearances, permits,\ncertifications or authorizations for IFPS, consistent with the Zero-Contact Policy under RA\nNo. 9485, as amended, and EO No. 170. In this regard, NGAs and LGUs may provide\nalternative digital payment options through service agreements with Bangko Sentral g\nPilipinas (BSP)-regulated private and/or public Payment System Providers (PSP) or\nelectronic Payment and Collection System Providers, subject to existing laws, rules and\nregulations."}},{"id":"PH-H17089-A7","no":7,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 7"},"text":{"en":"Action on the Application. All covered applications not acted upon\nwithin the prescribed period as provided under existing laws, shall be deemed approved\npursuant to Section 10 of A No. 9485, as amended; Provided, that all documentary\nrequirements have been submitted and all required fees have been paid, as indicated in the\nCitizen's Charter of concerned GAs and LGUs.\nSimilarly, if an NGA or LGU fails to act on an application or request for renewal of a\nlicense, clearance, permit, certification or authorization relative to the implementation of\nIFPs within the prescribed processing period, the validity of said license, clearance, permit,\ncertification, or authorization shall be deemed extended."}},{"id":"PH-H17089-A8","no":8,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 8"},"text":{"en":"One-Stop Shop for IPs. All GAs and LGUs shall set up or designate\nwithin their offices a One-Stop Shop for IPs, which will provide frontline services to\napplicants who are securing licenses, clearances, permits, certifications or authorizations\nfor IPs, subject to existing laws, rules and regulations.\nThe One-Stop Shop for IPs shall not be duplicative of existing One-Stop Shops or\nOne-Stop Action Centers established under existing laws, issuances, rules and regulations.\nIn this regard, GAs and LGUs may opt to integrate this One-Stop Shop for IPs into their\nexisting One-Stop Shops or Action Centers. For this purpose, an Account Officer, who shall\nserve as the focal person for facilitating the permits and licenses for IPs, and coordinating\nwith other permitting and licensing agencies or offices, shall be designated in every\nOne-Stop Shop for IPs."}},{"id":"PH-H17089-A9","no":9,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 9"},"text":{"en":"Data Sharing System. To ensure seamless data and information sharing\namong concerned departments, offices, and agencies, all GAs shall automate and\ncomputerize their database in accordance with RA No. 10173 or the \"Data Privacy Act of\n2012,\" and other existing laws, rules and regulations.\n3\n\nLGUs, in coordination with the DICT, are encouraged to adopt the electronic-LGU\n(eLGU) system or any similar program developed and maintained by the DICT, and ensure\nthe interoperability of their respective Information and Communications Technology\nplatforms for the expedited processing of licenses, clearances, permits, certifications and/or\nauthorizations for IPs."}},{"id":"PH-H17089-A10","no":10,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 10"},"text":{"en":"Implementation. The NEDA Board Committee on Infrastructure shall\nserve as the Steering Committee tasked to provide policy direction for effective\nimplementation of this Order.\nWithin thirty (30) working days from the effectivity of this Order, the Steering\nCommittee shall, in coordination with the Anti-Red Tape Authority, Department of the\nInterior and Local Government, and other relevant agencies, promulgate the necessary\nguidelines to ensure effective and efficient implementation of this Order, including, among\nothers, the establishment of a mechanism to: (a) track and report the compliance of NGAs\nand LGUs involved in the issuance of licenses, clearances, permits, certifications and/or\nauthorizations for IPs; and (b) encourage GAs and LGUs to prioritize and facilitate the\nreview and approval of licenses, clearances, permits, certifications or authorizations for the\nNEDA Board-approved IPs."}},{"id":"PH-H17089-A11","no":11,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 11"},"text":{"en":"Separability. If any part or provision of this Order shall be held invalid\nor unconstitutional, the provisions not affected thereby shall remain in full force and effect."}},{"id":"PH-H17089-A12","no":12,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 12"},"text":{"en":"Repeal. All orders, rules and regulations, and other issuances or parts\nthereof which are inconsistent with the provisions of this Order are hereby repealed or\nmodified accordingly."}},{"id":"PH-H17089-A13","no":13,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 13"},"text":{"en":"Effectivity. This Order shall take effect immediately upon publication in\nthe Official Gazette or in a newspaper of general circulation.\nDONE, in the City of Manila, this 30th\nof our Lord, Two Thousand and Twenty-Four.\nBy the President:\nLUCAS P. BERSAMIN\nExécutive-Secretary\nOffice of the President\nMALACAÑANG RECORDS OFFICE\nCERTIFIED COPY\nF-3-204 ACTING DIRECTOR IV\nREPUBLIC OF THE PHILIPPINES"}}],"pack":"ph-p157"};
  FT["PH-H17090"] = {"id":"PH-H17090","coverage":"full","language":"en","sourceName":"The LawPhil Project — Arellano Law Foundation","sourceUrl":"LawPhil (HTML full text only)  |  https://lawphil.net/executive/execord/eo1936/eo_60_1936.html","fetchedAt":"2026-10-28","articleCount":1,"structureMode":"WHOLE","title":{"zh":null,"en":"Authorizing the Acceptance of Philippine Commonwealth Bonds as Security for All Undertakings for Which the Giving of a Bond or Security Is Required By","orig":"Authorizing the Acceptance of Philippine Commonwealth Bonds as Security for All Undertakings for Which the Giving of a Bond or Security Is Required By"},"level":"law","status":"active","docNumber":"Executive Order No. 60","issuingBody":"President of the Philippines","promulgatedDate":"1936-10-23","completenessNote":"全文，共 1 条；逐字取自 LawPhil PDF 文本化成果（第三方 OCR，非机翻），原始文件 EO_00060_1936_html.txt","textQuality":"ocr-vendor","sourceFile":"菲律宾/法律原文/07_行政命令_EO/EO_00060_1936_html.txt","country":"PH","countryName":"菲律宾","layer":"intl","articles":[{"id":"PH-H17090-A1","no":1,"noLabel":{},"text":{"en":"MALACAÑAN PALACE\nBY THE PRESIDENT OF THE PHILIPPINES\n[ EXECUTIVE ORDER NO. 60, October 23, 1936 ]\nAUTHORIZING THE ACCEPTANCE OF PHILIPPINE COMMONWEALTH BONDS AS SECURITY\nFOR ALL UNDERTAKINGS FOR WHICH THE GIVING OF A BOND OR SECURITY IS REQUIRED\nI, MANUEL L. QUEZON, President of the Philippines, under authority conferred upon me by the\nConstitution and the existing laws, do hereby prescribe the following regulations and instructions for the\nconvenience of all holders of Philippine Commonwealth bonds, and for the guidance of all concerned:\n1. “Philippine Commonwealth bonds” as herein used shall be understood, for the purposes of this Order, to\nmean those referred to in paragraphs (six) and (seven) of section one of the Ordinance appended to the\nConstitution of the Philippines, and in paragraphs (six) and (seven) of section two (a) of Public Act Numbered\none hundred twenty-seven of the Congress of the United States, approved on March twenty-fourth, nineteen\nhundred and thirty-four, commonly known as the Tydings-McDuffie Act, and those to be hereafter issued by\nand under authority of law.\n2. Philippine Commonwealth bonds of any issue or denomination shall be accepted by all officers of the\nCommonwealth of the Philippines at their par value when tendered by the holder in lieu of bonds or other\nsecurity for the due performance or any public contract, obligations, or act required to be done, the due\nperformance of which is by law required to be or may be secured by the giving of bonds or undertakings or\ndeposit of cash security, or when tendered to secure the payment of any customs dues, tax, impost, internal\nrevenue license, firearms license, or other fees or charges imposed by authority of law.\n3. Said bonds shall not be receivable as cash for the payment of any public obligation, but shall be receivable\nas security in all cases where the giving of bonds or other security is provided by authority of law.\n4. When it is desired to tender said bonds as security for any purpose in the manner indicated, the same may\nbe deposited with the Treasurer of the Philippines for all cases arising in the City of Manila, or with the\nnearest provincial treasurer in the provinces. Said officers shall issue to the bondholder a certificate showing\nthe deposit of said bonds, for the particular purpose in view. Deposit slips used in invoicing said bonds to the\nTreasurer of the Philippines or the provincial treasurer shall indicate the number, kind, par value, and\nparticular purpose of the deposit, and that it is desired to use the certificate of deposit as security with a\ndesignated bureau, office, court, province, municipality, or other entity of the Commonwealth, as the case may\n5. The treasurer concerned shall thereupon accept said bond or bonds for deposit, issuing a special certificate\nof deposit therefore, showing briefly the amount and the purpose as indicated in the preceding paragraph.\n6. Such certificate of deposit upon tender to the bureau, office, clerk of court, province, municipality, or other\nentity indicated therein shall be accepted for purposes of security, bond, or suretyship, in the par value shown\nthereon in the same manner as any suitable and sufficient private or surety bond, or “cash in lieu of bond”\nmay be accepted in like circumstances and approved as such by the receiving officer or entity.\n7. Coupons maturing upon such bonds while in public custody as aforesaid may be delivered upon proper\nreceipt to the depositing bondholder under such regulations as the Treasurer of the Philippines may prescribe.\n8. The deposit of Philippine Commonwealth bonds shall not be accepted in cases where the security is to\npermanently remain with the Commonwealth, as for example, to secure a duplicate warrant or check to\nreplace a lost original, but only in those cases where upon compliance with the principal obligation the\nsecurity may be returned. In case of default upon the principal obligation, the bonds are to become the\nproperty of the Commonwealth as in other cases of default or failure where security has been given. The\nprocedure for the return of the bonds to the owner after full compliance with the conditions of the terms upon\nwhich the same were deposited shall be indicated on the special form of certificate of deposit to be used in\nthese cases."}}],"pack":"ph-p157"};
  FT["PH-H17091"] = {"id":"PH-H17091","coverage":"full","language":"en","sourceName":"The LawPhil Project — Arellano Law Foundation","sourceUrl":"","fetchedAt":"2026-10-28","articleCount":1,"structureMode":"WHOLE","title":{"zh":null,"en":"MALACANAN PALACE BY ITED PILSSIDAN OF DIS PHILIPPINGS MABOURIVI ORDER NO. 60 AHENDING INESGULIVA ORDER WAPBRID SSYANTI-SIs, Da DECEMBUR SONTY-ENO, WINDUZEN AMNDRED AND -RING DIS 30ARD OF DOOD INSPSOLION.","orig":"MALACANAN PALACE BY ITED PILSSIDAN OF DIS PHILIPPINGS MABOURIVI ORDER NO. 60 AHENDING INESGULIVA ORDER WAPBRID SSYANTI-SIs, Da DECEMBUR SONTY-ENO, WINDUZEN AMNDRED AND -RING DIS 30ARD OF DOOD INSPSOLION."},"level":"law","status":"active","docNumber":"Executive Order No. 60","issuingBody":"President of the Philippines","completenessNote":"全文，共 1 条；逐字取自 LawPhil PDF 文本化成果（第三方 OCR，非机翻），原始文件 EO_00060_1945.txt","textQuality":"ocr-vendor","sourceFile":"菲律宾/法律原文/07_行政命令_EO/EO_00060_1945.txt","country":"PH","countryName":"菲律宾","layer":"intl","articles":[{"id":"PH-H17091-A1","no":1,"noLabel":{},"text":{"en":"2\nfood standaras for adoption under\n(e) It shall further have such functions,\nnistration 08 0h8 Low, as way 0e Es\nsigned to it by the wireotor of Tealth.\nwhe decisions of the Board shall be advisory\nto the Director of lecita, and shall becone final\nwon sparovel he. the Secretars of Tealth and Publio\nsons at the her of louila, chis 31st day of only,\nIn the Year of our Load, nineteon jundred and forty-five,\nend os sis onomeclul of the inilispines, tha senon.\n110\nPresident of the Philippines\nSo tse President:"}}],"pack":"ph-p157"};
  FT["PH-H17092"] = {"id":"PH-H17092","coverage":"full","language":"en","sourceName":"The LawPhil Project — Arellano Law Foundation","sourceUrl":"","fetchedAt":"2026-10-28","articleCount":1,"structureMode":"WHOLE","title":{"zh":null,"en":"MALACANAN PALACE BY THE PRESIDINT OF THE PHILIPPINES DESIGNATING THE PHILIPPINE NATIONAL BANK AS FISCAL AGENT OF THE REFUBLIC OF THE PHILIPPINES IN THE UNITED STATES AND FOR OTHER FURPOSES.","orig":"MALACANAN PALACE BY THE PRESIDINT OF THE PHILIPPINES DESIGNATING THE PHILIPPINE NATIONAL BANK AS FISCAL AGENT OF THE REFUBLIC OF THE PHILIPPINES IN THE UNITED STATES AND FOR OTHER FURPOSES."},"level":"law","status":"active","docNumber":"Executive Order No. 60","issuingBody":"President of the Philippines","completenessNote":"全文，共 1 条；逐字取自 LawPhil PDF 文本化成果（第三方 OCR，非机翻），原始文件 EO_00060_1947.txt","textQuality":"ocr-vendor","sourceFile":"菲律宾/法律原文/07_行政命令_EO/EO_00060_1947.txt","country":"PH","countryName":"菲律宾","layer":"intl","articles":[{"id":"PH-H17092-A1","no":1,"noLabel":{},"text":{"en":"• 2 -\n6. Receive the appropriation for expenses of Del-\negates to the United Nations Organization and make\ndisbursements therefrom in accordance with rules and\nregulations which the Head of that office may deem pro-\nper to prescribe;\nHandle the working fund of the Purchasing Agency\nin New York, and make disbursements therefrom upon pres-\nentation of duly accomplished purchase vouchers by the\nPurchasing Ageney;\n8. Receive the appropriation for the Office of the\nPurchasing Agent and make disbursements therefrom on\nproperly accomplished vouchers;\n9. Reçeive the fund for payment of pensions and\ngratuities and make disbursements therefrom in accord-\nance with such rules and regulations which the Ambas-\nsador in Washington may deem proper to prescribe;\n10 Continue the redemption of Philippine currencies\nwhich it shall deposit with the Auxiliary Reserve Vault\nCommittee in Washington, D. C.;\n11. Keep appropriate books of accounts to record the\ntransactions involved and to show at all times the bal-\nances of funds in the United States in each depository or\nin the hands of each particular collecting and disbursing\nofficer, the expenses and the available balances of apo\npropriations; and\n12. To carry out such other functions pertaining to\ngovernment finances which the secretary of Finance may,\nwith the approval of the President of the Philippines,\nhereafter authorize.\nAll the powers and duties heretofore exercised by\nthe Philippine Embassy in Washington, D. C. or the Ambas-\nsador thereof in connection with the foregoing functions\nare hereby transferred to, and conferred upon, the Phil-\n1ppine National Bank acting through its Agency in New York.\nThe Secretary of Finance and the Auditor General\nshall prescribe such rules and regulations as may be\n- 3 -\nnecessary to effect the proper handling of, and account-\ning for, the funds and financial transactions of the\nRepublic of the Philippines which the Philippine National\nBank acting through its Agency in New York in its aapacity\nas Fiscal Agent of the Government may hereafter administer.\nThis Order shall take effect immediately.\nDone in the city of Mantla, this 1fWay of June,\nin the year of Our Lord, nineteen hundred and forty-\nseven and of the Independence of the Philippines, the\nPresident ur the Phil ones\nBy the President:\nEMILIO ABETIO\nChief of the Executive Office"}}],"pack":"ph-p157"};
  FT["PH-H17093"] = {"id":"PH-H17093","coverage":"full","language":"en","sourceName":"The LawPhil Project — Arellano Law Foundation","sourceUrl":"","fetchedAt":"2026-10-28","articleCount":1,"structureMode":"WHOLE","title":{"zh":null,"en":"MAL ACAÑ ANG BY THE PRESIDENT OF THE PHILIPPINES DESIGNATING THE BOARD OF LIQUIDATORS CREATED UNDER EXECUTIVE ORDER , DATED NOVIMBER 24, TO LIQUIDATE THE ASSETS AND TTARILT^TES OF TUE TAND SEMITTEMENT AND DEVELOFMENT CORPORATION","orig":"MAL ACAÑ ANG BY THE PRESIDENT OF THE PHILIPPINES DESIGNATING THE BOARD OF LIQUIDATORS CREATED UNDER EXECUTIVE ORDER , DATED NOVIMBER 24, TO LIQUIDATE THE ASSETS AND TTARILT^TES OF TUE TAND SEMITTEMENT AND DEVELOFMENT CORPORATION"},"level":"law","status":"active","docNumber":"Executive Order No. 60","issuingBody":"President of the Philippines","completenessNote":"全文，共 1 条；逐字取自 LawPhil PDF 文本化成果（第三方 OCR，非机翻），原始文件 EO_00060_1954.txt","textQuality":"ocr-vendor","sourceFile":"菲律宾/法律原文/07_行政命令_EO/EO_00060_1954.txt","country":"PH","countryName":"菲律宾","layer":"intl","articles":[{"id":"PH-H17093-A1","no":1,"noLabel":{"en":"SECTION 1"},"text":{"en":"The assets and liahilities of the land Settlement,\nand Development Corporation, otherwise lown as LASBDECO,\nbout heroitito dot M until , shall la tent at 03 in, the 3 dot nor 3,\ndated Novemher 24,'\nThe National Resettlement and Rehabilitation Aminis-\nfrat ShOt Air The National Resettlement and meha tilt at 00 At 60;\nHave from Ensulato are needed by repent dang inni one the sueto 84\nand objectives of Remblic Act No. 1160 and to submit to the Board\nof Liduidators an inventory thereof.\nThe Roard of Licuidators\nshall, with the approval of the President of the Philimines,\nfect the transfer to NAPPA of title to said properties, equirment,\nassets and rights, subject to the provisions of Section 10 of Re-\npahlic Act No. 1160.\nDone in the City of Manila, this 31st day of August, in the\nyear of Our Lord, nineteen hundred and fifty-four, and of the\nIndependence of the Philipnines, the ninth.\n(Sad.) RAMON MAGSAYSAY\nPresident of the Philippines\nBy the President:\n(Sed.) FRBD RIIZ CASTRO"}}],"pack":"ph-p157"};
  FT["PH-H17094"] = {"id":"PH-H17094","coverage":"full","language":"en","sourceName":"The LawPhil Project — Arellano Law Foundation","sourceUrl":"","fetchedAt":"2026-10-28","articleCount":1,"structureMode":"WHOLE","title":{"zh":null,"en":"MALACAÑANG OFFICE OF THE PRESIDENT OF THE PHILIPPINES","orig":"MALACAÑANG OFFICE OF THE PRESIDENT OF THE PHILIPPINES"},"level":"law","status":"active","docNumber":"Executive Order No. 60","issuingBody":"President of the Philippines","completenessNote":"全文，共 1 条；逐字取自 LawPhil PDF 文本化成果（第三方 OCR，非机翻），原始文件 EO_00060_1963.txt","textQuality":"ocr-vendor","sourceFile":"菲律宾/法律原文/07_行政命令_EO/EO_00060_1963.txt","country":"PH","countryName":"菲律宾","layer":"intl","articles":[{"id":"PH-H17094-A1","no":1,"noLabel":{},"text":{"en":"BY THE PRESIDENT OF THE PHILIPPINES\nEXECUTIVE ORDER NO. 60\nDECLARING THAT THE NATIONAL ANTHEM OF THE PHILIPPINES SHALL BE SUNG ONLY TO ITS FILIPINO LYRICS\nWHEREAS, the development and propagation of the National Language of the Philippines is one of the dreams of the heroes of our race, apart from being provided for in the Constitution of our Republic;\nWHEREAS, certain events occurring in our archipelago, and especially in other countries, concerning the singing of our National Anthem in a foreign language are quite conspicuous and are no longer in accord with the spirit of our nationalism; and\nWHEREAS, the Filipino Language is now one of our official languages;\nNOW, THEREFORE, I, DIOSDADO MACAPAGAL, President of the Republic of the Philippines, by virtue of the powers vested in me by law and in pursuance of the objectives of the Constitution and of Commonwealth Act No. 570, do hereby declare and order that the National Anthem of the Philippines shall be sung only to its Filipino lyrics on every occasion, whether here or in other countries.\nDone in the City of Manila, this nineteenth day of December, in the year of Our Lord, nineteen hundred and sixty-three.\n(Signed) DIOSDADO MACAPAGAL\nPresident of the Philippines\nBy the President:\n(Signed) RUFINO G. HECHANOVA\nExecutive Secretary\n[Translated from the original Filipino text.]"}}],"pack":"ph-p157"};
  FT["PH-H17095"] = {"id":"PH-H17095","coverage":"full","language":"en","sourceName":"The LawPhil Project — Arellano Law Foundation","sourceUrl":"","fetchedAt":"2026-10-28","articleCount":4,"structureMode":"ARTICLE","title":{"zh":null,"en":"MALACANANG RESIDENCE OF THE PRESIDENT OF TIE PIILIPPIITES BY THO PRESIDENT OF TUB FMILIPPINES EXECUTIVE ORDER? 1O. 60 PROMULGATING RULES AID REGULATIONS FOR TI CONTROL AND SUPERVISION OF THE IMPORTATION, SALE AND DOSSESSION OF CHMICALS USED AS INGREDIENTS IN THE MANUFACTURE OF EXPLOSIVES AND FOR OTHER","orig":"MALACANANG RESIDENCE OF THE PRESIDENT OF TIE PIILIPPIITES BY THO PRESIDENT OF TUB FMILIPPINES EXECUTIVE ORDER? 1O. 60 PROMULGATING RULES AID REGULATIONS FOR TI CONTROL AND SUPERVISION OF THE IMPORTATION, SALE AND DOSSESSION OF CHMICALS USED AS INGREDIENTS IN THE MANUFACTURE OF EXPLOSIVES AND FOR OTHER"},"level":"law","status":"active","docNumber":"Executive Order No. 60","issuingBody":"President of the Philippines","completenessNote":"全文，共 4 条；逐字取自 LawPhil PDF 文本化成果（第三方 OCR，非机翻），原始文件 EO_00060_1967.txt","textQuality":"ocr-vendor","sourceFile":"菲律宾/法律原文/07_行政命令_EO/EO_00060_1967.txt","country":"PH","countryName":"菲律宾","layer":"intl","articles":[{"id":"PH-H17095-A2","no":2,"noLabel":{"en":"SECTION 2"},"text":{"en":"The Chemicals referred to in Section\n1 hereof shall include, but shall not be limited to,\nthe following:\na, Potassium Chlorato\nb. Nitrates of Armoniun, Potassium and"}},{"id":"PH-H17095-A3","no":3,"noLabel":{"en":"SECTION 3"},"text":{"en":"Only persons or entities issued Permits\nto Purchase certain quantities of any of these chemicals\nby the Firearms and Explosives Office shall be alloved\nto purchase from licensed importers or dealers.\n121"}},{"id":"PH-H17095-A4","no":4,"noLabel":{"en":"SECTION 4"},"text":{"en":"All importers, , dealers and end-users\nof these chemicals are hereby required to securo tho\nnecessary license within three (3) months. from the ap-\nproval of this Order.\nFailure to do so shall be suffi-\ncient ground for tho confiscation of all such chemicals\nin their possession."}},{"id":"PH-H17095-A5","no":5,"noLabel":{"en":"SECTION 5"},"text":{"en":"All holders of permits and licenses\nissued under the provisions of this Executive Order\nshall keep and maintain a permanent record wherein\nall acquisitions, purchasos and dispositions of all\nsuch chemicals shall be entered chronologically, to-\ngether with the name and addresses of all porsons or\nentities to whom they are sold or issued. In the case\nof end users, they shall also maintain a permanent\nrecord indicating theroin chronologically how such\nchemicals were used and disposed of.\nAll entries in\nsaid record shall be supported by their corresponding\npermits issued by the Chief of the Firearms and Explo-\nsives Office of the Philippine Constabulary.\nrecords shall be open for inspection any time by the\npropor authorities.\nSecTIOn 6. Violation of any of the provisions of\nthis Order and the rules and regulations that may be\nissued in implementation thereof shall be sufficient\ncauso for the cancollation of the license and confis-\ncation of all such chemicals in tho possession of the\nlicensee and the imposition of a fine of not less than\n$600 nor more than /2,000, or imprisonment for not less\nthan three (3) months nor more than two (2) years,\nthe discretion of the Court, as provided undor Act No.\n3023. SECTION 7. Exccutivo Order No. 9 dated February\n1, 1954, is amended accordingly.\nSECTION 8, This Order shall take effect after\nfifteen (15) days following its publication in the\nOfficial Gazette.\nDone in the City of Manila, this 9th day of\nFebruary in the year of Our Lord, nineteen hundred and\nsixty-geven.\n(SGD.) FERDINAND B. MARCOS\nPresident of the Philippines\nBy the President:\n(SGD.) RAFADL M. SALAS\nExecutive Secretary\n122"}}],"pack":"ph-p157"};
  FT["PH-H17096"] = {"id":"PH-H17096","coverage":"full","language":"en","sourceName":"The LawPhil Project — Arellano Law Foundation","sourceUrl":"LawPhil (source has HTML full text only)","fetchedAt":"2026-10-28","articleCount":3,"structureMode":"ARTICLE","title":{"zh":null,"en":"Amending Section 4 of Executive Order No. 1061, Entitled \"Establishing the Philippine Rice Research Institute (PRRI)","orig":"Amending Section 4 of Executive Order No. 1061, Entitled \"Establishing the Philippine Rice Research Institute (PRRI)"},"level":"law","status":"active","docNumber":"Executive Order No. 60","issuingBody":"President of the Philippines","promulgatedDate":"1986-11-07","completenessNote":"全文，共 3 条；逐字取自 LawPhil PDF 文本化成果（第三方 OCR，非机翻），原始文件 EO_00060_1986_html.txt","textQuality":"ocr-vendor","sourceFile":"菲律宾/法律原文/07_行政命令_EO/EO_00060_1986_html.txt","country":"PH","countryName":"菲律宾","layer":"intl","articles":[{"id":"PH-H17096-A1","no":1,"noLabel":{"en":"Sec 1"},"text":{"en":"Section 4 of Executive Order No. 1061 is hereby amended to read as follows:\n\"Sec. 4. Board of Trustees The corporate powers of the Institute shall be exercised, and all its business\nactivities and properties shall be controlled by a Board of Trustees, hereinafter referred to as the Board,\ncomposed of the Minister of Agriculture and Food as Ex-Officio Chairman and twelve (12) other members to\nbe appointed by the President of the Philippines upon recommendation of the Minister of Agriculture and\nFood. The appointive members of the Board shall serve for two (2) years.\nThe Board shall meet regularly at least once a quarter or as often as the exigencies of the service demand. The\npresence of at least seven (7) members shall constitute a quorum, and the majority vote of the members\npresent, there being a quorum shall be necessary for the adoption of any resolution, rule, regulation, decision\nor any other act of the Board.\nThe members of the Board, including the Chairman, shall receive per diem, as the Board may determine, for\neach Board Meeting actually attended: Provided, That such per diem shall not exceed Two Thousand Pesos\n(P2,000.00) during any one month for each member. The said members shall also be entitled to reimbursable\ntransportation and representation allowances in going to and coming from Board Meetings and transacting\nofficial business for the Institute.\""}},{"id":"PH-H17096-A2","no":2,"noLabel":{"en":"Sec 2"},"text":{"en":"All laws, orders, issuances, rules and regulations or parts thereof inconsistent with this Executive\nOrder are hereby repealed or modified accordingly."}},{"id":"PH-H17096-A3","no":3,"noLabel":{"en":"Sec 3"},"text":{"en":"This Executive Order shall take effect immediately.\nDone in the City of Manila, this 7th day of November, in the year of Our Lord, nineteen hundred and"}}],"pack":"ph-p157"};
