  FT["PH-H17349"] = {"id":"PH-H17349","coverage":"full","language":"en","sourceName":"The LawPhil Project — Arellano Law Foundation","sourceUrl":"","fetchedAt":"2026-10-28","articleCount":12,"structureMode":"ARTICLE","title":{"zh":null,"en":"MALACAÑAN PALACE BY THE PRESIDENT OF THE PHILIPPINES INSTITUTIONALIZATION OF THE PHILIPPINE QUALIFICATIONS FRAMEWORK","orig":"MALACAÑAN PALACE BY THE PRESIDENT OF THE PHILIPPINES INSTITUTIONALIZATION OF THE PHILIPPINE QUALIFICATIONS FRAMEWORK"},"level":"law","status":"active","docNumber":"Executive Order No. 83","issuingBody":"President of the Philippines","completenessNote":"全文，共 12 条；逐字取自 LawPhil PDF 文本化成果（第三方 OCR，非机翻），原始文件 EO_00083_2012.txt","textQuality":"ocr-vendor","sourceFile":"菲律宾/法律原文/07_行政命令_EO/EO_00083_2012.txt","country":"PH","countryName":"菲律宾","layer":"intl","articles":[{"id":"PH-H17349-A1","no":1,"noLabel":{"en":"SECTION 1"},"text":{"en":"Establishment of the Philippine Qualifications Framework. The\nPhilippine Qualifications Framework (PQF) is hereby established with the flowing\nobjectives: 1) To adopt national standards and levels for outcomes of education; 2) To\nsupport the development and maintenance of pathways and equivalencies which\nprovide access to qualifications and assist people to move easily and readily between\nthe different education and training sectors and between these sectors and the labor\nOffice of the\n\nmarket; and, 3) To align the PQF with international qualifications framework to support\nthe national and international mobility of workers through increased recognition of the\nvalue and comparability of Philippine qualifications."}},{"id":"PH-H17349-A2","no":2,"noLabel":{"en":"SECTION 2"},"text":{"en":"PQF National Coordinating Committee. The PQF National\nCoordinating Committee is hereby created to be Chaired by the Secretary of the\nDepartment of Education (DepEd) with the following as members: a) Technical\nEducation and Skills Development Authority (TESDA); b) Commission on Higher\nEducation (CHED): c) Department of Labor and Employment (DOLE); and, d)\nProfessional Regulations Commission (PRC)."}},{"id":"PH-H17349-A3","no":3,"noLabel":{"en":"SECTION 3"},"text":{"en":"Functions of the PQF National Coordinating Committee. The\nPQF National Coordinating Committee shall issue the Implementing Rules and\nRegulations within sixty days of the effectivity of this EO. It shall also provide regular\nfeedback on the progress and accomplishments to the Office of the President with\nrespect to the implementation of this EO."}},{"id":"PH-H17349-A4","no":4,"noLabel":{"en":"SECTION 4"},"text":{"en":"Participation of the Industry Sector. Industry sector\nrepresentatives shall be consulted and tapped in the detailing and application of the\nPQF to ensure alignment of educational outcomes to job requirements."}},{"id":"PH-H17349-A5","no":5,"noLabel":{"en":"SECTION 5"},"text":{"en":"Level Descriptors. The PQF shall incorporate an 8-level\nQualifications Descriptors defined in terms of the following: knowledge, skills and\nvalues, application, and degree of independence."}},{"id":"PH-H17349-A6","no":6,"noLabel":{"en":"SECTION 6"},"text":{"en":"Learning Standards. DeEd, TESDA and CHED shall make\ndetailed descriptors for each qualification level based on learning standards in basic\neducation, competency standards of training regulations, and the policies and standards\nof higher education academic programs. They shall jointly implement national pilot\nprograms to determine its relevance and applicability in all levels of education."}},{"id":"PH-H17349-A7","no":7,"noLabel":{"en":"SECTION 7"},"text":{"en":"Review of Licensure Examinations. The PRC and CHED shall\nreview the framework and contents of the licensure examinations of each of the\nprofessions and align them with that of the PQF."}},{"id":"PH-H17349-A8","no":8,"noLabel":{"en":"SECTION 8"},"text":{"en":"Technical Secretariat. To ensure efficient and effective\nimplementation, DepEd, TESDA and CHED shall organize from their present staff\ncomplements a permanent Technical Secretariat. The Secretariat may contract the\nservices of technical experts and authorities on relevant areas of concern such as\nequivalencies, accreditation, curriculum development, educational measurement and"}},{"id":"PH-H17349-A9","no":9,"noLabel":{"en":"SECTION 9"},"text":{"en":"Funding. The funds necessary for the implementation of the PQF\nshall be charged against the existing appropriations of DepEd, TESDA and CHED.\n2\nOffice ofthe resident of the Philivines"}},{"id":"PH-H17349-A10","no":10,"noLabel":{"en":"SECTION 10"},"text":{"en":"Repealing Clause. All issuances, orders, rules, and regulations or\nparts thereof which are inconsistent with the provisions of this EO are hereby revoked\nand/or modified accordingly."}},{"id":"PH-H17349-A11","no":11,"noLabel":{"en":"SECTION 11"},"text":{"en":"Separability Clause. If any provision of this EO is declared invalid\nor unconstitutional, the other provisions unaffected shall remain valid and subsisting."}},{"id":"PH-H17349-A12","no":12,"noLabel":{"en":"SECTION 12"},"text":{"en":"Effectivity Clause. This EO shall take effect immediately upon its\npublication in a newspaper of general circulation.\nDONE, in the City of Manila, this Ist day of October\nLord, Two Thousand and Twelve.\n, in the year of our\nBy the President\nPAQUITO N. OCHOA, JR.\nExecutive Secretary\n@ffice of the Prentent of the Philippines\nCERTIFIED COPY:\nMARIANITO M. DIMAANDAL\nDIRECTOR IV\nBE 9 MALACARANG RECORDS OFFICE\n3"}}],"pack":"ph-p157"};
  FT["PH-H17350"] = {"id":"PH-H17350","coverage":"full","language":"en","sourceName":"The LawPhil Project — Arellano Law Foundation","sourceUrl":"","fetchedAt":"2026-10-28","articleCount":6,"structureMode":"ARTICLE","title":{"zh":null,"en":"MALACAÑAN PALACE BY THE PRESIDENT OF THE PHILIPPINES APPROVING AND ADOPTING THE NATIONAL TECHNICAL EDUCATION AND SKILLS DEVELOPMENT PLAN 2018-2022","orig":"MALACAÑAN PALACE BY THE PRESIDENT OF THE PHILIPPINES APPROVING AND ADOPTING THE NATIONAL TECHNICAL EDUCATION AND SKILLS DEVELOPMENT PLAN 2018-2022"},"level":"law","status":"active","docNumber":"Executive Order No. 83","issuingBody":"President of the Philippines","completenessNote":"全文，共 6 条；逐字取自 LawPhil PDF 文本化成果（第三方 OCR，非机翻），原始文件 EO_00083_2019.txt","textQuality":"ocr-vendor","sourceFile":"菲律宾/法律原文/07_行政命令_EO/EO_00083_2019.txt","country":"PH","countryName":"菲律宾","layer":"intl","articles":[{"id":"PH-H17350-A1","no":1,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 1"},"text":{"en":"Approval and Adoption of the NTESDP 2018-2022. The\nNTESDP 2018-2022 is hereby approved. All national government agencies and\ninstrumentalities are hereby enjoined, and all local government units, as well as the\nprivate sector, are hereby encouraged to adopt, disseminate and support the\nimplementation of the NTESDP 2018-2022, and refer to the same in the\ndevelopment and implementation of their respective TVET programs, projects and\nhereby directed to:"}},{"id":"PH-H17350-A2","no":2,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 2"},"text":{"en":"Implementation, Coordination and Monitoring. The TESDA is\na) Ensure that all skills development programs and schemes conform with\nthe quantitative and qualitative obiectives of the NTESDP 2018-2022 and\nTHE PRESIDENT OF THE PHILIPPINES\n\nall skills trainings and development are aligned with the Philippine\nQualifications Framework and all instituted national standards:\nb) Monitor the implementation of the NTESDP 2018-2022, and conduct\nperiodic assessment to evaluate its efficiency and effectivity; and\nc) Submit, through the Department of Trade and Industry, semi-annual\nreports to the Office of the President on the implementation of the"}},{"id":"PH-H17350-A3","no":3,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 3"},"text":{"en":"Funding. The necessary funding for the implementation of the\nNTESDP 2018-2022 shall be sourced from appropriations intended for the skills\ndevelopment and training programs of the TESDA and the respective budgets of\nconcerned GAs, subject to applicable budgeting, auditing and accounting rules and\nregulations."}},{"id":"PH-H17350-A4","no":4,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 4"},"text":{"en":"Separability. Should any provision of this Order be declared\ninvalid or unconstitutional, the other provisions not affected thereby shall remain\nvalid and subsisting."}},{"id":"PH-H17350-A5","no":5,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 5"},"text":{"en":"Repeal. All other issuances inconsistent with the provisions of this\nOrder are hereby repealed or modified accordingly."}},{"id":"PH-H17350-A6","no":6,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 6"},"text":{"en":"Effectivity. This Order shall take effect immediately.\nDONE, in the City of Manila, this 17th day of\nof Our Lord, Two Thousand and Nineteen\nBy the President:\nSALVADOR C. MEDIALDEA\nExecutive Secretary\nREPUBLIC OF THE PHILIPPINES\nOffice of the President\nMALACAÑANG RECORDS OFFICE\nCERTITED COPW\nATTY. CONCENCION A LAY E. FERROLINO-ERAD\n+ 619-2024\nDIRECTOR IV"}}],"pack":"ph-p157"};
  FT["PH-H17351"] = {"id":"PH-H17351","coverage":"full","language":"en","sourceName":"The LawPhil Project — Arellano Law Foundation","sourceUrl":"","fetchedAt":"2026-10-28","articleCount":6,"structureMode":"ARTICLE","title":{"zh":null,"en":"MALACAÑAN PALACE BY THE PRESIDENT OF THE PHILIPPINES REDUCING AND CONDONING REAL PROPERTY TAXES, INCLUDING INTERESTS AND/OR PENALTIES, ASSESSED ON POWER GENERATION FACILITIES OF INDEPENDENT POWER PRODUCERS UNDER BUILD-OPERATE-TRANSFER CONTRACTS WITH GOVERNMENT-OWNED OR -CONTROLLED CORPORATIONS","orig":"MALACAÑAN PALACE BY THE PRESIDENT OF THE PHILIPPINES REDUCING AND CONDONING REAL PROPERTY TAXES, INCLUDING INTERESTS AND/OR PENALTIES, ASSESSED ON POWER GENERATION FACILITIES OF INDEPENDENT POWER PRODUCERS UNDER BUILD-OPERATE-TRANSFER CONTRACTS WITH GOVERNMENT-OWNED OR -CONTROLLED CORPORATIONS"},"level":"law","status":"active","docNumber":"Executive Order No. 83","issuingBody":"President of the Philippines","completenessNote":"全文，共 6 条；逐字取自 LawPhil PDF 文本化成果（第三方 OCR，非机翻），原始文件 EO_00083_2025.txt","textQuality":"ocr-vendor","sourceFile":"菲律宾/法律原文/07_行政命令_EO/EO_00083_2025.txt","country":"PH","countryName":"菲律宾","layer":"intl","articles":[{"id":"PH-H17351-A1","no":1,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 1"},"text":{"en":"Reduction and Condonation. All liabilities for RPTs for CY 2024,\nincluding any special levies accruing to the Special Education Fund, on property,\nmachinery and equipment actually and directly used by IPPs for the production of\nelectricity under BOT scheme and similar contracts, whether denominated as Power\nPurchase Agreements, Energy Conversion Agreements or other contractual\nagreements, with GOCCs, assessed by LGUs and other entities authorized to impose\nRPTs for CY 2024, are hereby reduced to an amount equivalent to the tax due if\ncomputed based on an assessment level of 15% of the fair market value of said\nproperty, machinery and equipment depreciated at the rate of two percent (2%) per\nannum, less any amount already paid by the IPPs. All interests and/or penalties on\nsuch deficiency RPT liabilities are also hereby condoned and the concerned IPs are\nrelieved from payment thereof."}},{"id":"PH-H17351-A2","no":2,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 2"},"text":{"en":"Application to Future RPT Liabilities. All RPT payments made by\nthe IPPs over and above the reduced amount under Section 1 of this Order shall be\napplied to their RPT liabilities for succeeding years."}},{"id":"PH-H17351-A3","no":3,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 3"},"text":{"en":"Compliance by all Government Entities. All concerned\ndepartments, agencies, and instrumentalities, including GOCCs and LGUs, are\nhereby directed to strictly comply with this Order. Any violation of the provisions of this\nOrder shall be dealt with in accordance with relevant laws, rules and regulations.\n2\n\nFor this purpose, the Department of the Interior and Local Government (DILG),\nin coordination with DOF, is hereby directed to monitor the compliance of all concerned\nFurther, within six (6) months from the effectivity of this Order, the DOF shall\nsubmit to the President, through the Office of the Executive Secretary, a progress\nreport on the status of the implementation of this Order."}},{"id":"PH-H17351-A4","no":4,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 4"},"text":{"en":"Separability. If any part or provision of this Order shall be held\ninvalid or unconstitutional, the provisions not affected thereby shall remain in full force"}},{"id":"PH-H17351-A5","no":5,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 5"},"text":{"en":"Repeal. All orders, rules and regulations, and other issuances or\nparts thereof which are inconsistent with the provisions of this Order, are hereby\nrepealed or modified accordingly."}},{"id":"PH-H17351-A6","no":6,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 6"},"text":{"en":"Effectivity. This Order shall take effect immediately upon\npublication in the Official Gazette or in a newspaper of general circulation.\nDONE, in the City of Manila, this 13th\nyear of Our Lord, Two Thousand and Twenty-Five.\nFebruary, in the\nBy the President:\nLUCAS P. BERSAMIN\nExecutive Secretary\nOffice of the President\nMALACAÑAN RECORDS OFFICE\nCERTED COPY\nATTY. LOVELY V. STOLENTINO-NAVA\nDIRECTOR IV\nREPUBLIC OF THE PHILIPPINES\n3"}}],"pack":"ph-p157"};
  FT["PH-H17352"] = {"id":"PH-H17352","coverage":"full","language":"en","sourceName":"The LawPhil Project — Arellano Law Foundation","sourceUrl":"LawPhil (HTML full text only)  |  https://lawphil.net/executive/execord/eo1937/eo_84_1937.html","fetchedAt":"2026-10-28","articleCount":1,"structureMode":"WHOLE","title":{"zh":null,"en":"Ordering the Taking of Complete Classified Data on Real Property Ownership, Improvement, and Assessment Before Census Day, Designating Census Officers to Assist in This Work, and for Other Purposes","orig":"Ordering the Taking of Complete Classified Data on Real Property Ownership, Improvement, and Assessment Before Census Day, Designating Census Officers to Assist in This Work, and for Other Purposes"},"level":"law","status":"active","docNumber":"Executive Order No. 84","issuingBody":"President of the Philippines","promulgatedDate":"1937-01-20","completenessNote":"全文，共 1 条；逐字取自 LawPhil PDF 文本化成果（第三方 OCR，非机翻），原始文件 EO_00084_1937_html.txt","textQuality":"ocr-vendor","sourceFile":"菲律宾/法律原文/07_行政命令_EO/EO_00084_1937_html.txt","country":"PH","countryName":"菲律宾","layer":"intl","articles":[{"id":"PH-H17352-A1","no":1,"noLabel":{},"text":{"en":"MALACAÑAN PALACE\nBY THE PRESIDENT OF THE PHILIPPINES\n[ EXECUTIVE ORDER NO. 84, January 20, 1937 ]\nORDERING THE TAKING OF COMPLETE CLASSIFIED DATA ON REAL PROPERTY OWNERSHIP,\nIMPROVEMENT, AND ASSESSMENT BEFORE CENSUS DAY, DESIGNATING CENSUS OFFICERS\nTO ASSIST IN THIS WORK, AND FOR OTHER PURPOSES\nIn order to prepare the way to the final enumeration on Census Day, as provided in Commonwealth Act\nNumbered One hundred seventy, I, MANUEL L. QUEZON, President of the Philippines, by virtue of the\npower vested in me by sections one and twenty-nine of said Act, hereby order that complete classified data\nbased on the records of real property in the offices of the provincial treasurers, relating to real property\nownership, improvement, and assessment, shall be gathered and compiled, as of March thirty-first, nineteen\nhundred and thirty-seven. All provincial and city treasurers and assessors are hereby designated as Census\nofficers to assist in his work.\nIt is also hereby ordered that such preliminary gathering of other data or information as the Census\nCommissioner may deem fit, may be done anytime before Census Day.\nDone at the City of Manila, this twentieth day of January, in the year of Our Lord, nineteen hundred and\nthirty-seven, and of the Commonwealth of the Philippines, the second.\n(Sgd.) MANUEL L. QUEZON\nPresident of the Philippines\nBy the President:\n(Sgd.) ELPIDIO QUIRINO\nSecretary of the Interior"}}],"pack":"ph-p157"};
  FT["PH-H17353"] = {"id":"PH-H17353","coverage":"full","language":"en","sourceName":"The LawPhil Project — Arellano Law Foundation","sourceUrl":"","fetchedAt":"2026-10-28","articleCount":1,"structureMode":"WHOLE","title":{"zh":null,"en":"MALACAÑAN PALACE BY THE PRESIDENT OF THE PHILIPPINES PRESCRIBING THE PROCEDURE FOR COURSING CORRESPONDENCE TO AND FROM THE UNITED STATES AND FOREIGN COUNTRIES","orig":"MALACAÑAN PALACE BY THE PRESIDENT OF THE PHILIPPINES PRESCRIBING THE PROCEDURE FOR COURSING CORRESPONDENCE TO AND FROM THE UNITED STATES AND FOREIGN COUNTRIES"},"level":"law","status":"active","docNumber":"Executive Order No. 84","issuingBody":"President of the Philippines","completenessNote":"全文，共 1 条；逐字取自 LawPhil PDF 文本化成果（第三方 OCR，非机翻），原始文件 EO_00084_1946.txt","textQuality":"ocr-vendor","sourceFile":"菲律宾/法律原文/07_行政命令_EO/EO_00084_1946.txt","country":"PH","countryName":"菲律宾","layer":"intl","articles":[{"id":"PH-H17353-A1","no":1,"noLabel":{},"text":{"en":"pines, do hereby order that hereafter:\n1. All official communications and correspondence\non matters affecting the relations of the Government of\nthe Philippines with the United States and foreign coun\ntries from all departments, bureaus, offices, agencies,\nand instrumentalities of the Commonwealth Government,\nor of any provincial.\nmunicipal, or city government, to\nthe office of the United States High Commissioner; to\nlocal offices or officers of the military and naval for-\nces of the United States in the Philippines; to foreign\nconsular officers or agents in the Philippines; and to\npersons, corporations, offices, bureaus, or departments\nin the United States or in foreign countries, be sent to\n• the Office of Foreign Relations for transmittal to their\ndestination through proper channels: Provided, however,\nthat in urgent cases where it is imperative to catch an\noutgoing mail steamer or air mail the communication may\nbe mailed direct and a coy thereof simultaneously sent\nto the Office of Foreion Relations with a statement of\nsuch mailing and the date thereof.\n2. All official communications and correspondence\non matters affecting the relations of the Government of\nthe Philipines with the United States and foreign con-\ntires coming from the Office of the United States High\nCommissioner; from local offices or officers of the mili-\ntary and naval forces of the United States in the Phil-\nippines; from foreign consular officers or agents in •\nthe Philippines; from persons, corporations, offices,\nbureaus, or departments in the United States or in foreign\ncountries and from the Orfice of the Resident Commissioner\nto the United States heretofore received and handled by\nthe Office of the President shall hereafter be forwarded\nto the Office of Foreign Relations.\nExecutive Order numbered one hundred four, dated\nJune fourteenth, nineteen hundred and thirty-seven,\nall other executive orders which may be inconsistent\nwith the provisions of this executive order are hereby\n- 3 -\nThis Executive Order shall take effect as of January\n1, 1946.\nDone at the City of Manila, Philippines, this 2nd\nday of January, in the year of Our Lord, nineteen hundred.\nand forty-six, and of the Commonwealth of the Philippines,\nthe eleventh.\nSERGIO OSMEÑA\nPresident of the Philippines\nBy the President:\nSecretary to the President"}}],"pack":"ph-p157"};
  FT["PH-H17354"] = {"id":"PH-H17354","coverage":"full","language":"en","sourceName":"The LawPhil Project — Arellano Law Foundation","sourceUrl":"LawPhil (HTML full text only)  |  https://lawphil.net/executive/execord/eo1947/eo_84_1947.html","fetchedAt":"2026-10-28","articleCount":1,"structureMode":"WHOLE","title":{"zh":null,"en":"Transferring the Seat of Government of the Municipality of Sagay, Negros Occidental, From the Poblacion of Dalusan","orig":"Transferring the Seat of Government of the Municipality of Sagay, Negros Occidental, From the Poblacion of Dalusan"},"level":"law","status":"active","docNumber":"Executive Order No. 84","issuingBody":"President of the Philippines","promulgatedDate":"1947-08-26","completenessNote":"全文，共 1 条；逐字取自 LawPhil PDF 文本化成果（第三方 OCR，非机翻），原始文件 EO_00084_1947_html.txt","textQuality":"ocr-vendor","sourceFile":"菲律宾/法律原文/07_行政命令_EO/EO_00084_1947_html.txt","country":"PH","countryName":"菲律宾","layer":"intl","articles":[{"id":"PH-H17354-A1","no":1,"noLabel":{},"text":{"en":"MALACAÑAN PALACE\nBY THE PRESIDENT OF THE PHILIPPINES\nEXECUTIVE ORDER NO. 84\nTRANSFERRING THE SEAT OF GOVERNMENT OF THE MUNICIPALITY OF SAGAY, NEGROS\nOCCIDENTAL, FROM THE POBLACION OF DALUSAN\nUpon the recommendation of the Secretary of the Interior, and pursuant to the provisions of section 68 of the\nRevised Administrative Code, the seat of government of the municipality of Sagay, Negros Occidental, is\nhereby transferred from the poblacion to the sitio of Dalusan, barrio of Rizal, of the same municipality.\nThis Order shall take effect immediately.\nDone at the City of Manila, this 26th day of August, in the year of Our Lord, nineteen hundred and\nforty-seven, and of the Independence of the Philippines, the second.\n(Sgd.) MANUEL ROXAS\nPresident of the Philippines\nBy the President:\n(Sgd.) EMILIO ABELLO\nChief of the Executive Office"}}],"pack":"ph-p157"};
  FT["PH-H17355"] = {"id":"PH-H17355","coverage":"full","language":"en","sourceName":"The LawPhil Project — Arellano Law Foundation","sourceUrl":"","fetchedAt":"2026-10-28","articleCount":1,"structureMode":"WHOLE","title":{"zh":null,"en":"OF TIIE PUTIPPTNPS BY THE PRESIDENT OF THE PHILIPPINES","orig":"OF TIIE PUTIPPTNPS BY THE PRESIDENT OF THE PHILIPPINES"},"level":"law","status":"active","docNumber":"Executive Order No. 84","issuingBody":"President of the Philippines","completenessNote":"全文，共 1 条；逐字取自 LawPhil PDF 文本化成果（第三方 OCR，非机翻），原始文件 EO_00084_1964.txt","textQuality":"ocr-vendor","sourceFile":"菲律宾/法律原文/07_行政命令_EO/EO_00084_1964.txt","country":"PH","countryName":"菲律宾","layer":"intl","articles":[{"id":"PH-H17355-A1","no":1,"noLabel":{},"text":{"en":"031?00\n(2) Foster effective exchange of information and coordination\nof projeets, programs, and activities of various agencieS connected\nwith schistosomiasis control;\n(3) Establish effective liaison with participating .agencies; 6n4\n(4) Submit recommendations to the President on administrative\nor legislative measures that will effectively carry out ar nationai\ncontrol program for the disease.\nThe Commission shall meet regularly once a month\nand may hold such special meetiigs as the exigencies of\nthe undertaking may demand.\nDone in the City of Manila, this 1st day of June, in the\nyear of Our Lord, nineteen hundred and sixty-four.\nDroso^too MlcArnclr,\nBv the Presidenti\nPresiilent of the Ph'i'l'i'wines\nCu,rxto 0. Zar,otvan\nActing Eaeeuti.ue Secretarg"}}],"pack":"ph-p157"};
