  FT["PH-H17763"] = {"id":"PH-H17763","coverage":"full","language":"en","sourceName":"The LawPhil Project — Arellano Law Foundation","sourceUrl":"","fetchedAt":"2026-10-28","articleCount":4,"structureMode":"ARTICLE","title":{"zh":null,"en":"MALACANANt'i PMS LIBRARY EXECUTIVE ORDER DECLARING AND DELINEATING THE CULASI (CAPIZ) PORT UNDER THE ADMINISTRATIVE JURISDICTION OF THE PIllLIPPINE","orig":"MALACANANt'i PMS LIBRARY EXECUTIVE ORDER DECLARING AND DELINEATING THE CULASI (CAPIZ) PORT UNDER THE ADMINISTRATIVE JURISDICTION OF THE PIllLIPPINE"},"level":"law","status":"active","docNumber":"Executive Order No. 121","issuingBody":"President of the Philippines","completenessNote":"全文，共 4 条；逐字取自 LawPhil PDF 文本化成果（第三方 OCR，非机翻），原始文件 EO_00121_1999.txt","textQuality":"ocr-vendor","sourceFile":"菲律宾/法律原文/07_行政命令_EO/EO_00121_1999.txt","country":"PH","countryName":"菲律宾","layer":"intl","articles":[{"id":"PH-H17763-A1","no":1,"noLabel":{"en":"SECTION 1"},"text":{"en":"The territorial jurisdiction of the Port of Culasi (Capiz) is hereby\nexpanded and particularly described as follows:\n\"Beginning at point marked 1 on the plan at a distance of 281.81 m\nwith bearing a 87°58' W from BBM No.3 (Capiz Cad.), thence to point 2\nat a distance of 4.00m with bearing S 19°10' W, thence to point 3 at a\ndistance of 755.00m with bearing S 70°27 ' E, thence to point 4 at a\ndistance of 457.00m with bearing S 19°13' W, thence to point 5 at a\ndistance of 1,083.00m with bearing N 72°47' W, thence to point 6 at a\ndistance of 477.00m with bearing N 27°00' E, thence to point 7 at a\ndistance of37.65m with bearing N 44°15' E, thence to point 1, the point of\nbeginning at a distance of 246.84.00m with bearing S 69°58'E, all in all\ncomprising a total area of 502,469.95 sq.m. more or less.\""}},{"id":"PH-H17763-A2","no":2,"noLabel":{"en":"SEC 2"},"text":{"en":"The Culasi (Capiz) Port Zone, as expanded, is hereby placed under the\nadministrative jurisdiction of the Philippine Ports Authority, which shall, consistent with\nthe regional industrial plans of the Government, implement a program for the proper\nzoning, planning, development and utilization of the port."}},{"id":"PH-H17763-A3","no":3,"noLabel":{"en":"SEC 3"},"text":{"en":"All other orders, proclamations and issuances or portions thereof which\nare inconsistent with this Executive Order are hereby repealed or modified accordingly.\nNIIIIIIIIIIIIIIIIIIIIIIIIIIII!I\nPJEE Hologram # 5974\n\n-2-"}},{"id":"PH-H17763-A4","no":4,"noLabel":{"en":"SEC 4"},"text":{"en":"This Executive Order shall take effect immediately.\nDONE in the City of Manila, this 11 t~\nLord, nineteen hundred and ninety nine.\nin the year of our\n(==::;;;1(~-\nBy the President:\n11\"1'1'/11\"'/111\"'1'1111'\"\n# 5975\n-~%- ~\nRONALDO B. ZAMORA\nExecutive Secretary\n;::--:.._~\n~"}}],"pack":"ph-p157"};
  FT["PH-H17764"] = {"id":"PH-H17764","coverage":"full","language":"en","sourceName":"The LawPhil Project — Arellano Law Foundation","sourceUrl":"","fetchedAt":"2026-10-28","articleCount":7,"structureMode":"ARTICLE","title":{"zh":null,"en":"MALACAÑANG PMS.LIBRARY RECONSTITUTING THE BIPARTISAN EXECUTIVE-LEGISLATIVE ADVISORY COUNCIL ON SABAH ISSUES AND FOR OTHER","orig":"MALACAÑANG PMS.LIBRARY RECONSTITUTING THE BIPARTISAN EXECUTIVE-LEGISLATIVE ADVISORY COUNCIL ON SABAH ISSUES AND FOR OTHER"},"level":"law","status":"active","docNumber":"Executive Order No. 121","issuingBody":"President of the Philippines","completenessNote":"全文，共 7 条；逐字取自 LawPhil PDF 文本化成果（第三方 OCR，非机翻），原始文件 EO_00121_2002.txt","textQuality":"ocr-vendor","sourceFile":"菲律宾/法律原文/07_行政命令_EO/EO_00121_2002.txt","country":"PH","countryName":"菲律宾","layer":"intl","articles":[{"id":"PH-H17764-A1","no":1,"noLabel":{"en":"SECTION 1"},"text":{"en":"Reconstitution. - The Bipartisan Executive-Legislative\nAdvisory Council, hereinafter referred to as the Council, is hereby\nreconstituted and shall be composed of the following:\nFive (5) representatives from the Executive Branch to be\ndesignated by the President of the Republic of the Philippines;\nFive (5) members of the Senate which shall include a member\nfrom the minority party, to be designated by the Senate\nc. Five (5) members of the House of Representatives which shall\ninclude a member from the minority party, to be designated by\nthe Speaker of the House of Representatives; and\nThree (3) representatives from the private sector, to be\nappointed by the President of the Republic of the Philippines.\nThe President shall designate the Chairman of the Council."}},{"id":"PH-H17764-A2","no":2,"noLabel":{"en":"SECTION 2"},"text":{"en":"Functions. - The Council shall serve as an advisory\nbody to the President with respect to the broad range of issues\nconcerning Sabah.\nP¢MA Outgoing » 14612"}},{"id":"PH-H17764-A3","no":3,"noLabel":{"en":"SECTION 3"},"text":{"en":"Meetings. - The President shall call the initial\nmeeting of the Council, as reconstituted. Thereafter, the Council shall\nmeet as often as agreed upon by the body or as may be convened by the"}},{"id":"PH-H17764-A4","no":4,"noLabel":{"en":"SECTION 4"},"text":{"en":"Secretariat.\n- The Council shall reorganize its\nSecretariat to be headed by an Executive Director who shall be the\ncurrent Head of the Sabah Office of the Department of Foreign Affairs"}},{"id":"PH-H17764-A5","no":5,"noLabel":{"en":"SECTION 5"},"text":{"en":"Office. - The Council shall hold office at the DFA\nwhich shall ensure that the Council is provided with the necessary office\nspace and facilities."}},{"id":"PH-H17764-A6","no":6,"noLabel":{"en":"SECTION 6"},"text":{"en":"Funding. - Appropriations for the operations and\nactivities of the Council shall continue to be incorporated in the budget\nproposals under the DA."}},{"id":"PH-H17764-A7","no":7,"noLabel":{"en":"SECTION 7"},"text":{"en":"Effectivity. - This Executive Order shall take effect\nimmediately upon approval.\nCity of Manila, September 6, 2002.\nBy the President:\nALBERTO G. ROMULO\nExecutive Secretary\nPMS LIBRARY BCODE001942\nPOMA Outgoing * 14613\n2"}}],"pack":"ph-p157"};
  FT["PH-H17765"] = {"id":"PH-H17765","coverage":"full","language":"en","sourceName":"The LawPhil Project — Arellano Law Foundation","sourceUrl":"","fetchedAt":"2026-10-28","articleCount":5,"structureMode":"ARTICLE","title":{"zh":null,"en":"MALACAÑAN PALACE BY THE PRESIDENT OF THE PHILIPPINES DECLARING AND DELINEATING THE AGUTAYA PORT ZONE AND PLACING IT UNDER THE ADMINISTRATIVE JURISDICTION OF THE PHILIPPINE PORTS AUTHORITY (PPA)","orig":"MALACAÑAN PALACE BY THE PRESIDENT OF THE PHILIPPINES DECLARING AND DELINEATING THE AGUTAYA PORT ZONE AND PLACING IT UNDER THE ADMINISTRATIVE JURISDICTION OF THE PHILIPPINE PORTS AUTHORITY (PPA)"},"level":"law","status":"active","docNumber":"Executive Order No. 121","issuingBody":"President of the Philippines","completenessNote":"全文，共 5 条；逐字取自 LawPhil PDF 文本化成果（第三方 OCR，非机翻），原始文件 EO_00121_2012.txt","textQuality":"ocr-vendor","sourceFile":"菲律宾/法律原文/07_行政命令_EO/EO_00121_2012.txt","country":"PH","countryName":"菲律宾","layer":"intl","articles":[{"id":"PH-H17765-A1","no":1,"noLabel":{"en":"SECTION 1"},"text":{"en":"Port of Agutaya. The territorial jurisdiction of the Port of Agutaya\nsituated in Barangay Abagat, Municipality of Agutaya, Province of Palawan, is hereby\ndelineated and established, particularly described as follows:\nBeginning at a point marked 1 on the plan, thence:\n00'\n00'\n00'\n00'\n00'\n00'\n00'\n40.00 m. to point of beginning,\nContaining a total area of TWO HUNDRED SEVENTEEN THOUSAND THREE\nHUNDRED FOURTEEN SQUARE METERS AND TWELVE SQUARE DECIMETERS\n(217,314.12), more or less.\n@fice otthe Prestient of the 3Bhippines"}},{"id":"PH-H17765-A2","no":2,"noLabel":{"en":"SECTION 2"},"text":{"en":"PPA Jurisdiction. The Agutaya Port Zone, as delineated, is hereby\nplaced under the administrative jurisdiction of the PPA, which shall, consistent with the\nregional industrial plans of the government, implement a program for the proper zoning,\nplanning, development and utilization of the port."}},{"id":"PH-H17765-A3","no":3,"noLabel":{"en":"SECTION 3"},"text":{"en":"Repeal. All issuances, orders, rules and regulations, or parts\nthereof, which are inconsistent with this Executive Order are hereby repealed, amended\nor modified accordingly."}},{"id":"PH-H17765-A4","no":4,"noLabel":{"en":"SECTION 4"},"text":{"en":"Separability. If any provision of this Executive Order is declared\ninvalid or unconstitutional, the other provisions not affected thereby shall remain valid\nand subsisting."}},{"id":"PH-H17765-A5","no":5,"noLabel":{"en":"SECTION 5"},"text":{"en":"Effectivity. This Executive Order shall take effect immediately upon\npublication in a newspaper of general circulation.\nDONE, in the City of Manila, this 21st of December , in the vear of our\nLord, Two Thousand and Twelve.\nBy the President:\nPAQUITO N. OCHOA, JR.\nExecutive Secretary\nOffice of the BAreswent of the 7hüwpines\nCERTIFIED COPY-\nMARIANITU M. DIMRANDAL\nDIRECTOR IV 91.2-2013\nMALACANANG RECURDS O FICF\n2"}}],"pack":"ph-p157"};
  FT["PH-H17766"] = {"id":"PH-H17766","coverage":"full","language":"en","sourceName":"The LawPhil Project — Arellano Law Foundation","sourceUrl":"","fetchedAt":"2026-10-28","articleCount":11,"structureMode":"ARTICLE","title":{"zh":null,"en":"MALACAÑAN PALACE BY THE PRESIDENT OF THE PHILIPPINES GRANTING AUTHORITY TO THE DIRECTOR GENERAL OF THE FOOD ADMINISTRATION TO ISSUE EMERGENCY USE AUTHORIZATION AND VACCINES, PRESCRIBING CONDITIONS THEREFOR, AND FOR OTHER","orig":"MALACAÑAN PALACE BY THE PRESIDENT OF THE PHILIPPINES GRANTING AUTHORITY TO THE DIRECTOR GENERAL OF THE FOOD ADMINISTRATION TO ISSUE EMERGENCY USE AUTHORIZATION AND VACCINES, PRESCRIBING CONDITIONS THEREFOR, AND FOR OTHER"},"level":"law","status":"active","docNumber":"Executive Order No. 121","issuingBody":"President of the Philippines","completenessNote":"全文，共 11 条；逐字取自 LawPhil PDF 文本化成果（第三方 OCR，非机翻），原始文件 EO_00121_2020.txt","textQuality":"ocr-vendor","sourceFile":"菲律宾/法律原文/07_行政命令_EO/EO_00121_2020.txt","country":"PH","countryName":"菲律宾","layer":"intl","articles":[{"id":"PH-H17766-A1","no":1,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 1"},"text":{"en":"Emergency Use Authorization for COVID-19 Drugs and Vaccines. The\nDirector General of the FDA is hereby authorized to issue an Emergency Use Authorization\n(EUA), subject to conditions provided in this Order.\nOutside clinical trials and except in cases where a Compassionate Special Permit is\nissued, no unregistered COVID-19 drug and vaccine may be manufactured, sold, imported,\nexported, distributed or transferred without an EUA."}},{"id":"PH-H17766-A2","no":2,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 2"},"text":{"en":"Conditions for the Issuance of EUA. An EUA on a COVID-19 drug or\nvaccine shall be issued and remain valid only when all of the following circumstances are\ni. Based on the totality of evidence available, including data from adequate and well-\nknown controlled trials, it is reasonable to believe that the drug or vaccine may be\neffective to prevent, diagnose or treat COVID-19;\nThe known and potential benefits of the drug or vaccine when used to diagnose,\nprevent or treat COVID-19 outweigh the known and potential risks of the drug or\nvaccine, if any; and\nill. There is no adequate, approved and available alternative to the drug or vaccine for\ndiagnosing, preventing or treating COVID-19."}},{"id":"PH-H17766-A3","no":3,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 3"},"text":{"en":"Applications for EUA. An application for the issuance of an EUA shall be\nsubmitted by the industry or goverment agency concerned, such as the national procurer or\nthe public health program implementer.\nThe application should demonstrate compliance with current Good Manufacturing\nPractices, and accompanied by an undertaking by the manufacturer to complete the\ndevelopment of the drug and vaccine, among others.\n2"}},{"id":"PH-H17766-A4","no":4,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 4"},"text":{"en":"Reliance and Recognition. In evaluating applications for EUA, the FDA\nDirector General shall have the power to implement reliance and recognition processes for\nemergency use of drugs and vaccines. For this purpose, the FDA Director General may\naccept the regulatory decision of the WHO, US-CDC, or other internationally recognized and\nestablished regulatory authorities."}},{"id":"PH-H17766-A5","no":5,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 5"},"text":{"en":"Expert Panel. The FDA shall convene a panel composed of experts on\ndrug and vaccine development, which shall conduct a review of available data on the safety\nand effectiveness of a COVID-19 drug or vaccine applied for an EUA. After review, the panel\nshall submit to the FDA Director General its report and recommendations on the application"}},{"id":"PH-H17766-A6","no":6,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 6"},"text":{"en":"Validity of the EUA. An EUA issued pursuant to this Order shall be valid\nonly within the duration of the declared public health emergency due to COVID-19, without\nprejudice to the discretion of the FDA Director General to revisit or revoke the same, as may\nbe appropriate, to protect the general public health and safety."}},{"id":"PH-H17766-A7","no":7,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 7"},"text":{"en":"Post-Authorization Monitoring. The FDA, together with other concerned\noffices of the DOH, shall conduct post-authorization monitoring to track product deployment,\nadditional relevant information, and the status from the manufacturer concerning full-product\nlife-cycle. The holder of an EU shall be required to complete specific pharmacovigilance\nobligations, with a view to providing comprehensive data confirming a positive benefit-risk"}},{"id":"PH-H17766-A8","no":8,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 8"},"text":{"en":"Implementing Guidelines. The FDA shall formulate and issue guidelines,\nas may be necessary, for the effective implementation of this Order."}},{"id":"PH-H17766-A9","no":9,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 9"},"text":{"en":"Reports. The FDA shall submit to the President, through the DOH, a\nmonthly report on the implementation of this Order."}},{"id":"PH-H17766-A10","no":10,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 10"},"text":{"en":"Separability. If any part or provision of this Order shall be held\nunconstitutional or invalid, the other parts or provisions not affected thereby shall continue to\nbe in full force and effect."}},{"id":"PH-H17766-A11","no":11,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 11"},"text":{"en":"Effectivity. This Order shall take effect immediately upon publication in\nthe Official Gazette or in a newspaper of general circulation.\nDONE, in the City of Manila, this Ist day of December\nLord, Two Thousand and Twenty.\nin the Year of our\nBy the President:\nSALVADOR C. MEDIALDEA\nExecutive Secretary\n3\nOffice of the President\nMALACARANG RECORDS OFFICE\nATTY. CONCESCI\nREPUBLIC OF THE PHILIPPINES"}}],"pack":"ph-p157"};
  FT["PH-H17767"] = {"id":"PH-H17767","coverage":"full","language":"en","sourceName":"The LawPhil Project — Arellano Law Foundation","sourceUrl":"","fetchedAt":"2026-10-28","articleCount":19,"structureMode":"ARTICLE","title":{"zh":null,"en":"MALACAÑAN PALACE BY THE PRESIDENT OF THE PHILIPPINES PROVIDING FOR THE ELECTRIC VEHICLE INCENTIVE STRATEGY (EVIS)","orig":"MALACAÑAN PALACE BY THE PRESIDENT OF THE PHILIPPINES PROVIDING FOR THE ELECTRIC VEHICLE INCENTIVE STRATEGY (EVIS)"},"level":"law","status":"active","docNumber":"Executive Order No. 121","issuingBody":"President of the Philippines","completenessNote":"全文，共 19 条；逐字取自 LawPhil PDF 文本化成果（第三方 OCR，非机翻），原始文件 EO_00121_2026.txt","textQuality":"ocr-vendor","sourceFile":"菲律宾/法律原文/07_行政命令_EO/EO_00121_2026.txt","country":"PH","countryName":"菲律宾","layer":"intl","articles":[{"id":"PH-H17767-A1","no":1,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 1"},"text":{"en":"EVIS Program. The EVIS Program is hereby adopted to promote local\nmanufacturing of EVs, including their parts and components, attract investments to\nexpand domestic EV manufacturing operations, and develop the Philippines as a regional\nautomotive manufacturing hub, towards increasing the adoption and use of EVs, reducing\nthe country's dependence on fossil fuels and supporting the achievement of its\ngreenhouse gas emission reduction commitments.\nThe EVIS Program shall provide time-bound, targeted, performance-based, and\ntransparent fiscal support to encourage strategic investments in domestic EV\nmanufacturing. Other non-fiscal measures provided under existing laws, rules, and\nregulations shall continue to be implemented by the relevant government agencies."}},{"id":"PH-H17767-A2","no":2,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 2"},"text":{"en":"Coverage. The EVIS Program shall provide fiscal support for the\nmanufacture of hybrid and battery EVs, specifically passenger cars and commercial\nvehicles, including their parts and components, subject to the qualifications, terms, and\nconditions under this Order and its implementing guidelines."}},{"id":"PH-H17767-A3","no":3,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 3"},"text":{"en":"Functions of the BOI. The BOI, as the lead implementing and\ncoordinating agency of the EVIS Program, shall perform the following:\na. Act upon the recommendation/s of the Inter-Agency Committee on Electric\nVehicle Industry Development (IAC-EV) established under this Order;\nb. Oversee the implementation of the EVIS Program;\nc. Promulgate the necessary guidelines to implement this Order within one (1)\nmonth from its effectivity, in consultation with the lAC-EV;\nd. Prepare and submit the annual report on the performance of the EVIS Program\nto the Office of the President:\ne. Coordinate EV industry development efforts with all concerned agencies and\ninstrumentalities of the government; and\nf. Perform such other acts as may be necessary or incidental to the exercise of its\nfunctions and powers and the discharge of its duties under this Order."}},{"id":"PH-H17767-A4","no":4,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 4"},"text":{"en":"Inter-Agency Committee on Electric Vehicle Industry Development.\nThe IAC-EV is hereby created to assist the BOI in administering and implementing the\nEVIS Program. The IAC-EV shall be composed of an Undersecretary-level representative\nfrom each of the following agencies, who may designate an alternate with a rank not lower\nthan Director or its equivalent, whose acts shall be deemed the acts of the principal:\nChairperson :\nDepartment of Finance (DOF)\nDepartment of Energy\nDepartment of Transportation\nDepartment of Budget and Management (DBM)\n2\n\nThe BOI shall serve as the Secretariat of the IAC-EV and provide the necessary\ntechnical and administrative support to the Committee."}},{"id":"PH-H17767-A5","no":5,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 5"},"text":{"en":"Functions of the IAC-EV. The IAC-EV shall perform the following\nduties and functions:\na. Evaluate applications for registration under the EVIS Program;\nb. Recommend to the BOI the issuance of a Certificate of Registration for the\nparticipant and impose the corresponding terms and conditions;\nc. Evaluate eligibility of registered participants for fiscal support;\nd. Recommend to the BOI the approval for entitlement to fiscal support;\ne. Monitor overall EVIS performance and audit compliance of the EVIS Program;\n. Recommend to the BOI actions on requests of a registered participant in the\ng. Recommend to the BOl the withdrawal/forfeiture of the fiscal support in the\nevent that the registered participant fails to comply with the terms and\nconditions of its Certificate of Registration;\nh. Undertake studies and research, including review of existing government\nregulations, as needed, to make policy recommendations to enhance the\neffectivity of the EVIS and other related Programs, as well as in improving the\noverall performance of the EV industry;\ni. Call on other agencies as resource persons or enlist the assistance of or\nrequest information and documents from any department, bureau, office or\ninstrumentality, necessary to carry out its functions; and\nj. Perform such other functions as may be necessary."}},{"id":"PH-H17767-A6","no":6,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 6"},"text":{"en":"Enrollment Period and Criteria for Registration. Applicants may\napply for the enrollment of up to two (2) EV models under the EVIS Program. The\nprocedure and period for enrollment shall be identified in the implementing guidelines\nissued pursuant to this Order.\nIn evaluating applications for enrollment and registration under the EVIS Program,\nthe IAC-EV shall take into account, among others, the following\na. Investments in the manufacture or assembly of EVs, and their parts and\ncomponents;\nb. Planned total production volume;\nc. Expected economic impact of the proposed investment, including potential\ncontribution to industry linkages, job generation, and overall consumer welfare;\nd. Compliance, when applicable, with the Philippine National Standards of the\nBureau of Philippine Standards, United Nations Regulations (UNR) 100 and/or\ne. Proposed after-sales support services plan, including battery disposal or\nrecycling plan, and spare parts support for at least ten (10) years.\nUpon recommendation of the IAC-EV, the BOI shall issue a Certificate of\nRegistration to a qualified participant covering each approved EV model, subject to the\nposting of a performance bond in the amount to be determined by the BOI, in consultation\nwith the IAC-EV. A registered participant that is a vehicle manufacturer shall be deemed a\nparticipant under the Motor Vehicle Development Program.\n3\n\nIn the event of oversubscription, the lAC-EV shall recommend to the BOl for\napproval the top four (4) qualified applicants, taking into account, among others, the\nproject's fiscal and economic impact, and contribution to the domestic economy."}},{"id":"PH-H17767-A7","no":7,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 7"},"text":{"en":"Fiscal Support. Registered participants under the EVIS Program may\nbe entitled to the following fiscal support:\na. Fixed Investment Support (FIS). FIS equivalent to the applicable percentage of total\ncapital expenditure used for tooling, equipment, research and development cost,\nand engineering changes to manufacture the model/platform, including initial\nstart-up expense and training costs for the start-up operation for the use thereof,\nexcluding land, as follows:\n1. For the domestic manufacture or assembly of enrolled electric passenger\nvehicles and commercial vehicles:\n(i) Forty percent (40%) for battery EVs; and\n(li) Thirty percent (30%) for hybrid EVs, plug-in hybrid EVs, and fuel cell EVs.\n2. For the domestic manufacture of parts and components for enrolled electric\npassenger vehicles and commercial vehicles:\n(i) Forty percent (40%) for parts and components for battery EVs; and\n(ii) Thirty percent (30%) for parts and components for hybrid EVs, plug-in\nhybrid EVs, and fuel cell EVs.\nb. Production Volume Incentive (PI). PVI of up to twelve percent (12%) of the\nex-factory unit price but not to exceed Two Hundred Thousand Pesos\n(PhP200,000.00) per unit, for the domestic manufacture or assembly of enrolled\nelectric passenger vehicles and commercial vehicles."}},{"id":"PH-H17767-A8","no":8,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 8"},"text":{"en":"Criteria for Eligibility to FIS. The entitlement to the FIS under the\nEVIS Program shall be subject to compliance with the applicable eligibility criteria,\nincluding the following:\na. Undertaking of new investments in the manufacture or assembly of EVs,\nincluding their parts and components, for the enrolled models under the EVIS\nb. A minimum investment capital of Five Billion Pesos (PhP5,000,000,000.00) or\nits equivalent;\nc. The introduction of the enrolled EVs to the domestic or export market within\nthree (3) years from the issuance of a Certificate of Registration;\nd. Continued compliance with the registration requirements under the EVIS\nProgram; and\ne. Compliance with such other conditions as the BOI may prescribe at the time of\nregistration, pursuant to the implementing guidelines.\n\nThe registered participants shall be entitled to the FIS under the EVIS Program for\na maximum of ten (10) years from the date of registration of the enrolled EV models or\ntheir parts and components."}},{"id":"PH-H17767-A9","no":9,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 9"},"text":{"en":"Criteria for Eligibility for VI. The entitlement to the PVI under the\nEVIS Program for the domestic manufacture or assembly of enrolled EV models shall be\nsubject to compliance with the applicable eligibility criteria, including the following:\na. The manufacture of complete EV units;\nb. The manufacture of mandatory parts and components;\nc. Minimum planned production volume/capacity of ten thousand (10,000) EV\nd. Compliance with other conditions, if any, that the BOl shall impose at the time of\nregistration.\nThe registered participants shall be entitled to the PVI under the EVIS Program for\na maximum period of ten (10) years from the start of production of the enrolled EV"}},{"id":"PH-H17767-A10","no":10,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 10"},"text":{"en":"Annual Appropriation. The DBM, in coordination with the BOI, shall\npropose in the National Expenditure Program (NEP) the inclusion of the EVIS Program in\nthe annual General Appropriations Act to fund the fiscal support to be granted to\nregistered and eligible participants. For this purpose, the DBM shall indicate in NEP the\nannual estimated expenditure necessary to support the EVIS Program for that year, until\nthe amount of Sixty Billion Pesos (PhP60,000,000,000.00) is fully utilized and/or the\nfinancial obligations to the registered participants are fully paid, subject to the usual\nbudget preparation process.\nThe total fiscal support for the EVIS Program to be allocated to FIS and PVI shall\nnot exceed Sixty Billion Pesos (PhP60,000,000,000.00), with each enrolled model\nqualified for fiscal support in an amount not exceeding Fifteen Billion Pesos\n(PhP15,000,000,000.00) per model: Provided, that each registered participant may only\nenroll a maximum of two (2) models.\nThe entitlement to the fiscal support under the EVIS Program may be extended,\nsubject to review and recommendation by the BOI and approval by the FIRB as provided\nunder this Order."}},{"id":"PH-H17767-A11","no":11,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 11"},"text":{"en":"Tax Payment Certificate (TC). The fiscal support for registered and\neligible participants shall be evidenced by a non-transferable TC, which may be used to\ndefray their tax and duty obligations to the National Government, limited to income tax,\nexcise tax, value-added tax, and import duties.\nTowards this end, the BOI, DBM, DOF, Bureau of Internal Revenue, and Bureau of\nCustoms shall establish an efficient and effective mechanism for the availment, issuance,\nand use of the TPC, which may include the adoption of digital technologies and\ninteroperable electronic platforms to streamline its processing and administration,\nconsistent with existing policies, laws, and regulations.\n5"}},{"id":"PH-H17767-A12","no":12,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 12"},"text":{"en":"Monitoring, Compliance, and Enforcement. Registered program\nparticipants shall be subject to periodic audit by the BOI of their production volume,\nincluding parts importation volume, deliverables and commitments under the EVIS\nProgram, and compliance with the terms and conditions of their Certificate of Registration.\nRegistered participants engaged in the manufacture or assembly of EV parts and\ncomponents shall be audited periodically by the BOI to prevent parts trading.\nFailure to comply with the terms and conditions of the Certificate of Registration, or\nthe commitments made under the EVIS Program, including the failure to: (i) undertake the\nrequired investment in the manufacture of the enrolled EV model or the parts and\ncomponents thereof; or (ii) introduce the locally manufactured enrolled EV model and/or\nthe parts and components thereof to the domestic or export market within three (3) years\nfrom the date of registration, shall, after due process, be subject to the refund,\nsuspension, or forfeiture of fiscal support, cancellation of the Certificate of Registration,\nand/or the imposition of fines or such other penalties as may be allowed or prescribed\nunder the implementing guidelines subject to existing laws, rules, and regulations."}},{"id":"PH-H17767-A13","no":13,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 13"},"text":{"en":"Confidentiality of Business Information. Confidential business\ninformation submitted by registered participants under the EVIS Program shall be\nprotected from unauthorized use or public disclosure, subject to existing laws, rules, and\nregulations."}},{"id":"PH-H17767-A14","no":14,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 14"},"text":{"en":"No Double Availment of Incentives. Registered participants shall not\nbe allowed to register their activity under Title XIlI of RA No. 8424 or the \"National Internal\nRevenue Code of 1997,\" as amended, or any other government program granting\nincentives to the same activity."}},{"id":"PH-H17767-A15","no":15,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 15"},"text":{"en":"Reporting. The BOI shall submit to the DBM an annual report on the\navailment of fiscal support by registered participants under the EVIS Program, and shall\nfurnish the FIRB a copy thereof for monitoring and evaluation purposes."}},{"id":"PH-H17767-A16","no":16,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 16"},"text":{"en":"Review. The BOI shall review the implementation of the EVIS\nProgram, including the amount of support, every three (3) years from the effectivity of this\nOrder. When warranted, the BOI may recommend the reopening of the application period\nfor the enrollment of models or the extension of the Program, subject to the approval of\nThe BOI shall likewise conduct an annual review of the Program's targets vis-a-Vis\nthe registered participants' progress, including the utilization of fiscal support under this\nProgram. Upon recommendation of the IAC-EV, the BOI may strategically allocate or\nreallocate available fiscal support, including support that may be extended to newly\nenrolled models, to maximize the developmental impact of the EVIS Program, subject to\nexisting budgeting and accounting laws, rules, and regulations: Provided, that any\nallocation or reallocation of fiscal support shall remain subject to the registration criteria\nand periods of availment prescribed under this Order and the implementing guidelines."}},{"id":"PH-H17767-A17","no":17,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 17"},"text":{"en":"Separability Clause. If any section or part of this Order is declared\nunconstitutional or invalid, the other sections or provisions not otherwise affected shall\nremain in full force and effect.\n6"}},{"id":"PH-H17767-A18","no":18,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 18"},"text":{"en":"Repealing Clause. All issuances, orders, rules, and regulations, or\nparts thereof, that are inconsistent with the provisions of this Order, are hereby repealed\nor modified accordingly."}},{"id":"PH-H17767-A19","no":19,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 19"},"text":{"en":"Effectivity. This Order shall take effect immediately upon its\npublication in the Official Gazette or in any newspaper of general circulation.\nDONE, in the City of Manila, this 29th day of July\nyear of our Lord, Two Thousand and Twenty-Six.\nBy the President:\nRALPH 6. RECTO\nActing Executive Secretary\nREPUBLIC OF THE PHILIPPINES"}}],"pack":"ph-p157"};
  FT["PH-H17768"] = {"id":"PH-H17768","coverage":"full","language":"en","sourceName":"The LawPhil Project — Arellano Law Foundation","sourceUrl":"LawPhil (HTML full text only)  |  https://lawphil.net/executive/execord/eo1937/eo_122_1937.html","fetchedAt":"2026-10-28","articleCount":1,"structureMode":"WHOLE","title":{"zh":null,"en":"Creating a National Unemployment Board","orig":"Creating a National Unemployment Board"},"level":"law","status":"active","docNumber":"Executive Order No. 122","issuingBody":"President of the Philippines","promulgatedDate":"1937-10-08","completenessNote":"全文，共 1 条；逐字取自 LawPhil PDF 文本化成果（第三方 OCR，非机翻），原始文件 EO_00122_1937_html.txt","textQuality":"ocr-vendor","sourceFile":"菲律宾/法律原文/07_行政命令_EO/EO_00122_1937_html.txt","country":"PH","countryName":"菲律宾","layer":"intl","articles":[{"id":"PH-H17768-A1","no":1,"noLabel":{},"text":{"en":"MALACAÑAN PALACE\nBY THE PRESIDENT OF THE PHILIPPINES\n[ EXECUTIVE ORDER NO. 122, October 08, 1937 ]\nCREATING A NATIONAL UNEMPLOYMENT BOARD\nIn order to coordinate all Government and private efforts to reduce unemployment and to aid those who are in\ndistress on account of unavoidable unemployment, I, MANUEL L. QUEZON, President of the Philippines, by\nvirtue of the powers vested in me by law, do hereby create a National Unemployment Board, composed of the\nCommissioner of Health and Welfare as Chairman, and the Undersecretary of Public Works and\nCommunications, the Undersecretary of Agriculture and Commerce, the Undersecretary of Labor, the\nExecutive Secretary of the Associated Charities of Manila, and two other persons who shall be appointed by\nthe President, as members.\nIt shall be the duty of this Board to take a census of all unemployed persons in the Philippines, to ascertain\ntheir needs, to determine upon ways and means for relieving or ameliorating their conditions, and to advise the\nGovernment authorities concerned as to the expenditure of the funds now appropriated or which may hereafter\nbe appropriated for relief purposes.\nThe Board shall also be advise the appropriate Departments, Bureaus, offices, subdivisions, agencies, or\ninstrumentalities of the Commonwealth Government from time to time as to the unemployment situation in\nthe different localities in the Philippines with a view to giving employment, so far as practicable, to those in\nneed of aid on public works projects and other work carried out by any branch or agency of the Government.\nIt shall further seek to enlist the cooperation of private employers in the distribution of employment in such a\nmanner as to provide the maximum amount of relief from unemployment.\nThe National Unemployment Board is hereby authorized to establish branches or agencies in the provinces,\nchartered cities, and municipalities with a view to carrying out within their respective jurisdiction the purposes\nfor which the said Board is created.\nAll officers and employees of the National, provincial, and municipal governments are hereby enjoined to\ncooperate in every way possible with the National Unemployment Board, and to faithfully perform such\nduties as may be assigned to them by the said Board with the approval of the corresponding Department Head.\nExecutive Order Numbered Five hundred sixteen, series of nineteen hundred and thirty-four, and all other\nOrders which are consistent herewith are hereby revoked.\nDone at the City of Manila, this eight day of October, in the year of Our Lord, nineteen hundred and\nthirty-seven, and of the Commonwealth of the Philippines, the second.\n(Sgd.) MANUEL L. QUEZON\nPresident of the Philippines\nBy the President:\n(Sgd.) ELPIDIO QUIRINO\nSecretary of the Interior"}}],"pack":"ph-p157"};
  FT["PH-H17769"] = {"id":"PH-H17769","coverage":"full","language":"en","sourceName":"The LawPhil Project — Arellano Law Foundation","sourceUrl":"LawPhil (HTML full text only)  |  https://lawphil.net/executive/execord/eo1948/eo_122_1948.html","fetchedAt":"2026-10-28","articleCount":1,"structureMode":"WHOLE","title":{"zh":null,"en":"Organizing Certain Portion of the Municipality of Mambajao, Province of Oriental Misamis, Into An Independent Municipality Under the Name of","orig":"Organizing Certain Portion of the Municipality of Mambajao, Province of Oriental Misamis, Into An Independent Municipality Under the Name of"},"level":"law","status":"active","docNumber":"Executive Order No. 122","issuingBody":"President of the Philippines","promulgatedDate":"1948-03-19","completenessNote":"全文，共 1 条；逐字取自 LawPhil PDF 文本化成果（第三方 OCR，非机翻），原始文件 EO_00122_1948_html.txt","textQuality":"ocr-vendor","sourceFile":"菲律宾/法律原文/07_行政命令_EO/EO_00122_1948_html.txt","country":"PH","countryName":"菲律宾","layer":"intl","articles":[{"id":"PH-H17769-A1","no":1,"noLabel":{},"text":{"en":"MALACAÑAN PALACE\nBY THE PRESIDENT OF THE PHILIPPINES\n[ EXECUTIVE ORDER NO. 122, March 19, 1948 ]\nORGANIZING CERTAIN PORTION OF THE MUNICIPALITY OF MAMBAJAO , PROVINCE OF\nORIENTAL MISAMIS, INTO AN INDEPENDENT MUNICIPALITY UNDER THE NAME OF\nUpon the recommendation of the Secretary of the Interior, and pursuant to the provisions of section 68 of the\nRevised Administrative Code, the barrios of Binoni, Hubangon, Katuhogan and Mahinog and a certain portion\nof the barrio of Tupsan, all of the municipality of Mambajao, Province of Oriental Misamis, are hereby\norganized into an independent municipality under the name of Mahinog, with the seat of government at the\nbarrio of Mahinog.\nThe boundary line between the municipality Mahinog, as herein organized, and the municipality of Mambajao\nshall be the course of the Tupsan River from the point where it intersects the present Mambajao-Catarman\nboundary line, downstream and in a northeasterly direction to the mouth of this river on the shore of the\nMindanao Sea .\nThe municipality of Mambajao shall consist of its present territory, minus the territory comprised in the\nmunicipality of Mahinog , as herein organized.\nThe organization herein made shall take effect on July 1, 1948 .\nDone at the City of Manila, this 19th day of March, in the year of Our Lord, nineteen hundred and forty-eight,\nand of the Independence of the Philippines, the second.\n(Sgd.) MANUEL ROXAS\nPresident of the Philippines\nBy the President:\n(Sgd.) EMILIO ABELLO\nChief of the Executive Office"}}],"pack":"ph-p157"};
  FT["PH-H17770"] = {"id":"PH-H17770","coverage":"full","language":"en","sourceName":"The LawPhil Project — Arellano Law Foundation","sourceUrl":"","fetchedAt":"2026-10-28","articleCount":1,"structureMode":"WHOLE","title":{"zh":null,"en":"MALACAÑANG RESIDENCE OF THE PRESIDENT OF THE PHILIPPINES BY THE PRESIDENT OF THE PHILIPPINES DEFINING THE TERRITORIAL LIMITS OF THE CITY OF TRECE MARTIRES","orig":"MALACAÑANG RESIDENCE OF THE PRESIDENT OF THE PHILIPPINES BY THE PRESIDENT OF THE PHILIPPINES DEFINING THE TERRITORIAL LIMITS OF THE CITY OF TRECE MARTIRES"},"level":"law","status":"active","docNumber":"Executive Order No. 122","issuingBody":"President of the Philippines","completenessNote":"全文，共 1 条；逐字取自 LawPhil PDF 文本化成果（第三方 OCR，非机翻），原始文件 EO_00122_1955.txt","textQuality":"ocr-vendor","sourceFile":"菲律宾/法律原文/07_行政命令_EO/EO_00122_1955.txt","country":"PH","countryName":"菲律宾","layer":"intl","articles":[{"id":"PH-H17770-A1","no":1,"noLabel":{},"text":{"en":"Nor: All points are all temporary stake.\nCorner stone to point 1 S 52°-28' E 1,217.30 meters.\nArca - 9,990,008.29 square meters.\nDone in the City of Manila, this 18th day of July, in\nthe year of Our Lord, nincteen hundred and fifty-five, and\nof the Independence of the Philippines, the tenth.\nRAMON MAGSAYSAY\nPresident of the Philippines\nBy the President:\nMARIANO YENKO, JR.\nAssistant Executive Secretary"}}],"pack":"ph-p157"};
  FT["PH-H17771"] = {"id":"PH-H17771","coverage":"full","language":"en","sourceName":"The LawPhil Project — Arellano Law Foundation","sourceUrl":"","fetchedAt":"2026-10-28","articleCount":1,"structureMode":"WHOLE","title":{"zh":null,"en":"OFFICIAL GAZETTE MALACAÑANG RESIDENCE OF THE PRESIDENT OF THE PHILIPPINES BY THE PRESIDENT OF THE PHILIPPINES PROVIDING INSTRUCTIONS TO BE FOLLOWED IN THE CONDUCT OF PUBLIC AFFAIRS DURING THE TIME THAT THE PRESIDENT IS OUTSIDE THE PHILIPPINES","orig":"OFFICIAL GAZETTE MALACAÑANG RESIDENCE OF THE PRESIDENT OF THE PHILIPPINES BY THE PRESIDENT OF THE PHILIPPINES PROVIDING INSTRUCTIONS TO BE FOLLOWED IN THE CONDUCT OF PUBLIC AFFAIRS DURING THE TIME THAT THE PRESIDENT IS OUTSIDE THE PHILIPPINES"},"level":"law","status":"active","docNumber":"Executive Order No. 122","issuingBody":"President of the Philippines","completenessNote":"全文，共 1 条；逐字取自 LawPhil PDF 文本化成果（第三方 OCR，非机翻），原始文件 EO_00122_1964.txt","textQuality":"ocr-vendor","sourceFile":"菲律宾/法律原文/07_行政命令_EO/EO_00122_1964.txt","country":"PH","countryName":"菲律宾","layer":"intl","articles":[{"id":"PH-H17771-A1","no":1,"noLabel":{},"text":{"en":"the official calls of foreign dignitaries in behalf in repre-\nsentation of the President, and on such occasions the\nVice-President shall be entitled to the honors and cour-\ntesies due the President of the Philippines.\n6741\n6742:\nOFFICIAL GAZETTE\nDone in the City of Manila, this 3rd day of October,\nin the year of Our Lord, nineteen hundred and sixty-four.\nDIOSDADO MACAPAGAL\nPresident of the Philippines\nBy the President:\nJUAN S. CAncIO\nActing Assistant Executive Secretary"}}],"pack":"ph-p157"};
  FT["PH-H17772"] = {"id":"PH-H17772","coverage":"full","language":"en","sourceName":"The LawPhil Project — Arellano Law Foundation","sourceUrl":"LawPhil (HTML full text only)  |  https://lawphil.net/executive/execord/eo1968/eo_122_1968.html","fetchedAt":"2026-10-28","articleCount":1,"structureMode":"WHOLE","title":{"zh":null,"en":"Creating the Peace and Order Coordinating Council.","orig":"Creating the Peace and Order Coordinating Council."},"level":"law","status":"active","docNumber":"Executive Order No. 122","issuingBody":"President of the Philippines","promulgatedDate":"1968-03-11","completenessNote":"全文，共 1 条；逐字取自 LawPhil PDF 文本化成果（第三方 OCR，非机翻），原始文件 EO_00122_1968_html.txt","textQuality":"ocr-vendor","sourceFile":"菲律宾/法律原文/07_行政命令_EO/EO_00122_1968_html.txt","country":"PH","countryName":"菲律宾","layer":"intl","articles":[{"id":"PH-H17772-A1","no":1,"noLabel":{},"text":{"en":"MALACAÑAN PALACE\nBY THE PRESIDENT OF THE PHILIPPINES\n[ Executive Order No. 122, March 11, 1968 ]\nCREATING THE PEACE AND ORDER COORDINATING COUNCIL\nBy virtue of the powers vested in me by law, I, FERDINAND E. MARCOS, President of the Philippines, do\nhereby create the Peace and Order Coordinating Council to be composed of the following:\nThe President of the Philippines\nSecretary of Justice\nVice-Chairman\nExecutive Secretary\nMember and Executive Secretary\nChairman, Police Commission\nChief of Constabulary\nDirector, National Bureau of Investigation\nRepresentative of the Department of National Defense on Peace and Order\nThe Council shall coordinate the overall campaign against crime and for the maintenance of peace and order,\nwith the end in view of removing obstacles in the path of each law-enforcing agency and facilitating concerted\nand coordinated action and expediting the prompt investigation and prosecution of criminal cases.\nThe Council shall meet once a week and shall report directly to the President.\nIt may call upon any department, bureau, office, agency or instrumentality of the government for such\nassistance as it may need in the discharge of its functions.\nFull financial support shall be extended by the Secretary of Finance and the Commissioner of the Budget.\nDone in the City of Manila, this 11th day of March, in the year of Our Lord, nineteen hundred and sixty-eight.\n(Sgd.) FERDINAND E. MARCOS\nPresident of the Philippines\nBy the President:\n(Sgd.) RAFAEL M. SALAS\nExecutive Secretary"}}],"pack":"ph-p157"};
  FT["PH-H17773"] = {"id":"PH-H17773","coverage":"full","language":"en","sourceName":"The LawPhil Project — Arellano Law Foundation","sourceUrl":"LawPhil (source has HTML full text only)","fetchedAt":"2026-10-28","articleCount":10,"structureMode":"ARTICLE","title":{"zh":null,"en":"Abolishing the Office of Muslim Affairs and Cultural Communities.","orig":"Abolishing the Office of Muslim Affairs and Cultural Communities."},"level":"law","status":"active","docNumber":"Executive Order No. 122","issuingBody":"President of the Philippines","promulgatedDate":"1987-01-30","completenessNote":"全文，共 10 条；逐字取自 LawPhil PDF 文本化成果（第三方 OCR，非机翻），原始文件 EO_00122_1987_html.txt","textQuality":"ocr-vendor","sourceFile":"菲律宾/法律原文/07_行政命令_EO/EO_00122_1987_html.txt","country":"PH","countryName":"菲律宾","layer":"intl","articles":[{"id":"PH-H17773-A1","no":1,"noLabel":{"en":"Sec 1"},"text":{"en":"Title. This Executive Order shall otherwise be known as the Reorganization Act of Government\nAgencies on cultural communities and Muslim Affairs."}},{"id":"PH-H17773-A2","no":2,"noLabel":{"en":"Sec 2"},"text":{"en":"Reorganizational Changes. The Office of Muslim Affairs and Cultural Communities is hereby\nabolished and in its place are created, by the executive orders respectively creating them, the Office for\nNorthern Cultural Communities and the Office for Southern Cultural Communities, which shall absorb all the\nfunctions of the Bureau of National Minorities and the Office of Muslim Affairs, which shall absorb all the\nfunctions of the Bureau of Muslim Affairs."}},{"id":"PH-H17773-A3","no":3,"noLabel":{"en":"Sec 3"},"text":{"en":"Funds and Assets. Upon the approval of the executive orders respectively creating the Office for\nNorthern Cultural Communities, Office for Southern Cultural Communities and the Office on Muslim Affairs,\nthe assets and liabilities of the Office of Muslim Affairs and Cultural Communities shall be divided as\n(a) All records, equipment, facilities, choses in action, rights and other assets of the defunct Presidential\nAssistant on National Minorities brought into the merger under Executive Order No. 969, and all records,\nequipment, facilities, choses in action, rights and other assets presently assigned to the Bureau of National\nMinorities, including its units, field offices, sub-offices and service centers shall accrue in the Offices for\nNorthern Cultural Communities and Southern Cultural Communities;\n(b) All records, equipment, facilities, choses in action, rights and other assets of the defunct Ministry of\nMuslim Affairs brought into the merger under Executive Order No. 969 and all records, equipment, facilities,\nchoses in action, rights and other assets presently assigned to the Bureau of Muslim Affairs, including its\nunits, field offices, sub-offices and service centers shall accrue to the Office on Muslim Affairs;\n(c) The equipment, facilities, and other assets presently assigned to the staff services and their units shall be\ninventoried and divided among the three aforementioned Offices;\n(d) Unexpected balance of the appropriation and savings as well as liabilities, if any, shall be divided among\n\nthe three aforementioned Offices."}},{"id":"PH-H17773-A4","no":4,"noLabel":{"en":"Sec 4"},"text":{"en":"Implementing Agency. An implementing agency shall be designated by the President to plan and\noversee the implementation of the provisions of the preceding Section 3."}},{"id":"PH-H17773-A5","no":5,"noLabel":{"en":"Sec 5"},"text":{"en":"Personnel. Upon approval of this Execution Order, the officers (the term \"officer\" as used in this\nExecutive Order is intended to be within the meaning of the term \"official\" as used in the Freedom\nConstitution and the succeeding Constitution) and employees of the Office of Muslim Affairs and Cultural\nCommunities shall, in a hold over capacity, continue to perform their respective duties and responsibilities and\nreceive the corresponding salaries and benefits unless in the meantime they are separated from the service\npursuant to Executive Order No. 17 (1986) or Article III of the Freedom Constitution. Their rights and\nprivileges shall also be governed by the executive orders respectively creating the two aforementioned offices."}},{"id":"PH-H17773-A6","no":6,"noLabel":{"en":"Sec 6"},"text":{"en":"Exercise of Police Power. The abolition of the Office of Muslim Affairs and Cultural Communities as\nprescribed in the entirety of this Executive Order is hereby intended and deemed to be an exercise of the\npolice power of the State."}},{"id":"PH-H17773-A7","no":7,"noLabel":{"en":"Sec 7"},"text":{"en":"Funding. Funds needed to carry out the provisions of this Executive Order shall be taken from funds\navailable in the Office of the Muslim Affairs and Cultural Communities."}},{"id":"PH-H17773-A8","no":8,"noLabel":{"en":"Sec 8"},"text":{"en":"Separability. Any portion or provision of this Executive Order that may be declared unconstitutional\nshall have the effect of nullifying other portions or provisions hereof as long as such remaining portions or\nprovisions can still subsist and be given effect in their entirety."}},{"id":"PH-H17773-A9","no":9,"noLabel":{"en":"Sec 9"},"text":{"en":"Repealing Clause. All laws, ordinances, rules, regulations, other issuances or parts thereof, which the\ninconsistent with this Executive Order, are hereby repealed or modified accordingly."}},{"id":"PH-H17773-A10","no":10,"noLabel":{"en":"Sec 10"},"text":{"en":"Effectivity. This Executive Order shall take effect immediately upon the approval of the three\nexecutive orders respectively creating the three aforementioned Offices.\nAPPROVED in the City of Manila, Philippines, this 30th day of January, in the year of Our Lord, nineteen\nhundred and eighty-seven."}}],"pack":"ph-p157"};
  FT["PH-H17774"] = {"id":"PH-H17774","coverage":"full","language":"en","sourceName":"The LawPhil Project — Arellano Law Foundation","sourceUrl":"","fetchedAt":"2026-10-28","articleCount":1,"structureMode":"WHOLE","title":{"zh":null,"en":"EXECUTIVE ORDER NO. FOR THE SURRENDER AND LICENSING AND ESTABLISHING A CENTRAL RECORDS FOR ALL FIRF.ARMS","orig":"EXECUTIVE ORDER NO. FOR THE SURRENDER AND LICENSING AND ESTABLISHING A CENTRAL RECORDS FOR ALL FIRF.ARMS"},"level":"law","status":"active","docNumber":"Executive Order No. 122","issuingBody":"President of the Philippines","completenessNote":"全文，共 1 条；逐字取自 LawPhil PDF 文本化成果（第三方 OCR，非机翻），原始文件 EO_00122_1993.txt","textQuality":"ocr-vendor","sourceFile":"菲律宾/法律原文/07_行政命令_EO/EO_00122_1993.txt","country":"PH","countryName":"菲律宾","layer":"intl","articles":[{"id":"PH-H17774-A1","no":1,"noLabel":{},"text":{"en":"surrenders\n(6)\nany qualified\nindividual,\nor corporation,\nthe approval\nof the Chief,\nPhilippine\n3.\nMemorandum Receipts\ngovernment\ncorresponding\npreviously\nand recalled\nimmediately.\nHenceforth,\nMemorandum Receipts\ngovernment-owned\nthe same shall\ngovernment\n/;\n~.\n'.\n1,.regulations.\nperformance\n\"'\n.-\"1\n;\n\"'\"\"\n'.,\n..'lmplementlng\n4.\nThe Firearms\nand Explosives\nPhilippine\nrepository\ninformation\npertaining\nand ammunition,\nNo. 1866 and implenlentingrules\nand regulations,\ncomputerize.\n(6)\neffectivity\nExecutiveOrder.\n5.\nTo complete\nthe firearms\ngovernment\ngovernment-owned\ncontrolled\ncorporations,\ngovernment\nFEO a complete\nFEOreports\nand subsequent\nimportations.\ncomply herewith\nand regulations.\nsectionimmediately.\n6.\nDONE in the City\nday of September\nHundred and Ninety-Three.\n~\n/"}}],"pack":"ph-p157"};
  FT["PH-H17775"] = {"id":"PH-H17775","coverage":"full","language":"en","sourceName":"The LawPhil Project — Arellano Law Foundation","sourceUrl":"","fetchedAt":"2026-10-28","articleCount":2,"structureMode":"ARTICLE","title":{"zh":null,"en":"MALACANAN'G BY THE PRESIDENT OF THE PHILIPPINES EXECUTIVE ORDER NO. FOR THE FULL IMPLEMENTATION OF EXECUTIVE 13. 1993 AND EXTENDING FOR THE REGISTRATION OF LOOSE FIREARMS UNRE-REGISTERED","orig":"MALACANAN'G BY THE PRESIDENT OF THE PHILIPPINES EXECUTIVE ORDER NO. FOR THE FULL IMPLEMENTATION OF EXECUTIVE 13. 1993 AND EXTENDING FOR THE REGISTRATION OF LOOSE FIREARMS UNRE-REGISTERED"},"level":"law","status":"active","docNumber":"Executive Order No. 122","issuingBody":"President of the Philippines","completenessNote":"全文，共 2 条；逐字取自 LawPhil PDF 文本化成果（第三方 OCR，非机翻），原始文件 EO_00122_1994.txt","textQuality":"ocr-vendor","sourceFile":"菲律宾/法律原文/07_行政命令_EO/EO_00122_1994.txt","country":"PH","countryName":"菲律宾","layer":"intl","articles":[{"id":"PH-H17775-A2","no":2,"noLabel":{"en":"SEC 2"},"text":{"en":"Any per30n who surrenders the loose firearm may apply\nfor a licence to possess the same if qualified.\nor transfer the firearms\nto any- qualified individual.\nfirm or corporation.\nsubject to the approval\nof the Chief. Philippine\nNational Police. not later than 8 September\n1994.\nto re-register\nto Executive\nOrder No. 122-A may still register the same\nwithin the same period provided in Section 1 hereof."}},{"id":"PH-H17775-A4","no":4,"noLabel":{"en":"SEC 4"},"text":{"en":"This Executive Order shall take effect immediately.\nDONE in the City of Manila, this\nday of March, in the year\nof Our Lord, Nineteen Hundred and Ninety-Four.\n/-\n~\n,\nBy the President:\n1 ,.1,,'\""}}],"pack":"ph-p157"};
  FT["PH-H17776"] = {"id":"PH-H17776","coverage":"full","language":"en","sourceName":"The LawPhil Project — Arellano Law Foundation","sourceUrl":"","fetchedAt":"2026-10-28","articleCount":4,"structureMode":"ARTICLE","title":{"zh":null,"en":"MALACANANG PMS lIBRARY BY THE PRESIDENT OF THE PHILIPPINES","orig":"MALACANANG PMS lIBRARY BY THE PRESIDENT OF THE PHILIPPINES"},"level":"law","status":"active","docNumber":"Executive Order No. 122","issuingBody":"President of the Philippines","completenessNote":"全文，共 4 条；逐字取自 LawPhil PDF 文本化成果（第三方 OCR，非机翻），原始文件 EO_00122_1999.txt","textQuality":"ocr-vendor","sourceFile":"菲律宾/法律原文/07_行政命令_EO/EO_00122_1999.txt","country":"PH","countryName":"菲律宾","layer":"intl","articles":[{"id":"PH-H17776-A2","no":2,"noLabel":{"en":"Sec 2"},"text":{"en":"Functions.\nThe Philippine International\nFilm and Television Office\nshall facilitate\nthe institutionalization\nof a One-Stop-Shop System for Foreign\nFilm Production.\nIt shall also undertake the following:\n1\nfacilitate the promotion and marketing of the Philippines as location\nsite for the production of international\nfilms and television programs;\n2.\nformulate an incentive package for foreign film companies interested\nin shooting films in the country;\n3.\ntelevision\nfilm makers\nand artists\ninterested\ntelevision\non-location\nproduction\nPhilippines;\n....\nassist foreign film companies in processing pertinent documents and ::::\nvarious requirements relative to the production of international films :......\nin the country;\n....,\n4.\n5.\ncoordinate with various government agencies in assisting the entry\nand exit of foreign film producers, artists and production crew;\n6.\nprovide direct link between foreign production companies, producers,\nfilmmakers\nand artists\nwith local production\nmanpower services,\nlocal artists, bit players and technical crew an~ facilities;\n7.\npromote and market locally produced films and television programs\nto international\nfilm and television markets,\nin coordination\nconcerned government and private entities;\n8.\nfacilitate.\nlocally-produced\ntelevision\nproductions\ninternationally\nfilm and television\nfestivals and award giving bodies;\n-'\n-\n6266\n\n9.\nDepartment\nPhilippine\nservices of tourism\noflocation\nsites/resources\nproduction\n10.\nprescribe internal\nand operational systems and procedures for the\nexercise of its functions\nand the performance\nof its duties and\nresponsibilities,\nthe organization\nof a secretariat for the\nday to day operation of the Office as well as determination\ncorresponding\nqualifications,\nfunctions thereon;\n11.\npromulgate\nsuch rules and regulations\nand' exercise such other\npowers and functions as may be necessary to carry out effectively its\nmandate; and,\n12.\nperform such other functions as may be authorized by the President\nof the Philippines.\nand Functions\nof the Executive\nThe Chairman of the Committee shall exercise the following duties and functions:\n1.\ndirect and supervise the operations and internal affairs of the Office;\n2.\nestablish the organizational structure and the staffing pattern of the\nsecretariat;\n....\nappoint the administrative and technica) personnel;\n::::.\nsuspend, dismiss or otherwise discipline for cause any employee, .:::\nand/or approve or disapprove the appointment,' transfer or detail of .:..\n3.\n4,\n5.\napprove and submit the annual and supplemental\n6.\nauthorized\nand Responsibilities\nof the Executive\nExecutive Director of the Office shall be the head of the Secretariat. He shall\nexercise the following duties and responsibilities:\nand enforce the decisions, orders, rules and\nregulations issued by the Executive Committee;\n1111\n16256\n\n2.\nappointment\nsubordinate personnel; and,\nadministrative\n3.\nfacilitate the preparation of the annual and supplemental\nthe Office and the Committee."}},{"id":"PH-H17776-A5","no":5,"noLabel":{"en":"Sec 5"},"text":{"en":"Annual Report. The Office shall, within three months after the end\nof every fiscal year, submit its annual report to the President."}},{"id":"PH-H17776-A6","no":6,"noLabel":{"en":"Sec 6"},"text":{"en":"Initial\nFund. To carry out the provisions of this Executive Order,\nthe release of the initial sum not exceeding TEN MILLION PESOS (P10,OOO,OOO.OO)\nhereby authorized chargeable against the Organizational Adjustment Fund under\nthe 1999 GAA (R.A. 8745). Thereafter, the budget of the Office and the Committee\nshall be integrated in the annual budget of the Office of the President."}},{"id":"PH-H17776-A7","no":7,"noLabel":{"en":"Sec 7"},"text":{"en":"Effectivity.\nThis Executive Order shall take effect immediately.\nDONE in the City of Manila, this\nLord, nineteen hundred and ninety nine.\nJuly in the year of Our\nPresident of the Republic of the Philippines\nBy the President:\n-~~~\nRONALDO B. ZAMORA\nExecutive Secretary"}}],"pack":"ph-p157"};
  FT["PH-H17777"] = {"id":"PH-H17777","coverage":"full","language":"en","sourceName":"The LawPhil Project — Arellano Law Foundation","sourceUrl":"","fetchedAt":"2026-10-28","articleCount":8,"structureMode":"ARTICLE","title":{"zh":null,"en":"MALACAÑANG PMS, LIBRARY BY THE PRESIDENT OF THE PHILIPPINES EXECUTIVE ORDER NO.","orig":"MALACAÑANG PMS, LIBRARY BY THE PRESIDENT OF THE PHILIPPINES EXECUTIVE ORDER NO."},"level":"law","status":"active","docNumber":"Executive Order No. 122","issuingBody":"President of the Philippines","completenessNote":"全文，共 8 条；逐字取自 LawPhil PDF 文本化成果（第三方 OCR，非机翻），原始文件 EO_00122_2002.txt","textQuality":"ocr-vendor","sourceFile":"菲律宾/法律原文/07_行政命令_EO/EO_00122_2002.txt","country":"PH","countryName":"菲律宾","layer":"intl","articles":[{"id":"PH-H17777-A1","no":1,"noLabel":{"en":"SECTION 1"},"text":{"en":"Constituting a Coordinating Committee for the Philippine Solo\nExhibition in Shanghai, China. A Coordinating Committee (hereinafter referred to as\nthe \"Committee\") is hereby constituted to oversee and undertake the necessary\npreparations for the First Solo Philippine Trade Fair in Shanghai, China scheduled on 24-"}},{"id":"PH-H17777-A2","no":2,"noLabel":{"en":"SEC 2"},"text":{"en":"Composition. The Committee shall be co-chaired by the Secretary of the\nDepartment of Trade and Industry and the Chairman of the Committee on Trade and\nIndustry of the House of Representatives. The Committee shall have the following\nPOMA Outgoing * 14662\n\n2\n1. Secretary of the Department of Tourism\n2. Secretary of the Department of Agriculture\n3. Secretary of the Department of Foreign Affairs\n4. Representative from the Office of the President\n5. President of the Philippine Exporters Confederation, Inc.\nCommittee members from the government sector may designate their alternates\npreferably with the rank of at least Director or the equivalent rank thereto. The\nCommittee may likewise solicit assistance from any private person, entity or association\nfor the successful implementation of the project."}},{"id":"PH-H17777-A3","no":3,"noLabel":{"en":"SEC 3"},"text":{"en":"Functions. The Committee shall exercise the following functions and\nresponsibilities:\na. Ensure that the economic advantages of the First Solo Philippine Trade Fair\nare maximized through a concerted and cost-effective country promotion;\nb. Approve the theme, concept, and message of the First Solo Philippine Trade\nc. Act as the coordinating body between the private sector and various\ngovernment agencies for the smooth implementation of the First Solo\nPhilippine Trade Fair in Shanghai;\nd. Ensure the safety and protection of government and personal properties,\nexhibit materials, and special effects needed to complete the First Solo\nPhilippine Trade Fair;\nSeek the assistance of and coordinate with the private sector and other non-\ngovernment organizations, in implementing the First Solo Philippine Trade\nFair in Shanghai and meeting the necessary requirements for the exhibition;\nf. Call on any relevant department, bureau, or office of the government,\nincluding government-owned and controlled corporations to render such\nassistance as it may need in the discharge of its functions;\ng. Monitor the progress of the preparations for the First Solo Philippine Trade\nh. Undertake all other measures necessary to ensure the success of the First Solo\nPhilippine Trade Fair."}},{"id":"PH-H17777-A4","no":4,"noLabel":{"en":"SEC 4"},"text":{"en":"Project Management. The Center for International Trade Expositions\nand Missions (CITEM) shall be in charge of project management. It shall service the\nCoordinating Committee's technical and administrative requirements and shall be\nauthorized, through its Executive Director, to negotiate and conclude contracts relative to\nthe Project, including those covering the services of consultants and contractuals/service\nproviders whose terms of office will end no later than two (2) months after the conclusion\nof the projects. The Chairman and Co-Chairman may also detail additional personnel\nfrom member-agencies to assist CITEM."}},{"id":"PH-H17777-A5","no":5,"noLabel":{"en":"SEC 5"},"text":{"en":"Funding.\nThe total project cost of FORTY MILLION PESOS\n(P40,000,000) be funded as follows: the amount of P10,000,000.00 shall be sourced\nPOMA Outgoing * 14663\n\n=\n3\nfrom the President's Contingent Fund for Fiscal Year 2002 and 2003 while the amount of\nP12,000,000.00 shall be contributed by the Department of Trade and Industry from its\nbudget for Fiscal year 2002 and 2003.\nThe balance shall be raised by the private sector and other relevant government\nagencies, on a best-effort basis."}},{"id":"PH-H17777-A6","no":6,"noLabel":{"en":"SEC 6"},"text":{"en":"Term of Committee. The Committee shall cease to exist upon termination\nof the project in April 2003."}},{"id":"PH-H17777-A7","no":7,"noLabel":{"en":"SEC 7"},"text":{"en":"Submission of Quarterly Reports. The Committee shall submit a report\non the status of preparations for the First Solo Philippine Trade Fair to the President\nevery quarter as well as a terminal report within sixty (60) days from the termination of\nthe project."}},{"id":"PH-H17777-A8","no":8,"noLabel":{"en":"SEC 8"},"text":{"en":"Effectivity. This Executive Order shall take effect immediately.\nDone in the City of Manila, this 12th day of September, in the year of Our\nLord, two thousand and two.\nBy the President:\nAllen o-Lameis\nALBERTO G. ROMULO\nExecutive Secretary\nPOMA Outgoing # 14664\nPMS LIBRARY BCODE001943"}}],"pack":"ph-p157"};
  FT["PH-H17778"] = {"id":"PH-H17778","coverage":"full","language":"en","sourceName":"The LawPhil Project — Arellano Law Foundation","sourceUrl":"","fetchedAt":"2026-10-28","articleCount":5,"structureMode":"ARTICLE","title":{"zh":null,"en":"MALACAÑAN PALACE BY THE PRESIDENT OF THE PHILIPPINES DECLARING AND DELINEATING THE BALABAC PORT ZONE AND PLACING IT UNDER THE ADMINISTRATIVE JURISDICTION OF THE PHILIPPINE PORTS AUTHORITY (PPA)","orig":"MALACAÑAN PALACE BY THE PRESIDENT OF THE PHILIPPINES DECLARING AND DELINEATING THE BALABAC PORT ZONE AND PLACING IT UNDER THE ADMINISTRATIVE JURISDICTION OF THE PHILIPPINE PORTS AUTHORITY (PPA)"},"level":"law","status":"active","docNumber":"Executive Order No. 122","issuingBody":"President of the Philippines","completenessNote":"全文，共 5 条；逐字取自 LawPhil PDF 文本化成果（第三方 OCR，非机翻），原始文件 EO_00122_2012.txt","textQuality":"ocr-vendor","sourceFile":"菲律宾/法律原文/07_行政命令_EO/EO_00122_2012.txt","country":"PH","countryName":"菲律宾","layer":"intl","articles":[{"id":"PH-H17778-A1","no":1,"noLabel":{"en":"SECTION 1"},"text":{"en":"Port of Balabac. The territorial jurisdiction of the Port of Balabac\nsituated in Barangay Poblacion, Municipality of Balabac, Province of Palawan, is hereby\ndelineated and established, particularly described as follows:\nBeginning at a point marked 1 on the plan, thence:\n00'\n2,570.00 m. to point of beginning,\nContaining a total area of THIRTY-THREE MILLION ONE HUNDRED NINETY.\nNINE THOUSAND NINE HUNDRED SEVEN SQUARE METERS AND FIFTY-SEVEN\nSQUARE DECIMETERS (33,199,907.57), more or less.\n@itice ofthe 3resident of the Chimines"}},{"id":"PH-H17778-A2","no":2,"noLabel":{"en":"SECTION 2"},"text":{"en":"PPA Jurisdiction. The Balabac Port Zone, as delineated, is hereby\nplaced under the administrative jurisdiction of the PPA, which shall, consistent with the\nregional industrial plans of the government, implement a program for the proper zoning,\nplanning, development and utilization of the port."}},{"id":"PH-H17778-A3","no":3,"noLabel":{"en":"SECTION 3"},"text":{"en":"Repeal. All issuances, orders, rules and regulations, or parts\nthereof, which are inconsistent with this Executive Order are hereby repealed, amended\nor modified accordingly."}},{"id":"PH-H17778-A4","no":4,"noLabel":{"en":"SECTION 4"},"text":{"en":"Separability. If any provision of this Executive Order is declared\ninvalid or unconstitutional, the other provisions not affected thereby shall remain valid\nand subsisting."}},{"id":"PH-H17778-A5","no":5,"noLabel":{"en":"SECTION 5"},"text":{"en":"Effectivity. This Executive Order shall take effect immediately upon\npublication in a newspaper of general circulation.\nDONE, in the City of Manila, this 21st\nLord, Two Thousand and Twelve.\nof December\n, in the year of our\nBy the President:\nPAQUITO N. OCHOA, JR.\nExecutive Secretary\n@fice of the 3President of the 3Bhirpiner\nCERTIFIED COPY\nMARIANITU M. DIMAANDAL\n2"}}],"pack":"ph-p157"};
  FT["PH-H17779"] = {"id":"PH-H17779","coverage":"full","language":"en","sourceName":"The LawPhil Project — Arellano Law Foundation","sourceUrl":"","fetchedAt":"2026-10-28","articleCount":14,"structureMode":"ARTICLE","title":{"zh":null,"en":"MALACAÑAN PALACE BY THE PRESIDENT OF THE PHILIPPINES STRENGTHENING BORDER CONTROL THROUGH THE ADOPTION AND IMPLEMENTATION OF THE ADVANCE PASSENGER INFORMATION","orig":"MALACAÑAN PALACE BY THE PRESIDENT OF THE PHILIPPINES STRENGTHENING BORDER CONTROL THROUGH THE ADOPTION AND IMPLEMENTATION OF THE ADVANCE PASSENGER INFORMATION"},"level":"law","status":"active","docNumber":"Executive Order No. 122","issuingBody":"President of the Philippines","completenessNote":"全文，共 14 条；逐字取自 LawPhil PDF 文本化成果（第三方 OCR，非机翻），原始文件 EO_00122_2020.txt","textQuality":"ocr-vendor","sourceFile":"菲律宾/法律原文/07_行政命令_EO/EO_00122_2020.txt","country":"PH","countryName":"菲律宾","layer":"intl","articles":[{"id":"PH-H17779-A1","no":1,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 1"},"text":{"en":"Definitions. For purposes of this Order, the following terms shall mean:\na. API refers to an electronic communication containing passenger- or crew/non-crew-\nrelated information, which is transmitted to the BI prior to arrival or departure and\nmade available on the primary line at the port of entry. API includes data relating to\nthe: (i) flight, such as flight number, arrival and departure times; and (2) individual\npassenger or crew/non-crew, such as name, date of birth, gender, citizenship and\ntravel document data that may be found in the machine readable zone of the passport\nor its equivalent;\nb. API System (APIS) refers to an electronic communications svstem that collects\nbiographic data from machine readable passports, other official travel documents or\nbasic details provided by commercial carriers. APIS may either be interactive or non-\ninteractive/batch style and shall include other program or system authorized or\nrecommended under pertinent international standards and guidelines;\nCommercial Carriers are persons, corporations, firms or associations engaged in the\nbusiness of carrying or transporting passengers or goods, or both, by sea or air, for\ncompensation, offering their services to the public. A Commercial Carrier may be a\npublic/common or private carrier; and\nd. Passengers a person carried on board a vessel or aircraft, excluding the master and\nmembers of the crew or other persons employed or engaged in any capacity on board\nsuch commercial vessel or aircraft."}},{"id":"PH-H17779-A2","no":2,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 2"},"text":{"en":"API Requirement. The captain, master or agent, or owner of a commercial\ncarrier whose vessel or aircraft is arriving in or departing from any port within the Philippine\n2\n\nterritory, shall provide the Bl the API of its passengers, and those of the crew and non-crew\nThe API shall serve as initial security vetting of passengers, crew and non-crew members\nto effectivel facilitate and expedite the arrival and departure process of legitimate travelers\nduring primary inspection. This, however, shall not exempt any passenger, crew or non-crew\nmember from submitting to physical primary inspection at the immigration counters of the ports\nof entrv or departure."}},{"id":"PH-H17779-A3","no":3,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 3"},"text":{"en":"API Data Elements, Format and Transmission. The API data elements,\nmessage format, structure and transmission method shall, to the extent allowed by relevant\nlaws, conform to internationally recognized standards and practices. The BI shall ensure that\nthe data elements required are limited to the minimum necessary, and data integrity is protected."}},{"id":"PH-H17779-A4","no":4,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 4"},"text":{"en":"Verification of Information. After receipt of the API, the BI shall perform\nsecurity vetting or derogatory information verification of the passengers, crew or non-crew\nmembers using its database and, whenever necessary, other available law enforcement and\nnon-law enforcement databases, including notices issued by the International Criminal Police\nOrganization and those subject of UN Security Council sanctions and travel bans.\nIn the event that errors are found in the API, the BI shall provide an opportunity to correct\nsuch errors or perform corrections after verification based on travel or other related documents.\nAn individual may only seek access to the API supplied by the commercial carrier if he or she\nis the subiect of the data being accessed."}},{"id":"PH-H17779-A5","no":5,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 5"},"text":{"en":"Management of the API. The BI shall implement security measures to\nprotect and ensure the integrity and availability of the API, such as restricting access thereto\nand using recognized security mechanisms or other reasonable safeguards to prevent\nunauthorized access. Only personnel authorized by the Commissioner of Immigration shall have\naccess to the APIS."}},{"id":"PH-H17779-A6","no":6,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 6"},"text":{"en":"Single Window. The Bl is hereby designated as the sole government agency\nauthorized to receive or manage the API and other forms of API data."}},{"id":"PH-H17779-A7","no":7,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 7"},"text":{"en":"Information Sharing. Subject to existing treaties, laws, rules and\nregulations, and whenever consistent with national interest, the BI may share information\ncontained in the API in furtherance of regional or international security. The API may also be\nprovided to the following law enforcement agencies, in furtherance of national security, law\nenforcement, immigration, intelligence and counter-terrorism functions, as may be required for\npublic safety and order:\na. Department of Finance - Bureau of Customs;\nb. Department of Transportation (DOT) - Office for Air Transportation Security;\nc. DOTr - Philippine Coast Guard;\nd. Department of Health - Bureau of Quarantine;\ne. Department of Justice - National Bureau of Investigation;\nf. Department of the Interior and Local Government - Philippine National Police;\ng. Department of National Defense;\nh. National Intelligence Coordinating Agency;\nArmed Forces of the Philippines;\n¡. National Security Council; and\nk. Anti-Terrorism Council.\nWhere disclosure is authorized, the recipient agency is likewise bound to comply with\nRA No. 10173 and other relevant laws.\n3"}},{"id":"PH-H17779-A8","no":8,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 8"},"text":{"en":"Sanctions. Any unauthorized disclosure, sharing, publication or use of the\ninformation considered as API shall be punishable in accordance with the relevant provisions of\nRA No. 10173, as-well as criminal and civil service laws, rules and regulations.\nThe captain, master or agent, or owner of a commercial carrier shall be liable for the\npayment of appropriate administrative fines under CA No. 613 and its implementing rules and\nregulations, for failure to provide API to the BI or to include a passenger, crew or non-crew\nmember in the API. Such penalty shall be imposed regardless of whether the BI eventually\ncleared the person for entry into the country, and is without prejudice to the filing of appropriate\nadministrative, civil and/or criminal charges pursuant to existing laws, rules and regulations,\nCrew or non-crew members not included in the API shall be shall be dealt with in\naccordance with immigration protocols under relevant laws, rules and regulations. Passengers\nmay be similarly treated if it can be shown that they were complicit in the omission of their names\nand other data from the API."}},{"id":"PH-H17779-A9","no":9,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 9"},"text":{"en":"Retention and Destruction of Data. Unless the information is classified as\nterrorism- or crime-related, data collected in the APIS shall be maintained for a period of not\nmore than twelve (12) months from the date of collection. The data shall thereafter be erased,\ndestroyed or disposed of in accordance with such rules and regulations as may hereinafter be\npromulgated pursuant to Section 11 hereof."}},{"id":"PH-H17779-A10","no":10,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 10"},"text":{"en":"Funding. The amount necessary for the initial implementation of this Order\nshall be charged against existing appropriations of the Bl. The funding requirements for\nsucceeding years shall be included in the budget proposal of the Bl, subject to the usual budget\npreparation process."}},{"id":"PH-H17779-A11","no":11,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 11"},"text":{"en":"Implementing Rules and Regulations. The BI, in consultation with the\nNational Privacy Commission and other relevant agencies, shall issue rules and regulations for\nthe implementation of this Order, within sixty (60) days from its effectivity."}},{"id":"PH-H17779-A12","no":12,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 12"},"text":{"en":"Repeal. All orders, rules and regulations, issuances, or any part thereof,\ninconsistent with the provisions of this Order are hereby repealed, amended or modified\naccordingly."}},{"id":"PH-H17779-A13","no":13,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 13"},"text":{"en":"Separability. Should any part or provision of this Order be held\nunconstitutional or invalid, the other parts or provisions not affected thereby shall continue to be\nin full force or effect."}},{"id":"PH-H17779-A14","no":14,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 14"},"text":{"en":"Effectivity. This Order shall take effect immediately upon publication in the\nOfficial Gazette or a newspaper of general circulation.\nDONE, in the City of Manila, this 15th day of December\nour Lord Two Thousand and Twenty.\n, in the year of\nBy the President:\nSALVADOR C. MEDIALDEA\nExecutive Secretary\nOffice of the P\n4\n016005\nATTY. COBSCEPCIOR ZERY E. FERBOLIMO-EMAD\nVal 12/15/220 DIRECTORI"}}],"pack":"ph-p157"};
  FT["PH-H17780"] = {"id":"PH-H17780","coverage":"full","language":"en","sourceName":"The LawPhil Project — Arellano Law Foundation","sourceUrl":"","fetchedAt":"2026-10-28","articleCount":16,"structureMode":"ARTICLE","title":{"zh":null,"en":"MALACAÑAN PALACE BY THE PRESIDENT OF THE PHILIPPINES ESTABLISHING A NATIONAL POLICY FRAMEWORK FOR DEVELOPING THE CRITICAL MINERALS INDUSTRY AND REORGANIZING THE MINING INDUSTRY COORDINATING COUNCIL FOR THE PURPOSE","orig":"MALACAÑAN PALACE BY THE PRESIDENT OF THE PHILIPPINES ESTABLISHING A NATIONAL POLICY FRAMEWORK FOR DEVELOPING THE CRITICAL MINERALS INDUSTRY AND REORGANIZING THE MINING INDUSTRY COORDINATING COUNCIL FOR THE PURPOSE"},"level":"law","status":"active","docNumber":"Executive Order No. 122","issuingBody":"President of the Philippines","completenessNote":"全文，共 16 条；逐字取自 LawPhil PDF 文本化成果（第三方 OCR，非机翻），原始文件 EO_00122_2026.txt","textQuality":"ocr-vendor","sourceFile":"菲律宾/法律原文/07_行政命令_EO/EO_00122_2026.txt","country":"PH","countryName":"菲律宾","layer":"intl","articles":[{"id":"PH-H17780-A1","no":1,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 1"},"text":{"en":"National Policy Framework for Developing the Critical\nMinerals Industry. The National Policy Framework for Developing the Critical\nMinerals Industry is hereby established. It shall provide strategic direction for\ndeveloping the Critical Minerals Industry in the country, in accordance with relevant\nlaws, rules, and regulations."}},{"id":"PH-H17780-A2","no":2,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 2"},"text":{"en":"Guiding Principles. The National Policy Framework for\nDeveloping the Critical Minerals Industry shall be guided by the following principles:\na. State Ownership: Mineral resources in public and private lands within\nthe territory and exclusive economic zones of the Republic of the\nPhilippines are owned by the State and, as such, the State shall receive\nits fair share in the full economic value thereof. All critical mineral projects\nshall be considered as national priority projects, and entities undertaking\nsuch projects shall be considered contractors of the State. The\nexploration, development, utilization, and conservation of these resources\nshall be regulated by the State to ensure their rational utilization, thereby\ncontributing to national growth.\nb. Economic Development through Critical Minerals: The State shall\npromote the responsible development and utilization of critical minerals\nand support value-adding and downstream industries, recognizing that\nthese resources are crucial for the Philippines' national security and\ndevelopment, and serve as essential raw materials for industrial activities,\nincluding the clean energy transition, digital transformation, and\ninfrastructure development.\n2\n\nc. Environmental Protection and Social/Cultural Development: The\ngovernment shall implement responsible and sustainable mining\npractices to strengthen the industry's capacity to manage environmental\nimpacts, while ensuring that the social, cultural, and economic\ndevelopment of host and neighboring communities aligns with the United\nNations Sustainable Development Goals.\nd. Policy Stability and Enabling Mechanisms for Private Sector\nParticipation: The State, recognizing the key role of the private sector in\nadvancing the responsible development of the country's critical mineral\nresources, shall maintain a stable, predictable, transparent, and\ninternationall competitive investment environment. The State commits to\nhonoring validly executed agreements, ensuring regulatory consistency,\npromoting whole-of-government coordination, and facilitating the timely\nimplementation of strategically critical mineral projects, consistent with\nthe Constitution, RA No. 7942, EO 79 (s. 2012), and other applicable\nlaws, rules, and regulations."}},{"id":"PH-H17780-A3","no":3,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 3"},"text":{"en":"National Exploration and Mineral Reservation Program. The\nDepartment of Environment and Natural Resources (DENR), through the Mines and\nGeosciences Bureau (MGB), shall implement a national exploration and mineral\nreservation program to identify and evaluate new critical mineral deposits, prioritizing\nthose essential for clean energy transition, digital transformation, and infrastructure\ndevelopment. For this purpose, \"critical minerals\" shall refer to minerals that are\nessential inputs for clean energy transition technologies, advanced manufacturing,\ndigital infrastructure, national defense, and other strategic industries necessary to\npromote industrialization, energy security, economic resilience, and sustainable\ndevelopment.\nThe DENR, in consultation with the Mining Industry Coordinating Council\n(MICC), shall issue the Philippine Critical Minerals List within thirty (30) days from\nthe effectivity of this Order, and shall thereafter periodically review and update the\nsame, as may be necessary.\nThe DENR-MGB shall undertake preliminary exploration in identified\nprospective areas, such as but not limited to freed-up areas covered by cancelled,\nexpired, relinquished, or surrendered mining tenements and offshore areas with high\nprospectivity for critical minerals, and upon confirmation of mineral potential,\nrecommend their declaration as a mineral reservation."}},{"id":"PH-H17780-A4","no":4,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 4"},"text":{"en":"Strict Implementation of the \"Use It or Lose It\" Policy for\nCritical Minerals Mining Tenements. The DENR shall strictly enforce the timely\nand responsible development of critical mineral mining tenements. Critical mining\ntenements that are found to be in material non-compliance with approved project\ntimelines, work programs, or development commitments, without valid justification\ndue to force majeure or causes beyond the control of the contractor, shall be subject\nto cancellation or other appropriate sanctions, in accordance with existing laws,\nrules, and regulations. Any order of cancellation or imposition of sanctions shall take\neffect immediately upon issuance.\n3\n\nFor this purpose, the DENR, in consultation with MICC, shall, within thirty (30)\ndays from the effectivity of this Order, formulate and issue clear, uniform, and\nobjective criteria and procedures for the evaluation of compliance with mining\ntenement obligations and the determination of material non-compliance therewith,\nconsistent with applicable laws, rules, and regulations.\nThe DENR-MGB shall likewise issue guidelines governing the procedure of\ncancellation and disposition of areas covered by cancelled mining tenements\ninvolving critical minerals to ensure their timely and responsible development. Such\nguidelines shall include procedures for technical evaluation, mineral resource\nassessment, environmental and social screening, determination of the appropriate\nmode of disposition, qualification standards for prospective proponents, and such\nother requirements as may be necessary to promote the sustainable development of\ncritical mineral resources."}},{"id":"PH-H17780-A5","no":5,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 5"},"text":{"en":"Accelerated Privatization of Government-Owned Critical\nMineral Mining Assets. The Privatization and Management Office, in coordination\nwith the DENR-MGB and other concerned agencies, and consistent with existing\nlaws, rules, and regulations, is directed to accelerate the disposition and privatization\nof all government-owned critical mineral mining assets."}},{"id":"PH-H17780-A6","no":6,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 6"},"text":{"en":"Declaration of Freed-up Areas and Mining Assets as Mineral\nReservation. Areas covered by cancelled, expired, relinquished, surrendered, or\notherwise freed-up critical mining tenements may be considered and recommended\nfor declaration as critical mineral reservations, subject to:\na. The final verification and assessment by the DENR-MGB for mineral potential\nand adherence to principles of sustainable and responsible mining; and\nb. Strategic importance in relation to critical minerals and domestic\nindustrialization goals.\nThe declaration of these areas as mineral reservations shall be established\nthrough a Presidential proclamation or issuance, upon the recommendation of the\nDENR Secretary. Upon declaration, the DENR-MGB shall dispose of these areas\nsubject to the applicable guidelines on the disposition of the cancelled mining\ntenement and other relevant laws and regulations."}},{"id":"PH-H17780-A7","no":7,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 7"},"text":{"en":"Streamlining and Digitalizing the Mining Permitting Process\nthrough a Virtual One-stop Shop. The DENR-MGB, in coordination with relevant\ngovernment agencies and local government units (LGUs), is hereby directed to:\na. Within six (6) months from the effectivity of this Order, implement\nstreamlined requirements and procedures in processing all mining-related\napplications, including the conduct of public consultation, and establish an\ninter-agency monitoring committee for all mining applications.\nThe streamlined procedure shall apply simultaneous processing to replace\nthe current sequential process, set clear timelines, and establish a\nperformance based\naccountabilitv\ngovernment\n4\n\nagencies/Instrumentalities involved in the permitting process.\nb. Within one (1) year from the effectivity of this Order, develop and\noperationalize a fully integrated digital platform that consolidates all\nnational and local government permits, licenses, and regulatory\nclearances related to mining applications. For this purpose, the platform\nshall interconnect and integrate existing agency regulatory systems and\ndatabases, avoiding the duplication of functions or the establishment of\nredundant systems."}},{"id":"PH-H17780-A8","no":8,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 8"},"text":{"en":"Promotion of Value-Adding Critical Mineral Processing\nInvestments. The Department of Trade and Industry - Board of Investments\n(DTI-BOI), in coordination with DENR and in consultation with industry stakeholders,\nshall promote investments for value-added mineral processing covering the entire\nmineral value chain.\nFor this purpose, the DTI-BOI shall formulate and implement\ncomprehensive development strategy that shall:\na. Promote the establishment of downstream industries, with a focus on\ncritical mineral refining, advanced material processing, and the\nmanufacturing of finished products such as, but not limited to, batteries,\nelectronic components, and renewable energy technologies;\nb. Support the development of side-stream industries, including energy\ngeneration, water supply systems, transport and logistics, and critical\nmineral recovery and recycling;\nc. Develop an incentives offer sheet to support value-added critical mineral\nprocessing and downstream industry growth consistent with RA No.\n11534, or the \"Corporate Recovery and Tax Incentives for Enterprises Act,\"\nas amended, and other relevant laws or issuances;\nd. Facilitate public-private partnerships and cluster development models\nwhere mineral producers collaborate with manufacturing sectors to localize\nproduction chains;\nGrant domestic mineral processing plants priority access to mineral ores at\na fair, market-based price. The fair price shall be determined in\naccordance with transparent pricing benchmarks and allowable\nadiustments determined by the MICC: and\nf. Ensure a sufficient supply of critical minerals for downstream industries,\nparticularly when local resources are unavailable or insufficient in quantit\nor quality, by diversifying sources, facilitating international partnerships,\nand establishing mechanisms to mitigate global supply disruptions."}},{"id":"PH-H17780-A9","no":9,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 9"},"text":{"en":"Securing Strategic Partnerships and Agreements on Critical\nMinerals. The DENR, Department of Foreign Affairs, DTI-BOI, Department of\nEnergy, and other relevant agencies shall prioritize partnerships focused on\nresponsible sourcing standards for critical minerals and environmental, social, and\ngovernance criteria as formulated and adopted by the MICC."}},{"id":"PH-H17780-A10","no":10,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 10"},"text":{"en":"Reorganization of the Mining Industry Coordinating Council.\nThe MICC shall be reorganized as follows:\n5\n\nCo-Chairpersons:\nSecretary, DENR\nSecretary, Department of Finance\nExecutive Secretary, Office of the President\nSecretary, Department of Justice\nSecretary, Department of Science and Technology\nSecretary, Department of Budget and Management\nSecretary, DTI\nSecretary, Department of Economy, Planning, and\nDevelopment (DEPDev)\nSecretary, Department of the Interior and Local\nGovernment\nSecretary, Department of Labor and Employment\nChairperson, National Commission on Indigenous\nPresident, Union of Local Authorities of the\nPhilippines\nThe DEPDev shall serve as the Secretariat of the MICC, and shall provide\nadministrative and technical support to the Council.\nThe Co-Chairpersons and members of the MICC may designate their\nrespective alternates, with ranks not lower than Assistant Secretary or its equivalent,\nwho shall be fully authorized to decide for or on their behalf.\nThe MICC shall have regular quarterly meetings and such special meetings\nas may be called upon by the Co-Chairpersons when deemed necessary.\nThe MICC may also request assistance from other government agencies and\ninstrumentalities, including LGUs, to provide full and timely cooperation to ensure the\neffective and efficient implementation of this Order."}},{"id":"PH-H17780-A11","no":11,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 11"},"text":{"en":"Duties and Functions of the MICC. In relation to EO No. 79\n(s. 2012), the MICC shall expand its functions to advance the development of the\nCritical Minerals Industry. To this end, the MICC shall perform the following duties\nand functions, without prejudice to other functions as may be directed by the\nPresident, through the Executive Secretary:\na. Submit a comprehensive work plan for the Critical Minerals Industry to the\nOffice of the President within ninety (90) days from the effectivity of this\nb. Assess and review critical mineral mining-related laws, issuances, and\nagreements to identify regulatory gaps and recommend policies that\noptimize economic benefits, strengthen institutional governance, and\nenforce stricter environmental and social safeguards;\nc. Review investment-related aspects of the Critical Mineral Industry, and\nmonitor program implementation;\nd. Advise the President on timely, effective solutions to overcome barriers to\ninvestment and promote industry growth;\n6\n\ne. Formulate and adopt sourcing standards for critical minerals consistent\nwith environmental, social, and governance criteria;\nf. Evaluate the feasibility of issuing a national valuation framework to assess\nthe economic, social, and cultural effects of critical mining activities and\ntheir impact on free, prior, informed consent negotiations;\ng. Submit annual reports to the President, through the Office of the Executive\nSecretary, on the critical mineral reserves, semi-annual actual data, and\nmulti-year forecasts on the inventory, production, and consumption of\ncritical minerals; and\nh. Perform such other functions necessary to advance the development of\nthe Critical Minerals Industry."}},{"id":"PH-H17780-A12","no":12,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 12"},"text":{"en":"Funding. The funding requirements for the initial implementation\nof this Order shall be charged against the current and available appropriations of the\nconcerned agencies, subject to pertinent budgeting, accounting, and auditing laws,\nrules, and regulations. Thereafter, the funding requirements for its continued\nimplementation shall be included in the respective budget proposals of the\nconcerned agencies, subject to the usual budget preparation process and consistent\nwith government accounting and auditing laws, rules, and regulations."}},{"id":"PH-H17780-A13","no":13,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 13"},"text":{"en":"Supplemental Guidelines. The DEN and MGB, in coordination\nwith the MICC, shall formulate and issue supplemental guidelines to ensure effective\nimplementation of this Order."}},{"id":"PH-H17780-A14","no":14,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 14"},"text":{"en":"Separability. If any part or provision of this Order shall be held\nunconstitutional or invalid, other parts or provisions not affected thereby shall\ncontinue to be in full force and effect."}},{"id":"PH-H17780-A15","no":15,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 15"},"text":{"en":"Repeal. All other rules, regulations, and issuances or parts\nthereof, that are inconsistent with this Order, are hereby repealed or modified\naccordingly."}},{"id":"PH-H17780-A16","no":16,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 16"},"text":{"en":"Effectivity. This Order shall take effect immediately upon its\npublication in the Official Gazette or in a newspaper of general circulation.\nDONE, in the City of Manila, this 18th day of August in the year of our\nLord, Two Thousand and Twenty-Six.\nBy the President:\nURALPH G RECTO\nActing Execytive Secretary\nREPUBLIC OF THE PHILIPPINES\n7\nOffice of the President\nMALACAÑANG RECORDS OFFICE\nCERTINED COPY\n¡ATTY. YATRISHA ANALINE B. KOK\n75-19-2024\nDIRECTOR IV"}}],"pack":"ph-p157"};
  FT["PH-H17781"] = {"id":"PH-H17781","coverage":"full","language":"en","sourceName":"The LawPhil Project — Arellano Law Foundation","sourceUrl":"LawPhil (HTML full text only)  |  https://lawphil.net/executive/execord/eo1937/eo_123_1937.html","fetchedAt":"2026-10-28","articleCount":1,"structureMode":"WHOLE","title":{"zh":null,"en":"Promulgating Regulations to Govern Salvage Work in the Philippines","orig":"Promulgating Regulations to Govern Salvage Work in the Philippines"},"level":"law","status":"active","docNumber":"Executive Order No. 123","issuingBody":"President of the Philippines","promulgatedDate":"1937-10-15","completenessNote":"全文，共 1 条；逐字取自 LawPhil PDF 文本化成果（第三方 OCR，非机翻），原始文件 EO_00123_1937_html.txt","textQuality":"ocr-vendor","sourceFile":"菲律宾/法律原文/07_行政命令_EO/EO_00123_1937_html.txt","country":"PH","countryName":"菲律宾","layer":"intl","articles":[{"id":"PH-H17781-A1","no":1,"noLabel":{},"text":{"en":"MALACAÑAN PALACE\nBY THE PRESIDENT OF THE PHILIPPINES\n[ EXECUTIVE ORDER NO. 123, October 15, 1937 ]\nPROMULGATING REGULATIONS TO GOVERN SALVAGE WORK IN THE PHILIPPINES\nWHEREAS, as a matter of general policy, it is in the interest of the public service that the Government\npromulgate regulations to govern salvage work in the Philippines;\nNOW, THEREFORE, I, MANUEL L. QUEZON, President of the Philippines, by virtue of the powers vested\nin me by law, do hereby issue the following regulations for the guidance of all concerned:\n1. No vessel shall undertake any salvage work in the Philippines without securing a permit from the Insular\nCollector of Customs.\n2. Only vessels of America or Philippine registry shall be authorized to undertake salvage work when they are\navailable for such work.\n3. In case a foreign vessel is authorized to perform salvage work, permits shall be granted subject to the\ncondition that neither the vessel nor its officers and crew shall take use or visits ports which have not been\nlegally declared ports of entry for foreign shipping.\n4. Excepting cases of emergency where there is serious and imminent danger to life and property, no foreign\nvessel shall be authorized to undertake salvage work in the Philippines, unless the country in which said\nvessel is registered allows vessels of American and Philippine registry to perform salvage work under similar\nconditions within its territorial waters.\nDone at the City of Manila, this fifteenth day of October, in the year of Our Lord, nineteen hundred and\nthirty-seven, and of the Commonwealth of the Philippines, the second.\n(Sgd.) MANUEL L. QUEZON\nPresident of the Philippines\nBy the President:\n(Sgd.) ELPIDIO QUIRINO\nSecretary of the Interior"}}],"pack":"ph-p157"};
  FT["PH-H17782"] = {"id":"PH-H17782","coverage":"full","language":"en","sourceName":"The LawPhil Project — Arellano Law Foundation","sourceUrl":"LawPhil (HTML full text only)  |  https://lawphil.net/executive/execord/eo1948/eo_123_1948.html","fetchedAt":"2026-10-28","articleCount":1,"structureMode":"WHOLE","title":{"zh":null,"en":"Fixing Office Hours During the Hot Season","orig":"Fixing Office Hours During the Hot Season"},"level":"law","status":"active","docNumber":"Executive Order No. 123","issuingBody":"President of the Philippines","promulgatedDate":"1948-03-19","completenessNote":"全文，共 1 条；逐字取自 LawPhil PDF 文本化成果（第三方 OCR，非机翻），原始文件 EO_00123_1948_html.txt","textQuality":"ocr-vendor","sourceFile":"菲律宾/法律原文/07_行政命令_EO/EO_00123_1948_html.txt","country":"PH","countryName":"菲律宾","layer":"intl","articles":[{"id":"PH-H17782-A1","no":1,"noLabel":{},"text":{"en":"MALACAÑAN PALACE\nBY THE PRESIDENT OF THE PHILIPPINES\n[ EXECUTIVE ORDER NO. 123, March 19, 1948 ]\nFIXING OFFICE HOURS DURING THE HOT SEASON\nPursuant to the provisions of section 564 of the Revised Administrative Code, the office hours of all\nGovernment bureaus and offices, including the provincial, city and municipal governments, during the period\nfrom April 1 to June 1, 1948, both dates inclusive, are hereby fixed to five continuous hours which shall be\nfrom eight o’clock in the morning to one o’ clock in the afternoon. The provisions of this Order shall not\napply to the offices in the City of Baguio , whether national, provincial or municipal.\nThis order shall not oblige the head of any department, bureau, or office to reduce as herein provided the\noffice hours in his department, bureau, or office, but leaves the same in his discretion subject to the\nrequirements of the service.\nDone at the City of Manila , this 19th day of March, in the year of Our Lord, nineteen hundred and forty-eight,\nand of the Independence of the Philippines , the second.\n(Sgd.) MANUEL ROXAS\nPresident of the Philippines\nBy the President:\n(Sgd.) EMILIO ABELLO\nChief of the Executive Office"}}],"pack":"ph-p157"};
  FT["PH-H17783"] = {"id":"PH-H17783","coverage":"full","language":"en","sourceName":"The LawPhil Project — Arellano Law Foundation","sourceUrl":"","fetchedAt":"2026-10-28","articleCount":1,"structureMode":"WHOLE","title":{"zh":null,"en":"MALACAÑANg RESIDENCE OF THE PRESIDENT OF THE PHILIPPINES BY THE PRESIDENT OF THE PHILIPPINES CREATING THE TAGAYTAY DEVELOPMENT COMMISSION","orig":"MALACAÑANg RESIDENCE OF THE PRESIDENT OF THE PHILIPPINES BY THE PRESIDENT OF THE PHILIPPINES CREATING THE TAGAYTAY DEVELOPMENT COMMISSION"},"level":"law","status":"active","docNumber":"Executive Order No. 123","issuingBody":"President of the Philippines","completenessNote":"全文，共 1 条；逐字取自 LawPhil PDF 文本化成果（第三方 OCR，非机翻），原始文件 EO_00123_1955.txt","textQuality":"ocr-vendor","sourceFile":"菲律宾/法律原文/07_行政命令_EO/EO_00123_1955.txt","country":"PH","countryName":"菲律宾","layer":"intl","articles":[{"id":"PH-H17783-A1","no":1,"noLabel":{},"text":{"en":"mic, health, social, and community development of Tagay-\ntay City in particular and the country in general.\nThe Commission shall be composed of the following:\nMr. Ramon V. del Rosario\nCol. Salvador T. Villa\nMr. Felipe Monserrat\nMr. Anselmo Alquinto\nMr. Enrique Zobel ............\nMr. Leopoldo Coronel ..\n...\nMrs. Esperanza A. Zamora ...\nMayor Isaac Tolentino, Tagaytay City..........\nMr. Hector Moreno .......................\nThe Commission may create such committees as it\nmay deem necessary for the proper implementation of\nits projects and the attainment of its objectives.\nThe Commission is hereby authorized to call upon any\ndepartment, bureau, office, ageney or instrumentality of\nthe Government, or any official or employee thereof, for\nsuch assistance as it may need in the performance of its\nfunction. It may also call upon civic organizations,\nprivate entities and property owners for the same purpose.\nDone in the City of Manila, this 29th day of July, in\nthe year of Our Lord, nineteen hundred and fifty-five,\nand of the Independence of the Philippines, the tenth.\nRAMON MAGSAYSAY\nPresident of the Philippines\nBy the President:\nFRED RUIZ CaSTRO\nExecutive Secretary"}}],"pack":"ph-p157"};
  FT["PH-H17784"] = {"id":"PH-H17784","coverage":"full","language":"en","sourceName":"The LawPhil Project — Arellano Law Foundation","sourceUrl":"LawPhil (HTML full text only)  |  https://lawphil.net/executive/execord/eo1968/eo_123_1968.html","fetchedAt":"2026-10-28","articleCount":1,"structureMode":"WHOLE","title":{"zh":null,"en":"Further Amending Executive Order No. 58 Dated August 4, 1954, as Amended, By Giving the National Shrines Commission the Authority to Enter Into Any Contract for the Purpose of Converting Areas Into Tourist Spots and Leasing Them to Qualified Parties.","orig":"Further Amending Executive Order No. 58 Dated August 4, 1954, as Amended, By Giving the National Shrines Commission the Authority to Enter Into Any Contract for the Purpose of Converting Areas Into Tourist Spots and Leasing Them to Qualified Parties."},"level":"law","status":"active","docNumber":"Executive Order No. 123","issuingBody":"President of the Philippines","promulgatedDate":"1968-03-15","completenessNote":"全文，共 1 条；逐字取自 LawPhil PDF 文本化成果（第三方 OCR，非机翻），原始文件 EO_00123_1968_html.txt","textQuality":"ocr-vendor","sourceFile":"菲律宾/法律原文/07_行政命令_EO/EO_00123_1968_html.txt","country":"PH","countryName":"菲律宾","layer":"intl","articles":[{"id":"PH-H17784-A1","no":1,"noLabel":{},"text":{"en":"MALACAÑAN PALACE\nBY THE PRESIDENT OF THE PHILIPPINES\n[ Executive Order No. 123, March 15, 1968 ]\nFURTHER AMENDING EXECUTIVE ORDER NO. 58 DATED AUGUST 4, 1954, AS AMENDED, BY\nGIVING THE NATIONAL SHRINES COMMISSION THE AUTHORITY TO ENTER INTO ANY\nCONTRACT FOR THE PURPOSE OF CONVERTING AREAS INTO TOURIST SPOTS AND LEASING\nTHEM TO QUALIFIED PARTIES\nPursuant to the power vested in me by law, I, FERDINAND E. MARCOS, President of the Philippines, do\nhereby amend paragraph 5 of Executive Order No. 58 dated August 4, 1954, to read as follows:\n“The Commission shall conduct studies and prepare a general program for the development of national parks\nembracing all the historic areas and recommend to the President a plan for appropriate memorials or\nmonuments wherever they are deemed desirable, taking into account the topography, vegetation, end\nhistorical background of the places selected for the purpose. The Commission, is hereby authorized, with the\nprior approval of the President, to enter into any contract for the conversion of areas within national shrines\ninto tourist spots and to lease such areas to any citizen or citizens of the Philippines, or any corporation 60%\nof the capital stock of which belongs to Filipino citizens.”\nThis order shall take effect immediately.\nDone in the City of Manila, this 15th day of March, in the year of Our Lord, nineteen hundred and sixty-eight.\n(Sgd.) FERDINAND E. MARCOS\nPresident of the Philippines\nBy the President:\n(Sgd.) RAFAEL M. SALAS\nExecutive Secretary"}}],"pack":"ph-p157"};
  FT["PH-H17785"] = {"id":"PH-H17785","coverage":"full","language":"en","sourceName":"The LawPhil Project — Arellano Law Foundation","sourceUrl":"LawPhil (source has HTML full text only)","fetchedAt":"2026-10-28","articleCount":1,"structureMode":"WHOLE","title":{"zh":null,"en":"Reorganizing the Ministry of Social Services and Development, Now Referred to as Ministry of Social Welfare and Development.","orig":"Reorganizing the Ministry of Social Services and Development, Now Referred to as Ministry of Social Welfare and Development."},"level":"law","status":"active","docNumber":"Executive Order No. 123","issuingBody":"President of the Philippines","promulgatedDate":"1987-01-30","completenessNote":"全文，共 1 条；逐字取自 LawPhil PDF 文本化成果（第三方 OCR，非机翻），原始文件 EO_00123_1987_html.txt","textQuality":"ocr-vendor","sourceFile":"菲律宾/法律原文/07_行政命令_EO/EO_00123_1987_html.txt","country":"PH","countryName":"菲律宾","layer":"intl","articles":[{"id":"PH-H17785-A3","no":3,"noLabel":{"en":"Article III"},"text":{"en":"of the Freedom Constitution;\nHAVING IN MIND that, pursuant to Executive Order No. 5 (1986), it is directed that necessary and proper\nchanges in the organizational and functional structures of the government, its agencies and instrumentalities,\nbe effected in order to promote efficiency and effectiveness in the delivery of public services;\nCONSIDERING that the right to welfare is a basic right which is enshrined in the Constitution;\nBELIEVING that welfare encompasses a range of services which addresses the needs of the extremely\ndisadvantaged individual, family, group and community in a holistic manner;\nBELIEVING that the desired scheme is for welfare and development to be a shared concern between the State\nand its people;\nNOW, THEREFORE, I, CORAZON C. AQUINO, President of the Philippines, by virtue of the powers vested\nin me by the sovereign will of the Filipino People and the Freedom Constitution, do hereby order:\nSECTION 1 to Sec. 31\nSec. 2. Effectivity. This Executive Order shall take effect immediately upon its approval.\nAPPROVED in the City of Manila, Philippines, this 30th day of January, in the year of Our Lord, nineteen\nhundred and eighty-seven."}}],"pack":"ph-p157"};
  FT["PH-H17786"] = {"id":"PH-H17786","coverage":"full","language":"en","sourceName":"The LawPhil Project — Arellano Law Foundation","sourceUrl":"","fetchedAt":"2026-10-28","articleCount":1,"structureMode":"WHOLE","title":{"zh":null,"en":"MALACANANG BY THE PRESIDENT OF THE PHILIPPINES INSTITUTIONALIZING THE COMMITTEE ON FOWER CONSERVATION AND DEMAND MANAGEMENT","orig":"MALACANANG BY THE PRESIDENT OF THE PHILIPPINES INSTITUTIONALIZING THE COMMITTEE ON FOWER CONSERVATION AND DEMAND MANAGEMENT"},"level":"law","status":"active","docNumber":"Executive Order No. 123","issuingBody":"President of the Philippines","completenessNote":"全文，共 1 条；逐字取自 LawPhil PDF 文本化成果（第三方 OCR，非机翻），原始文件 EO_00123_1993.txt","textQuality":"ocr-vendor","sourceFile":"菲律宾/法律原文/07_行政命令_EO/EO_00123_1993.txt","country":"PH","countryName":"菲律宾","layer":"intl","articles":[{"id":"PH-H17786-A7","no":7,"noLabel":{"en":"SEC 7"},"text":{"en":"immediately.\nDone in the City\nday of September\n!\\,1~"}}],"pack":"ph-p157"};
  FT["PH-H17787"] = {"id":"PH-H17787","coverage":"full","language":"en","sourceName":"The LawPhil Project — Arellano Law Foundation","sourceUrl":"","fetchedAt":"2026-10-28","articleCount":3,"structureMode":"ARTICLE","title":{"zh":null,"en":"BY THE PRESIDENT OF THE PHILIPPINES","orig":"BY THE PRESIDENT OF THE PHILIPPINES"},"level":"law","status":"active","docNumber":"Executive Order No. 123","issuingBody":"President of the Philippines","completenessNote":"全文，共 3 条；逐字取自 LawPhil PDF 文本化成果（第三方 OCR，非机翻），原始文件 EO_00123_1999.txt","textQuality":"ocr-vendor","sourceFile":"菲律宾/法律原文/07_行政命令_EO/EO_00123_1999.txt","country":"PH","countryName":"菲律宾","layer":"intl","articles":[{"id":"PH-H17787-A1","no":1,"noLabel":{"en":"SECTION 1"},"text":{"en":"Repeal of EO No. 103 and EO No. 105. Executive\nOrder No. 103 s. 1999 and Executive Order No. 105 s. 1999 are hereby\nrepealed. The supervision of the NAFC shall revert to the Department of\nAgriculture.\nThe NAFC shall continue to perform its functions\nto its mandate.\n\nThe National\nFood Security\nshall be chaired\nthe National\nSecretariat\non Food Security organized\nto EO No. 86 shall act as the secretariat.\nTransitory\nAll planned or ongbing projects\nof the OPAFS are hereby transferred\nDA for review and\nimplementation\nor disposition, as appropriate."}},{"id":"PH-H17787-A3","no":3,"noLabel":{"en":"SECTION 3"},"text":{"en":"RepeaUn2 Clause. All other executive issuances and\nPresidential instructions\ninconsistent herewith are hereby repealed."}},{"id":"PH-H17787-A4","no":4,"noLabel":{"en":"SECTION 4"},"text":{"en":"Effectivitv.\nThis Order shall take effect immediately.\nDONE in the City of Manila, thiS'~~ay\nof July, in the year of Our\nLord, Nineteen Hundred and Ninety Nine.\n~,\nEJERCITO ESTRADA\nPMS LIBRARY:\nBy the President:\n~\nRONALDO B. ZAMORA\nExecu tive Secretary"}}],"pack":"ph-p157"};
  FT["PH-H17788"] = {"id":"PH-H17788","coverage":"full","language":"en","sourceName":"The LawPhil Project — Arellano Law Foundation","sourceUrl":"","fetchedAt":"2026-10-28","articleCount":8,"structureMode":"ARTICLE","title":{"zh":null,"en":"MALACANANG PMS LIBRARY BY THE PRESIDENT OF THE PHILIPPINES EXECUTIVE ORDER NO.","orig":"MALACANANG PMS LIBRARY BY THE PRESIDENT OF THE PHILIPPINES EXECUTIVE ORDER NO."},"level":"law","status":"active","docNumber":"Executive Order No. 123","issuingBody":"President of the Philippines","completenessNote":"全文，共 8 条；逐字取自 LawPhil PDF 文本化成果（第三方 OCR，非机翻），原始文件 EO_00123_2002.txt","textQuality":"ocr-vendor","sourceFile":"菲律宾/法律原文/07_行政命令_EO/EO_00123_2002.txt","country":"PH","countryName":"菲律宾","layer":"intl","articles":[{"id":"PH-H17788-A1","no":1,"noLabel":{"en":"SECTION 1"},"text":{"en":"The NWRB, presently under the DPWH, is hereby transferred to\nthe Office of the President.\nPOMA Outgoing * 14659\n\n21"}},{"id":"PH-H17788-A2","no":2,"noLabel":{"en":"SEC 2"},"text":{"en":"Pursuant to PD 424, the membership of the Board is hereby\nreconstituted to exclude those with direct claims on water resources. The new Board\nshall be composed of the following:\nSecretary of Environment and Natural Resources\nSecretary of Socio-Economic Planning\nSecretary of Justice\nSecretary of Finance\nSecretary of Health\nDirector, National Hydraulic Research Center (NHRC),\nUniversity of the Philippines\nExecutive Director, NWRB Secretariat"}},{"id":"PH-H17788-A3","no":3,"noLabel":{"en":"SEC 3"},"text":{"en":"The NWRB shall immediately initiate a review of the Implementing\nRules and Regulations (IRR) of the Water Code of the Philippines, and shall amend the\nsame as may be necessary to effectively implement and enforce the provisions of the\nCode. The NWRB shall likewise formulate a new/revised organization structure for its\nSecretariat to effectively and efficiently carry out its mandate under PDs 424 and 1067,\nsubject to approval by the President, through the Department of Budget and Management\n(DBM), and the Civil Service Commission."}},{"id":"PH-H17788-A4","no":4,"noLabel":{"en":"SEC 4"},"text":{"en":"Upon approval by the President of the new/revised organization and\nmanpower structure of the NWRB Secretariat, the NWRB shall then be transferred to\nDEN as a bureau for purposes of administrative control and supervision."}},{"id":"PH-H17788-A5","no":5,"noLabel":{"en":"SEC 5"},"text":{"en":"The DEN shall ensure that the NWRB Secretariat is managed\neffectively, efficiently and economically. For this purpose, DENR shall:\na. rationalize/harmonize its organizational structure, together with that of\nNWRB, to eliminate duplication of functions and facilitate integration and\ncoordination:\nb. ensure the effective and continuous implementation of NWRB's policies and\nprograms without unduly expanding its personnel and resource requirements;\nc. enjoin NWRB to utilize existing DENR structures and facilities to effectively\nperform its functions; and\nd. streamline the systems and procedures and/or decentralization of functions\nwith the end view of rendering faster service without surrendering appropriate\nUpon the effectivity of this Order, the Local Water Utilities\nAdministration (LWUA) shall cease and desist with its practice of regulating the water\nPOMA Outgoing * 14660\n\n31\ntariffs of Water Districts which shall hereinafter be undertaken by NWRB. However,\nLWUA, consistent with its mandate under PD No. 198, may continue reviewing the rates\"\nof water districts which it has financial exposure, with the end view of ensuring their\nfinancial viabilities.\nThe Presidential Task Force created under EO 374, series of 1996, as amended by\nEO 409, series of 1997, is hereby abolished."}},{"id":"PH-H17788-A7","no":7,"noLabel":{"en":"SEC 7"},"text":{"en":"If any provision of this Order is declared unconstitutional or invalid, the\nother provisions not affected thereby should remain in full force and effect."}},{"id":"PH-H17788-A8","no":8,"noLabel":{"en":"SEC 8"},"text":{"en":"All orders, executive issuances, rules and regulations, or parts thereof\ninconsistent with the provisions of this Executive Order are hereby repealed or modified\naccordingly."}},{"id":"PH-H17788-A9","no":9,"noLabel":{"en":"SEC 9"},"text":{"en":"This Executive Order shall take effect upon its publication in at least\none newspaper of general circulation in the Philippines.\nDONE in the City of Manila, this 12th day of September, in the year of our\nLord, two thousand and two.\nBy the President:\nALBERTO G. ROMULO\nExecutive Secretary\nPMS LIBRARY BCODE001952\nPOMA Outgoing * 14661"}}],"pack":"ph-p157"};
  FT["PH-H17789"] = {"id":"PH-H17789","coverage":"full","language":"en","sourceName":"The LawPhil Project — Arellano Law Foundation","sourceUrl":"","fetchedAt":"2026-10-28","articleCount":5,"structureMode":"ARTICLE","title":{"zh":null,"en":"MALACAÑAN PALACE BY THE PRESIDENT OF THE PHILIPPINES DECLARING AND DELINEATING THE RIZAL PORT ZONE AND PLACING IT UNDER THE ADMINISTRATIVE JURISDICTION OF THE PHILIPPINE PORTS AUTHORITY (PPA)","orig":"MALACAÑAN PALACE BY THE PRESIDENT OF THE PHILIPPINES DECLARING AND DELINEATING THE RIZAL PORT ZONE AND PLACING IT UNDER THE ADMINISTRATIVE JURISDICTION OF THE PHILIPPINE PORTS AUTHORITY (PPA)"},"level":"law","status":"active","docNumber":"Executive Order No. 123","issuingBody":"President of the Philippines","completenessNote":"全文，共 5 条；逐字取自 LawPhil PDF 文本化成果（第三方 OCR，非机翻），原始文件 EO_00123_2012.txt","textQuality":"ocr-vendor","sourceFile":"菲律宾/法律原文/07_行政命令_EO/EO_00123_2012.txt","country":"PH","countryName":"菲律宾","layer":"intl","articles":[{"id":"PH-H17789-A1","no":1,"noLabel":{"en":"SECTION 1"},"text":{"en":"Port of Rial. The territorial jurisdiction of the Port of Rizal situated\nin Barangay Punta Baja, Municipality of Rizal, Province of Palawan, is hereby\ndelineated and established, particularly described as follows:\nBeginning at a point marked 1 on the plan, thence:\n575.03 m. to point of beginning,\nContaining a total area of EIGHT HUNDRED FORTY-ONE THOUSAND SIX\nHUNDRED THIRTY-NINE SQUARE METERS AND THIRTY-SEVEN SQUARE\nDECIMETERS (841,639.37), more or less.\n@ffice of the President of the 39himpines"}},{"id":"PH-H17789-A2","no":2,"noLabel":{"en":"SECTION 2"},"text":{"en":"PPA Jurisdiction. The Rizal Port Zone, as delineated, is hereby\nplaced under the administrative jurisdiction of the PA, which shall, consistent with the\nregional industrial plans of the government, implement a program for the proper zoning,\nplanning, development and utilization of the port."}},{"id":"PH-H17789-A3","no":3,"noLabel":{"en":"SECTION 3"},"text":{"en":"Repeal. All issuances, orders, rules and regulations, or parts\nthereof, which are inconsistent with this Executive Order are hereby repealed, amended\nor modified accordingly."}},{"id":"PH-H17789-A4","no":4,"noLabel":{"en":"SECTION 4"},"text":{"en":"Separability. If any provision of this Executive Order is declared\ninvalid or unconstitutional, the other provisions not affected thereby shall remain valid\nand subsisting."}},{"id":"PH-H17789-A5","no":5,"noLabel":{"en":"SECTION 5"},"text":{"en":"Effectivity. This Executive Order shall take effect immediately upon\npublication in a newspaper of general circulation.\nDONE, in the City of Manila, this 21st of December , in the year of our\nLord, Two Thousand and Twelve.\nBy the President:\nPAQUITO N. OCHOA, JR.\nExecutive Secretary\nOffice of the\n3Brestent ofthe 39hilmines\nLEPTIFIED COPY.\n161-2-2010\nMARIANITE M DIMATANDAL\nDIRECTOR IV@1-2-20B\nMALACARANG RECORDS OFFICE"}}],"pack":"ph-p157"};
  FT["PH-H17790"] = {"id":"PH-H17790","coverage":"full","language":"en","sourceName":"The LawPhil Project — Arellano Law Foundation","sourceUrl":"","fetchedAt":"2026-10-28","articleCount":6,"structureMode":"ARTICLE","title":{"zh":null,"en":"MALACAÑAN PALACE BY THE PRESIDENT OF THE PHILIPPINES MODIFYING THE RATES OF IMPORT DUTY ON CERTAIN AGRICULTURAL PRODUCTS UNDER SECTION OTHERWISE KNOWN AS THE CUSTOMS MODERNIZATION AND TARIFF ACT","orig":"MALACAÑAN PALACE BY THE PRESIDENT OF THE PHILIPPINES MODIFYING THE RATES OF IMPORT DUTY ON CERTAIN AGRICULTURAL PRODUCTS UNDER SECTION OTHERWISE KNOWN AS THE CUSTOMS MODERNIZATION AND TARIFF ACT"},"level":"law","status":"active","docNumber":"Executive Order No. 123","issuingBody":"President of the Philippines","completenessNote":"全文，共 6 条；逐字取自 LawPhil PDF 文本化成果（第三方 OCR，非机翻），原始文件 EO_00123_2021.txt","textQuality":"ocr-vendor","sourceFile":"菲律宾/法律原文/07_行政命令_EO/EO_00123_2021.txt","country":"PH","countryName":"菲律宾","layer":"intl","articles":[{"id":"PH-H17790-A1","no":1,"noLabel":{"en":"SECTION 1"},"text":{"en":"Rates of Import Duty. The articles specifically listed in Annex\nA hereof, as classified in compliance with Section 1611 of RA No. 10863, shall be\nsubject to the Most Favoured Nation (MFN) rates of import duty in accordance with\nthe schedule indicated opposite each article.\nTHE PRESIDENT OF THE PHILIPPINES"}},{"id":"PH-H17790-A2","no":2,"noLabel":{"en":"SECTION 2"},"text":{"en":"Articles Represented with \" XX\". The rates of import duty\non tariff headings and subheadings which are not listed in Annex A hereof, and those\nlisted but represented by the symbol \"XXX\" shall remain in force and in effect."}},{"id":"PH-H17790-A3","no":3,"noLabel":{"en":"SECTION 3"},"text":{"en":"Levy on Articles. Upon the effectivity of this Order, all articles\nwhich are specifically listed in Annex A hereof and are entered into, or withdrawn\nfrom warehouses in the Philippines for consumption, shall be levied the MN rates of\nduty as therein prescribed."}},{"id":"PH-H17790-A4","no":4,"noLabel":{"en":"SECTION 4"},"text":{"en":"Repeal.\nAll other issuances, administrative rules and\nregulations, or parts thereof, which are inconsistent with this Order are hereby\nrepealed or modified accordingly."}},{"id":"PH-H17790-A5","no":5,"noLabel":{"en":"SECTION 5"},"text":{"en":"Separability. If any provision of this Order is declared invalid or\nunconstitutional, the other provisions not affected thereby shall remain valid and\nsubsisting."}},{"id":"PH-H17790-A6","no":6,"noLabel":{"en":"SECTION 6"},"text":{"en":"Effectivity. This Order shall take effect immediately after its\npublication in the Official Gazette or in a newspaper of general circulation, and shall\nbe applicable until 31 December 2022.\nDONE, in the City of Manila, this 15th day of\nyear of Our Lord, Two Thousand and Twenty One.\nBy the President:\nSALVADOR C. MEDIALDEA\nExecutive Secretary\nREPUBLIC OF THE PHILIPPINES\nOffice of the President\nMALACARANG RECORDS OFFICE\nATTY. CONCEPCION\nTE. FERROLINO-ENAD\n2\n\n(1)\n02.07\n2017\nDescription\n(2)\n(3)\nMeat and edible offal, of the\npoultry of heading 01.05,\nfresh, chilled or frozen.\n- Of fowls of the species Gallus\ndomesticus:\n0207.14\n-- Cuts and offal, frozen:\n0207.14.91\n- - - - Mechanically deboned or\nseparated meat\n0207.27.91\n- - - - Mechanically deboned or\nseparated meat:\nRates of Duty (%)\n2021\n2023\n(4)\n5\n40\n5\n5\n30\n40"}}],"pack":"ph-p157"};
  FT["PH-H17791"] = {"id":"PH-H17791","coverage":"full","language":"en","sourceName":"The LawPhil Project — Arellano Law Foundation","sourceUrl":"","fetchedAt":"2026-10-28","articleCount":3,"structureMode":"ARTICLE","title":{"zh":null,"en":"MALACANAN PALACE BY THE PRESIDENT OF THE PHILIPPINES TRANSFERRING THE ADMINISTRATIVE SUPERVISION OVER THE PRESIDENTIAL COMMISSION FOR THE URBAN POOR AND THE NATIONAL ANTI-POVERTY COMMISSION TO THE OFFICE OF THE PRESIDENT","orig":"MALACANAN PALACE BY THE PRESIDENT OF THE PHILIPPINES TRANSFERRING THE ADMINISTRATIVE SUPERVISION OVER THE PRESIDENTIAL COMMISSION FOR THE URBAN POOR AND THE NATIONAL ANTI-POVERTY COMMISSION TO THE OFFICE OF THE PRESIDENT"},"level":"law","status":"active","docNumber":"Executive Order No. 123","issuingBody":"President of the Philippines","completenessNote":"全文，共 3 条；逐字取自 LawPhil PDF 文本化成果（第三方 OCR，非机翻），原始文件 EO_00123_2026.txt","textQuality":"ocr-vendor","sourceFile":"菲律宾/法律原文/07_行政命令_EO/EO_00123_2026.txt","country":"PH","countryName":"菲律宾","layer":"intl","articles":[{"id":"PH-H17791-A1","no":1,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 1"},"text":{"en":"Transfer of PCUP and NAPC. The administrative supervision\nover PCUP and NAPC is hereby transferred to the OP."}},{"id":"PH-H17791-A2","no":2,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 2"},"text":{"en":"Repeal. EO No. 67 (s. 2018) is hereby amended. All other\nissuances, orders, rules, and regulations, or parts thereof that are inconsistent with\nthis Order, are hereby repealed or modified accordingly."}},{"id":"PH-H17791-A3","no":3,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 3"},"text":{"en":"Effectivity. This Order shall take effect immediately.\nDONE, in the City of Manila, this 18th day of August\nyear of Our Lord, Two Thousand and Twenty-Six.\nBy the President:\nKALPH G/KEUrO\nActing Exeputive Secretary\nREPUBLIC OF THE PHILIPPINES\nOffice of the President\nMALACAÑANG RECORDS OFFICE\nYAIrY. KATRISHA ANALINE B. KOK\n7 F5 - 262 DIRECTOR IV\n2"}}],"pack":"ph-p157"};
  FT["PH-H17792"] = {"id":"PH-H17792","coverage":"full","language":"en","sourceName":"The LawPhil Project — Arellano Law Foundation","sourceUrl":"LawPhil (HTML full text only)  |  https://lawphil.net/executive/execord/eo1937/eo_124_1937.html","fetchedAt":"2026-10-28","articleCount":1,"structureMode":"WHOLE","title":{"zh":null,"en":"Annexing a Certain Portion of the Barrio of Daanghari, Municipality of Navotas, Rizal, to the Poblacion of Said Municipality.","orig":"Annexing a Certain Portion of the Barrio of Daanghari, Municipality of Navotas, Rizal, to the Poblacion of Said Municipality."},"level":"law","status":"active","docNumber":"Executive Order No. 124","issuingBody":"President of the Philippines","promulgatedDate":"1937-10-23","completenessNote":"全文，共 1 条；逐字取自 LawPhil PDF 文本化成果（第三方 OCR，非机翻），原始文件 EO_00124_1937_html.txt","textQuality":"ocr-vendor","sourceFile":"菲律宾/法律原文/07_行政命令_EO/EO_00124_1937_html.txt","country":"PH","countryName":"菲律宾","layer":"intl","articles":[{"id":"PH-H17792-A1","no":1,"noLabel":{},"text":{"en":"MALACAÑAN PALACE\nBY THE PRESIDENT OF THE PHILIPPINES\n[ EXECUTIVE ORDER NO. 124, October 23, 1937 ]\nANNEXING A CERTAIN PORTION OF THE BARRIO OF DAANGHARI, MUNICIPALITY OF\nNAVOTAS, RIZAL, TO THE POBLACION OF SAID MUNICIPALITY\nUpon the petition of the municipal council of Navotas, Rizal, and recommendation of the provincial board of\nsaid province, concurred in by the Secretary of the Interior, the Secretary of Agriculture and Commerce, and\nthe Secretary of Public Works and Communications, and pursuant to the provisions of section sixty-eight of\nthe Revised Administrative Code, the present territory of the poblacion of the municipality of Navotas is\nhereby increased by annexing to it a portion of the barrio of Daanghari, which is bounded on the northeast by\nCalle M. Naval, on the southeast by Calle Francisca Pascual, on the southwest by Manila Bay, and on the\nnorthwest by Calle Burgos, which is described as follows:\nBeginning at a point marked “1” on plan Swo-15163, being N.21° 16’ W., 594.13 m. from B.L.L.M. No. 1,\nmunicipality of Navotas, thence S. 31° 49’ E., 19.35 m. to point “2;” thence S. 34° 38’ E., 42.70 m. to point\n“3;” thence S. 34° 48’ E., 16.66 m. to point “4;” thence S. 37° 51’ E.,39.50 m. to point “5;” thence S. 39°\n33’ E., 30.39 m to point “6;” thence S. 41° 52’ E., 8.29 m. to point “7;” thence S. 54° 48’ W., 21.46 m. to\npoint “8;” thence “8;” thence S 60° 58’ W., 25.01 m. to point “9;” thence S. 63° 59’ W., 44.62 m. to point\n“10;” thence S. 65° 03’ W., 55.78 m. to point “11;” thence S. 64° 37’ W., 182.12 m. to point “12;” thence S.\n64° 37’ W., 263.06 m. to point “13;” thence N.35° 30’ W., 118.73 m. to point “14;” thence N. 60° 28’ E.,\n275.10 m. to point of beginning. Containing an area of eighty-one thousand two hundred thirty-one square\nmeters (81,231), more or less. All points referred to are indicated on the plan; and on the ground are marked\nby P. L. S. concrete monuments, 15 by 60, except points “13” and “14”."}}],"pack":"ph-p157"};
  FT["PH-H17793"] = {"id":"PH-H17793","coverage":"full","language":"en","sourceName":"The LawPhil Project — Arellano Law Foundation","sourceUrl":"LawPhil (HTML full text only)  |  https://lawphil.net/executive/execord/eo1948/eo_124_1948.html","fetchedAt":"2026-10-28","articleCount":1,"structureMode":"WHOLE","title":{"zh":null,"en":"Abolishing the Municipal Districts of Borboanan, Macopa, Pili and Tagbayani in the Province of Surigao and Annexing the Territories Thereof to the Municipalities of Bislig and Surigao, Same Province","orig":"Abolishing the Municipal Districts of Borboanan, Macopa, Pili and Tagbayani in the Province of Surigao and Annexing the Territories Thereof to the Municipalities of Bislig and Surigao, Same Province"},"level":"law","status":"active","docNumber":"Executive Order No. 124","issuingBody":"President of the Philippines","promulgatedDate":"1948-03-23","completenessNote":"全文，共 1 条；逐字取自 LawPhil PDF 文本化成果（第三方 OCR，非机翻），原始文件 EO_00124_1948_html.txt","textQuality":"ocr-vendor","sourceFile":"菲律宾/法律原文/07_行政命令_EO/EO_00124_1948_html.txt","country":"PH","countryName":"菲律宾","layer":"intl","articles":[{"id":"PH-H17793-A1","no":1,"noLabel":{},"text":{"en":"MALACAÑAN PALACE\nBY THE PRESIDENT OF THE PHILIPPINES\n[ EXECUTIVE ORDER NO. 124, March 23, 1948 ]\nABOLISHING THE MUNICIPAL DISTRICTS OF BORBOANAN, MACOPA, PILI AND TAGBAYANI\nIN THE PROVINCE OF SURIGAO AND ANNEXING THE TERRITORIES THEREOF TO THE\nMUNICIPALITIES OF BISLIG AND SURIGAO, SAME PROVINCE.\nWHEREAS, the Provincial Governor of Surigao has reported that the municipal districts of Borboanan,\nMacopa, Pili and Tagbayani in said province had ceased to function as separate and independent municipal\ndistricts even before the outbreak of the war; that the non-Christian inhabitants of these municipal districts\nhave abandoned their respective places and moved to the Province of Agusan, and have not returned to the\nsaid municipal districts for resettlement;\nWHEREAS, there exists no more necessity for the continuation of the municipal district governments in the\nmunicipal districts named above in view of the absence of non-Christian population therein;\nNOW, THEREFORE, upon the recommendation of the Secretary of the Interior and pursuant to the provisions\nof section 68 of the Revised Administrative Code, the municipal districts of Borboanan, Macopa, Pili and\nTagbayani are hereby abolished, and the territory of the municipal district of Borboanan is hereby annexed to\nthe municipality of Bislig and those of the municipal districts of Macopa, Pili and Tagbayani are hereby\nannexed to the municipality of Surigao as separate barrios thereof, respectively.\nThe changes herein made shall take effect immediately.\nDone at the City of Manila, this 23rd day of March, in the year of Our Lord, nineteen hundred and forty-eight,\nand of the Independence of the Philippines , the second.\n(Sgd.) MANUEL ROXAS\nPresident of the Philippines\nBy the President:\n(Sgd.) EMILIO ABELLO\nChief of the Executive Office"}}],"pack":"ph-p157"};
  FT["PH-H17794"] = {"id":"PH-H17794","coverage":"full","language":"en","sourceName":"The LawPhil Project — Arellano Law Foundation","sourceUrl":"","fetchedAt":"2026-10-28","articleCount":1,"structureMode":"WHOLE","title":{"zh":null,"en":"MALACANANG RESIDENCE OF THE PREsIDEN'r OF THE PHILIPPINES BY THE PRESIDENT OF THE PHILIPPINES CREATING 'l'HE MUNICIPALITY OF RIZAL IN THE PROVINCE OF SURIGAO DEL NORTE","orig":"MALACANANG RESIDENCE OF THE PREsIDEN'r OF THE PHILIPPINES BY THE PRESIDENT OF THE PHILIPPINES CREATING 'l'HE MUNICIPALITY OF RIZAL IN THE PROVINCE OF SURIGAO DEL NORTE"},"level":"law","status":"active","docNumber":"Executive Order No. 124","issuingBody":"President of the Philippines","completenessNote":"全文，共 1 条；逐字取自 LawPhil PDF 文本化成果（第三方 OCR，非机翻），原始文件 EO_00124_1964.txt","textQuality":"ocr-vendor","sourceFile":"菲律宾/法律原文/07_行政命令_EO/EO_00124_1964.txt","country":"PH","countryName":"菲律宾","layer":"intl","articles":[{"id":"PH-H17794-A1","no":1,"noLabel":{},"text":{"en":". The municipality of Rizal shall begin to exist upon the\n<appointment and qualification of the ~,.fayor, Vice-Mayor,\nand a majority of the councilors thereof and upon the cer-\n\"u.'c.,.w.vu by the Secretary of Finance that said municipality\nis financially capable of providing for the statutory obliga-\ntions and ordinary essential services of a regular muni-\n, cipality and that the mother municipality of Dinagat, after\n··.the segregation therefrom of the territory comprised in\nthe municipality of Rizal, can still maintain creditably its\nIDtmicipal government, meet all its statutory and contrac-\ntual obligations, and provide for the essential municipal\nDone in the City of Manila, this 3rd day of October,\nin the year of Our Lord, llilleteenhundl'ed and sixty-foul'.\nBy the President:\nJUAN S. CANCIO\nDIOSDADO MACAPAGAL\nPi'esident of the PhUippines\nActing Asftistant Executive Secreta1'ij"}}],"pack":"ph-p157"};
  FT["PH-H17795"] = {"id":"PH-H17795","coverage":"full","language":"en","sourceName":"The LawPhil Project — Arellano Law Foundation","sourceUrl":"LawPhil (HTML full text only)  |  https://lawphil.net/executive/execord/eo1968/eo_124_1968.html","fetchedAt":"2026-10-28","articleCount":1,"structureMode":"WHOLE","title":{"zh":null,"en":"Fixing Office Hours During the Hot Season.","orig":"Fixing Office Hours During the Hot Season."},"level":"law","status":"active","docNumber":"Executive Order No. 124","issuingBody":"President of the Philippines","promulgatedDate":"1968-04-01","completenessNote":"全文，共 1 条；逐字取自 LawPhil PDF 文本化成果（第三方 OCR，非机翻），原始文件 EO_00124_1968_html.txt","textQuality":"ocr-vendor","sourceFile":"菲律宾/法律原文/07_行政命令_EO/EO_00124_1968_html.txt","country":"PH","countryName":"菲律宾","layer":"intl","articles":[{"id":"PH-H17795-A1","no":1,"noLabel":{},"text":{"en":"MALACAÑAN PALACE\nBY THE PRESIDENT OF THE PHILIPPINES\n[ EXECUTIVE ORDER NO. 124, April 01, 1968 ]\nFIXING OFFICE HOURS DURING THE HOT SEASON\nWHEREAS, Section 564 of the Revised Administrative Code, as amended by Republic Act No. 1880, reduces\nthe period of labor in the government service during the hot season to five continuous hours but at the same\ntime leaves the observance thereof to the discretion of heads of departments, bureaus and offices subject to the\nrequirements of the service; and\nWHEREAS, this Administration is determined to protect the health and welfare of government employees\nwithout, however, impairing the interest of the public at large, especially at this time when we are\nstrengthening the foundation of a sound and efficient public service;\nNOW, THEREFORE, pursuant to the provisions of Section 564 of the Revised Administrative Code, as\namended, the office hours from Monday to Friday of all departments, bureaus, offices, agencies and\ninstrumentalities of the Government, including the provincial, city and municipal governments and all\ncorporations owned or controlled by the Government, during the period from May 1 to 31, 1968, both dates\ninclusive, shall be from seven-thirty o’clock in the morning to twelve-thirty o’clock in the afternoon. The\nprovisions of this Order shall not apply to the offices in the City of Baguio, whether national, provincial or\nmunicipal and to officers and employees engaged in field work.\nHowever, in the interest of the service, the heads of departments, bureaus, offices, agencies and\ninstrumentalities of the Government, including the provincial and municipal governments and all corporations\nowned or controlled by the Government, are enjoined to require at least one-half of their personnel to be on\nduty in the afternoon.\nHeads of government agencies and/or offices involved in the implementation of the Administration’s crash\nrice program and public works construction projects shall make proper and necessary arrangements and/or\nadjustments in their respective jurisdictions of their office hours with a view to utilizing available manpower\nservices without detriment to the deadlines and time schedules of the said program and projects, provided that\nthe five-hour office schedule herein set shall not in any case be reduced.\nDone in the City of Manila, this 1st day of April, in the year of Our Lord, nineteen hundred and sixty-eight.\n(SGD.) FERDINAND E. MARCOS\nPresident of the Philippines\nBy the President:\n(SGD.) RAFAEL M. SALAS\nExecutive Secretary"}}],"pack":"ph-p157"};
  FT["PH-H17796"] = {"id":"PH-H17796","coverage":"full","language":"en","sourceName":"The LawPhil Project — Arellano Law Foundation","sourceUrl":"","fetchedAt":"2026-10-28","articleCount":4,"structureMode":"ARTICLE","title":{"zh":null,"en":"124, DATED SO JANUARY 1987, RE- ORGANIZING THE DEPARTMENT OF PU:BLIC WORICS AND HIGH- WAYS, REDEFINING ITS POWERS FUNCTIONS, AND FOR OTHER","orig":"124, DATED SO JANUARY 1987, RE- ORGANIZING THE DEPARTMENT OF PU:BLIC WORICS AND HIGH- WAYS, REDEFINING ITS POWERS FUNCTIONS, AND FOR OTHER"},"level":"law","status":"active","docNumber":"Executive Order No. 124","issuingBody":"President of the Philippines","completenessNote":"全文，共 4 条；逐字取自 LawPhil PDF 文本化成果（第三方 OCR，非机翻），原始文件 EO_00124_1987.txt","textQuality":"ocr-vendor","sourceFile":"菲律宾/法律原文/07_行政命令_EO/EO_00124_1987.txt","country":"PH","countryName":"菲律宾","layer":"intl","articles":[{"id":"PH-H17796-A3","no":3,"noLabel":{"en":"SEC 3"},"text":{"en":"This Executive Order shall take\neffect imnlediately.\nDone in the City of Manilal this 22nd day\nof July in the year of Our Lord, nineteen\nhundred and eighty-seven.\n(Sgd.) CORAZON C. AQUINO\nPresident of the Philippines\nBy the President:\n(Sgd.) JOKER P. ARROYO\nExecutive Secretary ItIFIV /0/08\nMALACANANG\nEXECUTIVE ORDER No. 124-8.\nREORGANIZING THE METROPOLITAN\nFLOOD CONTROL AND\nDRAINAGE COUNCIL, ATTACHING\nIT TO '!'HE DEP ARTI\\'1ENT OF PUB-\nLIC WORKS AND HIGHWAYS, PRO-\nFOR A METROPOLITAN\nFLOOD CONTROL AND\nTHE NATIONAL TREASURY AND\nFOR OTHER PURPOSES.\nC. AQUINO, President of the\nPhilippines, do hereby order:\nOr~er No, 124, dated 30 January 1987, re-\norganizing the Department of Public Works\n::o.nd Highways, is hereby amended as fol-\nAbolitions / Transfers.-\nCompliance into the following is hereby\nprescribed:\nPasig River\nDevelopment\nCouncil is hereby abolished and its\nflood control functions are u'ans-\nferred to the pertinent Bureau,\nServices, and Regional Office of the\nDepartment.\n(b) The Rural Waterworl{s Develop-\nment Corporat\\On is hereby abolish-\ned and its functions and assets\ntransferred to the LOcal Water Uti-\nlities Administration in accordance\nwith Sections 29 to 31 hereof.\n(c) The National\nCouncil is hereby renamed and re-\norganized as the National Water\nResources Board and shall continue\nto be attached to the Department:\nProvided; That all of its technical\nfunctions are hereby transferred to\nthe Bureau of Research and Stan-\ndards and other offices as deemed\nappropriate by the\nthere is an urgent need to miti-\ngate the recurring floods in Metropolitan\nManila which have caused significant econo-\nmic losses and public inconvenience;\nit is deemed exigent to establish\nan effective coordination mechanism among\nnational and local government agencies to\nachieve the efficient provision of flood control\nand drainage services for the peo,ple of Me-\ntropolitan Manila;\nWHEREA~, Section 29 of Executive Order\nNo. 124 dated 30 January 1987 prescribes\nthe reorganization of the Metropolitan\nManila Flood Control and Drainage Council i\nSEC. 2. Section 29 is hereby amended by\ndeleting subsection (a) and relettering sub-\n\nOFFICIAL GAZETTE\n3422-0-5\nflood control operations and project imple-\nmentation. The said Fund Account shall be\nsourced from the following:\na. All proceeds from the special metro-\npolitan flood tax levied on all admissicn\ntickets of movie houses in Metropolitan\nb. All proceeds from additional real estate\ntaxes not e:{ceeding one eight (1/8) cf\none percent (10;0) of the assessed value\nof real estate located within Metro.\npolitan Manila"}},{"id":"PH-H17796-A5","no":5,"noLabel":{"en":"SEC 5"},"text":{"en":"Implementing Agency.-The }~a-\ntional Capital Rf:'gion of the Department of\nPublic Works and High\\vays shall be the\nlead implementing agency responsible for toe\nplanning, design, construction, maintenance,\nand operation of flood control and dramage\nprojects in Metropolitan Manila based on the\npolicies, plans, and programs adopted by\n.*\nthe Council. It shall coordinate the flood\ncontrol activities of the different local Gov-\nernment units in Metropolitan Manila."}},{"id":"PH-H17796-A6","no":6,"noLabel":{"en":"SEC 6"},"text":{"en":"Repealing\norders, issuances, rules and rf:'gulations. or\nparts thereof, mconsistent with. this Exec-\nutive Order are nereby repealed or modified\naccordingly."}},{"id":"PH-H17796-A7","no":7,"noLabel":{"en":"SEC 7"},"text":{"en":"Effectivity.-.,This\nExecutive Or-\ndel: shall take effect immediately.\nDONE in the City of Manila, this 22nd day\nof July, in tfie year of Our Lord, nineteen\nhundred and eighty-seven.\nNow, THEREFORE,\nPresident of the Philippines, do hereby\n1. Reor{Janization of the M etro-\npolitan Manila Flood .Control and Drai1'.age\nCouncil. Pursuant to Section 29 (c) of the\naforementioned EJ~ecutive Order No. 124,\nthe Metropolitan Manila. Flood Control and\nDrainage Council, hereinafter referred to as\nthe Council. is hereby reorganized in ac-\ncordance with the provisions of this Exe-\ncutive Order and shall be attached to the De-\npartment of Public Works and Highways.\nSEc. 2. Composition of the Council. The\nCouncil shall be composed of the Secretary\nof Public Works and Highways as Chair-\nman; the Governor of the Metropolitan Ma-\nnila Commission as Vice-Chairman; and the\nMayors of the cities and municipalities com-\nprising Metropolitan Manila as ~/J.embers.\nSEC. 3. Powers and Functions of th8\nCouncil. The Council shall have the follow-\ning powers and functions:\na. Coordinate the development of policies,\nplans, and programs for flood control\nand draiQage in Metropolitan Manila,\nincluding the identification of project\npriorities\nb. Oversee the coordinated implementa-\ntion by the conl~erned agencies of such\npolicies\" plans, and programs\nc. Conduct consultations \\vith local com-\nmunities and adopt ap,propriate meas-\nures to make flood control and drain-\n.age services responsive to the needs\nof the general public\nd. Ensure the steady, adequate, and\ntimely availability of funds to under-\ntake flvod control and drainage projects\nin accordance vtith adopted plans and\n(Sgd.) CORAZON\nPresident of the Philippines\nSEC. 4. Metropolitan Manila Flood Control\nand Drainage Fund Account.-A Metropo-\nlitan Manila Flood Control and Drainage\nFund Account is hereby created and estab-\nlished in the National Treasury to finance\nBy the President:\n(Sgd.: .TOKER P. ARROYO\nExecutive Secretary"}}],"pack":"ph-p157"};
