  FT["PH-H17882"] = {"id":"PH-H17882","coverage":"full","language":"en","sourceName":"The LawPhil Project — Arellano Law Foundation","sourceUrl":"","fetchedAt":"2026-10-28","articleCount":3,"structureMode":"ARTICLE","title":{"zh":null,"en":"MALACANANG EXECUTIVE ORDER NO. APPRA:tT ING T TiY'E STREA~..,1'L INT","orig":"MALACANANG EXECUTIVE ORDER NO. APPRA:tT ING T TiY'E STREA~..,1'L INT"},"level":"law","status":"active","docNumber":"Executive Order No. 132","issuingBody":"President of the Philippines","completenessNote":"全文，共 3 条；逐字取自 LawPhil PDF 文本化成果（第三方 OCR，非机翻），原始文件 EO_00132_1993.txt","textQuality":"ocr-vendor","sourceFile":"菲律宾/法律原文/07_行政命令_EO/EO_00132_1993.txt","country":"PH","countryName":"菲律宾","layer":"intl","articles":[{"id":"PH-H17882-A1","no":1,"noLabel":{"en":"SECTION 1"},"text":{"en":"Streamlining of the Organization Structure. The organizational\nstructure of the Bureau of Internal Revenue shall define clearly the functions and\nresponsibilities of the National Office and those of the Regional Offices, as follows:\nThe National Office shall develop and formulate broad national tax\nadministration\npolicies and programs, for efficient\nand effective\nimplementation of internal revenue laws and regulations and establish the\n\ngeneral direction, guidance and control of the entire operations of internalrevenue\nservice. For this purpose, the following organizationaLchanges are\n.\nThe existing functional groups in the Bureau. are restructured to\neffect the functional reorientation of the Services and divisions under\nThe Legal. Service, which shaft be headed by an Assistant\nCommissioner who shalt be assisted by a Revenue Head\nExecutive Assistant, is placed directly under thee Office of the\nCommissioner, together with the Legislative, Ruling and\nResearch Division. (being renamed as Law Division) and\nAppeltate Division.. The Prosecutioft Division. and Litigation\nDivisioft are merged into the Litigation and Prosecution\nDivisioft, and the Personnel Inquiry Divisioft is transferred\nfrom the Inspection Service to the Legal Service.\nThe Intelligence and Investigation Office and the Inspection\nService are abolished. An Intelligence and Investigation\nService is hereby created to absorb the same functions of the\nabolished office and service. It shall be headed by an\nAssistant Commissioner who shall be assisted by a Revenue\nHead Executive Assistant. It is attacheddirectlyto1he Office\nof the Commissioner together with the Tax Fraud Division.\nThe Internal Security Division is transferred from the\nabolished Inspection Service to. the Intelligence\nInvestigation Service.\nThe Fiscal Control Division is\nabolished and its functions\nare transferred\nPerformance Monitoring Service and decentralized to the\nRegional Offices.\n,\n2\nThe Assessment and Collection Group shall be renamed as the\nOperations Group and supervised by a Deputy Commissioner who\nshall be appointed by the President upon recommendation of the\nSecretary of Finance. This Group shall be composed of the\nfollowing Services, each Service to be headed by an Assistant\nCommissioner who shall be assisted by a Revenue Head Executive\n2.1.\nAssessment Service -The existing National Audit Review\nDivision and Tax Credit/Refund Division are abolished and\ntheir functions are transferred to the Regional Offices. The\nAssessment Performance Control Division is renamed\nAssessment Performance Audit Division and transferred to\nthe Performance Monitoring Service. The Assessment\nPrograms Division, Asset Valuation Division and Audit Data\nBank Division are created under the Assessment Service.\n1.2.2 Collection Service -The existing Collection Enforcement\nDivision and Acc;ounts Receivable/Billing\nDivision are\nabolished and their functions are decentralized to the\nRevenue District Offices.\nThe Collection Performance\nEvaluation Division is renamed Collection Performance\n\nAudit DivisioR and transferred to the PerformaRce\nMonitoring Service. The Withholding Tax Division is\nrenamed Withholding Agents Monitoring Division under the\nCollection Service. The Revenue Accounting Division is\ntransferred from the Financial.. Service to the Collection\nService. The Collection Programs., Divisioa is created, and\nthe Large Taxpa refs Divisionis placed under the Collection\nThe Performance Monitoring Service is created under the\nOperations Group which shall be headed by an Assistant\nCommissioner who shall be assisted by a Revenue Head\nExecutive Assistant. The Regulatory Operations Monitoring\nDivision is created under the Performance Monitoring\nService. The Assessment Performance Audit Division and\nthe Collection Performance Audit Division are included in\nthis Service.\nThe Excise Tax Service and all. the divisions under it and the\nSpecial Operations Service and all. the divisions under it,\nexcept the International Tax Affairs Division which is\ntransferred to the Planning and Research Service, are\nabolished and their functions are decentralized to the\nRevenueOistrict Offices.\nThe Revenue Regional Offices and Revenue District Offices\nshall report to this Group.\n2.5\nThe Information Systems Group is created which shall be headed\nand supervised by a Deputy Commissioner who shall be appointed\nby the President upon reco.mmendation of the Secretary of Finance.\nThis Group shall be composed of the following Services, each\nService to be headed by an Assistant Commissioner who shall be\nassisted by a Revenue Head Executive Assistant.\n3\nThe Information Systems Operations Service is created with\nthe following divisions: Network and Systems Operations\nDivision, Document Processing Division and Field Technical\nSupport Division.\nThe Information Systems Development Service is created\nwith the following divisions: Systems Acquisition Division,\nApplication Design and Development Division, Systems\nProgramming and Database Management Division and\nQuality Assurance Division.\nThe Resource Management Group is created which shall be headed\nand supervised by a Deputy Commissioner who shall be appointed\nby the President upon recommendation of the Secretary of Finance.\nThis Group shall be composed of the following Services, each to be\nheaded by an Assistant Commissioner who shall be assisted by a\nRevenue Head Executive Assistant.\n4\n\nThe Planning and Research Service -which is,.. renamed as\nManagement Planning Service.. The Planning and Research\nDivision is renamed as the Planning Oivisioa.\nManagement Information and Data ControfSystem Di visioa\nand Public fufornlation anclAssistancec Division are renamed\n!Vlanagement Division and PublieInformation and Education..\nDivision, respectively. The Statistical Analysis Division.. is\nrenamed Statistics' Di-vision and transferred to the Planning\nand Research Sen:icefromcthe Financial Service.\n4,\n:\\..2\nFinancial Service and the Administrative Service are\nmerged into the Financial and Administrative\ntogether with the following: BudgetDivision, Disbursement\nAccounting Division which iscrenamediAccounting Division,\nRecords Division and Accountable Forms Division.\nProperty Division is merged with the GeneraL Services\nDivision.. The Procurement Division is created under. the\nFinancial and Administrative Service.\nThe Human Resource Development Service is created and'\nshall have the following divisions:\nPersonnel Division,\nCareer Development Division which is renamed Training\nDivision and Medical and Dental Division which are\ntransferred to the Human Resource Development Service\nfrom the abolished Administrative Service. The Career\nManagement Division is created under the Human Resource\nDevelopment Service.\n.43\nThe Computer Information Systems Service and its four\ndivisions- are all abolished.\n4\nThe Regional Offices shall directly execute the national policies and\nprograms prescribed by the Central Office for the enforcement of the\ninternal revenue laws of the Philippines. They shall have supervision and\ncontrol over the Revenue District Offices and shall be responsible for\ndirecting and coordinating their operations within the region.\n2\nThe Regional Offices shall be composed of the Office of the\nRegional Director. Finance Division. Administrative Division, Legal\nDivision. Assessment Division, Collection Division and Special\nInvestigation Division.\n2.\nThe Revenue District Offices shall implement programs, methods\nand procedures necessary for the efficient, effective and economical\nassessment and collection of internal revenue taxes in the revenue\ndistrict in accordance with the policies, standards and guidelines\nprescribed by the Central Office and the Revenue Regional Office.\n2.2"}},{"id":"PH-H17882-A2","no":2,"noLabel":{"en":"SECTION 2"},"text":{"en":"Redeployment of Personnel. The redeployment of officials and\nother personnel on the basis of the streamlining embodied in this Executive Order shall not\nresult in the dislocation of existing personnel nor in the diminution of rank and\ncompensation and shall take into account pertinent Civil Service Law and rules.\n\n~\nThe Bureau of Internal' Reve£lue shalt submit to the Department ot:Budget and\nM'anagement the realigned staffing pattern that shaft complement its streamlined\n0 rganizati on structure.\nSECTION... 3. Policy of Non-Extension. of Services Beyond Compulsory\nRetirement Age. I~shaltbe the policy of the Bureau of Internal Revenue not to allow any\nextension of service beyond the compulsory age of retirement ~n order not to' disrupt the\nrevelll:.teservice career system,-"}},{"id":"PH-H17882-A4","no":4,"noLabel":{"en":"SECTION 4"},"text":{"en":"Transfer of Presidential Appointees.. TheCornmissioner oflnternal\nRevenue is hereby authorized 10 transfer and assign appointees OF the President to positions\nor assignments, of equivalent rank in the Bureau if the exigencies, of the sel7Vice\n.SECTION 5. Funding. Funds needed to carry out the provisions of this Executive\nOrder shall be taken from funds available in the Bureau oflntemal Revenue.\nSECTION 6, Implementing Authority.. The Commissioner of Internal Revenue\nwith the' approvaYof the Secretary of Finance shall; issue the rules and regulalionsand other\nissuances as may be necessary to ensure the effective, imp.1ementation of the provisions of\nthis Exec uti ve Order..\nSECTION 7, Effectivity. This Executive Order shall take effect immediately\n'\n,\nnineteen hundred and ninety three,\nBy the President:\n~"}}],"pack":"ph-p157"};
  FT["PH-H17883"] = {"id":"PH-H17883","coverage":"full","language":"en","sourceName":"The LawPhil Project — Arellano Law Foundation","sourceUrl":"","fetchedAt":"2026-10-28","articleCount":6,"structureMode":"ARTICLE","title":{"zh":null,"en":"BY THE PRESillENT OF mE PmLIPPINES","orig":"BY THE PRESillENT OF mE PmLIPPINES"},"level":"law","status":"active","docNumber":"Executive Order No. 132","issuingBody":"President of the Philippines","completenessNote":"全文，共 6 条；逐字取自 LawPhil PDF 文本化成果（第三方 OCR，非机翻），原始文件 EO_00132_1999.txt","textQuality":"ocr-vendor","sourceFile":"菲律宾/法律原文/07_行政命令_EO/EO_00132_1999.txt","country":"PH","countryName":"菲律宾","layer":"intl","articles":[{"id":"PH-H17883-A1","no":1,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 1"},"text":{"en":"Declaration of Principles.- The following are hereby declared to be\namong the main principles to guide the Government in maritime and ocean affairs, and in\nthe conduct of its foreign policy:\nIn responding to the many challenges and opportunities\npresented by the archipelagic nature of the country, decisions and actions\nwith respect to national and international maritime and ocean affairs shall\nbe in accordance with a national maritime policy.\nIn the pursuit of sustainable development, the interactions\nof the terrestrial and marine resource uses in an archipelagic setting shall\nbe recognized, and used as the basis for encouraging all resource users to\nmutually support and reinforce each other.\n0\n\n3\nIn consideration of international trends and developments\nin the management of the maritime and ocean sectors, utmost priority shall\nbe given to the development and enhancement of the COWltry'S capabilities\nto contro~ utilize. protect. manage, and conserve its marine resources.\nSec.2. The Cabinet Committee on Maritime and Ocean Affairs.- The\nCabinet Committee on Maritime and Ocean Affairs (hereinafter referred to as\nis hereby composed of the following:\nSecretary of Foreign Affairs\nExecutive Secretary\nDirector-General of the National Security Council\nSecretary of National Defense\nSecretary of Environment and Natural ResoW'Ces\nSecretary of Agriculture\nSecretary of Socio-Economic Planning\nSecretary of Science and Technology\nSecretary of Transportation and Communications\nSecretary of Energy\nSecretary of Trade and Industry\nSecretary of Justice\nSecretary of Finance\nSecretary of Budget and Management\nSecretary of Interior and Local Government\nSecretary of Labor and Employment\nSecretary of Tourism\nThe CABCOM-MOA, through the Chairman, may recommend to the President\nthe appointment of additional members drawn from the Cabinet as may be necessary."}},{"id":"PH-H17883-A3","no":3,"noLabel":{"en":"Sec 3"},"text":{"en":"Functions of the CABCOM-MOA.- The CABCOM-MOA shall have the\nfollowing functions:\nTo fOntlulate and recommend a national maritime policy to\nthe President;\nTo coordinate the implementation of such policy and\nperiodically evaluate and refine it as necessary;\nTo identify and develop policy options in implementing\ninternational agreements on the oceans, as well as non-binding\ninstruments, to which the Philippines is a party or signatory;\n()\n\n4\nTo recommend policies, programs, and special projects\nnecessary to advance the national interest and fulfill\ninternational\ncommitments relative to the sustainable use of ocean resources and marine\nenvironmental protection:\nTo fonnulate and recommend programs, and special\nprojects to enhance the integrated and coordinated management of the\nmaritime and oceans interests of the Philippines, particularly in:\n(1) the protection of the archipelago, including the\ndefense of the national telTitory, and the development of\nnational capabilities to protect its marine resources;\n(2) the protection, conservation, and preservation of the\nmarine environment and ocean resources through the\nproper management of hwnan activities within its maritime\njurisdi cti on;\n(3) the development and promotion of Philippine\ninterests in shipping, seafaring, fishing, extraction of\nmineral and energy resources, and other ocean-based\nindustries.\nTo fomlulate programs, coordinate and/or undertake\nactivities to promote the archipelagic consciousness in the country\nespecially among the coastal communities.\nThe CABCOM-MOA\nshall meet quarterly, or as the need arises.\nconstitute itself into such Sub-committees as may be necessary to respond to special and\nspecific issues or problems, and, to this end, formulate such rules of procedure as may be\nnecessary to perform its functions. The CABCOM-MOA shall submit a quarterly report\nof its activities to the President.\nCABCOM-MOA Technical Committee.- There is hereby created a\nTechnical Committee (hereafter refened to as \"TechCom\"), consisting of representatives\nof each of the Members of the CABCOM-MOA.\nThe TechCom shall have the following functions:\n(1)\nto oversee the implementation of the decisions and\npolicies set by the CABCOM-MOA;\n0\n\n5\nto fonnulate and recommend decision, policies,\nprojects and programs with respect to the maritime\nand ocean affairs of the COWltry, for consideration\nby the CABCOM-MOA~\n(2)\nto coordinate the activities of all the concerned\nagencies in the implementation of international\nagreements on the maritime and ocean affairs, as\nwell as non-binding instruments, to which the\nPhilippines is a party or signatory;\n(3)\nto fonnulate\nand recommend positions and\nstrategies for maritime boundary delimitation, as\nwell as fisheries and maritime disputes settlement\nand other international\nagreements.\n(4)\nThe Chainnan may a1so call on specialists and representatives of the academe,\nprivate sector, non-government organizations, and such other government offices or\nagencies as may be necessary, to assist the CABCOM-MOA in policy and decision"}},{"id":"PH-H17883-A5","no":5,"noLabel":{"en":"Sec 5"},"text":{"en":"Maritime and Ocean Affairs Center.- The Law of the Sea Secretariat\ncreated under Executive Order No. 738, Series of 1981, and designated as an attached\nagency of the Department of Foreign Affairs, pursuant to Section 19, Chapter 6, Title 1,\nBook IV of the Re\"\\-ised Administrative Code of 1987, is hereby renamed, reconstituted\nand established as the \"Maritime and Ocean Affairs Center\" hereinafter referred to as the\n\"Center\", with the following expanded functions and responsibilities:\nAct as the secretariat to the CABCOM-MOA, and provide\nassistance and administrative support to the Chainnan in the management\nof the CABCOM-MO.t\\. and its TechCom;\nAssist in the development of national capabilities and\nhuman resoW\"ces for maritime and ocean affairs;\nUndertake, or cause to be undertaken, any of the following:\n(1)\nconsultations with the TechCom or any of\nits members, any government agency, concerned maritime\nand ocean sectors, non-government organizations,\nacad~me, and/or dte general public, on any maritime-\nrelated matters as may be deemed necessary;\n\n6\n(2)\nresearch programs and policy studies on any\nand/or all maritime sectors as may be needed by the\nregulatory,\ngovernmental strategic, or security purposes;\n(3)\ninformation\nacquisition, and preparations for any negotiation or other\nmodes of dispute settlement with other countries in matters\nconcerning the overlapping of maritime boundaries,\nfisheries, energy and mineral exploration, and exploitation\nin the ocean, or other agreements relating to the\nconservation,\nexploration,\nexploitation,\nprotection,\ndevelopment, and/or management of marine resources\nwithin the territorial seas and exclusive economic zone as\nwell as areas adjacent to the latter;\nCreate and maintain, or cause to be created and maintained,\na central database and information system on maritime and ocean affairs\nin support of maritime and ocean policy and decision-making;\nnetwork with, and mobilize national and/or\ninternational expertise and institutions in support of or to assist the\nGovernment in maritime and ocean policy and decision making;\nUndertake, or cause to be undertaken, acti~ties necessary\nto raise the national archipelagic consciousness and communicate, in a\ncoordinated manner, publicize national maritime and ocean interests and\nCoordinate the participation of the appropriate agencies of\ngovernment in international fora, meetings, and conferences that are\nrelevant to the maritime and ocean interests of the Philippines;\nRender a regular report to the CABCOM-MOA, through\nits Chairman, on all activitics und~rtaken by the Center.\nSource out and avail of grants, endowments or donations\nfrom foreign or local entities in accordance with existing laws to be\napplied to projects or studies to implement the policies or directives of the\nThe Chainnan of the CABCOM-MOA shall appoint the Secretary-General\nshall head the Center, and the staff that will provide the technical and administrative\nsupport under the supervision of an Executive Director. The Chaimlan of the CAB COM-\nMOA is hereby authorized to hire consultants and request the detail and secondment of\n~\n\n7\npersonnel from other government agencies and institutions in accordance with Civil\nService law, rules and regulations.\nThe Center may call on any department. bureau. office or agency of the\ngovernment, including government-owned and controlled corporations, to actively assist\nin the performance of its duties and fimctions."}},{"id":"PH-H17883-A6","no":6,"noLabel":{"en":"Sec 6"},"text":{"en":"Issuance of Implementing Rules.- The Secretary of Foreign Affairs, as\nChainnan of the CABCOM-MOA shall promulgate such rules, regulations and other\nissuances as may be necessary to ensure the efficient and effective implementation of this\nExecutive Order."}},{"id":"PH-H17883-A7","no":7,"noLabel":{"en":"Sec 7"},"text":{"en":"Repealing Clause.- The provisions of Executive Order No. 738 (1981)\nEstablishing the Cabinet Committee on the Treaty on the Law of the Sea; Executive\nOrder No. 328 (1988) Reconstituting the Cabinet Committee on the Law of the Sea; and\nExecutive Order No. 186 (1994) Expanding the Coverage of the Cabinet Committee on\nthe Law of the Sea and Renaming It As the Cabinet Committee on Maritime and Ocean\n\"I\\ffairs, that are inconsistent herewith are hereby repealed and superseded."}},{"id":"PH-H17883-A8","no":8,"noLabel":{"en":"Sec 8"},"text":{"en":"Effectivity.- This Order shall take effect immediately.\nDONE in the City of Manila, this:!!J:l!!. day of J V ~'\" in the year of our Lord,\nNineteen Hundred and Ninety Nine.\n.,\nBy the President:\nRONALDO B. ZAMORA\nExecutive Secretary\nPMS LIBRARY\n1IIIIIIIIIIIIIIIIIIIIIIIIIIIIIIIilili\nPMS LIBRARY BCODEOO4280"}}],"pack":"ph-p157"};
  FT["PH-H17884"] = {"id":"PH-H17884","coverage":"full","language":"en","sourceName":"The LawPhil Project — Arellano Law Foundation","sourceUrl":"","fetchedAt":"2026-10-28","articleCount":7,"structureMode":"ARTICLE","title":{"zh":null,"en":"MALACANANG PMS LIBRARY, AUTHORIZING THE CREATION OF THE PORO POINT MANAGEMENT CORPORATION AS THE IMPLEMENTING ARM OF THE BASES CONVERSION DEVELOPMENT AUTHORITY OVER THE PORO POINT SPECIAL ECONOMIC AND FREEPORT ZONE AND RENAMING THE JOHN HAY PORO POINT DEVELOPMENT CORPORATION AS THE JOHN HAY MANAGEMENT CORPORATION","orig":"MALACANANG PMS LIBRARY, AUTHORIZING THE CREATION OF THE PORO POINT MANAGEMENT CORPORATION AS THE IMPLEMENTING ARM OF THE BASES CONVERSION DEVELOPMENT AUTHORITY OVER THE PORO POINT SPECIAL ECONOMIC AND FREEPORT ZONE AND RENAMING THE JOHN HAY PORO POINT DEVELOPMENT CORPORATION AS THE JOHN HAY MANAGEMENT CORPORATION"},"level":"law","status":"active","docNumber":"Executive Order No. 132","issuingBody":"President of the Philippines","completenessNote":"全文，共 7 条；逐字取自 LawPhil PDF 文本化成果（第三方 OCR，非机翻），原始文件 EO_00132_2002.txt","textQuality":"ocr-vendor","sourceFile":"菲律宾/法律原文/07_行政命令_EO/EO_00132_2002.txt","country":"PH","countryName":"菲律宾","layer":"intl","articles":[{"id":"PH-H17884-A2","no":2,"noLabel":{"en":"SECTION 2"},"text":{"en":"Capitalization, Powers and Functions of PPMC.\nThe BCDA, as the incorporator and holding company of the PPMC, shall\ndetermine the capitalization, powers and functions of the PPMC, which\nshall be substantially similar to that of the capitalization, powers and\nfunctions of the JPDC."}},{"id":"PH-H17884-A3","no":3,"noLabel":{"en":"SECTION 3"},"text":{"en":"Transfer of Powers, Functions, Rights, Assets,\nLiabilities, Personnel, etc. - All powers vested in, and the functions\nand duties heretofore conferred upon the JPDC relating to the operation,\nmanagement, utilization and development of the PPSEFZ under existing\nlaws, rules and regulations, and under its Articles of Incorporation and\nBy-Laws, including all of its rights, assets, liabilities and personnel, shall\nbe transferred to the PPMC upon its incorporation under the Philippine\nCorporation Law and rules and regulations promulgated by the SEC. For\nthis purpose, the BCD is directed to take all the necessary steps\ntowards effecting the efficient transfer of powers, functions, duties,\nrights, assets, liabilities and personnel from JPDC to PPMC."}},{"id":"PH-H17884-A4","no":4,"noLabel":{"en":"SECTION 4"},"text":{"en":"Renaming the John Hay Poro Point Development\nCorporation as the John Hay Management Corporation. - The body\ncorporate created under EO 103, as amended by E0 31 known as the\nJohn Hay Poro Point Development Corporation (JPDC) is hereby renamed\nas the John Hay Management Corporation (JHMC) and shall be the\noperating and implementing arm of the BCDA over the JHSEZ. The\nBCDA is further directed to cause the amendment of the Articles of\nIncorporation and By-Laws of JPDC to implement this Executive Order.\nImplementation.\nBCDA shall implement this\nExecutive Order within a period of ninety (90) days from date of issuance\nof this Executive Order, including:\n2. .\nThe incorporation of the PPMC as provided in Section 1\nThe transfer of powers, functions, duties, rights, assets,\nliabilities and personnel from JPDC to PPMC as provided in\nSection 3 hereof; and\nThe amendment of the Articles of Incorporation and By-Laws\nof JPDC as provided in Section 4 hereof.\nBCDA shall submit a report to the President on all the actions\ntaken to implement this Executive Order within fifteen (15) days after the\nPPMC shall have been established in accordance with the Philippine\nCorporation Law, rules and regulations and approval of the amendment\nof the Articles of Incorporation and By-Laws of JPDC by the SEC.\n3\nPOMA Outgoing * 15515"}},{"id":"PH-H17884-A6","no":6,"noLabel":{"en":"SECTION 6"},"text":{"en":"Board of Directors. - The powers of JHMC and\nPPMC shall be vested in and exercised by a Board of Directors, both of\nwhich shall be composed of not more than eleven (11) members each;\nProvided, That, at least one (1) director shall be the BCDA Chairman and\na second director shall be the BCDA President or his designated\nrepresentative, in accordance with Section 16 of RA 7227.\nNo person shall be nominated as a member of the Board\nrepresenting the capital stock of the national government in JHMC and\nPPMC unless he is a Filipino citizen, of good moral character, and of\nrecognized competence in relevant fields, including but not limited to\neconomics, tourism, management, international relations, law or\nengineering."}},{"id":"PH-H17884-A7","no":7,"noLabel":{"en":"SECTION 7"},"text":{"en":"Role of Departments, Bureaus, Offices, Agencies\nand Instrumentalities. - All heads of departments, bureaus, offices,\nagencies and instrumentalities of the government are hereby directed to\ngive full support to the Poro Point conversion program and to coordinate\nwith BCDA to facilitate the necessary approvals to expedite the\nimplementation of various projects of the conversion program."}},{"id":"PH-H17884-A8","no":8,"noLabel":{"en":"SECTION 8"},"text":{"en":"Repealing Clause. - Section 1 of Executive Order\nNo. 31, s. 1998, insofar as it pertains to the composition of the Board of\nDirectors of JPDC, is hereby amended by Section 6 hereof. All other\nexecutive issuances, rules and regulations or parts thereof which are\ninconsistent with this Executive Order are hereby revoked, amended, or\nmodified accordingly."}},{"id":"PH-H17884-A9","no":9,"noLabel":{"en":"SECTION 9"},"text":{"en":"Effectivity. This Executive Order shall take effect\nimmediately.\nDONE in the City of Manila, this 3rd day of October in the year\nof our Lord, Two Thousand and Two.\nPolA Outgoing * 15516\nBy the President:\nAVELINO J. CRUZ, JR.\nActing Executive Secretary\nPMS LIBRARY BCODE001952"}}],"pack":"ph-p157"};
  FT["PH-H17885"] = {"id":"PH-H17885","coverage":"full","language":"en","sourceName":"The LawPhil Project — Arellano Law Foundation","sourceUrl":"","fetchedAt":"2026-10-28","articleCount":5,"structureMode":"ARTICLE","title":{"zh":null,"en":"MALACAÑAN PALACE BY THE PRESIDENT OF THE PHILIPPINES DECLARING AND DELINEATING THE ILIGAN PORT ZONE AND PLACING IT UNDER THE ADMINISTRATIVE JURISDICTION OF THE PHILIPPINE PORTS AUTHORITY (PPA)","orig":"MALACAÑAN PALACE BY THE PRESIDENT OF THE PHILIPPINES DECLARING AND DELINEATING THE ILIGAN PORT ZONE AND PLACING IT UNDER THE ADMINISTRATIVE JURISDICTION OF THE PHILIPPINE PORTS AUTHORITY (PPA)"},"level":"law","status":"active","docNumber":"Executive Order No. 132","issuingBody":"President of the Philippines","completenessNote":"全文，共 5 条；逐字取自 LawPhil PDF 文本化成果（第三方 OCR，非机翻），原始文件 EO_00132_2013.txt","textQuality":"ocr-vendor","sourceFile":"菲律宾/法律原文/07_行政命令_EO/EO_00132_2013.txt","country":"PH","countryName":"菲律宾","layer":"intl","articles":[{"id":"PH-H17885-A1","no":1,"noLabel":{"en":"SECTION 1"},"text":{"en":"Port of Iligan. The territorial jurisdiction of the Port of Iligan situated\nin Barangay Poblacion, Iligan City, Province of Lana del Norte, is hereby delineated\nand established, particularly described as follows:\nBeginning at a point marked 1 on the plan, being N. 49 deg. 18' W., 567.87 m.\nfrom BLLM No. 1, CAD 292, Iligan City, Lanao del Norte, thence:\n05'\n33'\n57'\n41'\n46*\n07'\n01'\n51'\n55'\n23'\n32'\n16\n35'\n53'\n01'\n57'\n47'\n36\n05'\n57'\n311\n17'\n@fice otthe Fresibent of the 39hiwpines\n\n49'\n22'\n13*\n111\n22'\n04'\n57'\n54'\n59'\n38'\n31'\n52'\n30'\n1.54 m. to point of beginning,\nContaining a total area of NINE HUNDRED FORTY-SEVEN THOUSAND TWO\nHUNDRED EIGHTEEN (947,218) SQUARE METERS, more or less."}},{"id":"PH-H17885-A2","no":2,"noLabel":{"en":"SECTION 2"},"text":{"en":"PPA Jurisdiction. The Iligan Port Zone, as delineated, is hereby\nplaced under the administrative jurisdiction of the PA, which shall, consistent with the\nregional industrial plans of the government, implement a program for the proper zoning,\nplanning, development and utilization of the port."}},{"id":"PH-H17885-A3","no":3,"noLabel":{"en":"SECTION 3"},"text":{"en":"Repeal. All issuances, orders, rules and regulations, or parts\nthereof, which are inconsistent with this Executive Order are hereby repealed, amended\nor modified accordingly."}},{"id":"PH-H17885-A4","no":4,"noLabel":{"en":"SECTION 4"},"text":{"en":"Separability. If any provision of this Executive Order is declared\ninvalid or unconstitutional, the other provisions not affected thereby shall remain valid\nand subsisting."}},{"id":"PH-H17885-A5","no":5,"noLabel":{"en":"SECTION 5"},"text":{"en":"Effectivity. This Executive Order shall take effect immediately upon\npublication in a newspaper of general circulation.\nDONE, in the City of Manila, this 14th day of March\nLord, Two Thousand and Thirteen.\n,in the year of our\nBy the President:\nPAQUITO N. OCHOA, JR.\nExecutive Secretary\nCERTIFIED COPY-\n2\nOffice of the resident of the Philipines\nMARIAMITE M DIMA&NDAL\nDIRECTOR IV\nMALACANANG RECORDS OFFICI"}}],"pack":"ph-p157"};
  FT["PH-H17886"] = {"id":"PH-H17886","coverage":"full","language":"en","sourceName":"The LawPhil Project — Arellano Law Foundation","sourceUrl":"","fetchedAt":"2026-10-28","articleCount":3,"structureMode":"ARTICLE","title":{"zh":null,"en":"MALACAÑAN PALACE BY THE PRESIDENT OF THE PHILIPPINES ADJUSTING THE DIVIDEND RATE OF THE LAND BANK OF THE","orig":"MALACAÑAN PALACE BY THE PRESIDENT OF THE PHILIPPINES ADJUSTING THE DIVIDEND RATE OF THE LAND BANK OF THE"},"level":"law","status":"active","docNumber":"Executive Order No. 132","issuingBody":"President of the Philippines","completenessNote":"全文，共 3 条；逐字取自 LawPhil PDF 文本化成果（第三方 OCR，非机翻），原始文件 EO_00132_2021.txt","textQuality":"ocr-vendor","sourceFile":"菲律宾/法律原文/07_行政命令_EO/EO_00132_2021.txt","country":"PH","countryName":"菲律宾","layer":"intl","articles":[{"id":"PH-H17886-A1","no":1,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 1"},"text":{"en":"Adjustment of Dividend Rate. Pursuant to Section 5 of RA No.\n7656, the percentage of net earnings to be declared and remitted by the LBP to the\nNational Government for CY 2019, is adjusted from at least fifty percent (50%) of its\nannual net earnings to 0%."}},{"id":"PH-H17886-A2","no":2,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 2"},"text":{"en":"Coverage. The adjusted dividend rate set forth in Section 1 of this\nOrder is only applicable to the LBP for CY 2019."}},{"id":"PH-H17886-A3","no":3,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 3"},"text":{"en":"Effectivity. This Order shall take effect immediately.\nDONE, in the City of Manila, this 28th day of April\nin the year of\nOur Lord, Two Thousand and Twenty-One.\nBy the President:\nOffice of the President\nMALACAMANG RECON\nSALVADOR C. MEDIALDEA\nExecutive Secretary (h\nTHE PRESIDENT OF THE PHILIPPINES CH\nPHILIPPINES\nATTY. CONCEPCIOR CASPERD: 20IB A 017656-E\n8 5-1-2021\nDIRECTOR IV"}}],"pack":"ph-p157"};
  FT["PH-H17887"] = {"id":"PH-H17887","coverage":"full","language":"en","sourceName":"The LawPhil Project — Arellano Law Foundation","sourceUrl":"LawPhil (HTML full text only)  |  https://lawphil.net/executive/execord/eo1937/eo_133_1937.html","fetchedAt":"2026-10-28","articleCount":1,"structureMode":"WHOLE","title":{"zh":null,"en":"Confirming the Election of Provincial and City Officers Elected on December 14, 1937","orig":"Confirming the Election of Provincial and City Officers Elected on December 14, 1937"},"level":"law","status":"active","docNumber":"Executive Order No. 133","issuingBody":"President of the Philippines","promulgatedDate":"1937-12-29","completenessNote":"全文，共 1 条；逐字取自 LawPhil PDF 文本化成果（第三方 OCR，非机翻），原始文件 EO_00133_1937_html.txt","textQuality":"ocr-vendor","sourceFile":"菲律宾/法律原文/07_行政命令_EO/EO_00133_1937_html.txt","country":"PH","countryName":"菲律宾","layer":"intl","articles":[{"id":"PH-H17887-A1","no":1,"noLabel":{},"text":{"en":"MALACAÑAN PALACE\nBY THE PRESIDENT OF THE PHILIPPINES\n[ EXECUTIVE ORDER NO. 133, December 29, 1937 ]\nCONFIRMING THE ELECTION OF PROVINCIAL AND CITY OFFICERS ELECTED ON DECEMBER\n14, 1937\nEach of the persons named below having been certified by the provincial and municipal boards of canvassers\nto have received a plurality of the votes legally cast at the ordinary election held in the provinces and cities on\nthe fourteenth day of December, nineteen hundred and thirty-seven, under the provisions of the new Election\nLaw, and there being in my opinion no reason why their elections should not be confirmed, the said election\nare, pursuant to the recommendation of the Secretary of the Interior, hereby confirmed in accordance with the\nsection four hundred seventy-two of the new Election Law:\nPROVINCIAL GOVERNORS\nBienvenido Valera\nMariano C. Atega\nManuel M. Calleja\nAlberto A. Villavert\nDomingo Cacho\nVicento J. Caedo\nCarlos P. Garcia\nJacinto Molina\nServando Liban\nMiguel Lukban\nCamarines Norte.\nAndres Hernandez\nCamarines sur.\nRamon Samonte\nGabriel K. Hernandez\nBuenaventura Rodriguez\nPacifico M. Sobrecarey\nRoque B. Ablan\nIlocos Norte.\nPedro Singson\nTomas Confesor\nAgustin A. Pintang\nArsenio Bonifacio\nFrancisco N. Nisce\nRafael Martinez\nMarinduque.\nMateo Pecson\nSantiago Garong\nAnselmo Bernad\nMisamis Occidental.\nGregorio Borromeo\nMisamis Oriental.\nValeriano M. Gatuslao\nNegros Occidental.\nJulian L. Teves\nNegros Oriental.\nAurelio Cecilio\nNueva Ecija.\nTomas Maddela\nNueva Viscaya.\nSofronio Española\nSotero Baluyot\nServillano de la Cruz\nPangasinan.\nEulogio Rodriguez, jr.\nJose Firmalo\nFelipe Abrigo\nTeodosio R. Diño\nPedro Coleto\nAlfonso A. Pablo\nCasiano A. Sandoval\nBernardo Farrales\nMatias C. Ranillo\nMEMBERS OF THE PROVINCIAL BOARDS\nLino Molina\nEriberto Cariño\nAgustin Caseñas\nPaciente Villa\nRemigio Sosito\nF. A. Perfecto\nBernardino Hernandez\nPedro M. Vego\nClemente Mata\nBernardo de Guzman\nFelipe E. Dimaculangan\nFrancisco G. Perez\nAgapito Hontanosas\nFortunato Halili\nHermogenes Dimaguiba\nPedro J. Villaflor\nSalvador Villacete\nCarlos V. de Jesus\nCamarines Norte\nRegino Z. Guinto\nCamarines Sur.\nM. V. del Gallego\nPlaton Patiño\nJose A. Urquiola\nCristina A. Suntay\nProceso Arenas\nVicente Lozada\nCesar M. Sotto\nRamon E. Kimpo\nDamaso T. Samonte\nIlocos Norte.\nFlorendo M. Pablo\nTomas V. Vargas\nCeferino de los Santos\nGabriel R. Visaya\nFabian R. Soberano\nEstanislao Alinea\nAgustin Gana\nBernardo Torres\nAtilano R. Cinco\nMarinduque.\nS. Palomares\nEpitacio Titong\nVicente Clemente\nMariano R. Basa\nAlfonso L. Adora\nFederico Apao\nMisamis Occidental.\nJose Vayson\nMisamis Oriental.\nAguedo Gonzaga\nNegros Occidental.\nGeneroso Villanueva\nNegros Oriental.\nAlberto V. Furbeyre\nConstancio Padilla\nNueva Ecija.\nPedro Pascual\nJuan Manzano\nNueva Viscaya.\nMelecio Padilla\nPedro P. Ponce De Leon\nDoroteo Soberano\nLazaro Yambao\nEmilio Santos\nPangasinan.\nJ. L. de Guzman\nSixto Antonio\nTomas Molina\nDomingo R. Reta\nIgnacio Molina\nVicente A. Dira\nRosendo Bandal\nAmado Golpeo\nJusto Dellosa\nJacinto P. Elpa\nJose Rendon\nLino Ignacio\nProtacio Santos\nE. C. Desembrana\nCesar Ramos\nGuadalupe Adaza\nLIEUTENANT GOVERNORS\nSubprovince\nGabriel Torrecampo\nCatanduanes\nSergio Jumauan\nNegros Oriental.\nSPECIAL MEMBER FOR THE SUBPROVINCE OF SIQUIJOR\nRafael Maglangit\nNegros Oriental.\nMEMBERS OF THE CITY COUNCILS\nTeodoro R. Reinoso\nSixto A. Gaerlan\nM. D.G. Cabaguio\nIsidro S. Bastida\nDonato C. Endriga\nAntonio Toribio\nMEMBERS OF THE MUNICIPAL BOARDS\nRegino Mercado\nFelipe Pacana\nLeandro A. Tojong\nJose P. Nolasco\nJose Fortich\nDominador J. Abella\nJuan Zamora\nEulogio Garganera\nSerapion Torre\nEvelio Zaldivar\nFortunato Ybiernas\nSerafin de la Cruz\nCrispino Melocoton\nLeopoldo Ganzon\nHermenegildo Atienza\nCarmen Planas\nManuel de la Fuente\nTeofilo Mendoza\nIñigo Ed. Regalado\nBartolome Gatmaitan\nAgaton Cecilio\nValeriano Fugoso\nMateo Herrera\nEustaquio Balagtas\nThe persons above named will qualify and assume office in accordance with law.\nDone at the City of Manila, Philippines, this twenty-ninth day of December, in the year of Our Lord, nineteen\nhundred and thirty-seven, and of the Commonwealth of the Philippines, the third.\n(Sgd.) MANUEL L. QUEZON\nPresident of the Philippines\nBy the President:\n(Sgd.) ELPIDIO QUIRINO\nSecretary of the Interior"}}],"pack":"ph-p157"};
  FT["PH-H17888"] = {"id":"PH-H17888","coverage":"full","language":"en","sourceName":"The LawPhil Project — Arellano Law Foundation","sourceUrl":"LawPhil (HTML full text only)  |  https://lawphil.net/executive/execord/eo1955/eo_133_1955.html","fetchedAt":"2026-10-28","articleCount":1,"structureMode":"WHOLE","title":{"zh":null,"en":"Fixing the Boundary Line Between the Municipalities of Padada and Hagonoy, Both of the Province of Davao","orig":"Fixing the Boundary Line Between the Municipalities of Padada and Hagonoy, Both of the Province of Davao"},"level":"law","status":"active","docNumber":"Executive Order No. 133","issuingBody":"President of the Philippines","promulgatedDate":"1955-09-23","completenessNote":"全文，共 1 条；逐字取自 LawPhil PDF 文本化成果（第三方 OCR，非机翻），原始文件 EO_00133_1955_html.txt","textQuality":"ocr-vendor","sourceFile":"菲律宾/法律原文/07_行政命令_EO/EO_00133_1955_html.txt","country":"PH","countryName":"菲律宾","layer":"intl","articles":[{"id":"PH-H17888-A1","no":1,"noLabel":{},"text":{"en":"MALACAÑAN PALACE\nBY THE PRESIDENT OF THE PHILIPPINES\n[ EXECUTIVE ORDER NO. 133, September 23, 1955 ]\nFIXING THE BOUNDARY LINE BETWEEN THE MUNICIPALITIES OF PADADA AND HAGONOY,\nBOTH OF THE PROVINCE OF DAVAO\nUpon the recommendation of the Provincial Board of Davao and pursuant to the provisions of section 68 of\nthe Revised Administrative Code, the boundary line between the municipalities of Padada and Hagonoy, both\nof the province of Davao, is hereby fixed in accordance with the agreement between the said municipalities, as\nFrom the mouth of the Padada River on the Davao Gulf following the course of said river upstream until it\nmeets the Bulatukan River; thence, following the course of the Bulatukan River upstream until it reaches B. B.\nM. No. 18 located on said river; and thence, a straight line running due west to the boundary line between the\nprovinces of Davao and Cotabato. (Reference: Map prepared and submitted by the office of the district\nengineer of Davao on August 16, 1955, based on the Sta. Cruz Cadastre, B. L. Cadastre No. 275, scale\n1:30,000.)"}}],"pack":"ph-p157"};
  FT["PH-H17889"] = {"id":"PH-H17889","coverage":"full","language":"en","sourceName":"The LawPhil Project — Arellano Law Foundation","sourceUrl":"LawPhil (HTML full text only)  |  https://lawphil.net/executive/execord/eo1968/eo_133_1968.html","fetchedAt":"2026-10-28","articleCount":1,"structureMode":"WHOLE","title":{"zh":null,"en":"Conferring Cabinet Rank Upon the Chairman of the Board of Investments.","orig":"Conferring Cabinet Rank Upon the Chairman of the Board of Investments."},"level":"law","status":"active","docNumber":"Executive Order No. 133","issuingBody":"President of the Philippines","promulgatedDate":"1968-06-05","completenessNote":"全文，共 1 条；逐字取自 LawPhil PDF 文本化成果（第三方 OCR，非机翻），原始文件 EO_00133_1968_html.txt","textQuality":"ocr-vendor","sourceFile":"菲律宾/法律原文/07_行政命令_EO/EO_00133_1968_html.txt","country":"PH","countryName":"菲律宾","layer":"intl","articles":[{"id":"PH-H17889-A1","no":1,"noLabel":{},"text":{"en":"MALACAÑAN PALACE\nBY THE PRESIDENT OF THE PHILIPPINES\n[ EXECUTIVE ORDER NO. 133, June 05, 1968 ]\nCONFERRING CABINET RANK UPON THE CHAIRMAN OF THE BOARD OF INVESTMENTS\nBy virtue of the powers vested in me by law, I, FERDINAND E. MARCOS, President of the Philippines, do\nhereby confer upon the Chairman of the Board of Investments the rank of a Member of the Cabinet, with all\nthe rights, honors and privileges pertaining to the position.\nDone in the City of Manila, this 5th day of June, in the year of Our Lord, nineteen hundred and sixty-eight.\n(SGD.) FERDINAND E. MARCOS\nPresident of the Philippines\nBy the President:\n(SGD.) RAFAEL M. SALAS\nExecutive Secretary"}}],"pack":"ph-p157"};
  FT["PH-H17890"] = {"id":"PH-H17890","coverage":"full","language":"en","sourceName":"The LawPhil Project — Arellano Law Foundation","sourceUrl":"","fetchedAt":"2026-10-28","articleCount":2,"structureMode":"ARTICLE","title":{"zh":null,"en":"REORGANIZING TUE DEPARTMENT OF TRADE AND INDUSTRY, ITS ATTACHED AGENCIES, AND FOR OTHER PURPOSES","orig":"REORGANIZING TUE DEPARTMENT OF TRADE AND INDUSTRY, ITS ATTACHED AGENCIES, AND FOR OTHER PURPOSES"},"level":"law","status":"active","docNumber":"Executive Order No. 133","issuingBody":"President of the Philippines","completenessNote":"全文，共 2 条；逐字取自 LawPhil PDF 文本化成果（第三方 OCR，非机翻），原始文件 EO_00133_1987.txt","textQuality":"ocr-vendor","sourceFile":"菲律宾/法律原文/07_行政命令_EO/EO_00133_1987.txt","country":"PH","countryName":"菲律宾","layer":"intl","articles":[{"id":"PH-H17890-A13","no":13,"noLabel":{"en":"SEC 13"},"text":{"en":"Office of the Undersecretary for International Trade.\nUndersecretary for International Trade shall include all the units\ninvolved In policy formulation, standards development, program development, and\nprogram monitoring of the development, regulatory, and service delivery\nprograms of the Department pertinent to international trade and commerce being\nimplemented by the Department's line operating units.\nThe Undersecretary for\nInternational Irade shall supervise the following:\nBureau of International Trade Relations.\nThis Bureau shall be the\nprimary agent responsible for all matters pertaining to foreigo trade\nrelations, whether bilateral, regional or multilateral, especially\nmarket access and market access related matters; formulate positions\nand strategies for trade negotiations, consultations and conferences\nas well as supervise trade negotiations,\nconsultations and\nconferences; coordinate with other Departments and ageneles of the\nPhilippine government with the view of assuring consistency in the\ngovernment's positions in crade negotiations and on other activities\npertaining to fovelgo trade relations; consult with Industry groups\nand provide technical advice and information on the above matters and\nactivities; identify tariff and non-tariff barriers affecting products\nof export Interest to the Philippines, and negotiate measures for\nliberalizing them at bilateral, regional and multilateral fora; and\nevaluate and submit recommendations on existing and proposed\ncommercial policies of the Philippines;\nBureau of Export Trade Promotion.\nThis Bureau shall formulate and\nmonitor programs, plans, and projects pertinent to the development,\npromotion, and expansion of the forefgn trade of the Philippines;\nformulate country and product export strategies; conduct research on\nnew product development and adaptation opportunities in the export\nmarkets, as well as identify the domestic supply base for such\nprepare situation reports on all export production; prepare\nand update country and regional market profiles;\nIntegrated Information system on all aspects of the\nmaintain all\nproducts and\ncommodities relevant to export marketing; formulate, plan, supervise,\n\ncoordinate and monitor the Implementation of both private and official\nincoming and outgoing missions,\nand review the results of such;\nand coordinate international subcontracting arrangements\nbetween and among foreign and Philippine Investors whereby production\noperations and facilities may be located in the Philippines: formulate\nand monitor the Implementation of polleles and guidelines for the\nregistration and certification of Dona fide exporters eligible for the\nvarlous export incentive programs of the Philippines; and revlew and\nidentify appropriate measures to minimize or deregulate export-import\nprocedures and other forelgn trade laws necessary to stimulate the\nInternational marketing of Philippine products;\nTrade Service Corps.\nThis Corps shall assist Philippine\nbusinessmen, producers, and exporters with marketing Information,\nproject development support, and laison with foreign government\ndevelop marketing and commercial intelligence\ndissemination\nto Philippine businessmen through the Trade\nInvestment\nInformation Center;\nprovide direct support to the\nDepartment's overseas promotional programs;\nPhilippine\nbusinessmen handle: trade complaints against foreign firms and\ngovernments:\nsupport Department units in import\nadministration,\nmonitoring of trade agreements, and Investments\npromotion; and be accountable for established foregn investment and\nexport targets for cheir respective areas of responsibility;\n(A) Center for International Trade Expositious and Missions.\nThis Center\nshall organize official participation In foreign trade fairs,\nexhibicions, and expositions, in accordance with che trade promotion\nprogram of the Departments prepare, review, and approve the exhibit\nplans and designs for official participation in foregn trade fairs,\nexpositions, and exhibitions and where necessary,\nprofessional consulting services such as display designers and\nadvertising; supervise the selection, collection, and shipmant of\ndisplay products and materials for use In such official participation;\nimplement Department polices and guidelines for servicing all\nincoming misslons and the conduct of all outgoing missions that are\nrelated to international trade fairs and exhibitions:\nofficial outgoing misstons related to international trade fairs and\nexhibitions; and assist privately organized outgoing missions related\nto International trade fairs and exhibitions;\nExport Marketing Board.\nBoard shall promote the\nestablishment of bonded manufacturing and trading factlities for the\nre-export of those products where a clear net value added may be\ngenerated based on the emerging comparative advantage of the\nPhilippine export Industry; study and analyze the international market\nfor specific products where the Philippines has or can develop\ncomparative advantage;\nrecommend to the\nBureau of Custons the\nlicensing of bonded manufacturing facilities and monitor all bonded\nmanufacturing sites, with the objective of ensuring operational\nefficiency;\nidentify and designate sites where export bonded\nmanufacturing sites shall be located with a view of dispersal to the\nregions; and Initiate studies on the development and maintenance of\nthe country's competitive advantage in export products;\n\n(f) Philippine\nThis Counc11 shall represent\nPhilippine shippers\nIn International liner conferences and negotiate\nIn their behalf, for more favorable freight and shipping rates;\nevaluate and Issue waivers to the use of Philippine flag carriers; and\nprovide assistance and Information to Philippine shippers, specially\nexporters, In matters related to shipping:\nPhilippine Trade Training Center.\nThIs Center shall develop training\nmodules on export and import techniques and procedures; raise the\nlevel of awareness of Philippine businessmen of export opportunities\nand the availability of alternative sources of import products or\ndiversified markets for exports; offer specialized courses for\nspecific industry groups directed at overcoming barriers to oversens\nmarket penetration; and conduct training programs 10 International\ntrade practices, Inspection techniques add exhibition mounting:\n(h) Product Development and Design Center of the Philippines. This Center\nshall provide produce identification, research, and development\nservices to the private sector; conduct seminars and workshops on\nproduct design and development; set up design exhibitioos; publish\nproduct design related materials;\nand conduct continuing research on\nproduct and product packaging design\ntrends and processing\ntechnologies.\n14. Offlce of the Undersecretary for Industry and Investments.\nordice of the Undersecretary for Industry and Investments shall supervise all\nageneles involved In the formulation and Implementation of programs and\nprofects pertinent to the development of domestic industries and the promotion\nof Investments in activities or enterprises critical to the Department's trade\nand Industry development program.\nSuch agencies are enumerated in Section 10\nThe functions of the two (2) bureaus are described below;\nfunctions and organizations of the other agencies are respectively\nand treated in Seceions 16 and 18 of this Executive Order.\n(al Bureau of Small and Medium Business Development.\nThis Bureau shall\nformulate and monitor development programs for private\nInstitutions\ninvolved in assisting the trade and industry sector, delivery\nmechanisms and linkages for marketing, financial and sub-contracting\nservices, and development programs for livelihood and micro, small and\ntadium enterprises.\nBureau of Import Services.\nThis Bureau shall monitor Import levels\nand prices, particularly liberallzed items; analyze and forecast\nimport levels; analyze and publish import return statistics;\nannual review of the substantive components of the Philippine Tariff\nSystem and submit recommendations thereon; perform such other\nfunctions on Import transactions as the President and/or the Central\nBank of the Philippines shall delegate or authorize: and ensure that\nthe Department^s views on goods under the jurisdiction of other\nDepartments are taken into consideration.\n15. office of the Undersecretary for Regional Operations.\nOffice of the Undersecretary for Regional Operations shall exercise supervision\nand control over the Department's Regional Offices, described In Section 9 (a)\nof chis Executive Order.\nIt shall be responsible for the fleld operations of\n\nthe Department, ensuring the full compliance with Department policies, rigorous\nimplementation of\nDepartment rules and regulatons, and the proper\nimplementation of Department plans and programs : the Regional\ntheir respective administrative jurisdictions.\n16. Line Corporate Agencies and Governess Entities.\nThe following\nare the Line Corporate Agencies and Government Entities, defied in Section 9\n(el of this Executive Order that will perform their specific regulatory\nfunctions, particular developmental responsibilities, and speclalized business\nactivities In a manner consonant with the Departmere's mandate, objectives,\npolicies, plans, and programs:\n(A) National Development Company.\nThis Compass shall promote Investments\nIn or establish enterprises for the express purposes of encouraging\nthe private sector to follow suit by provisg the finanedal viability\nof such enterprises; or of filling critfeal gaps in the Input-output\nstructure of Philippine commerce and indussy when the private\n1s unwilling or unable to engage In such asterprises because of the\nmagnitude of investments required or the risk complexion af the\nundertaking.\n(b) Garments and Textile Export Board.\nIsh Board, which shall be\nsupervised by the Undersecretary for asternational Trade, shall\noversee the Implementation of the games: and textile agreements\nbetween the Philippines and other countries.\nparticularly garments\nand textiles quotas;\nquote allocations and\nauthorizations; issue export licenses and adopt appropriate measures\nto expedite their processing, provide the necessary information and\nstatistios relating to the administratios of garments and textiles\nexport quotas and the flow of garments and textiles exports for\nmonitoring purposes and for negotiatioes with other countries;\nimplement rules and regulations for a administration\nInternational\ntextile agreements entered sato between the Philippines\nand Importing countries; and fix and coldest reasonable fees for the\nissuance of export quotas, export authorizations, export licenses, and\nother related services,\nIn accordance wits the Department policies,\nand regulations.\n(e) International Corfee Organization - Certifying Agency.\nwhich shall\nThIs Agency,\nbe supervised by the Undarsegretary for Interdationa1\nTrade, shall oversee the implementatios of the coffec agreements\nbetween the\nPhilippines and other couasies, particularly coffee\n(d) Philippine International Irading Corporatica.\nThis Corporation, which\nsupervised by the Undersecretary for Interoational Trade,\nengage In both export and import trading on new or non-\ntraditional products and markets not normally pursued by the private\nbusiness sector; provide a wide range of export oriented auxillary\nservices to the private sector; arrange for or establish comprehensive\nSVSLeme and physical facilities for handling the collection,\nprocessing, and distribution of cargoes an other commodities; monitor\nor coordinate risk Insurance services for existing Institutions;\npromote or organize, whenever warranted, production enterprises and\nindustrial establishments and collaborasa or associate in joint\n\nventure with any person, association, company,\ndomestic or foreign, in\nor entity, whether\nthe flelds of production,\nprocurement,\nand other related businesses;\nand provide technical,\nadvisory, investigatory, consultancy, and management services with\nrespect to any and all of the functions, activities, and operations of\nthe corporation.\nBoard of Investments.\nThis Board, which shall be supervised by the\nUndersecretary for Industry and Investments shall be responsible for\ncoordinating the formulation and Implementation of short, medium and\nlong term Industrial plaos as well as promoting investments In the\nPhilippines In accordance with national policies and prorities:\nregister, monitor, and grant Investment Incentives to Individual\nenterprises;\nformulate policies and guidelines aimed at creating an\nenvironment conducive to the expansion of existing Investments or\nattracting prospective Investments In the Philipines: Provided, That\nthe Board shall place primary emphasis on Its promotive functions.\nExport Processing Zone Authority, This Authority which shall be\nsupervised by the Undersecretary for Industry and Investments, shall\ndevelop and manage export procesaing zones, in consonance with\nDepartment policies and programs.\n17. Regional Offices.\nThe Department Is hereby authorized to\nestablish, operate and maintain a Department-wide regional office in ench\nthe country's administrative regions.\nEach Regional Office shall be headed Ly\na Regional Director who shall be assisted by an Assistant Regional Director.\nRegional Office shall have, within its administrative region, the Following\nImplement pertinent laws, and the rules, regulations, policies, plans,\nprograms and projects of the Department;\n(b) Provide efficient and effective service to the people;\n(c) Coordinate with the regional offices of other departments, offices and\nagencies in the region;\n(d) Coordinate with the local government units;\n(e) Perform ocher functions as may be provided by law or appropriately\nassigned by the Secretary.\n18. Organiaational Changes.\nThe following organizational changes\nshall apply to the various agencies enumerated hereunder:\nThe Bureau of Industrial Development is hereby abolished and its\nDOWers and functions transferred to the appropriate units\nDepartment.\n(6)\nThe Philippine Cement Industry Authority, the Commission for Heavy\nEngineering Industries, and the Presidential Advisory Committee on the\nCopper Industry are hereby abolished. Their policy formulation and\nplanning functions are hereby transferred to the Board of Investments\nand their implementing functions are transferred to the pertinent line\noperating units of the Department.\n\nThe Construction Industry Authority of the Philippines and the Iron\nand Steel Authority are hereby retained as attached agencies of the\nDepartment: Provided, That these Authorities shall review annually the\ncapability and trustworthiness of the entities accredited by it.\n(d) The Construction Manpower Development Center and the Construction\nManpower Development Foundation are transferred to the National\nIndustrial Manpower Training Council.\nThe National Cottage Industries Development Authority Is hereby\nreorganized into the Cottage Industry Technology Center and Its\nfunetions other than technology development and training, are hereby\ntransferred to the Bureau of Small and Medium Business Development and\nrelevant line operating units of the Department.\n(F) The Price Stabilization Council Is hereby abolished, but its powers\nand functions may be exercised by the Secretary of Trade and Industry\nin emergency situations as the Secretary deems appropriate.\n(8)\nThe Philippine Patents Office is hereby converted into the Bureau\nPatents, Trademarks and Technology Transfer.\nThe Technology Transfer Board is hereby abolshed and Its powers and\nfunctions transferred\nLo the Bureau of Patents, Trademarks and\nTechnology Transfer and the appropriate line operating units of the\nDepartment\n(1)\nThe Bureau of Domestic Trade Is hereby abolished and its appropriate\npowers and functions are hereby transferred to the Bureau of Trade\nRegulation aod Consumer Protection and the Bureau of Domestic\nPromotion, respectively.\n(1)\nThe Bureau of Forego Trade Is hereby abolished and Its appropriate\npowers and functions are hereby transferred to the Bureau of\nTrade Promotion and the Bureau of Import Services, respectively.\n(k) The Bureau of Small and Medium Industries is hereby reorganized as the\nBureau of Small and Medium Business Development.\n(1)\nThe Trade and Industry Information Center is hereby reorganized as\nthe Trade and Investment Information Center\nPlanning Service\nOperational Planing.\nis hereby reorganized as the Office\nService is hereby reorganized as the Office of Legal\nThe Administrative Service is hereby reorganized as the General\nAdministrative Service.\nThe Financial and Management Service 1s hereby reorganized as the\nFinancial Management Service.\n\n(4)\nProduct Standards Agency Is hereby reorganized as the Bureau\nProduct Standards.\nPublic Relations Office, the Human Resource Development Service\nand the Management Information Service are hereby created.\n(5}\nThe NDC-Nacida Raw Materials Corporation is hereby abolished,\npowers and functions transferred to the appropriate units\nDepartment.\nThe Metals Industry Research and Development Center 1s hereby\ncransferred to the National Science and Technology\nProvided, however, That the transfer shall be covered by a memorandum\nof agreement defining the relationship of the Department and\nCenter and the manner by which equipment and resources shall be\naccessed, and that the Investment and trade promotion aspects\npertaining to the metals industry are recognized to be the funetions\nof the Department In cooperation with the National Science and\nTechnology Authority.\nThe Philippine Textile Research Institute is hereby transferred to the\nNational Science and Technology Authority: Provided, however, That the\ntransfer shall be covered by a memorandum of agreement defining the\nrelationship of the Department and the Institute and the manner by\nwhich equipment and resources are accessed; Provided, Further That the\nInvestment and trade promotion aspects pertainlig to the textile\nIndustry are recognized to be the functions of the\nDepartment 1n\ncooperation with the National Science and Technology Authority.\nThe Philippine\nTrade Exhibition Center is hereby merged with the\nCenter For International Trade Expositions and Missions, with the\nlatter as the surviving entity.\nThe Trade Policy\nOffice Is hereby reorganized as the Bureau of\nInternational Trade Relations.\n(x) The Videogram Regulatory Board is hereby attached to the Department.\nThe Design Center of the Philippines Is hereby reorganized into the\nProduct Develooment and Design Center of the Philippines.\n19. Transitory\nProvisions.\nIn accomplishing the acts of\nreorganization herein prescribed, the following transitory provisions shall be\ncomplled with, unless otherwise provided elsewhere in this Executive Order.\nThe transfer of functions which results in the abolition of the\ngovernment unit that\nappropriations,\nhas exercised them shall Include the\nfunds, records, equipment, facilities, other assets\nand personnel as may be necessary to the proper discharge of the\ntransferred functions.\nThe abolished unit's remaining appropriations\nand funds, if any, shall revert to the General Fund and its remaining\nassets, If any, shall be allocated to such appropriate units as the\nSecretary shall determine or shall otherwise be disposed of In\naccordance with the Government Auditing Code and other pertinent laws,\nrules and regulations.\nIts liabilities, if any, shall likewise be\n\ntreated in accordance with the Government Auditing Code and other\npertinent laws, rules and regulations.\nIts personnel, shall, in a\nhold-over capacity, continue to perform their duties and\nresponsibilities and receive the corresponding salaries and benefits:\nProvided, That the personnel, whose positions are not included in the\nDepartment's new position structure and staffing pattern approved and\nprescribed by the Secretary under Section 21 hereof or who are not\nreappointed, shall be deemed separated from the service and shall be\nentitled to the benefits provided for under the second paragraph of\nthe same Section 21.\nThe transfer of funetions which does not result in the abolicion of\nthe government unit that has exercised them shall Include the\nappropriations, funds, records, , equipment, facilities, other assets\nand personnel as may be necessary to the proper discharge\ntransferred funetions.\nThe liabilities,\nthat may have been\n† n connection with the discharge of\nthe transferred\nfunctions, shall be treated In accordance with the Government Auditing\nCode and ocher pertinent laws, rules and regulations.\nIts personnel\nshall, in a hold-over capacity, continue to perform their respective\nduties and responsibilities and receive the corresponding salaries and\nbenefits: Provided, That the personnel, whose position Is not Included\nIn the Department's new position structure and staffing pattern\napproved and prescrlbed by the Secretary under Section 21 hereof or\nwho has not been reappointed, shall be deemed separated from the\nservice and shall be enticed co the benefits provided for under the\nsecond paragraph of the same Section 21.\nIn case of merger or consolidation of government units, the new Or\nunit shall exercise the functions (subject tO the\nreorganization herein prescribed and the laws, rules and regulations,\npertinent to the exercise of such functions) and shall acquire the\nappropriations, funds, records, equipment, facilities, other assets,\nliabilities If any, and personnel of (1) the unfts that compose the\nmerged wait or (2) the absorbed unit, as the case may be.\npersonnel shall, in a hold-over capacity, continue to perform their\nrespective duties and responsibilities and receive the\nsalacies and benefits: Provided,\ncorresponding\nThat any personnel, whose position\nis not included In the Department's new posttion structure and\nstaffing pattern approved and prescribed by the Secretary under"}},{"id":"PH-H17890-A21","no":21,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 21"},"text":{"en":"hereof or who is not reappointed, shall be deemed separated\nfrom the service and shall be entitled to the benefits provided under\nthe second paragraph of the same Section 21.\nThe transfer of a government unit shall Include the functions,\nappropriations, funds, records, equipment, facilities, if any, of the\ntransferred unit as\nwell as the personnel thereof, as may be\nnecessary, who shall, in a hold-over capacity, continue to perform\ntheir respective duties and responsibilities and receive\ncorresponding salaries and benefits: Provided, That the personnel of\nthe transferred unit whose positions are not Included in the new\nposition structure and staffing pattern approved and prescribed by the\nSecretary or who are not reappointed shall be deemed separated from\nthe service and shall be entitled to the benefies provided under the\nsecond paragraph of Section 21 hereof.\n\nIn case of termination of a function which does not result fo the\nabolition of the government unic which has performed such function,\nthe appropriations and funds Intended to finance the discharge of such\nfunction shall revert to the General Fund, while the records,\nequipment, facilities, choses in action, rights and other assets used\nIn connection with the discharge of such function shall be allocated\nto the appropriate units as the Secretary shall determine or shall\notherwise be disposed In accordance with the Government Auditing Code\nand other pertinent laws, rules and regulations.\nThe personnel who\nhave performed such functions, whose positions are not Included In the\nnew position structure and staffing pattern approved and prescribed by\nSecretary under Section 21 hereof or who have not been\nreappointed, shall be deemed separated from the service and shall be\nentitled to the benefits provided under the second paragraph of the\nsame Section 21.\n(E) In case of the abolition of a government unit which does not result In\nthe transfer of its functions to another unit, the appropriations and\nfunds of the abolished unit shall revert to the General Fund, while\nthe records, equipment, facilities, choses in action, rights, and\nother assets thereof shall be allocated to such appropolate units as\nthe Secretary shall determine.\nThe liabilitles of the abolished unit\nshall be treated in accordance with the Government Auditing Code and\nother pertinent laws, rules and regulations, while the personnel\nthereof, whose posision is not included in the Department's new\nposition structure and staffing pattern approved and prescribed by\nthe Secretary under Section 21 hereof or who has not been reappointed,\nshall be deemed separated from the service and shall be entitled\nthe benefits provided under the second paragraph of the same section\n21.\nOrder shall\nFunds needed to carry out the provisions of this\nbe taken Erom funds avallable in the Department.\n21.\nNew Structure and Pattero.\nUpon approval of this Executive\nOrder, the officers and employees of the Department and agencies attached\nIt, shall, in a hold-over capacity, continue to perform their respective duties\nand responsibilities and recelve the corresponding salaries and benefits.\nThe new position structures and staffing patterns of the Department and\nagencies attached to it, shall be approved and prescribed by the Secretary\nwithin one hundred twenty (120) days from the approval of this Executive Order\nand the authorized positions created thereunder shall be filled with regular\nappointments by him or by the President, as the case may be. Those incumbents\nwhose positions are not included therein or who are no reappointed shall be\ndeemed separated from the service.\nThose separated from the.\nservice shall\nreceive the retirement benefits to which they may be entitled under existing\nlaws, rules and regulations.\nOtherwise, they shall be paid the equivalent of\none-month basic salary for every year of service, or the equivalent nearest\nfraction thereof\nFavorable to them on the basis of highest salary received,\nbut in no case shall such payment exceed the equivalent of twelve (12) months\n\nPerformance Evaluation.\nThe Secretary is hereby\nrequired to formulate and enforce a systen of measuring and evaluating\nperiodically and objectively the performance of the Department and submit the\nsame annually to the President.\n23. Notice or Consent Requirement.\nIf any reorganizational change\nherein authorized is of such substance or materfality as to prejudice third\npersons with rights recognized by law or contract such as notice to or consent\nof creditors Is required to be made or obtained pursuant to any agreement\nentered Into with any of such creditors, such notice or consent requirement\nshall be complied with prior to the implementation of such reorgaoizational\n24. Prohibition Against Change.\nNo change in the reorganization\nherein prescribed shall be valid except upon prfor approval of the President.\nfor the purpose of promoting efficiency and effectiveness in the delivery of\npublic services.\n25. Implementing Authority of Secretary.\nThe Secretary shall issue\nsuch rules, regulations and other Issuances as may be necessary to ensure the\neffective Implementation of the provisions of this Executive Order.\n26. Separability.\nAny portion or provision of this Executive Order\n*that may be declared unconstitutional shall not have the effect of nullifying\nother portions or provisions hereof as long as such remaining portions\nprovisions can still subsist and be given effect lo their entirety.\n27 .\nRepealing Clause.\nAll laws, ordinances, rules, regulations,\nother Issuances or parts thereof, which are inconsistent with this Executive\nOrder, are hereby repealed or modifled accordingly.\n28. Effectivity.\nimmediately upon its approval.\nThis Executive Order shall take effect\nAPPROVED In the City of Manila, Philippines, this 27th\nFebruery, in the Year of Our Lord, Nineteen Hundred and Eighty-Seven.\nbraym b. Aquint\nBy the President:\nPOKER P. ARROYO"}}],"pack":"ph-p157"};
