  FT["PH-H18396"] = {"id":"PH-H18396","coverage":"full","language":"en","sourceName":"The LawPhil Project — Arellano Law Foundation","sourceUrl":"","fetchedAt":"2026-10-28","articleCount":1,"structureMode":"WHOLE","title":{"zh":null,"en":"IVIl1...U-C.f:.$iJ:.TG EXECUTI.VE ORDER l~O. 188","orig":"IVIl1...U-C.f:.$iJ:.TG EXECUTI.VE ORDER l~O. 188"},"level":"law","status":"active","docNumber":"Executive Order No. 188","issuingBody":"President of the Philippines","completenessNote":"全文，共 1 条；逐字取自 LawPhil PDF 文本化成果（第三方 OCR，非机翻），原始文件 EO_00188_1987.txt","textQuality":"ocr-vendor","sourceFile":"菲律宾/法律原文/07_行政命令_EO/EO_00188_1987.txt","country":"PH","countryName":"菲律宾","layer":"intl","articles":[{"id":"PH-H18396-A1","no":1,"noLabel":{},"text":{"en":"Corporation\nectivities\nbe directed,\ncontrolled\nand Jlanaged by a\nBoard of Directors\nbe cvmposed of\n(7)\nTrallSporction\nc,nd Coillillu~ic&';:;ions,\nI\"l&nct~(.;r al~ G.ov::rnor\nI-letropoli\ntan l'Ianile\nCOillEisEion,\nv-ice-Chairman;\nof Trad'e ~:lQ Ir...uustry;\nand the C11airllian. of the\n:;j;.:;velopment Bank\nof the Philippines.\nas alternate\nmembers 0 \"~hey shall\nprincipals\nOrdex spall\nimmediately.\n...{\n.-2\n-\nof Ou~: La~~d, nineteen\nand eighty-saven..\n~\n..\n'; '.~\n?hi lip pines\n~'~\n.\n~\n\"\nJ,OKE'~ P. j'RROYO\nFy:~,c\"t. i ve Secretary\n\\' ,\n,\n~\n.\""}}],"pack":"ph-p157"};
  FT["PH-H18397"] = {"id":"PH-H18397","coverage":"full","language":"en","sourceName":"The LawPhil Project — Arellano Law Foundation","sourceUrl":"","fetchedAt":"2026-10-28","articleCount":1,"structureMode":"WHOLE","title":{"zh":null,"en":"GUIDELINES ON THE ENTRY AND STAY OF FOREIGN STUDENTS IN THE PHILIPPINES AND THE ESTABLISHMENT OF AN INTER- AGENCY COMMITTEE FOR THE PURPOSE","orig":"GUIDELINES ON THE ENTRY AND STAY OF FOREIGN STUDENTS IN THE PHILIPPINES AND THE ESTABLISHMENT OF AN INTER- AGENCY COMMITTEE FOR THE PURPOSE"},"level":"law","status":"active","docNumber":"Executive Order No. 188","issuingBody":"President of the Philippines","completenessNote":"全文，共 1 条；逐字取自 LawPhil PDF 文本化成果（第三方 OCR，非机翻），原始文件 EO_00188_1994.txt","textQuality":"ocr-vendor","sourceFile":"菲律宾/法律原文/07_行政命令_EO/EO_00188_1994.txt","country":"PH","countryName":"菲律宾","layer":"intl","articles":[{"id":"PH-H18397-A1","no":1,"noLabel":{},"text":{"en":"Certificate of Eligibility for Admission (CEA)\n194111\nfrom the Decs for certain courses of study, such\nas in medicine and in nursing, where restrictions\nmay exist on the enrollment of foreign students\ndue to a shortage of facilities.\nOnce issued, the\nCEA shall remain valid for the duration of the\ncourse of study, provided the student attends his\nclasses and continues to receive satisfactory\n(3)\nThe DECS, in consultation with the Commission on\nHigher Education, shall determine what courses of\nstudy require the issuance of a CEA and shall draw\nup a list for this purpose not later than sixty\n(60) days from the effectivity of this Executive\nOrder. Said list may be updated by the DECS from\ntime to time as may be necessary.\nDECS shall provide all schools with\ncomparative equivalences for the major foreign\neducational\nconcerning\nsystems, and should any question\nequivalences arise,\nconcerned shall secure the comments of the DECS\nbefore accepting a foreign student for enrollment.\n(5) Enrollment in any level shall require completion\nof the lower particular level, for example, an\napplicant for the tertiary or collegiate level\nshould be a graduate of high school or its\nequivalent.\n(6) Elementary, secondary and tertiary enrollment in\nPhilippine schools by the spouses and children of\nthe following categories will be treated on the\nsame basis as Philippine nationals: (a) permanent\nforeign residents, (b) aliens with valid working\npermits, (c) foreign diplomat personnel, and (d)\nfrom duly accredited international\norganizations residing in the Philippines, and (e)\nholders of Special Investor's Resident Visa (SIR)\nand Special Retiree's Resident Visa (SRRV).\nIssuance of Visas.\n(7) The procedure and documentation for the issuance\nof visas shall be kept to minimum.\napplicants for student visa shall submit the\nfollowing documents to the Philippine Foreign\nEstablishments\n(PFSE) located in the\ncountry of their residence:\n(a) A copy of the Notice of Acceptance from a\nPhilippine school and where applicable, a\ncopy of the CEA;\n(b) Documentary proof of support to\nexpenses incidental to their studies, such as\nboard and lodging as well as return air\n(c) Authenticated scholastic records;\nAuthenticated Police Clearance\nCertificate\nfrom the applicant's country of origin or\nResults of medical examinations conducted by\nan authorized physician; and\n(f) Other documents that may be required in the\nindividual case by the Consular Officer,\nprovided that it shall not be the task of the\nPFSE to determine the applicants scholastic\nfitness for the program applied for.\ndocumentary requirements are in order, the\nPFSE concerned shall issue a student visa.\nC. Arrival and Stay in the Philippines.\n(8) The process for duly authorized foreign students\nto enter and stay in the Philippines, including\nthe issuance of the\nCertificate of\nRegistration (AR), shall be facilitated.\nstudent's authorized period of stay shall be\nconsistent with the length of the course of study\nto which he has been accepted by a Philippine\n(9) It shall be the responsibility of the individual\nschool in which the foreign student is enrolled to\nreport promptly at the close of each enrollment\nperiod, to the Bureau of Immigration, those\nforeign students who have been accepted by the\nschool but who failed to register, either for the\nfirst time or for subsequent terms.\nthe individual school shall also report promptly\nafter the end of each term, those students who\nwere absent from the final examinations for the\nThe reporting herein required shall be\nstrictly complied with by the individual school.\n(10) Appropriate arrangements shall be made by the\nagencies concerned for foreigners who are already\nPhilippines under other valid visa\narrangements, to facilitate their conversion into\nprerequisites listed herein are complied with.\nSecurity Matters.\n(11) The appropriate authorities may check whenever\nnecessary the activities of foreign students\nbrought to its attention, whose activities appear\nto be inimical to the security of the state. They\nshall be responsible for the apprehension of\nforeign students not complying with Philippine\nImmigration laws and regulations.\nFor instance, a\nreport that a foreign student is under employment\nshall be immediately forwarded to the Bureau of\nImmigration as basis for the cancellation of the\nforeign student's entry permit and for initiation\nof deportation proceedings.\n(12) Those agencies charged with the maintenance of\ninternal security shall undertake steps necessary\nto safeguard national security interests, without\nin any way further encumbering the process of\napplication,\nauthorization of foreign students in the\nPhilippines.\nEstablishment and\nComposition of the\nCommittee on Foreign Students.\nThere is hereby created an Inter-\nAgency Committee on Foreign Students herein referred to as the\nCommittee, which shall have the following membership:\nDepartment of Education, Culture and Sports\nDepartment of Foreign Affairs\nCommission on Higher Education\nBureau of Immigration\nNational Bureau of Investigation\nNational Intelligence Coordinating Agency\nCo-Chairman\nresponsibilities:\nDuties and Responsibilities of the Committee.\nthe following duties and\n(1) Promulgate simplified procedures and implementing\nguidelines governing the entry and stay of foreign\nstudents in the Philippines in accordance with the\nprovisions of this Executive Order within sixty (60)\ndays from the effectivity thereof;\n(2) Monitor and coordinate the implementation\nOrder by the departments and\n(3) Meet regularly to assess the progress of the whole\nprogram, to ensure that the promotion of the\nPhilippines as a center for education in the region is\neffectively encouraged and undertaken;\n(4) Request representatives from other agencies and/or the\nprivate sector to attend its meetings, when it deems\nnecessary and proper.\nRepealing Provision.\nThis Executive Order\nrepeals Executive Order No. 104, dated 4 December 1967 and all\nother executive issuances, regulations, or any parts thereof,\nwhich are inconsistent with the provisions of this Executive\nEffectivity. This Executive Order shall take\neffect immediately.\nONEnen the city of Manila, Philippines, this 19K\nJuly in the year of Our Lord, Nineteen Hundred and Ninety-Four.\nBy the President:\nTEOFISTO Y. GUINGONA, JR.\nExecutive Secretary"}}],"pack":"ph-p157"};
